E["item:a-simple-compass"] = {t="item",n="A Simple Compass",z="stormwind",s="At the burned Alexston Farmstead in Westfall, A Simple Compass waits in a small chest. It belonged to Baros Alexston before he became Stormwind's City Architect.",h="At the burned Alexston Farmstead in Westfall, A Simple Compass waits in a small chest.",sec={{t="A Boyhood Keepsake",b="Baros Alexston grew up working his family's farm in Westfall. His simple compass was his first navigational instrument, and may have stirred his interest in geometry, drafting, and exploration. The Defias Brotherhood raided and burned the farmstead, leaving the compass in a sturdy chest among the ruins as bandits overran the farmland.",sp=0},{t="Sentimental Value",b="Baros's father escaped the destruction but could not carry the family's possessions to safety. The compass offers little use to a master builder within Stormwind City's stone walls, yet it holds great meaning for Baros. Its return would restore a rare, intact link to his humble beginnings and the peaceful countryside of his childhood.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is A Simple Compass?",a="A Simple Compass is a modest, non-magical pocket compass Baros Alexston owned as a boy on his family's Westfall farm.",al={"simple compass","alexston compass","baros compass"},it="identity"},{q="Where is the compass located?",a="The compass is inside Alexston's Chest in the burned-out ruins of the Alexston Farmstead, just west of Sentinel Hill in Westfall.",al={"where to find compass","compass location","alexston chest location"},gp=true},{q="Who wants this compass returned?",a="Baros Alexston, Stormwind's City Architect, wants the compass returned. He can be found near the town hall in Cathedral Square.",al={"who needs the compass","compass turn in","who owns the compass"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why was the compass left behind at the farm?",a="The Defias outlaws raided and burned the Alexston farm. Baros's father fled for his life and could not carry the family's heavier possessions, leaving the chest in the wreckage.",al={"why did they leave the compass","what happened to the farm"},it="origin"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Helping Baros Alexston recover his keepsake shows the human cost of the Defias uprising. Even prominent leaders in Stormwind have lost their family homes to the turmoil in Westfall.",["race:Human"]="As a human of the kingdom, you can see in the compass the contrast between Stormwind City's safe, gilded courtyards and Westfall's abandoned, lawless frontier."},kw={"alexston","baros","beginnings","chest","compass","farmstead","stormwind","westfall"},rel={"npc:baros-alexston","quest:399","subzone:alexston-farmstead","zone:westfall","subzone:sentinel-hill","subzone:cathedral-square","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"A Simple Compass","Humble Beginnings"}}
E["item:bartleby-s-mug"] = {t="item",n="Bartleby's Mug",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind, a stubborn brawler keeps Bartleby's Mug close. A warrior must win it in a tavern brawl, then watch Bartleby drain his drink before he surrenders it.",h="In Stormwind, a stubborn brawler keeps Bartleby's Mug close.",sec={{t="A Brawler's Prize",b="Bartleby keeps his mug close, and a young warrior in Stormwind must wrest it from him. The stubborn brawler gives it up only after a fight leaves him beaten. Even then, Bartleby drains every last drop before handing over the mug as proof of victory.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Bartleby's Mug used for?",a="A warrior takes Bartleby's Mug as proof of victory in a training trial. Bringing it to the drill instructor shows the warrior could defeat a stubborn tavern brawler and make him surrender it.",al={"bartleby mug purpose","why do i need bartlebys mug","what does the mug do"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Who owns the mug originally?",a="Bartleby owns the mug. The belligerent drunk spends his time drinking and brawling, and gives it up only after an aspiring warrior beats him in a fistfight. He finishes his drink first.",al={"who is bartleby","bartlebys owner","who has the mug"},it="identity"},{q="Who asks for Bartleby's Mug?",a="Burlguard asks for Bartleby's Mug. The warrior trainer in Stormwind watches the brawl and requires the mug as proof before continuing the warrior's martial education.",al={"who wants the mug","who do i give bartlebys mug to","bartlebys mug turn in"},it="target",gp=true},{q="What is Bartleby's Mug?",a="Bartleby's Mug is the personal drinking vessel of Bartleby, a brawling tavern patron in Stormwind. The mug serves as concrete proof of a young warrior's prowess—surrendered by Bartleby only after being thoroughly bested in combat, and only once he has taken the time to finish every last drop inside it.",al={"what is bartlebys mug","bartleby mug","mug of bartleby"},it="identity",add="481c5411"},{q="Why does Burlguard want Bartleby's Mug?",a="Burlguard demands the mug as physical evidence that you stood your ground and defeated Bartleby in a tavern brawl. Taking a committed drinker's beloved mug is no small feat; surrendering it proves that you persuaded Bartleby with your fists and are ready to continue your warrior training.",al={"why want bartlebys mug","why does burlguard want the mug","burlguard mug purpose"},it="why_wanted",add="a3659338"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As an Alliance warrior, you earn Bartleby's Mug by wrestling it from him. The fight calls for grit and force when words fail."},kw={"bartleby","bartleby's mug","burlguard","stormwind","tavern brawl","warrior training"},rel={"quest:1665","quest:1640","quest:1639","quest:1638","npc:bartleby","topic:warrior"},src={"Bartleby's Mug","Bartleby's Mug (quest)"}}
E["item:black-claw-stout"] = {t="item",n="Black Claw Stout",z="stormwind",s="Beneath Stormwind, Zardeth of the Black Claw prepares a drink for Lord Wishock. The stout is delivered as an ordinary tavern beverage.",h="Beneath Stormwind, Zardeth of the Black Claw prepares a drink for Lord Wishock.",sec={{t="A Toxic Draught",b="Zardeth of the Black Claw works beneath the notice of Stormwind's city guard, in the operation below the Slaughtered Lamb's taprooms. Lord Wishock repeatedly threatens to shut it down, though he runs up unpaid bar tabs upstairs. Zardeth decides to settle the score with the noble's weakness for strong drink. He disguises a lethal dose in a common tavern refreshment.",sp=1},{t="Quiet Assassination",b="Lord Wishock receives the stout in Stormwind Keep's Hall of Petitioners. His pompous arrogance and thirst leave him eager to accept what he mistakes for a servant's attentive offering. The noble downs the brew on the spot. Its poison acts almost instantly, silencing one of the cult's most persistent political critics under the Royal Court's very noses.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Black Claw Stout?",a="Zardeth of the Black Claw concocts Black Claw Stout in the catacombs beneath the Slaughtered Lamb in Stormwind's Mage Quarter for Lord Wishock.",al={"what is this drink","black claw stout lore","poison brew"},it="identity"},{q="Who is the target of the stout?",a="Lord Wishock is the target, a high-handed noble in the Hall of Petitioners who campaigns to shut down the warlock haven while drinking there on credit.",al={"who drinks it","who dies from black claw stout","wishock target"},it="target"},{q="Who created the brew?",a="Zardeth of the Black Claw brews the stout in the crypts beneath the Slaughtered Lamb.",al={"creator of black claw stout","who made this","zardeth brew"},it="origin"},{q="Why is Lord Wishock offered the stout?",a="Zardeth sends Lord Wishock the stout in the Hall of Petitioners, asking the courier to see how the noble likes his special brew.",al={"does wishock die","black claw stout effect"},sp=1},{q="Why does Zardeth want you to deliver Black Claw Stout to Lord Wishock?",a="Lord Wishock is a hypocritical noble who spends his days lobbying to shut down the Slaughtered Lamb while spending his nights upstairs drinking and running up an unpaid tavern tab. To silence him permanently, Zardeth concocted this deadly special brew to exploit Wishock's weakness for liquor and eliminate him under the guise of offering a refreshing drink.",al={"why deliver black claw stout","why give wishock black claw stout","zardeth wishock stout why"},sp=1,it="why_wanted",add="a6b6f1b7"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="For Stormwind's hidden warlock coven, the brew is an errand. A meddling noble wants its haven beneath the Slaughtered Lamb shut down.",["faction:Alliance"]="Carrying the brew into Stormwind Keep brings the warlocks operating beneath the Slaughtered Lamb close to the capital's nobles."},kw={"black claw stout","hall of petitioners","lord wishock","poison","slaughtered lamb","stormwind keep","zardeth"},rel={"quest:335","npc:zardeth-of-the-black-claw","quest:397"},src={"Black Claw Stout","A Noble Brew (2)"}}
E["item:book-stresses-of-iron"] = {t="item",n="Book: Stresses of Iron",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind Keep, Margulf Blaggon’s book on metallurgy has been lent to Northshire Abbey for copying.",h="In Stormwind Keep, Margulf Blaggon’s book on metallurgy has been lent to Northshire Abbey for copying.",sec={{t="A Borrowed Volume",b="Margulf Blaggon wrote about the practical and theoretical sides of metallurgy. Milton Sheaf cared for the volume in the Royal Library of Stormwind Keep. The library lent it to Northshire Abbey, where Brother Paxton copied it by hand for his own collection. Paxton’s work took far longer than expected, and Brother Kristoff waited anxiously in Cathedral Square for the book to return to the city.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the book about?",a="Margulf Blaggon’s book covers metallurgy and metalworking, in both theory and practice.",al={"what is stresses of iron","stresses of iron topic","book contents"},it="identity"},{q="Why was the book at Northshire Abbey?",a="Brother Paxton borrowed the book from Stormwind’s Royal Library to copy it by hand for his own collection before returning the original.",al={"why did paxton have it","why in northshire"},it="history"},{q="Who wanted the book returned?",a="Brother Kristoff wanted the book returned. Waiting in Cathedral Square, he urgently asked for it, and an adventurer traced its whereabouts between the Royal Library and Northshire.",al={"who needs the book","who is waiting for it"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where does Stresses of Iron come from, and who wrote it?",a="The book was penned by Margulf Blaggon as a scholarly treatise on metallurgy. Its home is the Royal Library inside Stormwind Keep, though Brother Paxton borrowed the volume and brought it to Northshire Abbey so he could painstakingly transcribe a copy for his own shelves.",al={"who wrote stresses of iron","stresses of iron author","origin of stresses of iron"},it="origin",add="7d684098"}},ang={["profession:Blacksmithing"]="Margulf Blaggon’s book explores iron’s strengths and the practical limits of working with it."},kw={"brother kristoff","brother paxton","margulf blaggon","metallurgy","milton sheaf","northshire abbey","royal library","stresses of iron"},rel={"quest:346","quest:344","quest:343","npc:brother-kristoff","subzone:royal-library","subzone:northshire-abbey","subzone:cathedral-square","subzone:stormwind-keep"},src={"Book: Stresses of Iron","Return to Kristoff"}}
E["item:burning-blood-quest-item"] = {t="item",n="Burning Blood (quest item)",z="stormwind",s="In Duskwood, Burning Blood is gathered from the Nightbane worgen. Grimand Elmore needs twenty vials for experiments in smithing.",h="In Duskwood, Burning Blood is gathered from the Nightbane worgen.",sec={{t="A Volatile Reagent",b="Nightbane worgen prowl Duskwood with a strange fury, and their blood burns with real heat. The fluid can be drawn from worgen haunting the timberlands and Roland's Doom. Though foul to gather, its heat draws the interest of armorers seeking to temper resilient plate.",sp=0},{t="Elmore's Experiment",b="Grimand Elmore works as an armorer in Stormwind's Dwarven District. He wants to test smithing methods developed by his former student Furen Longbeard. For the experiment, Elmore needs Burning Blood and a dense burning rock held by the worgen chieftain Gutspill. Those who bring back the bubbling fluid are promised sturdy warrior armor from his forge.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Burning Blood?",a="Burning Blood is a hot bodily fluid taken from Nightbane worgen in Duskwood. Grimand Elmore needs it for smithing experiments.",al={"burning blood lore","what is burning blood","worgen blood"},it="identity"},{q="Where does Burning Blood come from?",a="Burning Blood comes from Nightbane worgen in Duskwood, especially those around Roland's Doom.",al={"where to get burning blood","who drops burning blood","burning blood location"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Grimand Elmore need it?",a="Grimand Elmore needs Burning Blood to test smithing methods developed by Furen Longbeard. With a burning rock, he plans to forge protective mail for a warrior.",al={"why grimand wants burning blood","grimand elmore blood quest"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why is the blood of the Nightbane burning?",a="Nightbane are unnatural fiends summoned by dark, chaotic magic. The curse in their blood gives it a fierce, unnatural heat.",al={"why do worgen have burning blood","is worgen blood fire"},it="power"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="Grimand Elmore uses Burning Blood to test smithing methods and promises durable plate armor to warriors who bring it to him.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="Smiths can use unusual materials like burning worgen blood to quench and temper heavy metals at extreme heat."},kw={"burning blood","duskwood","furen longbeard","grimand elmore","gutspill","nightbane","roland's doom","worgen"},rel={"quest:1705","item:burning-rock","quest:1700","subzone:roland-s-doom","zone:duskwood","topic:worgen","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Burning Blood (quest item)","Burning Blood (quest)"}}
E["item:burning-rock"] = {t="item",n="Burning Rock",z="stormwind",s="In Duskwood, Burning Rock smolders in the depths of Roland's Doom. Gutspill, leader of the Nightbane worgen, carries it, and Grimand Elmore in Stormwind needs it with fiery worgen blood to forge enchanted armor for promising warriors.",h="In Duskwood, Burning Rock smolders in the depths of Roland's Doom.",sec={{t="A Smoldering Prize",b="Gutspill carries Burning Rock through the shafts of Roland's Doom. Grimand Elmore in Stormwind wants its heat for armor made with fiery worgen blood. He is testing smithing techniques developed by his peer Furen Longbeard, to make tough plates for veteran fighters.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Burning Rock found?",a="Gutspill carries Burning Rock inside Roland's Doom in eastern Duskwood.",al={"burning rock location","who drops burning rock","where to get burning rock"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who wants the Burning Rock?",a="Grimand Elmore, a dwarven smith in Stormwind City's Dwarven District, wants Burning Rock to test experimental smithing techniques.",al={"who needs burning rock","who turns in burning rock","grimand elmore burning rock"},gp=true},{q="Why does Grimand Elmore need it?",a="Grimand plans to test crafting techniques developed by Furen Longbeard. With Nightbane worgen blood, the smoldering rock provides heat for forging a unique suit of armor.",al={"burning rock use","why burning rock","what does burning rock do"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What connection does this rock have to the worgen?",a="The Nightbane worgen in Roland's Doom have strange fiery traits, including burning blood. Their leader, Gutspill, keeps Burning Rock deep in the mine. Whether the worgen found it there or brought it with them is unknown.",al={"why do worgen have burning rock","gutspill burning rock lore"},it="ties"},{q="What is the Burning Rock?",a="The Burning Rock is a rare, heated mineral found deep within the haunted woods of Duskwood. Held by Gutspill, the leader among the feral Nightbane worgen occupying Roland's Doom, this fiery stone retains intense heat and is sought after for specialized smithing and metallurgy.",al={"what is burning rock","burning rock item","about burning rock"},it="identity",add="a40de154"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you brave Roland's Doom for Burning Rock. Grimand Elmore rewards your valor with custom armor forged using its heat.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="As a blacksmith, you can study Burning Rock as an unusual heat source. Stormwind and Ironforge armorers explore unorthodox ways to smelt and temper armor."},kw={"burning rock","duskwood","furen longbeard","grimand elmore","gutspill","nightbane worgen","roland's doom"},rel={"quest:1705","subzone:roland-s-doom","quest:1700","item:burning-blood-quest-item","topic:worgen","zone:duskwood","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Burning Rock","Burning Blood (quest)"}}
E["item:cask-of-scalder"] = {t="item",n="Cask of Scalder",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind, a cask of Barleybrew Scalder is on its way to an old acquaintance. The fiery ale carries a favor between dwarves.",h="In Stormwind, a cask of Barleybrew Scalder is on its way to an old acquaintance.",sec={{t="A Dwarven Bargain",b="Travelers who have proved themselves across the Rethban Gauntlet carry Barleybrew Scalder to Furen Longbeard in Stormwind's Dwarven District. The dwarf is an artisan shieldsmith, and he considers dry times intolerable. A cask of the warming ale gives Yorus Barleybrew a way to call in an old favor and secure fine dwarven craftsmanship.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is inside the Cask of Scalder?",a="Barleybrew Scalder fills the cask, a fiery brew crafted by the Barleybrew family. Dwarves prize its strong flavor and warming punch.",al={"what drink is in this","scalder ale","barleybrew scalder"},it="item"},{q="Who is this cask intended for?",a="The cask is meant for Furen Longbeard, an expert dwarf shieldsmith who works in Stormwind's Dwarven District.",al={"who gets the cask","where do i bring this","scalder recipient"},it="target"},{q="Why is this cask being delivered to Furen Longbeard?",a="Furen owes Yorus Barleybrew a favor. The cask eases Furen's thirst during what he calls dry times and persuades him to forge a sturdy, exceptional shield for the courier.",al={"why furen wants scalder","shieldsmith favor","purpose of cask"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is the Cask of Scalder?",a="The Cask of Scalder is a wooden keg filled with Barleybrew Scalder, a hearty brew produced by the Barleybrew family. Yorus Barleybrew entrusts it to you as a gift and introduction for his dwarven friend in Stormwind, the shieldsmith Furen Longbeard.",al={"what is cask of scalder","cask of scalder","what is scalder"},it="identity",add="df3534f2"},{q="Where does the Cask of Scalder come from, and who made it?",a="The cask is provided by Yorus Barleybrew in Redridge Mountains following your triumph through the Rethban Gauntlet. Brewed by the renowned Barleybrew clan, this distinctive draught is brought out as a hearty favor worthy of securing a masterwork dwarf-forged shield.",al={"who made cask of scalder","cask of scalder origin","where did cask of scalder come from"},it="origin",add="1fd358f8"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you can seek Furen Longbeard's renowned smithing by bringing him a cask of fine ale, an essential rite of passage for reliable protection.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you know that delivering a fresh cask of Barleybrew's finest can seal a deal or settle an old obligation."},kw={"ale","barleybrew","cask of scalder","dwarven district","furen longbeard","shieldsmith","stormwind"},rel={"quest:1702","npc:furen-longbeard","subzone:dwarven-district","quest:1699","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Cask of Scalder","The Shieldsmith"}}
E["item:charred-horn"] = {t="item",n="Charred Horn",z="stormwind",s="Charred Horns are the rugged, heat-baked horns harvested from youthful chimaeras dwelling in the crags of the Stonetalon Mountains. Tough enough to withstand harsh elemental forces, they serve as an essential tempering component in specialized armorsmithing.",h="Charred Horns are the rugged, heat-baked horns harvested from youthful chimaeras dwelling in the crags of the...",sec={{t="A Rare Smithing Component",b="Harvested from fledgling and young chimaeras nesting across the craggy heights of the Stonetalon Mountains, Charred Horns are coveted for their unnatural resistance to flame and blunt force. The dwarven armorsmith Furen Longbeard, working from his forge in Stormwind, requires a collection of these horns to craft fire-hardened mail. Combined with venomous spider fangs from the Wetlands, phlogiston from Razorfen Kraul, and the galvanized horn of a chimaera matriarch, these calcified horns provide the core structural reinforcement necessary to produce an exceptionally resilient suit of protective armor.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What creatures drop Charred Horns?",a="They are gathered from fledgling chimaeras and young chimaeras native to the rugged terrain of the Stonetalon Mountains in Kalimdor.",al={"where to get charred horn","who drops charred horn","charred horn source"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Who wants these horns in Stormwind?",a="The master armorsmith Furen Longbeard asks for them. He uses their flame-tempered nature as raw material to forge an exceptionally sturdy mail chestpiece for promising warriors.",al={"who uses charred horn","turn in charred horn","furen longbeard horns"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why does Furen require so many of them?",a="Furen requires twelve Charred Horns to supply enough raw, heat-treated material to properly reinforce the rings and plates of his fire-hardened mail.",al={"why 12 charred horns","purpose of charred horn"},it="motive"},{q="Are these different from the Galvanized Horn?",a="Yes. Charred Horns come in quantity from the lesser, younger chimaeras of Stonetalon, whereas the Galvanized Horn is a single, far rarer trophy taken directly from a Chimaera Matriarch.",al={"galvanized horn vs charred horn","difference between horns"},gp=true},{q="What is a Charred Horn?",a="A Charred Horn is a tough, blackened horn harvested from the young and fledgling chimaeras that roam the peaks of the Stonetalon Mountains. Hardened by the harsh mountain climate and the elemental nature of the beasts, these horns possess unique durability, making them a prized raw material for specialized blacksmithing.",al={"what is charred horn","charred horn lore","about charred horn"},it="identity",add="785d7f85"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="Furen Longbeard specifically enlists rising warriors to retrieve these horns across Kalimdor, rewarding their perilous journey with custom fire-hardened mail.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="These beasts' horns showcase an exotic smithing technique, utilizing the naturally flame-cured biological material of Kalimdor predators to temper mail links."},kw={"charred horn","chimaera","fire hardened mail","furen longbeard","stonetalon","stonetalon mountains"},rel={"quest:1701","item:galvanized-horn","npc:furen-longbeard","zone:stonetalon","item:furen-s-instructions","item:scorched-spider-fang","item:vial-of-phlogiston"},src={"Charred Horn","Fire Hardened Mail"}}
E["item:cloth-request"] = {t="item",n="Cloth Request",z="stormwind",s="At the Canal Tailor and Fit Shop, Rema Schneider receives Harlan Bagley's request for fresh cloth and knitted goods. His shelves are emptying quickly.",h="At the Canal Tailor and Fit Shop, Rema Schneider receives Harlan Bagley's request for fresh cloth and knitted...",sec={{t="A Run on Sturdy Goods",b="Harlan Bagley asks Rema Schneider for a fresh supply of knitted garments and cloth. Bagley notes a sudden and unsettling surge in trade: citizens and travelers are buying armor and sturdy clothing as if bracing for a brutal season. The rush leaves Rema puzzled and wary. The House of Nobles has announced no open war, so Rema wonders why city folk are quietly armoring themselves and whether the crown's leaders are hiding unrest.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Cloth Request?",a="The Cloth Request is Harlan Bagley's written order to Rema Schneider for fresh cloth and knitted wear to restock his store.",al={"what is cloth request","cloth request item","harlan order slip"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Harlan Bagley need more cloth?",a="Bagley's business has been unusually busy. Townsfolk and travelers have bought armor and sturdy clothing in large quantities, exhausting his stock.",al={"why harlan needs cloth","why is bagley out of stock","bagley resupply reason"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where does this request need to go?",a="The order goes to Rema Schneider at the Canal Tailor and Fit Shop, along Stormwind's waterways.",al={"where do i take the cloth request","who gets cloth request","cloth request delivery"},gp=true},{q="Why are people in Stormwind buying so much armor and clothing?",a="Neither merchants nor commoners know for certain. Rema Schneider finds the sudden rush unnerving and wonders whether the noble court is concealing brewing hostilities or danger from the public.",al={"why are people buying armor","is stormwind at war","rema schneider suspicions"}},{q="Where does the Cloth Request come from, and who wrote it?",a="The request is penned by Harlan Bagley, a shopkeeper in Stormwind. Experiencing a sudden surge in business as citizens purchase sturdy clothes and armor, Bagley writes the requisition to secure another shipment of knitted clothing and keep his shelves stocked.",al={"who wrote cloth request","cloth request origin","where did cloth request come from"},it="origin",add="b4374b3c"}},ang={["profession:Tailoring"]="The request points to Stormwind's textile trade, where neighborhood clothiers like the Schneiders supply general stores and outfitters with woven goods.",["faction:Alliance"]="Stormwind's citizens feel uneasy and prepare for strife, despite the regency making no official announcements."},kw={"canal tailor shop","cloth request","harlan bagley","rema schneider","resupply","stormwind"},rel={"quest:333","npc:rema-schneider","npc:harlan-bagley"},src={"Cloth Request","Harlan Needs a Resupply"}}
E["item:crate-of-lightforge-ingots"] = {t="item",n="Crate of Lightforge Ingots",z="stormwind",s="In Duskwood, the Crate of Lightforge Ingots carries hope against Morbent Fel. The rare consecrated metal is bound for the Dwarven District in Stormwind.",h="In Duskwood, the Crate of Lightforge Ingots carries hope against Morbent Fel.",sec={{t="A Sacred Delivery",b="Duskwood's hope rests in this crate of lightforge iron. The rare metal can channel holy power against dark entities, while Morbent Fel's protections turn aside ordinary steel. Only an artisan who knows its temper and honors its sacred nature can work it.",sp=0},{t="The Weaponsmith of Stormwind",b="Grimand Elmore is to receive the crate in Stormwind's Dwarven District. The skilled dwarven weaponsmith has not worked with lightforge iron in years, but agrees to forge it into a sanctified weapon. Its power is meant to break Morbent Fel's defenses and strike him down.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is inside this crate?",a="The crate holds consecrated lightforge iron, gathered for a weapon meant to pierce the necromancer Morbent Fel's magical defenses.",al={"crate contents","what is lightforge iron","what is in the box"},it="identity"},{q="Who is supposed to receive this crate?",a="The crate is meant for Grimand Elmore, a skilled dwarven weaponsmith in Stormwind's Dwarven District.",al={"who do i bring the crate to","crate recipient","where does the crate go"},it="target"},{q="Why is lightforge iron needed?",a="Morbent Fel's protections turn aside ordinary steel. Lightforge iron can channel holy power against dark entities.",al={"why lightforge iron","why not normal iron","morbent fel weakness"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who crafted the crate?",a="Glorin Steelbrow packed the lightforge iron you recovered into the crate for delivery to Grimand Elmore in Stormwind.",al={"who packed the ingots","who gave the crate"},it="origin"}},ang={["profession:Blacksmithing"]="Working lightforge iron is a rare art. Even Grimand Elmore can go years without handling the sacred metal.",["class:Paladin"]="These ingots answer the Holy Light, making weapons forged from them a natural bane to necromancers and their undead minions."},kw={"crate","dwarven district","grimand elmore","ingots","iron","lightforge","morbent fel","stormwind"},rel={"quest:322","quest:321","quest:1700","quest:55","subzone:dwarven-district","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Crate of Lightforge Ingots","Blessed Arm"}}
E["item:darnassus-marzipan"] = {t="item",n="Darnassus Marzipan",z="stormwind",s="At Hallow's End, Darnassus innkeepers hand out festive marzipan to visitors who dance for it. Crafted in the night elven capital for the autumn celebration, this sweet is one of four treats Jesper needs.",h="At Hallow's End, Darnassus innkeepers hand out festive marzipan to visitors who dance for it.",sec={{t="A Taste of the World Tree",b="During Hallow's End, Alliance capitals share a tradition of lighthearted trick-or-treating. Dwarves offer sharp mints, Stormwind makes chewy nougat, and Darnassus innkeepers prepare delicate marzipan for visitors. To receive a piece, you must show some festive spirit and dance when the innkeeper asks. The sweet is one of four regional treats sought by Jesper, a sick orphan in Stormwind's Cathedral Square who cannot go out to collect sweets himself.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Darnassus Marzipan used for?",a="During Hallow's End, Jesper needs Darnassus Marzipan as one of four distinct sweets. He is a sick orphan at the orphanage in Stormwind's Cathedral Square. Bring it with candies from Ironforge, Gnomeregan, and Stormwind, and you receive a bundle of festive pumpkin treats.",al={"darnassus marzipan use","what do i do with marzipan"},it="item",gp=true},{q="How do you obtain Darnassus Marzipan?",a="During Hallow's End, Darnassus innkeepers give you marzipan after asking you to perform a quick dance.",al={"how to get darnassus marzipan","where to get marzipan"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Why can't Jesper get the marzipan himself?",a="Jesper is sick and cannot go out trick-or-treating. He is at the Stormwind orphanage in Cathedral Square and relies on adventurers to collect the distant treats for him.",al={"why does jesper need candy","why can't jesper go"},it="motive"},{q="What is Darnassus Marzipan?",a="Darnassus Marzipan is a festive confectionery crafted in the night elven capital of Darnassus. Handed out to revelers during the autumn festival of Hallow's End, this almond-paste sweet is one of the four traditional holiday candies given to travelers willing to perform festive tricks for a treat.",al={"what is darnassus marzipan","darnassus marzipan lore","what kind of candy is darnassus marzipan"},it="identity",add="06b4a124"},{q="Where does Darnassus Marzipan come from, and who made it?",a="The confection originates from the night elf capital of Darnassus atop the boughs of Teldrassil. During Hallow's End, the city's innkeeper distributes the sweet treat to visitors who entertain the tavern with a dance, celebrating the shared bonds and merriment of the Alliance across Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms.",al={"where does darnassus marzipan come from","who makes darnassus marzipan","darnassus marzipan origin"},it="origin",add="cf1db7fa"},{q="Why does anyone want Darnassus Marzipan?",a="Beyond being an elven holiday delicacy, it is sought by those unable to celebrate Hallow's End on their own. Jesper, a sick orphan boy in Stormwind's Cathedral Square, asks travelers to go trick-or-treating on his behalf so he can enjoy treats from across the Alliance.",al={"why want darnassus marzipan","who wants darnassus marzipan","why collect darnassus marzipan"},it="why_wanted",add="1983589f"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a kaldorei, you can share the lighter customs of autumn. Darnassus innkeepers offer sugary marzipan to travelers who honor their hospitality with a lively dance.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you can gather treats from Darnassus, Ironforge, and Stormwind. Hallow's End brings the far-flung peoples of the Alliance together in shared festivities."},kw={"candy","darnassus","darnassus marzipan","hallow's end","jesper","marzipan","treats"},rel={"quest:8311","quest:8357","item:gnomeregan-gumdrop","zone:darnassus","topic:alliance"},src={"Darnassus Marzipan","Hallow's End Treats for Jesper!"}}
E["item:defias-docket"] = {t="item",n="Defias Docket",z="stormwind",s="Defias operatives have hidden their orders at Addle's Stead in western Duskwood. The docket gives Stormwind's search for its missing emissary a lead into the Brotherhood's plans.",h="Defias operatives have hidden their orders at Addle's Stead in western Duskwood.",sec={{t="A Trail into the Dark",b="Master Elling Trias points investigators toward Duskwood as they follow leads on the kingdom's missing diplomat. Watcher Backus has noted unusual Defias movements converging on Addle's Stead, the derelict farm south of the road from Westfall. A strongbox on the property holds the Defias Docket. Its records track the Brotherhood's movements, revealing work that reaches beyond highway robbery and local banditry.",sp=0},{t="The Web of Conspiracy",b="The papers prove so intricate and politically dangerous that Watcher Backus refuses to keep them. He fears severe punishment from his superiors if they catch him handling the docket. Back at Trias' Cheese shop in Stormwind City, the papers reveal an elaborate abduction scheme backed by extensive Defias resources. They also name underworld operators, including one codenamed 'Fist.'",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Defias Docket?",a="The Defias Docket is a bundle of official orders and documents belonging to the Defias Brotherhood. It details their plans and covert operations around Duskwood and Westfall.",al={"what is the docket","defias papers","missing diplomat docket"},it="identity"},{q="Where is the Defias Docket found?",a="You find the docket locked inside a Defias strongbox at the dilapidated farmhouse in Addle's Stead, south of the road from Westfall into western Duskwood.",al={"docket location","where to find defias docket","addle's stead docket"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why was the docket kept in Duskwood?",a="Defias operatives used Addle's Stead as a remote staging post between Westfall and Duskwood. They coordinated a high-priority operation there, away from Stormwind's primary patrols.",al={"why is it in duskwood","defias at addle's stead"},it="motive"},{q="Who analyzes the docket?",a="Watcher Backus examines the docket briefly, then sends it to Elling Trias in Stormwind City. Trias' private intelligence network specializes in deciphering covert underworld communications.",al={"who gets the docket","who reads the docket"},it="target"},{q="Where does the Defias Docket come from, and who made it?",a="The docket is an official set of paperwork drafted by the Defias Brotherhood itself. It was drawn up to outline their covert schemes and coordinate agents across regions. Operatives stashed the documents securely inside a strongbox at Addle's Stead, a quiet farmstead just across the Duskwood border, where brotherhood members congregated before you uncovered it.",al={"who wrote the defias docket","defias docket origin","where did the docket come from"},it="origin",add="b7a864a3"},{q="Why does anyone want the Defias Docket?",a="Investigators looking into the missing diplomat need hard proof of the conspiracy. Watcher Backus recognizes the docket as far too intricate to be a simple decoy, and Elling Trias in Stormwind uses its contents to pierce the secrecy of the Brotherhood's plans, including uncovering references to key figures like 'Fist.'",al={"why is the docket important","why want defias docket","who wants the defias docket"},sp=1,it="why_wanted",add="4693de43"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you can see how the Defias Brotherhood uses cipher work and covert logistics behind the appearance of common outlawry.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can see that the documents reveal a coordinated Defias plot reaching far beyond common banditry."},kw={"addle's stead","defias docket","defias strongbox","duskwood","elling trias","the missing diplomat","watcher backus"},rel={"quest:1241","subzone:addle-s-stead","npc:watcher-backus","npc:elling-trias","zone:duskwood","zone:westfall","npc:jorgen","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Defias Docket","The Missing Diplomat (5)","The Missing Diplomat (6)"}}
E["item:defias-tower-key"] = {t="item",n="Defias Tower Key",z="stormwind",s="At Klaven's Tower in Westfall, the Defias Tower Key proves an infiltrator reached the guarded perimeter. Stormwind operatives seek it from the malformed drones outside.",h="At Klaven's Tower in Westfall, the Defias Tower Key proves an infiltrator reached the guarded perimeter.",sec={{t="A Prize from the Twisted Guard",b="Klaven's Tower stands on the Westfall coast as a Defias Brotherhood stronghold. Recent shipments from Duskwood brought new guards to its perimeter: malformed Defias drones, undead and covered in spikes. SI:7 operatives watch the grounds and direct field agents to pick the pockets of these sentries. Fighting them head-on is not the way to prove the perimeter has been breached. The key shows an infiltrator got through without raising an alarm.",sp=0},{t="Uncovering the Duskwood Connection",b="The key leads to a chest inside Klaven's Tower, bound with shipments from Duskwood. The chest holds Klaven Mortwake's Journal. When the journal reaches Master Mathias Shaw in Stormwind, it reveals a conspiracy beyond ordinary highway robbery. The Defias joined with the Venture Company to traffic specialized troll poisons discovered by Zanzil the Outcast. Those mixtures can raise the dead, explaining the grotesque, coughing abominations around the tower.",sp=1}},faq={{q="How do you obtain the Defias Tower Key?",a="You must pickpocket one of the malformed Defias drones guarding Klaven's Tower in Westfall. The key cannot be taken from a defeated enemy.",al={"where do i get the key","how to get defias tower key","who drops defias tower key"},gp=true},{q="What does the Defias Tower Key open?",a="The key does not unlock the tower door or the Duskwood Chest inside. Master Mathias Shaw requires it as proof that an operative infiltrated the perimeter undetected.",al={"does it open the duskwood chest","what door does this open","what does defias key unlock"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="What are the malformed Defias drones guarding the tower?",a="They are grotesque, spiked undead guards around Klaven's Tower. Agent Kearnen does not know what made them and asks operatives to investigate the shipment they guard.",al={"who holds the key","what are the tower guards","what is the spiked zombie"},sp=1,it="threat"},{q="Who sends operatives to retrieve this key?",a="Agent Kearnen, an SI:7 scout watching Klaven's Tower's perimeter, directs field rogues to get the key and retrieve the Duskwood Chest's contents for Master Mathias Shaw in Stormwind.",al={"who gives the quest","who wants the key"},it="allies"},{q="What is the Defias Tower Key?",a="It is an iron key carried by the grotesque guards surrounding Klaven's Tower in Westfall. SI:7 operative Agent Kearnen spotted it in the possession of the spiked undead monstrosity guarding the site, identifying it as vital evidence of the Defias Brotherhood's clandestine operations at the fortification.",al={"defias tower key","what is defias tower key","defias key"},it="identity",add="a3164c95"},{q="Why does SI:7 want the Defias Tower Key?",a="Master Mathias Shaw and Agent Kearnen require rogue operatives to secure the key while infiltrating the tower to investigate mysterious shipments arriving from Duskwood. Bringing it back proves you successfully penetrated the perimeter and retrieved the sinister secrets locked within Klaven Mortwake's stronghold.",al={"why get defias tower key","who wants defias tower key","why retrieve defias key"},it="why_wanted",add="2bb6b303"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue working with SI:7, you must use stealth and pickpocketing to acquire the Defias Tower Key, while keeping lethal poisons in mind.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help Stormwind investigate the Defias Brotherhood's strange shipments from Duskwood by securing intelligence from Klaven's Tower."},kw={"agent kearnen","defias tower key","duskwood chest","klaven mortwake","klaven's tower","malformed defias drone","mathias shaw","si:7"},rel={"quest:2359","npc:mathias-shaw","item:klaven-mortwake-s-journal","zone:duskwood","quest:2300","topic:venture-company","topic:troll"},src={"Defias Tower Key","Klaven's Tower (quest)"}}
E["item:delivery-to-mathias"] = {t="item",n="Delivery to Mathias",z="stormwind",s="Keryn Sylvius sends a sealed parcel from Goldshire to Master Mathias Shaw in Stormwind. The delivery gives a promising rogue entry into SI:7's inner workings.",h="Keryn Sylvius sends a sealed parcel from Goldshire to Master Mathias Shaw in Stormwind.",sec={{t="A Courier's Test",b="A parcel from the Lion's Pride Inn to the Stormwind Barracks may look like ordinary courier work. For a budding rogue, it is an audition for Stormwind Intelligence. Local trainer Keryn Sylvius entrusts the package to novice cutpurses, giving them a direct introduction to Master Mathias Shaw. The delivery tests whether they can cross the capital quietly, keep a low profile, and follow discreet orders without asking questions.",sp=0},{t="Gateway to SI:7",b="The handoff brings an operative into SI:7 headquarters in Old Town. Mathias Shaw uses such deliveries to separate pretenders from true talents. Those who present the parcel without faltering receive high-stakes field assignments, beginning with covert reconnaissance and infiltration against Defias smuggling networks in Elwynn Forest.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is inside the Delivery to Mathias?",a="The parcel stays sealed to its courier. It may hold intelligence reports, trainee assessments, or confidential material about local threats such as the Defias Brotherhood in Elwynn.",al={"what is in the package","delivery contents","parcel contents"},it="item"},{q="Who sends this delivery?",a="Keryn Sylvius hands over the delivery. She is a rogue operative and trainer stationed upstairs at the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire.",al={"who gave me this parcel","package sender","keryn sylvius package"},it="origin"},{q="Where does Mathias Shaw keep his headquarters?",a="Mathias Shaw keeps his headquarters on the second floor of the SI:7 building, in the southeastern corner of Old Town within the Stormwind Barracks compound.",al={"where is mathias shaw","where to deliver package","shaw location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens after presenting the parcel to Shaw?",a="After Shaw confirms your capability, he initiates you into field espionage and sends you to infiltrate Jerod's Landing. There, you steal a shipping schedule from a Defias dockmaster.",al={"next quest after delivery","what does shaw do","after delivery to mathias"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="What is the Delivery to Mathias?",a="It is a sealed parcel entrusted to you by Keryn Sylvius, the rogue trainer stationed in Goldshire. Handed over under the guise of an errand, it serves primarily as your introduction and test of competence before Master Mathias Shaw at SI:7 headquarters in Stormwind.",al={"what is delivery to mathias","delivery to mathias package","keryn sylvius package"},it="identity",add="1dd6c783"},{q="Why does Mathias Shaw want this delivery?",a="Master Mathias Shaw leads SI:7, Stormwind's intelligence guild, and Keryn Sylvius was tasked with routing work and scouting promising recruits his way. Carrying the parcel safely to Old Town proves you can follow covert instructions and handle sensitive assignments for the crown's spymaster.",al={"why does shaw want the delivery","why deliver package to mathias","why does mathias want this"},it="why_wanted",add="2bd7511f"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you carry a package that marks a passage from petty back-alley brawling into royal intelligence under Mathias Shaw.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance operative, you carry covert dispatches between regional scouts and the capital, helping Stormwind's secretive espionage apparatus counter internal subversion."},kw={"delivery to mathias","goldshire","keryn sylvius","mathias shaw","old town","package","si:7","stormwind"},rel={"quest:2205","npc:mathias-shaw","npc:keryn-sylvius","quest:2206","subzone:old-town","zone:stormwind","subzone:goldshire","item:shipping-schedule"},src={"Delivery to Mathias","Seek out SI: 7"}}
E["item:dust-devil-debris"] = {t="item",n="Dust Devil Debris",z="stormwind",s="Across Westfall, Dust Devils leave charged grit in their wake. Mages value this debris as a reagent for enchanting parchment and binding messaging spells into scrolls.",h="Across Westfall, Dust Devils leave charged grit in their wake.",sec={{t="Air Spun into Parchment",b="Dust Devils sweep across Westfall’s plains as violent whirlwinds. When one is struck down, the living storm collapses into charged dust and grit called Dust Devil Debris. A faint trace of the elemental vortex remains in the residue. In Stormwind, arcane practitioners such as Collin Mauren prize it for specialized sorcery. Infused into enchanted ink and parchment, the grit helps a wizard bind an airy messaging spell to a scroll, carrying words across the kingdom.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Dust Devil Debris used for?",a="Collin Mauren uses Dust Devil Debris to craft a specialized messaging scroll. Its lingering elemental energy helps him place delicate communication magic on paper.",al={"dust devil debris use","why get dust devil debris","debris purpose"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where does this debris come from?",a="Dust Devil Debris comes from the remains of Dust Devils, hostile air elementals roaming Westfall’s barren farmlands and roads.",al={"where to find debris","dust devil drops","westfall debris"},it="origin"},{q="Why are Dust Devils dangerous?",a="Dust Devils are hostile air elementals that roam Westfall. Collin Mauren warns that collecting their debris means facing dangerous creatures.",al={"why elementals in westfall","westfall dust devils origin"}},{q="Who is Collin Mauren?",a="Collin Mauren is a human mage in Stormwind’s Mage Quarter. He uses his arcane expertise to craft enchanted scrolls and magical components for fellow practitioners and curious researchers.",al={"collin mauren","who wants debris"},it="people"},{q="What is Dust Devil Debris?",a="Dust Devil Debris consists of the swirling grit, dirt, and residual magical matter left behind when a dust devil is defeated in Westfall. These elemental whirlwinds scour the arid plains, and their remains retain enough ambient power to serve as potent reagents for enchanters and scribes.",al={"what is dust devil debris","dust devil debris","dust devil debris item"},it="identity",add="2f6e3759"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you can see how elemental remnants serve scribing and communication magic, joining raw elemental chaos with arcane discipline."},kw={"collin mauren","dust devil debris","dust devils","messaging spell","scroll","stormwind","westfall"},rel={"quest:1076","zone:westfall","npc:collin-mauren","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Dust Devil Debris","Devils in Westfall"}}
E["item:furen-s-instructions"] = {t="item",n="Furen's Instructions",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind, Furen's Instructions name the materials needed for fire-hardened mail. Furen Longbeard gives the parchment to Alliance warriors he has tested.",h="In Stormwind, Furen's Instructions name the materials needed for fire-hardened mail.",sec={{t="A Master Smith's Demands",b="Furen Longbeard offers to forge a resilient suit of mail for a warrior who has proved himself through simpler smithing work. The dwarven armorer asks the warrior to fetch the rare components himself. His parchment records what is needed and sends the warrior across continents to gather it.",sp=0},{t="Exotic Components",b="The parchment calls for a dangerous journey through the Eastern Kingdoms and Kalimdor. The hardened links need dozens of scorched spider fangs from damp caves in the Wetlands, along with horns from fire-breathing chimaeras in the crags of Stonetalon Mountains. The list also calls for a galvanized horn from the chimaera matriarch and a vial of volatile phlogiston held deep within Razorfen Kraul, a quilboar bastion.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Furen's Instructions?",a="Furen's Instructions are a written list Furen Longbeard gives Alliance warriors in Stormwind. It names the exotic materials needed to craft fire-hardened mail.",al={"furens instructions","what are furens instructions","furen list"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Furen Longbeard?",a="Furen Longbeard is a master dwarven armorer in Stormwind's Dwarven District. He tests seasoned warriors and makes durable protective gear for them.",al={"who is furen","furen longbeard","furen stormwind"},it="people"},{q="Where do the materials on the list come from?",a="The list calls for scorched spider fangs from the Wetlands, charred horns and a galvanized horn from chimaeras in Stonetalon Mountains, and a vial of phlogiston from Roogug in Razorfen Kraul.",al={"where do i find the items","furen materials locations","materials on furen list"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What does Furen forge with these materials?",a="Furen uses the materials and his smithing secrets to forge a specialized piece of fire-hardened mail for the warrior.",al={"what armor does furen make","fire hardened mail reward","furen crafting reward"},it="purpose"},{q="Where did Furen's Instructions come from, and who made it?",a="Furen Longbeard, an accomplished dwarven smith working in Stormwind, wrote this document himself. Knowing the secrets to crafting exceptional mail armor, he penned this detailed ledger to outline the rare components needed across the world so an ambitious warrior would know precisely what to seek.",al={"who wrote furen's instructions","where do furen's instructions come from","furen instructions origin"},it="origin",add="82702a01"},{q="Why is Furen's Instructions important?",a="The instructions serve as your guide for an arduous scavenger hunt across Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms. Furen requires you to keep them on hand while gathering scorched fangs, chimaera horns, and alchemical phlogiston, ensuring you bring back the exact reagents he needs to forge fire-hardened armor.",al={"why do i need furen's instructions","why are furen's instructions wanted","furen instructions purpose"},it="why_wanted",add="42eefba8"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As an Alliance warrior, you face trials against fierce beasts and quilboar to earn heavy mail armor.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="As a blacksmith, you can see how Furen's recipe combines beast reagents with rare alchemical distillations to temper armor beyond ordinary forging."},kw={"charred horn","fire hardened mail","furen longbeard","furen's instructions","galvanized horn","razorfen kraul","scorched spider fang","stonetalon","vial of phlogiston","wetlands"},rel={"quest:1701","npc:furen-longbeard","item:scorched-spider-fang","item:charred-horn","item:galvanized-horn","item:vial-of-phlogiston","zone:stonetalon","zone:razorfenkraul"},src={"Furen's Instructions","Fire Hardened Mail"}}
E["item:furen-s-notes"] = {t="item",n="Furen's Notes",z="stormwind",s="Furen's Notes carry his discoveries in metallurgy and armorsmithing from Stormwind to Alliance craftsmen. After forging protective gear for veteran warriors, Furen Longbeard sends copies to help fellow smiths refine their work.",h="Furen's Notes carry his discoveries in metallurgy and armorsmithing from Stormwind to Alliance craftsmen.",sec={{t="A Master's Discoveries",b="In Stormwind's Dwarven District, Furen Longbeard forges specialized armaments for warriors and records the methods and discoveries he makes along the way. Dwarven metalworking keeps changing, so he makes several copies for other smiths to use and build upon. His notes describe practical ways to temper, reinforce, and shape armor against deadly blows.",sp=0},{t="Dispatched Across the Alliance",b="Furen sends copies to trusted contacts in the Alliance's crafting networks. Grimand Elmore may scoff at a fellow smith he claims to have taught, but the notes still hold useful insights. Copies cross the Great Sea to night elven craftsmen, including Mathiel on Darnassus's Warrior's Terrace. Shared needs in battle bring their different traditions into contact.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is contained within Furen's Notes?",a="Furen's Notes contain descriptions of armorsmithing techniques and discoveries in metallurgy that Furen Longbeard developed while making custom armor for seasoned warriors.",al={"what are furen's notes","what is in furens notes","furen notes content"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Furen Longbeard?",a="Furen Longbeard is a master dwarven armorsmith in Stormwind's Dwarven District. He guides rising warriors and makes specialized defensive wargear.",al={"who wrote this","who is furen","furen longbeard"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Grimand Elmore get angry about the notes?",a="Grimand Elmore claims he taught Furen everything the dwarf knows, and resents the suggestion that his former student can teach him something new. Still, Grimand admits the notes describe techniques worth trying.",al={"why is grimand mad","grimand elmore reaction","grimand proud"}},{q="Who receives copies of Furen's Notes?",a="Furen sends copies to trusted colleagues across the Alliance, including weapon smith Grimand Elmore in Stormwind, night elven smith Mathiel in Darnassus, and gnomish blacksmith Klockmort Spannerspan in Ironforge.",al={"who gets furens notes","where do the notes go","deliver furens notes"}},{q="How does Mathiel react to the notes?",a="Mathiel, a night elf blacksmith on Darnassus's Warrior's Terrace, welcomes Furen's findings with enthusiasm. He sees them as a grand discovery and an honor to bring into his own work.",al={"mathiel reaction","mathiel darnassus","what does mathiel think"}},{q="Why does anyone want Furen's Notes?",a="The notes document groundbreaking smithing techniques that Furen Longbeard developed while forging specialized warrior armor. Blacksmiths across the Alliance—such as Mathiel in Darnassus and Grimand Elmore in Stormwind—stand to gain valuable metallurgical insights from them. Even artisans skeptical of Furen's skill, like Elmore, recognize innovative ideas inside that they are eager to test at their own anvils.",al={"why do blacksmiths want furen's notes","furen's notes value","why share furen's notes"},it="why_wanted",add="224f803f"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, your armor trials in Stormwind lead directly to these notes. They record practical ideas shaped by the needs of frontline combat.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="As a blacksmith, you see the exchange of specialized armorcrafting knowledge among dwarven, elven, and gnomish artisans across the Alliance."},kw={"blacksmithing","dwarven district","furen","furen longbeard","furen's notes","grimand elmore","klockmort spannerspan","mathiel"},rel={"quest:1700","quest:1703","quest:1704","subzone:dwarven-district","subzone:warrior-s-terrace","zone:darnassus","topic:warrior"},src={"Furen's Notes","Grimand Elmore (quest)","Mathiel (quest)"}}
E["item:galvanized-horn"] = {t="item",n="Galvanized Horn",z="stormwind",s="In the Charred Vale, chimaera matriarchs bear horns that Stormwind and Thunder Bluff armorers seek. These hardened growths go into specialized armor for warriors.",h="In the Charred Vale, chimaera matriarchs bear horns that Stormwind and Thunder Bluff armorers seek.",sec={{t="Trophy of the Charred Vale",b="Chimaera matriarchs prowl the Charred Vale in the Stonetalon Mountains. Their horns grow unusually hard through ash, flame, and survival. Lesser fledgling chimaeras yield brittle, blackened horns, but a matriarch's horn has strength like treated metal. Furen Longbeard in Stormwind and Orm Stonehoof in Thunder Bluff both seek one as a test of martial valor and a key ingredient for exceptional mail armor.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does a Galvanized Horn come from?",a="A Galvanized Horn comes from a chimaera matriarch in the Charred Vale, in the western Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"where to get galvanized horn","how to get galvanized horn","galvanized horn drop"},it="origin"},{q="Why do smiths want this specific horn?",a="Master armorers prize the horn's density and heat resistance. They use it to reinforce specialized suits of mail and plate armor.",al={"what is galvanized horn for","galvanized horn use"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who accepts the Galvanized Horn?",a="Furen Longbeard in Stormwind seeks the horn for fire-hardened armor for Alliance warriors. Orm Stonehoof in Thunder Bluff seeks it as proof of strength and to fashion a warrior's helm for Horde warriors.",al={"who needs galvanized horn","galvanized horn turn in"},gp=true},{q="How does it differ from a regular Charred Horn?",a="Common Charred Horns come from lesser, fledgling chimaeras. A Galvanized Horn comes from a mature matriarch and has a denser, tempered structure suited to masterwork smithing.",al={"charred horn vs galvanized horn","is it different from charred horn"}},{q="What is a Galvanized Horn?",a="A Galvanized Horn is a rare, hardened horn taken from a Chimaera Matriarch dwelling within Kalimdor's Stonetalon Mountains. Unlike ordinary chimaera horns, it has been toughened by the harsh, fire-ravaged environment of the Charred Vale, making it exceptionally resilient and prized by master armorsmiths across both the Alliance and the Horde.",al={"galvanized horn identity","what is galvanized horn","galvanized horn lore"},it="identity",add="39b0e048"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, slaying a matriarch and securing her Galvanized Horn tests your endurance and power. It proves your mettle to master armorers in Stormwind or Thunder Bluff.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="As a blacksmith, the horn shows how organic materials hardened in extreme conditions can match or exceed worked metals in custom armor reinforcement."},kw={"charred vale","chimaera matriarch","fire hardened mail","furen longbeard","galvanized horn","orm stonehoof","stonetalon mountains"},rel={"quest:1701","quest:1844","subzone:charred-vale","zone:stonetalon","npc:furen-longbeard","item:charred-horn","item:vial-of-phlogiston","zone:thunderbluff"},src={"Galvanized Horn","Fire Hardened Mail","Chimaeric Horn"}}
E["item:gnomeregan-gumdrop"] = {t="item",n="Gnomeregan Gumdrop",z="stormwind",s="During Hallow's End, Gnomeregan Gumdrops reach travelers from the exiled gnomes. One sweet helps sick Jesper celebrate at the Stormwind orphanage.",h="During Hallow's End, Gnomeregan Gumdrops reach travelers from the exiled gnomes.",sec={{t="A Taste of Gnomish Ingenuity",b="At Ironforge's Mystic Ward, Talvash del Kissel hands out Gnomeregan Gumdrops to travelers who play along with his Hallow's End tricks. Innkeepers across the Alliance offer regional treats, but the exiled gnomes have no capital inn of their own. The radioactive disaster drove them from their underground kingdom, yet they still share their distinct sweets with the Alliance.",sp=0},{t="A Treat for Jesper",b="Sick Jesper is confined to the Stormwind orphanage in Cathedral Square and cannot travel the continents to trick-or-treat. Travelers gather four regional sweets from Alliance capitals to bring the holiday to him: Gnomeregan Gumdrop, Stormwind Nougat, Ironforge Mint, and Darnassus Marzipan.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does a Gnomeregan Gumdrop come from?",a="Talvash del Kissel gives out Gnomeregan Gumdrops in Ironforge's Mystic Ward when you play one of his Hallow's End tricks.",al={"who gives gnomeregan gumdrop","how to get gumdrop","gumdrop location"},it="origin"},{q="Why isn't this candy handed out in Gnomeregan?",a="Troggs overran and irradiated Gnomeregan, forcing its surviving gnomes into exile. Many now live alongside the dwarves in Ironforge, including Talvash del Kissel.",al={"why ironforge","why is talvash in ironforge"},it="place"},{q="What is this candy used for?",a="You bring this sweet to Jesper, a sick orphan boy at the Stormwind orphanage in Cathedral Square. It is one of four festive sweets gathered for him during Hallow's End.",al={"what does gumdrop do","jesper candy"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What other treats are collected alongside it?",a="Jesper also asks for Stormwind Nougat, Ironforge Mint, and Darnassus Marzipan. You gather each in its respective Alliance capital.",al={"other candies","hallows end sweets"},it="item"},{q="What is a Gnomeregan Gumdrop?",a="A Gnomeregan Gumdrop is a festive confectionery representing the gnomish people, distributed during the holiday of Hallow's End. While named after the lost technological wonder of Gnomeregan, the treat is dispensed by gnomes taking refuge in the dwarven capital of Ironforge, most notably the tinkerer Talvash del Kissel.",al={"what is gnomeregan gumdrop","gnomeregan gumdrop candy","gnome gumdrop lore"},it="identity",add="243db981"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="Though gnomes have no reclaimed city of their own, their signature sweet joins those of the great Alliance capitals during Hallow's End.",["faction:Alliance"]="You travel among human, dwarven, and gnomish communities to gather this sweet, sharing the Alliance's close bonds during seasonal celebrations."},kw={"candy","gnomeregan gumdrop","hallow's end","ironforge","jesper","stormwind","talvash del kissel"},rel={"quest:8311","quest:8355","npc:talvash-del-kissel","item:darnassus-marzipan","zone:gnomeregan"},src={"Gnomeregan Gumdrop","Hallow's End Treats for Jesper!"}}
E["item:klaven-mortwake-s-journal"] = {t="item",n="Klaven Mortwake's Journal",z="stormwind",s="Inside a chest from Duskwood, Klaven Mortwake's Journal records the Defias Brotherhood's search for a way to raise the dead. SI:7 operatives recovered it from the Defias tower in northeastern Westfall.",h="Inside a chest from Duskwood, Klaven Mortwake's Journal records the Defias Brotherhood's search for a way to...",sec={{t="A Gruesome Formula",b="The Defias tower rises along the ridges of northern Westfall, where strange shipments arrive from the shadowy borders of Duskwood. Twisted, non-human sentries guard the tower. SI:7 had watched the place for a long time, and a journal in the topmost chest revealed what the shipments carried. Klaven Mortwake recorded research into alchemical methods of raising mindless undead drones. Alchemists associated with the Zanzil trolls in Stranglethorn had found a way to do it with specialized poisons and brews. The Defias Brotherhood sought to duplicate their method for its own ranks.",sp=1},{t="Intelligence for SI:7",b="Master Mathias Shaw leads Stormwind's intelligence service, SI:7, and sought Mortwake's journal to trace the Brotherhood's wider alliances. The notes confirm experiments in reanimation and illicit support linking Duskwood, the Venture Company, and the Defias. For rogues serving the crown, recovering the research marks a step toward mastering poisons.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Klaven Mortwake's Journal?",a="Klaven Mortwake's Journal is a research notebook compiled by Klaven Mortwake, an operative in the Defias tower in northeastern Westfall. It contains notes on alchemical necromancy and illicit supply routes.",al={"what is klavens journal","mortwake journal","what is this item"},it="identity"},{q="Where is the journal found?",a="The journal is locked inside a Duskwood Chest on the top floor of the Defias tower in northern Westfall. Undead sentries guard it, and a key taken from one of Klaven's monstrous guards opens the chest.",al={"where to find klavens journal","klaven journal location","duskwood chest location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What secrets are written inside the journal?",a="The journal says that the Zanzil trolls of Stranglethorn Vale devised toxic potions that can raise and control the dead. The Defias Brotherhood was trying to acquire and use the recipe.",al={"what does the journal say","journal secrets","zanzil poison"},it="power"},{q="Who wants this journal?",a="Master Mathias Shaw, leader of Stormwind's SI:7 intelligence agency, wants the journal to monitor Defias logistics and teach crown operatives about the dangers and uses of tactical poisons.",al={"who turns in klaven journal","who do i give the journal to","mathias shaw journal"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where does Klaven Mortwake's Journal come from, and who made it?",a="The journal belongs to Klaven Mortwake, who oversaw the Defias Brotherhood's stronghold at the tower in Westfall. It was shipped along with sinister undead guards and a chest arriving out of Duskwood, detailing dark alchemical secrets originating from Zanzil the Outcast's trolls in Stranglethorn Vale.",al={"who wrote klaven's journal","klaven mortwake journal origin","where did klaven get the journal"},sp=1,it="origin",add="887d3337"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you prove your skill in lockpicking and stealth by entering the tower and taking Mortwake's journal. The work also introduces you to brewing lethal poisons.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you give Stormwind's spymasters proof that the Defias uprising reaches beyond disgruntled laborers. The journal reveals ties to troll witch-doctors and alchemical necromancy."},kw={"defias tower","duskwood chest","journal","klaven mortwake","mathias shaw","poisons","si:7","zanzil"},rel={"quest:2359","npc:mathias-shaw","item:defias-tower-key","quest:2300","zone:westfall","zone:duskwood","topic:venture-company","topic:troll"},src={"Klaven Mortwake's Journal","Klaven's Tower (quest)"}}
E["item:letter-to-jorgen"] = {t="item",n="Letter to Jorgen",z="stormwind",s="A sealed letter calls on Jorgen in Stormwind City to help with a missing diplomat.",h="A sealed letter calls on Jorgen in Stormwind City to help with a missing diplomat.",sec={{t="A Dispassionate Summons",b="A diplomat bound for Theramore failed to arrive for talks with Lady Jaina Proudmoore, and royal investigators moved quickly to keep the matter quiet. While official agents searched the capital, other channels stirred. The letter bypasses military bureaucracy and seeks out Jorgen, a gruff veteran who fishes beneath the great statues in the Valley of Heroes. It invokes old obligations and draws him into a covert inquiry amid rumors of a Defias conspiracy.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this letter?",a="The letter introduces its bearer and calls on Jorgen to honor an old obligation. It sends the bearer to the Valley of Heroes so Jorgen can help investigate a missing diplomat without drawing public attention.",al={"what does letter to jorgen do","why letter to jorgen","letter purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Jorgen?",a="Jorgen is a reclusive contact just inside Stormwind's gates who spends his time fishing in the Valley of Heroes. He dislikes interruptions, but a past debt binds him to help when shown the letter.",al={"who is jorgen","jorgen npc","jorgen stormwind"},it="people"},{q="What disappearance does the letter relate to?",a="A prominent diplomat left Stormwind by ship for Theramore to meet Lady Jaina Proudmoore, then vanished along the way. Suspicion falls on the Defias Brotherhood, though the full plot remains closely guarded.",al={"what diplomat is missing","who disappeared","missing diplomat"},it="threat"},{q="Where is the letter delivered?",a="The letter is carried to the Valley of Heroes, Stormwind City's grand entrance lined with monuments to the heroes of the Second War. Jorgen fishes by the water near the front gates.",al={"where do i take the letter","jorgen location","where is jorgen"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the Letter to Jorgen?",a="This letter is a confidential message dispatched concerning the quiet disappearance of a Stormwind diplomat en route to Theramore. Because official royal agents are already scouring the city openly, this sealed note enlists private, discreet contacts outside ordinary crown channels to investigate the suspected involvement of the Defias Brotherhood.",al={"what is letter to jorgen","letter to jorgen item","about letter to jorgen"},it="identity",add="0eeb183b"},{q="Where does the Letter to Jorgen come from, and who wrote it?",a="The letter was penned by Bishop DeLavey in Stormwind, who sought an independent inquiry into the missing diplomat. Trusting personal allies over conspicuous crown investigators, he drafted the message specifically to call upon an old friend named Jorgen, currently keeping a low profile by the waters of the Valley of Heroes.",al={"who wrote letter to jorgen","who sent letter to jorgen","letter to jorgen origin"},it="origin",add="5d64bfbf"},{q="Why is the Letter to Jorgen wanted?",a="Jorgen needs the letter because it outlines a covert obligation he cannot ignore. While reluctant to be pulled away from his quiet fishing, the contents of the missive persuade him to assist in unraveling the Defias plot before panic breaks out across the capital.",al={"why deliver letter to jorgen","why does jorgen need the letter","purpose of giving letter to jorgen"},it="why_wanted",add="9fd54092"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The letter concerns the Alliance's fragile stability and seeks a quiet response to an incident that threatens ties between Stormwind and Theramore.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you know that quiet dispatches and reluctant street informants can be necessary when uncovering trouble in the capital."},kw={"jaina proudmoore","jorgen","letter to jorgen","missing diplomat","stormwind","theramore","valley of heroes"},rel={"quest:1241","npc:jorgen","subzone:valley-of-heroes","zone:stormwind","npc:jaina-proudmoore","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Letter to Jorgen","The Missing Diplomat (2)"}}
E["item:musquash-root"] = {t="item",n="Musquash Root",z="stormwind",s="Beneath the Stonewrought Dam, Musquash Root grows in the Wetlands. The rare root is hard to gather, and a hidden coven beneath Stormwind needs it for a brew.",h="Beneath the Stonewrought Dam, Musquash Root grows in the Wetlands.",sec={{t="A Rare Ingredient",b="Musquash Root grows in the damp ground beneath the Stonewrought Dam's falls. The mist and secluded setting make it hard to gather. Few herbalists seek it, but practitioners of the darker arts prize its chemical and alchemical properties.",sp=0},{t="The Warlock's Scheme",b="Zardeth of the Black Claw seeks Musquash Root and the Tear of Tilloa beneath Stormwind, in the Slaughtered Lamb. The rare plants will form a subtle brew to neutralize Lord Wishock, a member of the House of Nobles who has begun investigating the city's hidden coven of warlocks.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is Musquash Root found?",a="Musquash Root grows in the Wetlands, at the foot of the falls beneath the Stonewrought Dam.",al={"where is musquash root","musquash root location","how to find musquash root"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Musquash Root used for?",a="Zardeth of the Black Claw wants Musquash Root and the Tear of Tilloa for a brew meant to keep Lord Wishock occupied and halt his push for an investigation into Stormwind's warlock coven.",al={"what does musquash root do","musquash root purpose","why do i need musquash root"},it="purpose"},{q="Who wants this root harvested?",a="Zardeth of the Black Claw, a warlock in the catacombs beneath the Slaughtered Lamb in Stormwind's Mage Quarter, directs agents to retrieve Musquash Root.",al={"who needs musquash root","musquash root quest giver","who asks for musquash root"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who is Lord Wishock?",a="Lord Wishock is a member of Stormwind's House of Nobles. After learning of the warlock coven in the city, he began urging the council to open a formal investigation.",al={"who is wishock","lord wishock"},it="target"},{q="What is Musquash Root?",a="Musquash Root is a rare botanical specimen that grows specifically in the damp, misty spray at the base of the waterfall beneath the Stonewrought Dam in the Wetlands. Known among dark apothecaries and warlocks for its potent natural properties, it serves as a crucial reagent in brewing deceptive draughts and poisons when combined with other rare flora.",al={"what is musquash root","musquash root lore","musquash root info"},it="identity",add="32cf7ee1"},{q="Where does Musquash Root come from, and who made it?",a="Musquash Root is a naturally occurring plant rather than an artificial creation. It flourishes exclusively in the Wetlands, rooted in the wet stone and saturated soil at the foot of the cascading falls directly below the grand Stonewrought Dam.",al={"musquash root origin","where does musquash root grow","who made musquash root"},it="origin",add="d9341dd1"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock beneath the Slaughtered Lamb, you need this root to silence nosy nobles and protect your fragile sanctuary in the city.",["profession:Herbalism"]="As an herbalist, you can see how the damp ground beneath the Stonewrought Dam's falls supports unusual and dangerous flora."},kw={"a noble brew","lord wishock","musquash root","stonewrought dam","tear of tilloa","wetlands","zardeth"},rel={"quest:335","quest:397","item:tear-of-tilloa","subzone:stonewrought-dam","zone:wetlands","topic:house-of-nobles","zone:duskwood","subzone:darkshire"},src={"Musquash Root","A Noble Brew"}}
E["item:perenolde-tiara"] = {t="item",n="Perenolde Tiara",z="stormwind",s="In the ruins of Alterac, an emerald-studded heirloom of the Perenolde family has turned up again. Dwarven craftsmen of Ironforge made it, and collectors in Stormwind now seek it.",h="In the ruins of Alterac, an emerald-studded heirloom of the Perenolde family has turned up again.",sec={{t="A Relic of a Ruined Kingdom",b="The Perenolde family ruled Alterac before the kingdom fell during the Second War. Their treasures included a delicate tiara, made by master jewelers in Ironforge and set with brilliant emeralds. After King Aiden Perenolde’s treachery brought Alterac to ruin, the tiara vanished amid the devastation of the high crags.",sp=0},{t="The Miser's Prize",b="Grel'borg the Miser, an ogre mage, unearthed the tiara while searching Alterac’s ruins for abandoned wealth. Word of the surviving relic reached Count Remington Ridgewell, a wealthy noble in Stormwind who collects famous relics for his family museum. Now the count seeks to take the tiara from the ogre.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Perenolde Tiara?",a="The Perenolde Tiara is an heirloom of Alterac’s royal Perenolde family. Dwarven jewelers in Ironforge crafted it and set it with emeralds before it was lost in the kingdom’s downfall.",al={"perenolde tiara lore","what is this tiara","alterac tiara"},it="identity"},{q="Who possesses the tiara now?",a="Grel'borg the Miser, an ogre mage, found the tiara among Alterac’s snowbound ruins. He guards it while searching the ruined kingdom for more treasure.",al={"where is the tiara","who drops the tiara","grelborg tiara"},it="place"},{q="Why does Count Remington Ridgewell want it?",a="Count Remington Ridgewell collects historic and prestigious antiquities for his family museum in Stormwind. He wants the tiara as a crown jewel from a fallen human kingdom.",al={"who wants the tiara","why does remington want it","remington ridgewell motive"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who were the Perenoldes?",a="The Perenoldes ruled the kingdom of Alterac. During the Second War, King Aiden Perenolde betrayed the Alliance to the Orcish Horde, and his realm fell into ruin.",al={"perenolde family","house of perenolde","rulers of alterac"},it="history"},{q="Where does the Perenolde Tiara come from, and who made it?",a="The tiara hails from the ruined northern kingdom of Alterac, where it served as a prized family heirloom for the royal House of Perenolde. Rather than being forged by human artisans, it is said to have been crafted by master dwarven jewelers in Ironforge, who set the ornate piece with the finest emeralds.",al={"who made perenolde tiara","origin of perenolde tiara","where was tiara crafted"},it="origin",add="da959daa"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you can see Ironforge’s gemcraft in the emeralds its master jewelers cut and set for the human royalty of the north.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you face a bitter reminder of House Perenolde, whose betrayal during the Second War nearly destroyed the original Alliance of Lordaeron."},kw={"alterac","emeralds","grel'borg","ironforge","miser","perenolde","remington","ridgewell","tiara"},rel={"quest:543","npc:count-remington-ridgewell","topic:alterac-kingdom","subzone:ruins-of-alterac","zone:alterac","zone:ironforge","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Perenolde Tiara","The Perenolde Tiara"}}
E["item:pristine-spider-silk"] = {t="item",n="Pristine Spider Silk",z="stormwind",s="Stormwind mages seek Pristine Spider Silk for robes woven to endure enchantments. The fine thread comes from venomous spiders in Duskwood.",h="Stormwind mages seek Pristine Spider Silk for robes woven to endure enchantments.",sec={{t="Weaving the Arcane",b="Stormwind mages need silk strong enough to bear enchantments and the wear of an adept. Tailors use common spider silk, but the strands gathered from carrion recluses and black widow hatchlings in Duskwood are more resilient. Mages from the Wizard's Sanctum send rising adepts into those woods to collect the silk. Master tailor Wynne Larson then weaves it into a robe for an adept.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does Pristine Spider Silk come from?",a="Pristine Spider Silk comes from carrion recluses and black widow hatchlings in Duskwood.",al={"where to get pristine spider silk","who drops pristine spider silk","pristine spider silk location"},it="origin"},{q="Who crafts garments from this silk?",a="Wynne Larson, a clothier in Stormwind's Mage Quarter, weaves the collected silk into a robe for the Wizard's Sanctum.",al={"who uses pristine spider silk","who turns silk into robes","wynne larson robe"}},{q="Why do the mages require this specific silk?",a="The mages need silk resilient enough for an adept's robe to bear enchantments and wear. The silk from Duskwood's spiders has the needed strength and quality.",al={"why pristine silk","magic spider silk use"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is Pristine Spider Silk?",a="Pristine Spider Silk is an exceptionally fine, immaculate webbing spun by the arachnids haunting Duskwood. Unlike the common, tattered webs found clinging to trees throughout the shadowed forest, only the purest, unblemished strands qualify as pristine. Clothiers and wizards prize it highly for its superior quality and texture, utilizing it as the essential base fabric for tailoring distinguished garments suited for practicing mages.",al={"pristine spider silk","what is pristine silk","pristine silk item"},it="identity",add="dfaa8e27"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage of Stormwind, you are sent into Duskwood to gather this fine thread and earn a robe suited to your growing arcane stature.",["profession:Tailoring"]="As a tailor, you work with delicate, resilient thread gathered from deadly spiders, a fine natural textile for magical robes."},kw={"black widow hatchling","carrion recluse","duskwood","mage robe","pristine spider silk","wizard's sanctum","wynne larson"},rel={"quest:1940","npc:wynne-larson","zone:duskwood","topic:mage","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:alliance"},src={"Pristine Spider Silk","Pristine Spider Silk (quest)"}}
E["item:report-on-the-defias-brotherhood"] = {t="item",n="Report on the Defias Brotherhood",z="stormwind",s="At Stormwind Keep, a report on the Defias Brotherhood carries the findings of a long investigation to the royal court. City Architect Baros Alexston entrusts it to the adventurer who uncovered the conspiracy.",h="At Stormwind Keep, a report on the Defias Brotherhood carries the findings of a long investigation to the...",sec={{t="A Dispatch for the Throne",b="City Architect Baros Alexston prepared a report for Stormwind's leaders after a long investigation into unrest in Westfall and nearby lands. He entrusted the document to the adventurer who unraveled the conspiracy. The report is carried to Stormwind Keep, where it is meant to accompany a personal audience about the conspirators' schemes and the danger they pose to the kingdom.",sp=0},{t="Reception at the Keep",b="King Varian Wrynn is away on a diplomatic journey when the courier reaches the throne room. Royal advisors and the regency governing for the boy-king Anduin receive the report in his place. They commend the courier for stopping VanCleef's plans. Lady Katrana Prestor is among the court figures present as the warnings reach the regency.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Report on the Defias Brotherhood?",a="The Report on the Defias Brotherhood is an official briefing by Baros Alexston, gathering intelligence on Edwin VanCleef, his subterranean army, and the wider Defias conspiracy against Stormwind.",al={"what is this report","defias report item","baros alexston report"},sp=1,it="identity"},{q="Who wrote this report?",a="Baros Alexston, Stormwind's City Architect, prepared the report. He once worked alongside the stonemasons before they broke away to form the Defias Brotherhood.",al={"who made the defias report","report author"},sp=1,it="origin",bt={"defias.masons"}},{q="Why am I delivering this to Stormwind Keep?",a="Baros Alexston believes the adventurer who uncovered the conspiracy deserves to present the findings to the throne and earn royal recognition for protecting the realm.",al={"why do i deliver this","audience with the king delivery"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Does King Varian read the report?",a="No. King Varian Wrynn is away on a diplomatic voyage when you reach Stormwind Keep. His court and regency receive the report in his place.",al={"does the king read it","varian wrynn audience"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Delivering the report brings the long struggle to secure Westfall and warn Stormwind's leaders of the insurrection at its borders to the royal court.",["race:Human"]="As a human of the realm, you carry a report that reflects the unresolved conflict between Stormwind's noble house and the stonemasons who rebuilt the city."},kw={"audience with the king","baros alexston","defias","report","stormwind keep","vancleef","westfall"},rel={"quest:396","npc:baros-alexston","topic:defias-brotherhood","subzone:stormwind-keep","zone:stormwind","quest:65","topic:varian-wrynn","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Report on the Defias Brotherhood","An Audience with the King"}}
E["item:scorched-spider-fang"] = {t="item",n="Scorched Spider Fang",z="stormwind",s="Across the Wetlands, Scorched Spider Fangs are taken from Cave Stalkers and Leech Stalkers. Furen Longbeard in Stormwind needs fifty to strengthen mail for Alliance warriors.",h="Across the Wetlands, Scorched Spider Fangs are taken from Cave Stalkers and Leech Stalkers.",sec={{t="A Dwarven Smith's Formula",b="In Stormwind, blacksmith Furen Longbeard uses unusual methods to strengthen mail. He calls for fifty scorched fangs from the giant spiders of the Wetlands. Their dense, venomous, toughened substance reinforces the mail links as he tempers them.",sp=0},{t="Stalkers of the Wetlands",b="Cave Stalkers and Leech Stalkers bear the fangs Furen needs. They live in the Wetlands' sunken valleys and burrows, where damp and rot surround their hardened, scorched mandibles. Gathering fifty means venturing into deep hollows and facing the spiders in their swarms.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are Scorched Spider Fangs used for?",a="Furen Longbeard in Stormwind needs fifty Scorched Spider Fangs to forge durable chest armor for Alliance warriors. The work also calls for components from Stonetalon and Razorfen Kraul.",al={"what do i do with scorched spider fangs","scorched spider fang purpose","who needs scorched spider fangs"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Where can I find Scorched Spider Fangs?",a="Cave Stalkers and Leech Stalkers in the Wetlands carry Scorched Spider Fangs. Search their damp burrows, hillsides, and excavation caverns.",al={"scorched spider fang drop location","which spiders drop scorched spider fang","where to farm scorched spider fangs"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does a blacksmith need so many spider fangs to make armor?",a="Furen Longbeard uses unusual dwarven methods to strengthen mail. He treats its links with hardened fangs, phlogiston, and beast horns.",al={"why 50 fangs","why does furen need spider fangs"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Can any adventurer collect and turn in these fangs?",a="Anyone traveling through the Wetlands can kill the spiders and take their mandibles. Furen commissions the armor only for aspiring warriors seeking to earn fire-hardened mail.",al={"is scorched spider fang warrior only","who can turn in scorched spider fangs"},gp=true},{q="What is a Scorched Spider Fang?",a="A Scorched Spider Fang is a hardened, heat-treated venomous tooth harvested from predatory arachnids like Cave Stalkers and Leech Stalkers lurking in the Wetlands. Their blackened, brittle appearance belies an extraordinary density, making them prized among skilled armorers seeking rare components for advanced forging techniques.",al={"what is scorched spider fang","scorched spider fangs","scorched fang"},it="identity",add="a7a99cbb"},{q="Where do Scorched Spider Fangs come from?",a="These fangs are not crafted by mortal hands; they are harvested directly from the giant arachnids of the Wetlands, specifically Leech Stalkers and Cave Stalkers. Constant exposure to the subterranean elements and the natural alchemy of their venom gives these fangs their blackened, fire-treated resilience.",al={"where do scorched spider fangs come from","origin of scorched spider fang","scorched spider fang source"},it="origin",add="c6d8f632"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you face Furen Longbeard's trial of gathering fifty fangs. The work tests your endurance and provides the raw parts for your mail armor.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="As a blacksmith, you can see how Furen uses scorched chitin and fangs in mail links, following rare dwarven armoring traditions beyond ordinary smelting."},kw={"cave stalker","fire hardened mail","furen longbeard","leech stalker","scorched spider fang","stormwind","wetlands"},rel={"quest:1701","npc:furen-longbeard","zone:wetlands","item:charred-horn","item:galvanized-horn","item:vial-of-phlogiston","item:furen-s-instructions","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Scorched Spider Fang","Fire Hardened Mail"}}
E["item:sealed-description-of-thredd-s-visitor"] = {t="item",n="Sealed Description of Thredd's Visitor",z="stormwind",s="Warden Thelwater seals a report about a visitor to Bazil Thredd in the Stormwind Stockade. The confidential account helps track a covert operative moving through Stormwind's political and criminal spheres.",h="Warden Thelwater seals a report about a visitor to Bazil Thredd in the Stormwind Stockade.",sec={{t="A Mysterious Patron",b="Prisoner Bazil Thredd spent years in the Stockade without a visitor. Then a quiet man began coming once or twice each week, carrying valid identification papers under the name Maelik. Warden Thelwater took note of the unusual visits and wrote down the man's appearance. He sealed the description so no meddling eyes could read it before proper investigators acted.",sp=0},{t="From Stonemasons to Spies",b="City architect Baros Alexston found no clear match in the description, though he suspected the visitor might be tied to the Defias rebellion. Alexston sent the sealed envelope to Master Mathias Shaw, who leads Stormwind's intelligence service, SI:7. Shaw recognized the man as a lethal mercenary who uses names including Marzon and now does dirty work for Lord Gregor Lescovar.",sp=1,bt={"q373.5"}}},faq={{q="Who wrote this description?",a="Warden Thelwater, head warden of the Stormwind Stockade, wrote and sealed the document. He grew suspicious when an unknown man began visiting the imprisoned Defias leader, Bazil Thredd, regularly.",al={"who wrote it","author of description","who penned the note"},it="origin"},{q="Who is the visitor described in the paper?",a="The visitor used papers bearing the name Maelik. Warden Thelwater recorded his appearance so investigators could identify him.",al={"who was visiting thredd","who is maelik","visitor identity"},sp=2,it="identity"},{q="Why was the visitor meeting with Bazil Thredd?",a="Thelwater grew suspicious when Thredd began receiving regular visits after years without any. The sealed description is being investigated to learn the visitor's purpose.",al={"why visit thredd","thredd visitor purpose"},sp=2,it="motive"},{q="Where does this sealed document need to be taken?",a="Take the document first to city architect Baros Alexston in Stormwind. After examining the unfamiliar description, Alexston directs you to deliver it to Master Mathias Shaw at SI:7 headquarters in Old Town.",al={"where do i bring it","who wants the description"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why is the description of Thredd's visitor so important?",a="For years, Bazil Thredd sat abandoned in the Stockade without a single visitor. When a mysterious figure carrying papers under the name 'Maelik' suddenly began visiting him weekly, Warden Thelwater grew suspicious of a deeper conspiracy. Unmasking this visitor is vital to uncovering who in Stormwind is actively coordinating with the Defias Brotherhood's incarcerated leadership, leading investigators to seek out Mathias Shaw's intelligence network to identify the shadowy liaison.",al={"why do they want the description","sealed description thredd why wanted","why is the visitor description important"},sp=1,it="why_wanted",add="7193ccc9"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you can see how false names, forged papers, and visits to a prison cell drew Mathias Shaw's attention when he compared the man's appearance with SI:7 intelligence.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can see the weakness in Stormwind's security: conspirators can pass through the Stockade's gates with falsified credentials."},kw={"baros alexston","bazil thredd","maelik","mathias shaw","sealed description","stockade","warden thelwater"},rel={"quest:392","quest:393","npc:baros-alexston","npc:mathias-shaw","quest:2300","topic:defias-brotherhood","subzone:old-town","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Sealed Description of Thredd's Visitor","The Curious Visitor","Shadow of the Past (quest)"}}
E["item:sealed-note-to-elling"] = {t="item",n="Sealed Note to Elling",z="stormwind",s="Jorgen sends a sealed dispatch through Stormwind to Elling Trias, the proprietor of Trias' Cheese. The fisherman’s message draws Trias into a quiet inquiry about a vanished diplomat.",h="Jorgen sends a sealed dispatch through Stormwind to Elling Trias, the proprietor of Trias' Cheese.",sec={{t="A Quiet Hand-Off",b="Jorgen gives a strict charge for the sealed note in Stormwind: place it in Elling Trias's hands and keep silent. The stakes leave no room for careless talk. Trias runs a cheese shop in the Trade District, where Jorgen's message brings the inquiry into the diplomat's disappearance to his counter.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is written inside the sealed note?",a="The note stays sealed until it reaches Elling Trias. It carries Jorgen's report and directs the courier to Trias for further inquiries into the diplomat's disappearance.",al={"note contents","what does the note say","letter text"},it="item"},{q="Why does a cheese vendor receive secret intelligence?",a="Elling Trias runs an unassuming cheese shop in the Trade District as a public front. Beneath that appearance, he has an extensive underground network of ears and eyes across the city, making him valuable in delicate investigations.",al={"why elling trias","why cheese shop","is trias a spy"}},{q="Who is Jorgen?",a="Jorgen is a fisherman found down by the water in Stormwind's Valley of Heroes. He has some history with Elling Trias and Bishop DeLavey, who calls on him for discreet matters kept from prying eyes.",al={"who wrote the note","jorgen lore","watchman jorgen"},it="people"},{q="What is the missing diplomat case about?",a="A Stormwind diplomat sent to Theramore to meet Jaina Proudmoore never arrived. Royal authorities quietly investigate every suspicious lead to avoid causing panic in the streets.",al={"missing diplomat lore","who is the diplomat","why missing diplomat"},it="threat"},{q="What is the Sealed Note to Elling?",a="It is a confidential message given to you by Jorgen, intended specifically for the ears—and eyes—of Elling Trias. Wax-sealed to ensure secrecy, it carries urgent information regarding the investigation into the missing diplomat, entrusted to you for safe hand-delivery across Stormwind.",al={"what is sealed note to elling","sealed note to elling item","what is jorgens note"},it="identity",add="76232759"},{q="Where does the Sealed Note to Elling come from?",a="The note was written and sealed by Jorgen. After questioning and evaluating the trail regarding the kingdom's missing diplomat, Jorgen pens this discrete dispatch and places it directly into your hands to bring to Elling Trias.",al={"who wrote the sealed note to elling","where did the sealed note come from","who gave sealed note to elling"},it="origin",add="2cd529f3"},{q="Why is the Sealed Note to Elling needed?",a="The disappearance of the diplomat is a matter of utmost delicacy and state security. Jorgen cannot speak openly on the streets, so the note serves as a quiet introduction and intelligence handover to Elling Trias, bringing Trias into the investigation without alerting prying eyes.",al={"why deliver the sealed note","why does elling trias need the note","why is jorgens note important"},it="why_wanted",add="92e95eae"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue familiar with Stormwind's shadow networks, you may recognize Elling Trias as more than a cheese merchant. This discreet correspondence fits the work of those networks.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you carry Jorgen's message in service to the Crown, helping advance an investigation vital to Stormwind's political stability."},kw={"elling trias","jorgen","sealed note to elling","stormwind","the missing diplomat","trade district","trias cheese"},rel={"npc:elling-trias","npc:jorgen","quest:1241","subzone:trade-district","zone:stormwind","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Sealed Note to Elling","The Missing Diplomat (3)"}}
E["item:sealed-note-to-watcher-backus"] = {t="item",n="Sealed Note to Watcher Backus",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind, Elling Trias sends a sealed note to Watcher Backus in Duskwood. He asks the Night Watch guard to report Defias activity near Darkshire.",h="In Stormwind, Elling Trias sends a sealed note to Watcher Backus in Duskwood.",sec={{t="A Word for the Watch",b="Elling Trias agrees to use his contacts to help search for the missing diplomat. He seals a note for Watcher Backus, a Night Watch guard stationed in Duskwood. Trias sends a traveler south through the forest to deliver it by hand. He hopes Backus will report any Defias seen near Darkshire.",sp=0},{t="Trias's Far-Reaching Eyes",b="Elling Trias sells cheese in Stormwind's Trade District and keeps contacts beyond the city. His note reaches Watcher Backus, a guard of Darkshire's wary Night Watch. The town faces threats from undead and savage beasts, yet Backus receives Trias's message warmly. Their bond shows that Trias has earned respect beyond Stormwind.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who wrote this note?",a="Elling Trias wrote the note. He owns Trias' Cheese in Stormwind City's Trade District and secretly works as a spy and information broker.",al={"who wrote sealed note to watcher backus","author of note","who gives note"},it="origin"},{q="Why is it being sent to Watcher Backus?",a="Watcher Backus serves in Darkshire's Night Watch and is a trusted contact of Elling Trias. Trias asks him to report local sightings or rumors of Defias Brotherhood activity around Duskwood.",al={"who is watcher backus","why send to backus","what is backus role"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where can Watcher Backus be found?",a="Watcher Backus patrols the road just north of Darkshire in Duskwood, watching the forest approaches to town.",al={"where is backus","watcher backus location","find watcher backus"},it="target",gp=true},{q="What happens after the note is delivered?",a="Backus recognizes Trias's name and trusts his request. He sets aside his usual caution toward travelers and agrees to help investigate suspicious activity in the woods.",al={"what does backus say","after delivering note"},it="next_step"},{q="What is the Sealed Note to Watcher Backus?",a="It is a confidential message written by Elling Trias, the master cheese merchant of Stormwind, meant for Watcher Backus in Duskwood. Trias sends it along with you to enlist Backus's aid in gathering intelligence on local Defias Brotherhood activity as part of the ongoing investigation into the missing diplomat.",al={"what is sealed note to watcher backus","sealed note to watcher backus purpose","trias note to backus"},it="identity",add="8647b8fc"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The note shows how personal ties and informal intelligence help hold the Alliance's frayed territories together when official channels fail.",["class:Rogue"]="Trias relies on an ordinary guard for local information, a way to gather intelligence far beyond city walls."},kw={"darkshire","duskwood","elling trias","night watch","sealed note","the missing diplomat","watcher backus"},rel={"npc:watcher-backus","quest:1241","subzone:darkshire","zone:duskwood","npc:jorgen"},src={"Sealed Note to Watcher Backus","The Missing Diplomat (4)"}}
E["item:shipping-schedule"] = {t="item",n="Shipping Schedule",z="stormwind",s="At Jerod's Landing, the Defias Brotherhood moves contraband along Elwynn's waterways. Its dockmaster guards a schedule that maps shipments between Redridge and Westfall, and SI:7 wants it.",h="At Jerod's Landing, the Defias Brotherhood moves contraband along Elwynn's waterways.",sec={{t="Smuggling at Jerod's Landing",b="South of Goldshire, Jerod's Landing sits on the Elwynn bank of the Nazferiti River. The Defias Brotherhood seized the landing as a hub for river traffic. From there, they move contraband between Redridge and Westfall along waterways beyond the Stormwind Guard's notice. Their dockmaster keeps the Shipping Schedule close, recording these shipments.",sp=0},{t="In the Crosshairs of SI:7",b="Master Mathias Shaw leads SI:7, Stormwind's intelligence agency, and ordered the schedule stolen. It can map Defias supply lines, while taking it tests new operatives. The theft must be made inside the dock house, from the dockmaster's pockets. If the operative is caught, SI:7 denies any connection, leaving no trail to its barracks in Stormwind.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Shipping Schedule?",a="The Shipping Schedule records contraband shipments handled by the Defias Brotherhood dockmaster at Jerod's Landing. It tracks cargo ferried between Redridge and Westfall through Elwynn Forest's inland waters.",al={"defias shipping schedule","what is this document","dockmaster schedule"},it="identity"},{q="Who wants this schedule recovered?",a="Master Mathias Shaw, head of SI:7, wants the schedule recovered. He uses it to track Defias smuggling and test promising rogues in the field.",al={"who needs the schedule","mathias shaw schedule","who takes the shipping schedule"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where is the schedule found?",a="The Defias Dockmaster carries the schedule inside the dock house at Jerod's Landing. The landing is on the Nazferiti River south of Goldshire in Elwynn Forest; the document must be taken from him there.",al={"shipping schedule location","where is the dockmaster","how to get the schedule"},it="place"},{q="What is Jerod's Landing used for?",a="The Defias Brotherhood seized Jerod's Landing as a transit point for smuggling. Its river access links their operations in Redridge with their strongholds in Westfall.",al={"jerods landing defias","why do defias have jerods landing","defias dock elwynn"},it="purpose"},{q="Where does the Shipping Schedule come from, and who made it?",a="The schedule is kept by the Defias Brotherhood's dockmaster stationed at Jerod's Landing, south of Goldshire. It details the outlaw syndicate's river operations, tracking the movement of illicit goods and contraband smuggled between the Redridge Mountains and Westfall.",al={"who wrote the shipping schedule","shipping schedule origin","who made defias shipping schedule"},it="origin",add="45ccd8c3"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, taking the schedule from the dockmaster's pockets tests the stealth and pickpocketing SI:7 expects of operatives seeking to join its ranks."},kw={"defias","dockmaster","elwynn forest","jerod's landing","mathias shaw","shipping schedule","si:7","smuggling"},rel={"quest:2206","subzone:jerod-s-landing","npc:mathias-shaw","quest:2205","zone:elwynn","subzone:goldshire","zone:westfall","topic:rogue"},src={"Shipping Schedule","Snatch and Grab"}}
E["item:stormpike-s-request"] = {t="item",n="Stormpike's Request",z="stormwind",s="Mountaineer Stormpike sends a written commission from Loch Modan to Stormwind City. He asks Furen Longbeard to craft him a shield of exceptional dwarven quality.",h="Mountaineer Stormpike sends a written commission from Loch Modan to Stormwind City.",sec={{t="A Northern Commission",b="Mountaineer Stormpike needs a sturdy shield while stationed in Loch Modan. He trusts no ordinary smith with the work and asks Furen Longbeard, whose craft he greatly admires. Furen now lives among the humans in Stormwind's Dwarven District, having left Ironforge. Stormpike assumes a king's ransom drew him south, so traveling adventurers carry the commission across the kingdoms.",sp=0},{t="The Stormpike Line",b="Furen Longbeard receives Stormpike's letter in Stormwind's Dwarven District and agrees to make the shield. A proud and established member of the Stormpike clan, known across Khaz Modan for its martial grit and wealth, Furen welcomes word and business from his northern homeland. He sets to work on the mountaineer's order.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Stormpike's Request?",a="Mountaineer Stormpike's letter from Loch Modan asks Furen Longbeard to forge him a high-quality shield.",al={"what is this letter","stormpike order item","stormpike request"},it="identity"},{q="Who wrote this letter?",a="Mountaineer Stormpike wrote the letter. He is a dwarven sentry guarding the passes of Loch Modan and deeply admires Furen Longbeard's smithing.",al={"who sent stormpikes request","who wrote it","mountaineer stormpike"},it="origin"},{q="Where does this letter need to go?",a="The letter is addressed to Furen Longbeard at his forge in Stormwind City's Dwarven District.",al={"where do i take stormpikes request","who gets this letter","deliver stormpikes request"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does Stormpike hire a smith all the way in Stormwind?",a="Stormpike considers Furen's skill unmatched and will accept no other armorer. Furen left Ironforge to work among the humans in the south.",al={"why furen","why not forge in ironforge","why send to stormwind"},it="motive"},{q="Why does Furen Longbeard want Stormpike's Request?",a="This written order commissions a finely crafted dwarven shield. Furen Longbeard, an armorsmith residing in Stormwind's Dwarven District, values business from the renowned Stormpike clan. He knows the family is not only proud and esteemed throughout Khaz Modan, but also wealthy enough to pay handsomely for exceptional craftsmanship.",al={"why does furen want this","why is stormpikes request wanted","stormpikes request why wanted"},it="why_wanted",add="181a24c8"}},ang={["profession:Blacksmithing"]="Stormpike's request shows the standing of master armorers: patrons across kingdoms seek skilled dwarven smiths.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you carry a bond of clan and craft between the mountaineers guarding Khaz Modan and craftsmen living abroad in human cities."},kw={"blacksmith","dun morogh","dwarven district","furen longbeard","request","shield","stormpike","stormwind"},rel={"quest:1338","npc:furen-longbeard","npc:mountaineer-stormpike","subzone:dwarven-district","quest:1339","zone:ironforge","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Stormpike's Request","Stormpike's Order"}}
E["item:tear-of-tilloa"] = {t="item",n="Tear of Tilloa",z="stormwind",s="In Duskwood, the Tear of Tilloa grows on the Mistmantle estate near Darkshire. Its alchemical use draws interest from those seeking rare reagents.",h="In Duskwood, the Tear of Tilloa grows on the Mistmantle estate near Darkshire.",sec={{t="A Garden in the Gloom",b="The Tear of Tilloa grows on the grounds of Stalvan Mistmantle’s estate outside Darkshire. Duskwood’s soil has turned hostile to wholesome vegetation, yet the small white flower persists among the shadowed plots. It grows rarely and in a secluded place, drawing those who seek uncommon reagents beyond lawful markets.",sp=0},{t="A Concoction for the Nobles",b="Beneath Stormwind’s streets, Zardeth of the Black Claw seeks the Tear of Tilloa to brew a draught for Lord Wishock. A member of the House of Nobles, Wishock threatens to investigate shadowy operations beneath the capital. Zardeth combines the flower with Musquash Root from beneath the Stonewrought Dam to make a brew meant to distract and incapacitate Wishock before an official probe can begin.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where does the Tear of Tilloa grow?",a="The flower grows on the outskirts of Darkshire in Duskwood, in the overgrown garden of the Mistmantle family estate.",al={"tear of tilloa location","where is tear of tilloa","tilloa spot"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who wants the Tear of Tilloa?",a="Zardeth of the Black Claw seeks the flower while operating covertly beneath Stormwind City, where he needs it for a special draught.",al={"who needs tear of tilloa","tear of tilloa quest giver","who wants it"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is the flower used for?",a="The flower is combined with Musquash Root to make a brew intended to incapacitate Lord Wishock and silence his calls to investigate dark dealings beneath the capital.",al={"tear of tilloa purpose","what does tear of tilloa do","noble brew flower"},sp=1,it="purpose"},{q="Who is Lord Wishock?",a="Lord Wishock is a nobleman in Stormwind’s House of Nobles. After learning of subversive operations beneath the city, he began urging the council to investigate.",al={"wishock","who is wishock","lord wishock"}},{q="What is the Tear of Tilloa?",a="The Tear of Tilloa is a delicate, rare white flower that blossoms in Duskwood. Specifically found within the untended Garden of Stalvan on the outskirts of Darkshire, this quiet plant holds potent properties coveted by practitioners of dark arts who operate far away in the tunnels beneath Stormwind.",al={"what is tear of tilloa","tear of tilloa flower","tear of tilloa"},it="identity",add="e7b72a0d"},{q="Where does the Tear of Tilloa come from?",a="The flower grows naturally in the overgrown Garden of Stalvan, located just beyond the safety of Darkshire in the shadowed forest of Duskwood. No mortal artisan created it; it simply blooms undisturbed amid the tragic estate grounds of the former Mistmantle home.",al={"where does tear of tilloa come from","who made tear of tilloa","tear of tilloa origin"},it="origin",add="d8c5f010"}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="As a herbalist, you may find the Tear of Tilloa growing in Duskwood’s blighted ground, far from the usual lush fields.",["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you may know the Tear of Tilloa as a reagent sought by occult operatives beneath the capital for brews meant to silence probing nobles."},kw={"a noble brew","darkshire","mistmantle","stalvan","tear of tilloa","tilloa","wishock","zardeth"},rel={"quest:335","quest:397","item:musquash-root","subzone:darkshire","zone:duskwood","topic:house-of-nobles","subzone:stonewrought-dam"},src={"Tear of Tilloa","A Noble Brew"}}
E["item:the-general-s-response"] = {t="item",n="The General's Response",z="stormwind",s="General Marcus Jonathan sends word to Lakeshire while Redridge waits for aid. His dispatch acknowledges Magistrate Solomon's plea against the Blackrock orcs and gnolls, but offers no immediate reinforcements from Stormwind.",h="General Marcus Jonathan sends word to Lakeshire while Redridge waits for aid.",sec={{t="A Diplomatic Standoff",b="Magistrate Solomon sends an urgent plea to Stormwind City for troops to defend Redridge from the gathering Blackrock orc clans and Gnoll warbands. General Marcus Jonathan replies that the plea has been forwarded to the throne, but no soldiers are being sent now. He orders the letter returned to Lakeshire. Solomon is left troubled by Stormwind's delay and suspicious that something is wrong with its leaders.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is written in The General's Response?",a="General Marcus Jonathan mourns the dead and says he will make the King aware of Lakeshire's plight. He hopes to bring reinforcements and confides that His Majesty has been scarce and acting oddly.",al={"letter contents","what does the letter say","generals letter"},it="item"},{q="Why can't General Marcus Jonathan send troops to Lakeshire?",a="General Jonathan awaits the King's response before promising reinforcements. In confidence, he tells Solomon that His Majesty has been scarce and acting oddly.",al={"why no reinforcements","why doesn't stormwind help lakeshire","why no help"},it="conflict"},{q="How does Magistrate Solomon react to the letter?",a="Magistrate Solomon is deeply unsettled by the dispatch. Stormwind's slowness makes no sense to him while Lakeshire faces such danger, and he fears the neglect points to worse trouble in the kingdom.",al={"solomon reaction","what does solomon think","solomon response"}},{q="What is The General's Response?",a="It is an official sealed dispatch written by General Marcus Jonathan, commander of the Stormwind City Guard, addressed to Magistrate Solomon in Redridge. Carried by messengers between the capital and Lakeshire, the missive delivers the high command's formal reply regarding Redridge's desperate plea for royal reinforcements.",al={"what is the generals response","generals response item","what is this letter"},it="identity",add="3ebc4cbb"},{q="Where does The General's Response come from, and who made it?",a="The letter is penned directly by General Marcus Jonathan within Stormwind City. After receiving Magistrate Solomon's urgent petition at the Valley of Heroes, Jonathan drafts this formal reply while awaiting word from the royal court, entrusting you to carry it back to the magistrate in Lakeshire.",al={"who wrote the generals response","where did the generals response come from","who sent the generals response"},it="origin",add="174955dc"},{q="Why does anyone want The General's Response?",a="Magistrate Solomon is anxiously awaiting this dispatch to learn whether Stormwind will deploy soldiers to rescue Lakeshire from the Blackrock orcs and gnolls. Delivering it gives the beleaguered town leadership clear word on what aid the kingdom can—or cannot—provide.",al={"why does solomon want the letter","who wants the generals response","why deliver the generals response"},it="why_wanted",add="d0ef00e9"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Stormwind's response shows the strain on the Grand Alliance. Lakeshire bleeds while the court appears strangely unresponsive to its plight.",["race:Human"]="For humans of the southern kingdoms, the delayed reply shows the growing rift between people fighting for survival in the provinces and the secluded nobility in Stormwind Keep."},kw={"general marcus jonathan","lakeshire","magistrate solomon","messenger to stormwind","redridge","stormwind","the generals response"},rel={"npc:general-marcus-jonathan","npc:magistrate-solomon","quest:120","subzone:lakeshire","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"The General's Response","Messenger to Stormwind (2)"}}
E["item:thurman-s-sewing-kit"] = {t="item",n="Thurman's Sewing Kit",z="stormwind",s="At Larson Clothiers, Thurman's Sewing Kit is needed for his tailoring work. The tools belong to young apprentice Thurman Schneider, who left them behind at his family's canal home to avoid a long day of stitching.",h="At Larson Clothiers, Thurman's Sewing Kit is needed for his tailoring work.",sec={{t="A Reluctant Apprentice's Tools",b="Thurman's Sewing Kit holds the everyday tools of an apprentice tailor: needles, shears, and thread. Young Thurman Schneider studies tailoring at Larson Clothiers, deep in Stormwind's Mage Quarter near the Mage Tower. His mother, Rema Schneider, knows he cannot do his work without the kit, so she asks passersby along the Canals to carry it to the shop. When Thurman gets the tools, his reaction shows he left them behind on purpose, hoping to trade a day of stitching garments for leisure.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is inside Thurman's Sewing Kit?",a="The kit holds needles, shears, and thread, the tools Thurman Schneider needs for his tailoring work at Larson Clothiers.",al={"what's in the kit","sewing kit contents","thurman shears"},it="item"},{q="Who does this sewing kit belong to?",a="The kit belongs to Thurman Schneider, a young apprentice working under the Larsons in Stormwind's Mage Quarter.",al={"who owns the kit","thurman owner","who is thurman"},it="identity"},{q="Why was the kit left behind at Thurman's home?",a="Rema thought Thurman had rushed out and forgotten the kit, but he left it behind on purpose, hoping to avoid his work at Larson Clothiers for the day.",al={"why did thurman forget his kit","did thurman forget on purpose","why leave sewing kit"},it="motive"},{q="Where does this kit need to be delivered?",a="Take the kit to Larson Clothiers, deep in Stormwind City's Mage Quarter near the Mage Tower.",al={"where do i take the kit","larson clothiers location","thurman location"},it="target"},{q="Why does Rema Schneider want Thurman's Sewing Kit delivered?",a="Thurman is an apprentice tailor at Larson Clothiers in the Mage Quarter. His mother, Rema Schneider, asks you to deliver the kit so he can carry out his daily tailoring duties. However, Thurman secretly left his tools behind on purpose, hoping to avoid his chores and shirk work for the day.",al={"why deliver thurmans sewing kit","why does thurman need his sewing kit","why want sewing kit"},it="why_wanted",add="128c9147"}},ang={["profession:Tailoring"]="Every tailor knows the drudgery of early apprenticeship, though few go so far as young Thurman Schneider and leave their shears behind."},kw={"larson clothiers","mage quarter","rema schneider","sewing kit","stormwind canals","thurman schneider","thurman's sewing kit"},rel={"quest:334","npc:rema-schneider","subzone:mage-quarter","subzone:canals-stormwind-city","zone:stormwind","quest:332"},src={"Thurman's Sewing Kit","Package for Thurman"}}
E["item:ur-s-treatise-on-shadow-magic"] = {t="item",n="Ur's Treatise on Shadow Magic",z="stormwind",s="Stormwind's mages once guarded Ur's Treatise on Shadow Magic, but Morganth stole the perilous tome and hid it in the Tower of Ilgalar.",h="Stormwind's mages once guarded Ur's Treatise on Shadow Magic, but Morganth stole the perilous tome and hid it...",sec={{t="A Dangerous Legacy",b="Ur of Dalaran wrote a treatise on shadow magic and its subtle, corruptive nature. The mages of the Wizard's Sanctum in Stormwind feared that such arts could bring doom and ruin to the unwary, so they sealed the volume against readers. After Morganth surrendered to dark arts and Stormwind's magical circle exiled him, he took the tome east into the Redridge Mountains, to his stronghold at the Tower of Ilgalar.",sp=0},{t="The Warded Secrets",b="High Sorcerer Andromath feared Morganth might master the dark lore in Ur's work, so he sent adventurers to breach the Tower of Ilgalar and reclaim it. Morganth had sunk deep into forbidden magic, but the warding seals Stormwind's circle placed on the treatise held firm against him. The book remained unopened until it was recovered.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who was Ur?",a="Ur was a respected wizard and scholar from Dalaran. He studied extraplanar creatures, dark arts, and esoteric magic, including shadow craft.",al={"who wrote this book","ur of dalaran","who is ur"},it="people"},{q="Why is the treatise so dangerous?",a="Shadow magic can corrupt an untrained practitioner and bring doom and ruin. High Sorcerer Andromath warns against probing its forbidden depths.",al={"why is the book dangerous","what does the book do","shadow magic danger"},it="danger"},{q="Who stole Ur's Treatise on Shadow Magic?",a="Morganth stole the tome after he was banished from Stormwind's wizard order for succumbing to dark magic. He retreated to the Tower of Ilgalar in Redridge.",al={"who stole the book","morganth stolen book","who took the treatise"}},{q="Did Morganth manage to read the treatise?",a="No. Stormwind's mages sealed the tome, and their wards held fast, keeping Morganth from opening it before its recovery.",al={"did morganth read it","did the seals hold","was the book opened"},sp=1},{q="Is this the same work as The Book of Ur?",a="Both works are by Ur and closely related. The Book of Ur is a broader grimoire kept in the ruins of Shadowfang Keep, while the Treatise on Shadow Magic appears to be an excerpt or specialized volume focused on shadow arts.",al={"the book of ur difference","book of ur shadowfang","is this the book of ur"},it="ties"},{q="What is Ur's Treatise on Shadow Magic?",a="It is a potent and guarded tome detailing the forbidden mysteries of shadow magic. Kept under protective wards by the mages of the Wizard's Sanctum in Stormwind, the book contains powerful occult knowledge that, if unsealed, could bring doom and ruin upon anyone reckless enough to study it.",al={"what is ur's treatise","urs treatise on shadow magic","what is the treatise on shadow magic"},it="identity",add="9052da59"},{q="Where does Ur's Treatise on Shadow Magic come from, and who made it?",a="The book was penned by the gifted Kirin Tor mage Ur of Dalaran, a scholar who dedicated himself to researching dark arts, otherworldly entities, and shadow magic. His dangerous writings eventually made their way to Stormwind, where the city's mages sealed the treatise away to keep its secrets locked from the untrained.",al={"who wrote ur's treatise","where did ur's treatise come from","origin of urs treatise on shadow magic"},it="origin",add="0481e4cc"},{q="Why does anyone want Ur's Treatise on Shadow Magic?",a="Practitioners seduced by dark powers seek the treatise for its formidable arcane and shadow secrets. The renegade mage Morganth stole it to augment his own occult might, while High Sorcerer Andromath and the mages of Stormwind urgently seek its return to ensure its seals remain intact and its perils safely locked away.",al={"why is the treatise wanted","why do mages want ur's treatise","why does morganth want the treatise"},it="why_wanted",add="9d095b57"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage of Stormwind, you help contain the treatise and preserve the Sanctum's safety after one of its own succumbed to dark temptations.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you know Morganth's presence in Redridge threatens the kingdom's eastern frontier. Retrieving the powerful artifact matters to Stormwind's security."},kw={"andromath","dalaran","ilgalar","morganth","redridge","sanctum","shadow magic","tome","treatise","ur"},rel={"quest:1938","subzone:tower-of-ilgalar","quest:249","quest:1939","quest:1013","zone:redridge","topic:mage","subzone:dalaran"},src={"Ur's Treatise on Shadow Magic","Ur's Treatise on Shadow Magic (quest)"}}
E["item:vial-of-phlogiston"] = {t="item",n="Vial of Phlogiston",z="stormwind",s="A Vial of Phlogiston is an alchemical substance used by master armorers to temper extraordinarily resilient mail. Guarded within the quilboar stronghold of Razorfen Kraul, it is coveted by both Alliance and Horde smiths forging specialized battle armor for promising warriors.",h="A Vial of Phlogiston is an alchemical substance used by master armorers to temper extraordinarily resilient...",sec={{t="Essence of the Forge",b="Phlogiston is an intensely volatile, fire-bearing substance prized in esoteric metallurgy. Both the dwarven smith Furen Longbeard in Stormwind and the near-blind orc armorer Thun'grim Firegaze in the Barrens consider it an indispensable component for hardening warrior armor beyond ordinary physical limits. Without this alchemical agent, the specialized forging techniques required for Fire Hardened Mail or the Horde's Brutal Armor cannot be completed.",sp=0},{t="Retrieved from the Brambles",b="Obtaining a Vial of Phlogiston requires venturing into the tangled thickets of Razorfen Kraul, located at the southern tip of the Barrens. The phlogiston is held deep within the bristling redoubt by the geomancer Roogug. Whether recovered for Furen in Stormwind or carried across the dust to Thun'grim's anvil, the substance demands a perilous descent into hostile quilboar territory.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is phlogiston used for?",a="Master smiths use phlogiston as an alchemical tempering catalyst. It provides the extreme, concentrated heat needed to harden raw mail and iron into extraordinarily durable warrior armor.",al={"vial of phlogiston use","what does phlogiston do","why do i need phlogiston"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who carries the Vial of Phlogiston?",a="The vial is carried by Roogug, a quilboar geomancer dwelling deep within the thorned tunnels of Razorfen Kraul in the southern Barrens.",al={"who drops vial of phlogiston","vial of phlogiston drop","where to get vial of phlogiston"},it="origin"},{q="Which smiths require this material?",a="Both Furen Longbeard in Stormwind and Thun'grim Firegaze in the Barrens require a Vial of Phlogiston to forge unique, hardened armor suits for seasoned warriors.",al={"who wants vial of phlogiston","phlogiston quest","what quests need phlogiston"}},{q="What is the Vial of Phlogiston?",a="The Vial of Phlogiston contains an exceptionally rare alchemical substance renowned among master armorers for its intense heat and tempering properties. Highly sought after by specialized smiths in both the Alliance and the Horde, the fiery essence is used as a critical catalyst in forging resilient, tempered mail armor fit for seasoned warriors.",al={"what is vial of phlogiston","phlogiston lore","vial of phlogiston item"},it="identity",add="3ab06e7f"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="Acquiring a Vial of Phlogiston is an essential milestone in earning iconic tempered armor, proving a warrior's ability to breach Razorfen Kraul.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="Phlogiston represents high-level specialized metallurgy, functioning as a vital flux for tempering legendary mail plate."},kw={"brutal armor","fire hardened mail","furen longbeard","phlogiston","razorfen kraul","roogug","thun'grim firegaze","vial of phlogiston"},rel={"quest:1701","quest:1838","zone:razorfenkraul","npc:furen-longbeard","quest:1502","topic:razorfen","item:charred-horn","item:galvanized-horn"},src={"Vial of Phlogiston","Fire Hardened Mail","Brutal Armor"}}
E["item:wine-ticket"] = {t="item",n="Wine Ticket",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind, Renato Gallina hands out Wine Tickets to bring customers to his family's shop. Present one to Suzetta Gallina for a complimentary bottle of Pinot Noir.",h="In Stormwind, Renato Gallina hands out Wine Tickets to bring customers to his family's shop.",sec={{t="Promoting the Family Vintage",b="Renato Gallina promotes the Gallina Winery with printed tickets near Stormwind's Trade District. The winery is a boutique vintage shop along the nearby canals. Each ticket promises a complimentary sample of Pinot Noir, drawing curious passersby and newly arrived adventurers toward the family business in hopes they become loyal customers.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What do I do with the Wine Ticket?",a="Take the Wine Ticket to Suzetta Gallina at the Gallina Winery along the canals in Stormwind's Trade District. She will redeem it for a complimentary bottle of Pinot Noir.",al={"wine ticket use","how to use wine ticket","where do i bring wine ticket"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Who hands out these tickets?",a="Renato Gallina hands out the tickets near the Trade District, drawing prospective customers to his family's wine shop.",al={"who gives wine ticket","where to get wine ticket"},it="origin"},{q="What kind of wine does the ticket reward?",a="The ticket can be redeemed for a bottle of Pinot Noir, one of the finest wines the Gallina family sells in the kingdom.",al={"wine ticket reward","what wine do i get"},it="purpose"},{q="What is the Wine Ticket?",a="The Wine Ticket is a promotional voucher and advertising pamphlet distributed on the streets of Stormwind. It serves as an invitation to the Gallina Winery, entitling anyone who holds it to a complimentary sample of the Gallina family's finest vintages.",al={"what is wine ticket","wine ticket item","wine shop advert ticket"},it="identity",add="eb06e870"},{q="Why does Suzetta Gallina want the Wine Ticket?",a="Suzetta Gallina collects the ticket to confirm you received the winery's street promotion from her brother, Renato Gallina. Exchanging the voucher honors their marketing offer and welcomes new patrons into their canal-side shop with a free bottle of Pinot Noir.",al={"why does suzetta want the ticket","why turn in wine ticket","why want wine ticket"},it="why_wanted",add="38c548d0"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="A bottle of Pinot Noir from this ticket pairs well with hearty meats and cheeses gathered throughout the Eastern Kingdoms."},kw={"gallina winery","pinot noir","renato gallina","stormwind canals","suzetta gallina","trade district","wine ticket"},rel={"quest:332","npc:suzetta-gallina","subzone:trade-district","subzone:canals-stormwind-city","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Wine Ticket","Wine Shop Advert"}}
E["npc:amber-kearnen"] = {t="npc",n="Amber Kearnen",z="stormwind",s="In Westfall, Amber Kearnen watches the Defias Brotherhood for SI:7. From a hidden vantage point, she tracks their unlawful activity for Master Mathias Shaw.",h="In Westfall, Amber Kearnen watches the Defias Brotherhood for SI:7.",sec={{t="Eyes on the Tower",b="Amber Kearnen scouts for SI:7 in Westfall, far from the halls of Stormwind Keep. She watches an abandoned tower the Defias Brotherhood has taken over. Master Mathias Shaw leads her work directly. Kearnen briefs covert operatives sent to stop Defias threats and gather intelligence across the contested countryside.",sp=0},{t="A Deadly Assignment",b="Amber Kearnen keeps watch on Klaven Mortwake, a Defias who has taken shelter in the tower southeast of Sentinel Hill. After weeks watching the tower, she briefs infiltrating rogues on the strange, inhuman guards that came with a shipment from Duskwood. She sends them to steal the tower key, enter the tower, and discover what lies in the Duskwood chest, including Klaven's journal. Her patience and careful notes aid the Crown's covert operations against the Defias.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Amber Kearnen?",a="Amber Kearnen works for SI:7, Stormwind's elite intelligence division. As a field agent and scout, she tracks Defias activity in Westfall.",al={"amber kearnen","who is kearnen","agent kearnen"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Amber Kearnen be found?",a="Amber Kearnen keeps watch in the wilds of Westfall, near the abandoned Alliance watchtower occupied by the Defias Brotherhood.",al={"amber kearnen location","where is kearnen","where is amber kearnen"},it="why_here",gp=true},{q="What is her connection to Mathias Shaw?",a="Amber Kearnen answers directly to Master Mathias Shaw, the leader of SI:7. Shaw sends fellow agents to her in Westfall to hear what she knows about Defias activity there.",al={"kearnen mathias shaw","who does kearnen work for"},it="ties"},{q="What role does she play in Klaven's Tower?",a="Amber Kearnen watches the tower held by Klaven Mortwake. She briefs Alliance rogues sent by SI:7 on how to slip inside, evade Defias guards, and recover Klaven's journal.",al={"klavens tower","amber kearnen klavens tower","what does she do at the tower"},it="purpose"},{q="Whose side is Amber Kearnen on?",a="Amber Kearnen is a loyal operative of the Alliance, serving within Stormwind's premier intelligence agency, SI:7. She answers directly to SI:7 leadership, operating covertly in the field to protect the kingdom from domestic subversion and hostile factions.",al={"amber kearnen faction","who does amber kearnen work for","is amber kearnen alliance"},it="side",add="b2881d9a"},{q="What does Amber Kearnen want?",a="Her primary objective is keeping watch on the Defias Brotherhood and neutralizing their operations in Westfall. She focuses on gathering intelligence regarding Klaven Mortwake and aiding field operatives tasked with infiltrating his tower to recover vital Defias documents.",al={"amber kearnen goal","what is amber kearnen trying to do","amber kearnen mission"},it="wants",add="e7eadf92"},{q="Why is Amber Kearnen stationed in Westfall?",a="SI:7 dispatched her to Westfall to maintain constant reconnaissance on an abandoned Alliance watchtower seized by the Defias Brotherhood. Stationed in concealment nearby, she observes enemy movements and provides covert support to agents sent to penetrate the stronghold.",al={"why is amber kearnen here","amber kearnen westfall why","why is agent kearnen in westfall"},it="why_here",add="e7dcbc70"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As an Alliance rogue, you can rely on Agent Kearnen as your field contact while you plan your infiltration of Klaven's Tower.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can look to Kearnen as Stormwind's covert agent in Westfall, working against the Defias Brotherhood without alarming the populace."},kw={"amber","defias","kearnen","klaven mortwake","klaven's tower","mathias shaw","rogue","si:7","westfall"},rel={"npc:mathias-shaw","quest:2359","topic:defias-brotherhood","zone:westfall","quest:2300","topic:alliance"},src={"Amber Kearnen"}}
E["npc:archbishop-benedictus"] = {t="npc",n="Archbishop Benedictus",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind City, Archbishop Benedictus leads the Church of the Holy Light from the Cathedral of Light. He guides the faithful and the Alliance through uncertain times.",h="In Stormwind City, Archbishop Benedictus leads the Church of the Holy Light from the Cathedral of Light.",sec={{t="Shepherd of the Holy Light",b="Archbishop Benedictus took the Church’s leadership after his mentor, Archbishop Alonsus Faol, died. He had seen the First and Second Wars devastate the kingdoms and helped oversee the building of the Cathedral of Light in Stormwind City. He vowed to uphold the virtues of the faith. After Lordaeron fell and the Scourge rose during the Third War, the human kingdoms looked to him for spiritual guidance. From the Cathedral, he counsels the royal court, trains newly initiated priests, and directs holy crusades against the undead and demonic forces threatening Azeroth.",sp=0},{t="A Beacon of Hope",b="Across the Alliance, people regard Archbishop Benedictus as a gentle, wise, and benevolent patriarch. He offers the public hope and rallies heroes against dark threats, including Amnennar the Coldbringer in Kalimdor. He also helps purify cursed relics brought by faithful adventurers.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Archbishop Benedictus?",a="Archbishop Benedictus leads the Church of the Holy Light and is the highest religious authority in the Grand Alliance. From the Cathedral of Light in Stormwind City, he guides the faithful and counsels the kingdom’s leaders.",al={"benedictus","archbishop stormwind","leader of church of the holy light"},it="identity"},{q="What is his relationship to Alonsus Faol?",a="Archbishop Benedictus was the foremost pupil of Archbishop Alonsus Faol, founder of the Knights of the Silver Hand. After Faol died, Benedictus took up leadership of the Church and continued his mentor’s work.",al={"faol student","alonsus faol benedictus"},it="ties"},{q="What tasks does Benedictus oversee for adventurers?",a="Archbishop Benedictus directs Alliance heroes against the Scourge, including expeditions into Razorfen Downs to slay the lich Amnennar the Coldbringer. He also uses holy power to cleanse corrupted artifacts such as the Cursed Eye of Paleth.",al={"benedictus quests","what does archbishop benedictus do"},it="purpose"},{q="What is his stance on the undead?",a="Archbishop Benedictus calls for the Forsaken to receive a swift, permanent death. His follower Commander Karl Philips says the Archbishop asks only for their hearts to be brought back and burned at the Cathedral of Light.",al={"benedictus forsaken","benedictus views on scourge"}},{q="Whose side is Archbishop Benedictus on?",a="Archbishop Benedictus stands firmly with the Grand Alliance and the Church of the Holy Light. Residing in Stormwind's Cathedral of Light, he serves as the spiritual father to human and dwarven faithful alike, guiding the kingdom's priests and offering counsel in King Varian Wrynn's absence.",al={"archbishop benedictus faction","is benedictus alliance","who does benedictus serve"},it="side",add="40ad9930"},{q="What does Archbishop Benedictus want?",a="Benedictus seeks to preserve and spread the virtues of the Holy Light across a fractured world. Following the devastating loss of Lordaeron to the Scourge, he strives to shelter the faithful, train a new generation of priests, and root out dark corruption wherever it threatens the Alliance.",al={"benedictus goal","what is benedictus trying to do","benedictus motive"},it="wants",add="ae63c6cb"},{q="Why is Archbishop Benedictus famous?",a="Benedictus is renowned as the supreme leader of the Church of the Holy Light. Having studied directly under the revered Archbishop Alonsus Faol and helped oversee the construction of Stormwind's magnificent Cathedral of Light, he is venerated throughout the Eastern Kingdoms as a beacon of pious wisdom and steadfast leadership.",al={"why is benedictus well known","is benedictus famous","benedictus reputation"},it="fame",add="5f68afea"}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you look to Archbishop Benedictus, who oversees the training, doctrines, and vows of all Alliance priests as head of the Church of the Holy Light.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can look to Archbishop Benedictus for moral guidance and spiritual comfort for refugees. He also guides high-ranking paladins and commanders."},kw={"alonsus faol","archbishop","benedictus","cathedral of light","church of the holy light","eye of paleth","priest","stormwind"},rel={"subzone:cathedral-of-light","topic:church-of-the-holy-light","topic:light","zone:stormwind","quest:293","topic:varian-wrynn","subzone:razorfen-downs-classic"},src={"Archbishop Benedictus"}}
E["npc:archmage-malin"] = {t="npc",n="Archmage Malin",z="stormwind",s="Outside the Wizard's Sanctum in Stormwind City, Archmage Malin directs arcane affairs. A former pupil of Archmage Trelane, he coordinates field agents seeking magical artifacts and rare reagents across the Eastern Kingdoms.",h="Outside the Wizard's Sanctum in Stormwind City, Archmage Malin directs arcane affairs.",sec={{t="Watcher of the Wizard's Sanctum",b="Archmage Malin is the central contact for Stormwind's arcane practitioners, stationed beneath the Wizard's Sanctum in the Mage Quarter. He learned magic under Archmage Trelane, and now works to protect the scattered legacy of his former master. While acolytes study inside the tower, Malin watches over matters across the realm that need magical oversight.",sp=0},{t="Eyes in the Highlands",b="Archmage Malin directs much of his attention north, to the perilous ruins of the Arathi Highlands. He sent his trusted associates, Skuerto and Apprentice Kryten, to recover Archmage Trelane's lost possessions and secure delicate spell components. From the capital, Malin coordinates their work and relies on capable Alliance travelers to carry instructions, supplies, and intelligence to his agents in hostile territory.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Archmage Malin?",a="Archmage Malin is a high-ranking human mage in Stormwind City. Outside the Wizard's Sanctum in the Mage Quarter, he oversees research, dispatches field apprentices, and helps maintain order among the capital's magical practitioners.",al={"archmage malin lore","who is malin","malin stormwind"},it="identity"},{q="What is Malin's connection to Archmage Trelane?",a="Archmage Trelane was Archmage Malin's master and mentor. Malin remains deeply loyal to Trelane and coordinates efforts to find and recover his former master's belongings and magical relics in the Arathi Highlands.",al={"malin trelane","who was malin master","archmage trelane connection"},it="ties"},{q="Why does Malin send adventurers to the Arathi Highlands?",a="Archmage Malin sends travelers to reach his agents, Skuerto and Apprentice Kryten, in the Arathi Highlands. The journey is dangerous and communication is difficult, so he needs them to carry requests, magical supplies, and instructions for recovering Trelane's artifacts.",al={"malin request quest","why arathi","skuerto quest"},it="wants"},{q="Where can Archmage Malin be found?",a="Archmage Malin stands outside the Wizard's Sanctum entrance at the tower's base, in Stormwind City's Mage Quarter. From there, he overlooks the ramps leading up to the sanctum's portal chamber.",al={"where is malin","archmage malin location","malin map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Archmage Malin on?",a="Archmage Malin is loyal to the Alliance and serves within Stormwind City. Positioned prominently outside the Wizard's Sanctum in the Mage Quarter, he works closely with other human mages and relies on trusted agents and Alliance adventurers to carry out his requests across the Eastern Kingdoms.",al={"is malin alliance","malin faction","who does malin serve"},it="side",add="deac5a59"},{q="Why is Archmage Malin here in Stormwind?",a="Archmage Malin stands outside the Wizard's Sanctum to coordinate magical efforts and supervise operations away from the capital. While he remains in Stormwind, he dispatches agents like Skuerto and Apprentice Kryten into distant, perilous regions such as the Arathi Highlands, calling upon capable travelers passing through the city to assist them.",al={"why is malin in stormwind","malin purpose wizards sanctum","why is malin outside the sanctum"},it="why_here",add="77b45b55"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As an Alliance mage visiting the Wizard's Sanctum, you see Malin connect formal study in Stormwind with the hazards of recovering lost relics in the wild.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you know Malin's operatives in Arathi seek powerful artifacts before they fall into the hands of the Syndicate, the Boulderfist ogres, or the Horde."},kw={"arathi highlands","archmage malin","kryten","mage quarter","malin","skuerto","stormwind","trelane","wizard's sanctum"},rel={"subzone:mage-quarter","zone:stormwind","npc:skuerto","quest:690","zone:arathi","subzone:sanctum-stromgarde-keep","topic:alliance","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Archmage Malin"}}
E["npc:argos-nightwhisper"] = {t="npc",n="Argos Nightwhisper",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind's Park, Argos Nightwhisper guides Alliance travelers toward Darkshore. His brother Gershala studies the corruption spreading there.",h="In Stormwind's Park, Argos Nightwhisper guides Alliance travelers toward Darkshore.",sec={{t="A Kaldorei in the Human Capital",b="Argos Nightwhisper lives among the night elves gathering in Stormwind's Park. The district's quiet groves recall the kaldorei's ancestral woodlands. Like others of his kin stationed in the human kingdom, Argos connects the new allies across the Great Sea. Reports from across the ocean trouble him. He urges capable Alliance champions to travel to Auberdine in Darkshore, where his brother Gershala needs help against the spreading corruption.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Argos Nightwhisper?",a="Argos Nightwhisper is a night elf who lives in Stormwind City. He represents Darnassus in the eastern Alliance capital, helping travelers and directing them to passage to Kalimdor.",al={"argos nightwhisper","who is argos","argos stormwind"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Argos Nightwhisper be found?",a="You can find Argos in the Park, Stormwind City's green district where visiting night elves gather.",al={"argos location","where is argos","find argos nightwhisper"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What does Argos ask adventurers to do?",a="Argos asks seasoned adventurers to travel to Auberdine in Darkshore, where his brother Gershala needs help studying the corruption spreading through the land.",al={"corruption abroad quest","argos quest","why go to darnassus"},it="wants"},{q="Is Argos related to other Nightwhispers?",a="Yes. Argos is the brother of Gershala Nightwhisper, a night elf scholar in Auberdine in Darkshore. That is why Argos sends travelers there.",al={"nightwhisper family","argos relatives"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Argos Nightwhisper on?",a="Argos Nightwhisper stands firmly with the Alliance and his kaldorei kin. As a night elf residing among the emissaries and travelers in Stormwind's Park, he remains loyal to Darnassus while assisting travelers and heroes dedicated to the defense and well-being of the Alliance.",al={"argos nightwhisper faction","is argos alliance","who does argos serve"},it="side",add="50b5b885"},{q="Why is Argos Nightwhisper in Stormwind?",a="Argos stays within the Park, the verdant sanctuary set aside for the night elves in Stormwind City. Like many of his kin in the human capital, he serves as an envoy and point of contact between Darnassus and the Eastern Kingdoms, seeking capable champions to assist with kaldorei concerns abroad.",al={"why is argos in stormwind","argos nightwhisper why here","what is argos doing in stormwind"},it="why_here",add="e48f5556"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a kaldorei far from Kalimdor, you may find Argos a familiar face. He points travelers toward his brother in Darkshore and the threats endangering their homeland.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance hero, you can look to Argos as a link between the Eastern Kingdoms and Kalimdor. He encourages young heroes to cross the sea and aid the night elves."},kw={"argos","auberdine","corruption abroad","darnassus","kaldorei","nightwhisper","park","stormwind"},rel={"subzone:park","zone:darnassus","quest:3765","topic:night-elf","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Argos Nightwhisper"}}
E["npc:baros-alexston"] = {t="npc",n="Baros Alexston",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind City Hall, Baros Alexston keeps watch over the capital he helped rebuild. Once a close friend of Edwin VanCleef in the Stonemasons Guild, he stayed loyal to the crown when the guild fractured.",h="In Stormwind City Hall, Baros Alexston keeps watch over the capital he helped rebuild.",sec={{t="From the Farmstead to the Scaffold",b="Baros grew up on the Alexston Farmstead in Westfall's rolling grasslands. Thieves overran and burned the family homestead while he was young. Before they fled, his father hurriedly hid their cherished heirlooms across the grounds. Baros later journeyed to the capital and joined the Stonemasons Guild. For years, he labored beside Guildmaster Edwin VanCleef as they raised Stormwind anew from the ashes of the First War.",sp=0},{t="A Bitter Parting of Ways",b="When Stormwind's rebuilding ended, the House of Nobles refused the agreed payment. Furious protests followed, the Stonemasons Guild dissolved, and deadly riots filled the streets. Edwin VanCleef led the unpaid artisans into exile, where they formed the Defias Brotherhood. The nobles offered Baros the post of City Architect if he disavowed the uprising. Baros disagreed with the guild's turn toward violent banditry and accepted, leaving a bitter rift between himself and his former comrades.",sp=1,bt={"defias.masons"}},{t="The Ghost in the Dead Mines",b="Baros oversees the capital's upkeep from his desk in City Hall, and Mathias Shaw of SI:7 discreetly owes him a favor. After VanCleef fell in the depths of the Deadmines, an unsent letter addressed to Baros remained on the Defias leader's corpse. Its presence recalls the bond broken by politics, treason, and bloodshed over Stormwind's foundations.",sp=1,bt={"defias.hideout"}}},faq={{q="Where can I find Baros Alexston?",a="You can find Baros Alexston inside Stormwind City Hall, on the north side of Cathedral Square in Stormwind City.",al={"baros alexston location","where is baros alexston","baros stormwind"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Baros Alexston's role in Stormwind?",a="Baros oversees Stormwind City's construction, upkeep, and architectural planning as its Chief Architect.",al={"baros job","baros title","what does baros do"},it="identity"},{q="How does Baros know Edwin VanCleef?",a="Baros and Edwin VanCleef were close colleagues in the Stonemasons Guild, laboring side by side to rebuild Stormwind after the First War. When the House of Nobles refused to pay the workers, VanCleef led a rebellion while Baros stayed to become City Architect.",al={"baros and vancleef","did baros know edwin","baros stonemasons"},sp=1,it="ties"},{q="Why didn't Baros join the Defias Brotherhood?",a="Baros disagreed with the guild's turn toward violent revolt. The nobles offered him the City Architect post on the condition that he refuse to follow VanCleef, and Baros accepted.",al={"why did baros stay","baros defias split","why did baros betray stonemasons"},sp=1,it="side",bt={"defias.masons"}},{q="What is the unsent letter found on Edwin VanCleef?",a="After Edwin VanCleef died in the Deadmines, an unsent letter addressed to Baros Alexston was found on his body. It speaks to lingering resentment and unresolved history between the former craftsmen.",al={"unsent letter quest","vancleef unsent letter","letter to baros"},sp=1,it="item",bt={"defias.hideout"}},{q="What is Baros Alexston's connection to Westfall?",a="Baros grew up on the Alexston Farmstead in Westfall, and after thieves burned it, his family fled. He recruits adventurers to reclaim his childhood possessions, including his first compass.",al={"alexston farmstead","baros westfall","baros childhood"},it="history"},{q="Why is Baros Alexston in Stormwind City Hall?",a="Baros Alexston works from City Hall in Cathedral Square as Stormwind's chief architect. When the Stonemasons Guild rebelled over unpaid wages, Baros refused to join Edwin VanCleef's violent uprising. In exchange for his loyalty and ideological break with the guild, the crown offered him the official position of city architect, where he oversees the kingdom's public works and building projects.",al={"why is baros alexston here","baros alexston city hall why","what is baros doing in stormwind"},it="why_here",add="47ce41c7"},{q="What does Baros Alexston want?",a="Baros seeks to serve the city of Stormwind honorably while confronting the ghosts of his past. On a personal level, he wishes to recover lost family heirlooms, such as his first compass, hidden away before thieves burned down his childhood farm in Westfall. Politically, he is deeply concerned with uncovering treachery in the city and seeing an end to the Defias Brotherhood's violent campaign.",al={"baros alexston motives","what does baros want","baros goals"},it="wants",add="8a4dbaf4"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can see in Baros the painful compromise that split the Stonemasons Guild. Its craftsmen had poured their lives into rebuilding the capital.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue in Stormwind, you have a connection through Baros to Master Mathias Shaw and SI:7, who quietly owe the architect a favor despite his past ties to VanCleef.",["race:Human"]="As a human from Westfall, you may recognize Baros's surname from the ruined Alexston Farmstead, now overrun by thieves and gnolls."},kw={"alexston","architect","baros","cathedral square","city hall","defias","farmstead","stonemasons","unsent letter","vancleef"},rel={"npc:edwin-vancleef","topic:stonemasons-guild","topic:defias-brotherhood","quest:373","quest:399","subzone:alexston-farmstead","npc:mathias-shaw","topic:house-of-nobles"},src={"Baros Alexston"}}
E["npc:bartleby"] = {t="npc",n="Bartleby",z="stormwind",s="Bartleby drinks and picks fights at the Pig and Whistle Tavern in Stormwind's Old Town. His stubborn hold on his ale makes him a test for aspiring warriors who must face him in a tavern brawl.",h="Bartleby drinks and picks fights at the Pig and Whistle Tavern in Stormwind's Old Town.",sec={{t="A Fixture at the Pig and Whistle",b="Bartleby spends his days at the Pig and Whistle Tavern in Stormwind's Old Town. The tavern draws a rougher crowd than the taprooms of Cathedral Square. He clings to his favorite mug, drinks cheap ale, nurses grievances, and picks fights with anyone who disturbs him.",sp=0},{t="A Warrior's Rite of Passage",b="Stormwind's warrior trainers see a practical test in Bartleby. Harry Burlguard sends fledgling fighters to find him and take his mug. They must trade bare-knuckle blows with the intoxicated brawler, proving they have the grit to face an unruly opponent at close quarters.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Bartleby?",a="Bartleby is an unruly patron of the Pig and Whistle Tavern in Stormwind's Old Town. He gets thoroughly intoxicated and refuses to give up his mug without a fistfight.",al={"bartleby lore","who is bartleby","bartleby stormwind"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Bartleby?",a="You can find Bartleby drinking on the ground floor of the Pig and Whistle Tavern in Stormwind's Old Town.",al={"bartleby location","where is bartleby","bartleby pig and whistle"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why do warriors need to fight him?",a="Harry Burlguard, a warrior trainer in Old Town, sends young recruits to Bartleby to test their combat ability. Taking his mug by force shows they can handle a sudden brawl and tough opposition.",al={"why beat bartleby","warrior quest bartleby","bartleby purpose"},it="motive"},{q="What happens when you confront him?",a="When challenged for his mug, Bartleby drinks a potion to bolster his fortitude and turns hostile. He brawls unarmed in the tavern until beaten into submission.",al={"fight bartleby","beat bartleby quest","bartleby brawl"},gp=true},{q="Does Bartleby belong to any faction or organization?",a="Bartleby is a civilian of Stormwind and a habitual drunkard. He has no known ties to the Defias Brotherhood or the city guard.",al={"is bartleby defias","bartleby faction","bartleby alliance"},it="side"},{q="Why won't he just hand over his mug?",a="Bartleby is belligerent, heavily intoxicated, and obstinate. He treats requests for his drink or mug as insults and would rather settle matters with his fists than part with his booze.",al={"bartlebys mug","bartleby ale mug","why fight for mug"},it="wants"},{q="Why is Bartleby here in Old Town?",a="Bartleby spends his days drowning himself in drink at the Pig and Whistle Tavern. He has no grand ambitions or duties in Old Town beyond lingering near the bar, nursing his ale, and guarding his prized mug from anyone bold enough to bother him.",al={"why is bartleby at the pig and whistle","bartleby location why","why is bartleby in stormwind"},it="why_here",add="59ff692a"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a young warrior in Stormwind, you remember your duel with Bartleby. Taking the stubborn drunk's mug makes for a memorable test of hand-to-hand combat.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you see the gritty, working-class side of Stormwind's Old Town, where local disputes are settled over overturned barstools rather than royal decree."},kw={"bartleby","brawl","burlguard","drunk","mug","old town","pig and whistle","tavern","warrior"},rel={"subzone:pig-and-whistle-tavern","quest:1640","quest:1639","quest:1665","subzone:old-town","zone:stormwind","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Bartleby"}}
E["npc:bishop-delavey"] = {t="npc",n="Bishop DeLavey",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind Keep, Bishop DeLavey hears the court's quiet concerns. He represents the Church of the Holy Light in the Petitioner's Chamber, where matters of faith and state meet.",h="In Stormwind Keep, Bishop DeLavey hears the court's quiet concerns.",sec={{t="A Bishop at Court",b="Bishop DeLavey advises Stormwind's court from within the keep. While Archbishop Benedictus tends to the Cathedral of Light, DeLavey lives among the nobility and petitioners. He brings spiritual counsel to the court while reckoning with the kingdom's politics. His place there lets him hear whispered rumors and delicate grievances before they reach Highlord Bolvar Fordragon or the young King Anduin.",sp=0},{t="A Delicate Inquiry",b="A missing diplomat has drawn Bishop DeLavey into a secret inquiry. The diplomat was sent to meet Lady Jaina Proudmoore in Theramore but never arrived. To prevent panic, the court keeps the disappearance quiet. Suspecting the Defias Brotherhood, DeLavey goes around the usual guard channels. He uses private contacts and discreet adventurers, including the fisherman Jorgen, to reach hidden informants such as Elling Trias.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where can Bishop DeLavey be found?",a="Bishop DeLavey is in the Petitioner's Chamber inside Stormwind Keep, just off the main entryway where subjects gather to petition the royal court.",al={"delavey location","where is bishop delavey","delavey keep"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is his role in Stormwind Keep?",a="Bishop DeLavey represents the Church of the Holy Light at Stormwind's royal court. He handles church affairs, advises the nobility, and quietly takes up sensitive matters for the kingdom.",al={"delavey job","who is bishop delavey","what does delavey do"},it="purpose"},{q="Why is he investigating the missing diplomat?",a="The diplomat vanished while traveling to meet Lady Jaina Proudmoore in Theramore. Bishop DeLavey suspects Defias interference and investigates through trusted channels to keep the crisis from alarming the public.",al={"missing diplomat delavey","why does delavey care about the diplomat"},it="motive"},{q="How is DeLavey connected to Elling Trias?",a="Bishop DeLavey passes messages through intermediaries, including the fisherman Jorgen, to Elling Trias, a master of cheese who secretly gathers intelligence for SI:7.",al={"delavey and trias","delavey si7 contact"},sp=1,it="ties"},{q="Who is Bishop DeLavey?",a="Bishop DeLavey is a senior human cleric of the Church of the Holy Light stationed within Stormwind Keep. Acting as the Church's official emissary to the royal court, he attends to clerical and administrative affairs among the nobility and regency.",al={"who is delavey","bishop delavey identity","who is bishop delavey"},it="identity",add="9f3cf19d"},{q="Whose side is Bishop DeLavey on?",a="DeLavey is fully loyal to the Church of the Holy Light and the Grand Alliance of Stormwind. He works directly on behalf of the realm's welfare, seeking to protect the crown and quietly untangle threats to the kingdom before panic spreads through the streets.",al={"delavey faction","is bishop delavey alliance","who does bishop delavey serve"},it="side",add="8f5e30a8"},{q="What does Bishop DeLavey want?",a="DeLavey wants to uncover the truth behind the disappearance of a vital Stormwind diplomat dispatched to Theramore. Because news of the disappearance could destabilize the court, he aims to investigate quietly through reliable third parties and back-channel intelligence.",al={"what is delavey trying to do","bishop delavey goals","what does delavey want"},it="wants",add="663bbb38"},{q="Why is Bishop DeLavey in Stormwind Keep?",a="DeLavey resides in the Petitioner's Chamber to represent the Church of the Holy Light before Highlord Bolvar Fordragon and the royal court. From this post, he advises the crown on church affairs and stays close to the kingdom's political maneuvers.",al={"why is delavey in the keep","why is bishop delavey here","delavey petitioners chamber"},it="why_here",add="44aea1e7"}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest, DeLavey shows how closely the Church of the Holy Light is involved in Stormwind's politics, where faith meets statecraft and covert affairs.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can see DeLavey's discreet inquiry at work to protect the fragile peace between Stormwind and Lady Jaina Proudmoore's outpost of Theramore."},kw={"bishop delavey","delavey","elling trias","holy light","jorgen","missing diplomat","petitioner's chamber","stormwind keep"},rel={"quest:1241","subzone:petitioner-s-chamber","subzone:stormwind-keep","npc:elling-trias","npc:jorgen","npc:jaina-proudmoore","topic:defias-brotherhood","topic:church-of-the-holy-light"},src={"Bishop DeLavey"}}
E["npc:bolvar-fordragon"] = {t="npc",n="Bolvar Fordragon",z="stormwind",s="Stormwind’s crown and armies rest with Bolvar Fordragon while King Varian is missing. As Regent and Supreme Commander of Stormwind’s armed forces, he stands beside young King Anduin in Stormwind Keep and tries to hold the kingdom together. Domestic troubles grow, while Lady Katrana Prestor’s counsel often delays his military decisions.",h="Stormwind’s crown and armies rest with Bolvar Fordragon while King Varian is missing.",sec={{t="Regent of the Realm",b="King Varian vanished on the way to a peace summit on Theramore Isle, leaving Stormwind in political disarray. Ten-year-old Prince Anduin was crowned to preserve continuity, while Highlord Bolvar Fordragon took up the work of ruling as Regent. A venerated paladin devoted to the crown, Bolvar now faces a kingdom under strain. Stormwind’s soldiers are spread thin across Westfall, Redridge, and Duskwood. Lady Katrana Prestor’s dismissive counsel adds to the burden, repeatedly blocking him from sending royal troops to towns on the frontier.",sp=0},{t="A Web of Deceit",b="Town magistrates and frontier marshals plead for reinforcements against the Defias Brotherhood and Blackrock orcs, but Lady Prestor quietly shapes royal decrees and belittles every report of danger. Bolvar respects the counsel of the nobility and hesitates to act without undeniable proof. Unwittingly, he leaves the crown unable to act. When compelling evidence arrives, such as warnings from investigators in Theramore or news of missing field officers, the Regent sets aside court custom and turns to independent adventurers.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why is Bolvar ruling instead of King Varian?",a="King Varian Wrynn disappeared under suspicious circumstances while sailing to a diplomatic summit at Theramore Isle. His ten-year-old son Anduin was crowned to preserve political order, while Highlord Bolvar Fordragon became Regent, governing the kingdom and commanding its armies until Varian is found.",al={"where is the king","why is bolvar in charge","who is the regent"},it="why_here"},{q="Why won't Bolvar send soldiers to help Redridge or Westfall?",a="Stormwind’s standing armies are stretched thin guarding its core territories and borders. Lady Katrana Prestor, Bolvar’s chief advisor, repeatedly questions reports from places such as Lakeshire, calls them exaggerations, and counsels against sending royal forces. Without military proof, Bolvar instead deputizes independent adventurers to intervene.",al={"why no stormwind army","why won't bolvar send help","lakeshire troops"},it="motive"},{q="What is Bolvar's relationship with Lady Katrana Prestor?",a="Lady Katrana Prestor is the foremost royal councilor to Stormwind’s throne. Bolvar respects her political judgment and knowledge of noble affairs, yet she continually urges restraint and counsels him to dismiss reports of dragons, orcs, and Defias plots.",al={"bolvar and prestor","who is lady prestor to bolvar"},it="ties"},{q="What is Bolvar's connection to young Prince Anduin?",a="Bolvar is not related to Anduin, but he is the young king’s fierce protector, guardian, and mentor. He stands beside Anduin’s throne in Stormwind Keep, shielding him from court intrigue and keeping the Wrynn dynasty secure until Varian returns.",al={"anduin and bolvar","is bolvar anduin's father"},it="ties"},{q="Who is Highlord Bolvar Fordragon?",a="Highlord Bolvar Fordragon is a venerated paladin and the Regent of Stormwind. As the Supreme Commander of the kingdom's military forces, he governs on behalf of the young King Anduin Wrynn following the suspicious disappearance of King Varian Wrynn. Renowned for his noble spirit and honor, he bears the tremendous weight of maintaining order and defending the realm during one of Stormwind's most vulnerable eras.",al={"who is bolvar","bolvar identity","who is highlord bolvar"},it="identity",add="634d3c0f"},{q="Whose side is Bolvar Fordragon on?",a="Bolvar is utterly dedicated to the Kingdom of Stormwind and the Alliance. His loyalty lies foremost with House Wrynn, fiercely protecting young Prince Anduin and working to safeguard the kingdom's territories despite severe political turmoil and depleted garrisons.",al={"bolvar allegiance","what faction is bolvar","bolvar faction"},it="side",add="946cb7aa"},{q="What does Bolvar Fordragon want?",a="Above all, Bolvar seeks to maintain the stability of Stormwind, discover the fate of the missing King Varian, and protect young Anduin Wrynn from those who would exploit his youth. He strives to address the growing threats of the Defias Brotherhood and the Blackrock orcs, attempting to balance the defense of outlying territories like Redridge and Westfall with the advice of the royal court.",al={"bolvar goals","what is bolvar trying to do","bolvar motive"},it="wants",add="309206e7"},{q="Why is Bolvar Fordragon famous?",a="Bolvar is renowned as a paladin of exceptional determination, valor, and unbreakable moral conviction. As Highlord, Regent and Supreme Commander of Stormwind's forces, his leadership and stalwart honor have made him one of the most respected military minds and paladins in the entire Alliance.",al={"why is bolvar famous","bolvar reputation","is bolvar renowned"},it="fame",add="e6552818"}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, Bolvar embodies the Alliance’s martial ideal: devotion to the Light and unwavering duty to his people, even as political schemes mount.",["faction:Alliance"]="As Supreme Commander of Stormwind, Bolvar leads the human military and balances local rebellions against the Alliance’s wider obligations."},kw={"anduin wrynn","bolvar","fordragon","highlord","katrana prestor","regent","stormwind keep"},rel={"npc:anduin-wrynn","npc:onyxia","zone:stormwind","topic:varian-wrynn","topic:defias-brotherhood","npc:magistrate-solomon","subzone:theramore-isle","npc:jaina-proudmoore"},src={"Bolvar Fordragon"}}
E["npc:brother-joshua"] = {t="npc",n="Brother Joshua",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind, Brother Joshua guides those who come to the Cathedral of Light to learn the ways of the Holy Light. He trains novice priests to heal wounds and strengthen their allies.",h="In Stormwind, Brother Joshua guides those who come to the Cathedral of Light to learn the ways of the Holy...",sec={{t="A Mentor in the Cathedral",b="Brother Joshua waits near the main altar in Stormwind's Cathedral of Light, ready to teach new servants of the faith. A priest of the Church of the Holy Light, he instructs them in healing, protective wards, and the focus needed to commune with the Light. Young human priests beginning their service to the Alliance find one of their first guides in him.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Brother Joshua?",a="Brother Joshua is a human priest and trainer of the Church of the Holy Light. He teaches aspiring priests their spells, rituals, and sacred duties in Stormwind's Cathedral of Light.",al={"who is brother joshua","brother joshua role","joshua priest"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Brother Joshua?",a="Brother Joshua stands near the high altar toward the back of the Cathedral of Light, in Cathedral Square in Stormwind City.",al={"brother joshua location","where is brother joshua","where is joshua"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What services does he offer?",a="Brother Joshua teaches priests new ranks of divine and restorative spells and can reset their spiritual talents.",al={"what does joshua do","brother joshua training","can joshua train me"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Brother Joshua on?",a="Brother Joshua serves the Church of the Holy Light and stands firmly with the Grand Alliance. Devoted to the teachings of the Light, he ministers beneath the arches of Stormwind's Cathedral of Light, lending spiritual guidance and support to his fellow citizens and Alliance travelers alike.",al={"brother joshua allegiance","brother joshua faction","who does brother joshua serve"},it="side",add="cce3d5dc"},{q="What does Brother Joshua want?",a="Brother Joshua seeks to spread the tenets of the Holy Light and guide promising acolytes in their sacred calling. His days are dedicated to training novice priests, deepening their communion with the Light, and ensuring the faithful of Stormwind remain steadfast through troubled times.",al={"brother joshua goal","what is brother joshua trying to do","brother joshua purpose"},it="wants",add="2e9120b0"},{q="Why is Brother Joshua here?",a="Stationed within Stormwind's Cathedral of Light, Brother Joshua carries out his duties near the altar as an ordained instructor of the priesthood. From this seat of spiritual authority, he mentors those called to the cloth and offers aid to visitors seeking the wisdom of the Light.",al={"why is brother joshua in stormwind","why is brother joshua in the cathedral","brother joshua location reason"},it="why_here",add="2e708272"},{q="Who is Brother Joshua tied to?",a="Brother Joshua is tied to the clergy of the Church of the Holy Light and works alongside the priests and paladins staffing the Cathedral of Light. Through his clerical obligations, he also maintains relations with other organizations, such as the Cenarion Circle, when duty calls for mutual aid.",al={"brother joshua connections","brother joshua church","who does brother joshua answer to"},it="ties",add="5cfd3f6a"}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you can study the Holy Light with Brother Joshua in Stormwind and learn new prayers and disciplines as you advance.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can find Joshua in the Cathedral of Light, at the heart of your kingdom."},kw={"brother joshua","cathedral of light","holy light","human priest","priest trainer","stormwind"},rel={"subzone:cathedral-of-light","topic:church-of-the-holy-light","topic:light","topic:stormwind-kingdom","quest:5628"},src={"Brother Joshua"}}
E["npc:brother-kristoff"] = {t="npc",n="Brother Kristoff",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind's Cathedral Square, Brother Kristoff preaches beneath Uther's statue. A human priest of the Church of the Holy Light, he stands outdoors near the great statue of Uther the Lightbringer and seeks practical books for sermons on spiritual strength.",h="In Stormwind's Cathedral Square, Brother Kristoff preaches beneath Uther's statue.",sec={{t="A Preacher by the Statue",b="Brother Kristoff serves the Church of the Holy Light in Cathedral Square, beneath the statue of Uther the Lightbringer. He works among the citizens and pilgrims who pass through the plaza, rather than remaining within the Cathedral of Light. For sermons such as the Fortitude of the Spirit, he turns to worldly comparisons. In The Stresses of Iron, he finds a way to explain how the mortal soul endures pressure, comparing the Holy Light's gift of inner resolve to the tempered strength of worked metal.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Brother Kristoff?",a="Brother Kristoff is a human priest and scholar of the Church of the Holy Light. He works outdoors in Stormwind's Cathedral Square, near the great statue of Uther the Lightbringer.",al={"brother kristoff lore","who is kristoff","kristoff stormwind"},it="identity"},{q="What does Brother Kristoff do in Cathedral Square?",a="Brother Kristoff prepares sermons on the Light and faith. He is working on a sermon about the Fortitude of the Spirit and seeks references in books about metallurgy to explain spiritual resilience.",al={"kristoff purpose","kristoff role","why is brother kristoff standing outside"},it="why_here"},{q="Why does Brother Kristoff need a book about iron?",a="Brother Kristoff seeks The Stresses of Iron for his sermon on fortitude. He uses iron under stress as an earthly comparison for how devotion to the Holy Light strengthens the mortal spirit against adversity.",al={"the stresses of iron","speaking of fortitude book","why does kristoff want metallurgy"},it="wants"},{q="Whose side is Brother Kristoff on?",a="Brother Kristoff serves the Church of the Holy Light and the Alliance. As a brother within the priesthood, his devotion lies with the Holy Light and the spiritual guidance of Stormwind's people, standing faithfully beneath the shadow of the Cathedral of Light.",al={"brother kristoff faction","who does brother kristoff serve","brother kristoff alliance"},it="side",add="610da828"},{q="Who is Brother Kristoff tied to?",a="Brother Kristoff is a member of the clergy of the Church of the Holy Light, based at the Cathedral of Light in Stormwind. He works alongside his fellow priests and paladins in Cathedral Square to tend to the spiritual needs of the kingdom's citizens and defenders.",al={"brother kristoff connections","brother kristoff church","who is brother kristoff affiliated with"},it="ties",add="8237c000"}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you may value Brother Kristoff's grounded approach to the liturgy. He draws on practical arts to teach the deeper mysteries of inner fortitude.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="As a blacksmith, you may find it amusing that a cleric of the Light turns to books about iron stress and metallurgy to teach the clergy about resilience."},kw={"brother kristoff","cathedral of light","cathedral square","fortitude","kristoff","stresses of iron","uther statue"},rel={"subzone:cathedral-square","subzone:cathedral-of-light","topic:church-of-the-holy-light","quest:343","quest:346","topic:light","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Brother Kristoff"}}
E["npc:brother-sarno"] = {t="npc",n="Brother Sarno",z="stormwind",s="At the Cathedral of Light in Stormwind City, Brother Sarno welcomes visitors and worshipers. The human cleric also directs Alliance travelers to Ironforge, where Tinkmaster Overspark needs help reclaiming Gnomeregan.",h="At the Cathedral of Light in Stormwind City, Brother Sarno welcomes visitors and worshipers.",sec={{t="A Welcoming Voice in the Cathedral",b="Inside the Cathedral of Light in Stormwind, Brother Sarno greets pilgrims and travelers at the entrance. A brother of the Church of the Holy Light, he welcomes those who come seeking prayer, comfort, or guidance. His kind manner puts visitors at ease amid the cathedral’s daily life.",sp=0},{t="Ties to Ironforge",b="Brother Sarno also helps the Alliance beyond the cathedral. When word reached him that Tinkmaster Overspark in Ironforge needed help with his rogue invention, Techbot, in Gnomeregan, Sarno directed capable travelers toward Dun Morogh. His help supports the gnomes displaced from their home.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Brother Sarno?",a="Brother Sarno stands just inside the main entrance to the Cathedral of Light in Cathedral Square, Stormwind City, to the left of the doors.",al={"sarno location","where is brother sarno","cathedral greeter"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What does Brother Sarno do?",a="Brother Sarno welcomes visitors and worshipers at the Cathedral of Light. He also directs travelers to Tinkmaster Overspark in Ironforge to help with problems in Gnomeregan.",al={"brother sarno role","what does sarno do"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does a Stormwind priest send people to Gnomeregan?",a="Word reached the clergy that Tinkmaster Overspark needed help reclaiming rogue technology such as Techbot. Brother Sarno directed capable champions toward Ironforge to assist.",al={"sarno gnomeregan quest","why does sarno care about gnomes"},it="motive"},{q="Does he belong to any specific order?",a="Brother Sarno is an ordained member of the Church of the Holy Light. He serves beneath the cathedral’s prelates and Archbishop Benedictus in Stormwind.",al={"sarno faction","brother sarno order"},it="ties"},{q="Who is Brother Sarno?",a="Brother Sarno is a human priest of the Church of the Holy Light stationed inside the grand Cathedral of Light in Stormwind City. Positioned just inside the main entrance to the left, he serves as a friendly face to greet visitors and pilgrims entering the sanctuary.",al={"who is brother sarno","brother sarno identity","who is sarno"},it="identity",add="61335d44"},{q="Whose side is Brother Sarno on?",a="Brother Sarno is a devout servant of the Church of the Holy Light and a loyal member of the Grand Alliance. He supports the citizens of Stormwind and maintains close, cooperative ties with the Alliance's allies, including the gnomes and dwarves of Khaz Modan.",al={"brother sarno faction","brother sarno allegiance","who does brother sarno serve"},it="side",add="52c947c9"},{q="What does Brother Sarno want?",a="Beyond welcoming worshippers into the Cathedral of Light, Brother Sarno looks out for capable Alliance adventurers. He directs helpful travelers toward Ironforge to assist Tinkmaster Overspark with a troublesome mechanical creation named Techbot deep within the fallen city of Gnomeregan.",al={"what does brother sarno want","brother sarno goals","brother sarno motive"},it="wants",add="3cc89cc1"},{q="Why is Brother Sarno in the Cathedral?",a="Brother Sarno stands near the front entrance of the Cathedral of Light to welcome worshippers, pilgrims, and weary travelers seeking solace. From this post, he also keeps an ear open for distant troubles and connects visiting champions with allies in need.",al={"why is brother sarno here","why is sarno in cathedral","brother sarno location why"},it="why_here",add="222a0285"}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you can see Brother Sarno welcoming visitors in Stormwind, showing the hospitality and gentle grace of the Holy Light.",["race:Gnome"]="Though Brother Sarno serves in a human house of worship, he directs willing travelers toward Ironforge to help Gnomeregan recover."},kw={"brother sarno","cathedral of light","church of the holy light","stormwind","techbot","tinkmaster overspark"},rel={"subzone:cathedral-of-light","quest:2923","zone:stormwind","topic:church-of-the-holy-light","zone:ironforge","zone:gnomeregan","topic:light"},src={"Brother Sarno"}}
E["npc:caretaker-folsom"] = {t="npc",n="Caretaker Folsom",z="stormwind",s="Along Stormwind’s Canals near the Park, Caretaker Folsom tends the remains of a noble household. He once oversaw the Flintridge estate; now he sells what survived its bloody end.",h="Along Stormwind’s Canals near the Park, Caretaker Folsom tends the remains of a noble household.",sec={{t="A House in Ruins",b="Folsom followed his father into a life of service as caretaker of the Flintridge estate. That life ended with the massacre of the household. The manor stood abandoned, and its remaining funds eventually ran out. Left to watch over what remained, Folsom now sends the family's surviving heirlooms and possessions to auction.",sp=0},{t="Ties to a Dark Tale",b="Investigators following the bloody history of Stalvan Mistmantle are often sent to Folsom along Stormwind's canal walkways. Grief weighs on him, and he is reluctant to speak. He holds surviving Flintridge possessions and documents that reveal Stalvan's disturbing descent and his eventual disappearance into the shadows of Duskwood.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Caretaker Folsom?",a="Caretaker Folsom serves in Stormwind City and once tended the Flintridge family estate. After the massacre that killed the entire family, he was left in charge of their remaining property.",al={"folsom","who is folsom","caretaker folsom lore"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Caretaker Folsom?",a="You can find Caretaker Folsom along the Canals' stone walkways in Stormwind City, near the entrance to the Park.",al={"where is caretaker folsom","folsom location","caretaker folsom stormwind"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happened to the Flintridge family?",a="The Flintridge family was massacred at their estate years ago. With no heirs left to claim it, the manor was shuttered and its funds eventually ran out.",al={"flintridge murder","what happened to flintridge","who killed the flintridges"},sp=1,it="history"},{q="Why is Folsom selling off family heirlooms?",a="The Flintridge family's remaining funds eventually ran dry. Folsom now sends what remains of the estate's possessions to auction.",al={"why auction","flintridge auction","folsom auction"},it="wants"},{q="What is his role in The Legend of Stalvan?",a="Folsom helps those piecing together Stalvan Mistmantle's tragedy by sharing the surviving personal effects and clues from the Flintridge manor.",al={"stalvan quest folsom","the legend of stalvan folsom"},it="purpose"},{q="Whose side is Caretaker Folsom on?",a="Caretaker Folsom is a loyal subject of Stormwind and a devoted servant of the tragic Flintridge family. He holds no malice or hidden political allegiances, spending his days by the city canals merely striving to honor the memory and final affairs of the household he and his father faithfully served.",al={"caretaker folsom faction","who does folsom serve","folsom allegiance"},it="side",add="2b9b56eb"},{q="Why is Caretaker Folsom here?",a="You find Caretaker Folsom beside the canals in Stormwind because the Flintridge household's funds have entirely dried up. Forced to settle the estate after the family's violent demise, he remains in the capital overseeing the grim process of inventorying and auctioning off their surviving family heirlooms.",al={"why is folsom in stormwind","why is caretaker folsom here","what brought folsom here"},it="why_here",add="bbc99921"},{q="Who is Caretaker Folsom tied to?",a="Folsom is bound by blood and service to the noble Flintridge estate. His father held the post of caretaker before him, and Folsom devoted his life to maintaining their household until Stalvan Mistmantle brought ruin and slaughter upon the entire family.",al={"folsom connections","who is folsom connected to","caretaker folsom flintridge"},sp=1,it="ties",add="8f9af06f"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance investigator tracking Duskwood's most infamous murderer, you can turn to Folsom for a living link to the Flintridge household's final days."},kw={"canals","caretaker folsom","flintridge","folsom","mistmantle","park","stalvan","stormwind"},rel={"quest:66","subzone:canals-stormwind-city","subzone:park","zone:duskwood","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Caretaker Folsom"}}
E["npc:collin-mauren"] = {t="npc",n="Collin Mauren",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind's Mage Quarter, Collin Mauren studies practical magic and crafts useful spells from natural reagents. He also makes arcane scrolls for his friend Gaxim Rustfizzle, a gnome engineer and explorer.",h="In Stormwind's Mage Quarter, Collin Mauren studies practical magic and crafts useful spells from natural...",sec={{t="Scholar of the Arcane",b="In Stormwind's Mage Quarter, Collin Mauren studies magic's practical uses. He crafts arcane formulas to solve specific problems, drawing on natural anomalies and raw components gathered across Azeroth. Their properties help him make functional scrolls and reagents for friends and travelers.",sp=0},{t="Aiding Gaxim Rustfizzle",b="Collin Mauren is helping his friend Gaxim Rustfizzle set off NG-5 explosives from a distance. Gaxim, a gnome tinkerer, needed a way to trigger them remotely, so Collin devised a messaging spell for a scroll. To impress the spell on it, Collin uses debris from Westfall's erratic Dust Devils. He awaits word on how Gaxim's scheme fares.",sp=0},{t="Exotic Studies in Stonetalon",b="Collin Mauren's studies reach from Stormwind across the Great Sea to Kalimdor's Stonetalon Mountains. He seeks the scales of the region's basilisks, whose resilient hides interest him as materials for synthesizing new spells. Travelers heading into Kalimdor often receive his requests for these rare hides. The scales fuel his study of how primal creature anatomy can steady complex enchantments.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can Collin Mauren be found?",a="Collin Mauren can be found in Stormwind City's Mage Quarter, among the towers and shops used by the capital's arcane scholars.",al={"collin mauren location","where is collin mauren","collin mauren stormwind"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What kind of magic does Collin specialize in?",a="Collin specializes in applied enchantments and utility spells. He experiments with natural components such as elemental debris and beast scales to craft scrolls, including a messaging spell for Gaxim's remote explosives, as well as other unique dweomers.",al={"collin mauren research","what does collin mauren do","collin mauren magic"},it="power"},{q="Who is Gaxim Rustfizzle and how is Collin connected to him?",a="Gaxim Rustfizzle is an adventurous gnome tinkerer and Collin's friend. When Gaxim needed to detonate his explosives from afar, Collin made him a scroll bearing a messaging spell.",al={"gaxim rustfizzle friend","collin and gaxim","who is gaxim rustfizzle"},it="ties"},{q="Why does Collin need elemental debris from Westfall?",a="Collin needs debris from one of Westfall's Dust Devils to impress a messaging spell onto a scroll. Gaxim Rustfizzle needs the spell to set off his NG-5 explosives from a distance.",al={"devils in westfall quest","why dust devils","westfall dust devils quest"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why is Collin interested in the Stonetalon Mountains?",a="Collin studies basilisk scales from the Stonetalon Mountains in Kalimdor for their magical properties. He uses their sturdy, naturally resistant hides as bases for synthesizing new incantations.",al={"stonetalon basilisks","retrieval for mauren","stonetalon scales collin"},it="motive"},{q="Is Collin aligned with the Kirin Tor?",a="Collin lives in the Mage Quarter and practices traditions common among Alliance wizards. He works chiefly as an independent researcher and reagent crafter, rather than as an active Dalaran representative.",al={"is collin kirin tor","collin mauren dalaran","mage quarter collin"},it="side"},{q="Who is Collin Mauren?",a="Collin Mauren is a human mage residing in the Mage Quarter of Stormwind City. A scholarly researcher and crafter of incantations, he experiments with arcane formulae and enchanting parchment, utilizing rare components from distant lands to fashion magical scrolls for his peers and traveling adventurers.",al={"who is collin","collin mauren lore","who is mauren"},it="identity",add="f243f9d9"},{q="Why is Collin Mauren in Stormwind?",a="Collin makes his home in Stormwind's Mage Quarter, surrounded by the city's libraries, academies, and fellow practitioners of the arcane. From this bustling haven, he can conduct his experiments in peace while securing exotic reagents brought in by adventurers passing through the capital.",al={"why is collin here","why is collin mauren in stormwind","what is collin doing in stormwind"},it="why_here",add="b186ecef"},{q="What does Collin Mauren want?",a="Collin seeks uncommon mystical reagents to perfect his spellcraft. Whether procuring elemental debris from Westfall's dust devils to craft specialized messaging scrolls for his friend Gaxim Rustfizzle, or acquiring basilisk scales from the Stonetalon Mountains, he is driven by arcane curiosity and the demands of curious travelers.",al={"collin mauren motive","what does collin want","what is collin looking for"},it="wants",add="8e195ded"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a Mage, you can see Collin's experimental approach to spellcraft: he uses reagents such as elemental debris and basilisk scales to weave utility magic.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you share a city with Collin, whose quiet studies in Stormwind's Mage Quarter reflect the scholarly pursuits of human wizards.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can see how Collin supplies adventurers with utility magic for communication and trade across the faction, from Westfall to Kalimdor."},kw={"basilisk","collin mauren","dust devils","gaxim rustfizzle","mage quarter","stonetalon","stormwind","westfall"},rel={"npc:gaxim-rustfizzle","subzone:mage-quarter","zone:stormwind","quest:1076","quest:1077","quest:1078","quest:1075","zone:westfall"},src={"Collin Mauren"}}
E["npc:count-remington-ridgewell"] = {t="npc",n="Count Remington Ridgewell",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind Keep, Count Remington Ridgewell tends a collection fit for a noble’s pride. A wealthy human in the House of Nobles, he gathers rare artifacts, heirlooms, and fine art.",h="In Stormwind Keep, Count Remington Ridgewell tends a collection fit for a noble’s pride.",sec={{t="A Connoisseur of Antiquities",b="Count Remington Ridgewell favors antiquities over military campaigns or local uprisings. His family’s personal museum holds jewelry and artifacts, and he spends his wealth gathering relics from fallen civilizations and houses across Azeroth. To fill his gallery, he finances adventurers and sends field agents such as Mayara Brightwing to retrieve rare objects from dangerous ruins, from Alterac’s mountain redoubts to the volcanic wastes of the Burning Steppes.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Count Remington Ridgewell?",a="Count Remington Ridgewell is a human noble and antiquities collector in Stormwind Keep’s Petitioner's Chamber. He spends his family fortune on relics, jewels, and art from across the world.",al={"who is remington ridgewell","remington ridgewell","count ridgewell"},it="identity"},{q="What artifacts does Count Ridgewell seek?",a="Ridgewell seeks lost heirlooms for his museum. Among them are the Perenolde Tiara from Alterac’s ruins and historical Dark Iron dwarf treasures from the Ruins of Thaurissan.",al={"ridgewell quests","perenolde tiara quest","what does he want"},it="wants"},{q="Who is Mayara Brightwing?",a="Mayara Brightwing is an agent employed by Count Ridgewell. He sent her to the Burning Steppes to scout for antiquities in the ancient Ruins of Thaurissan.",al={"mayara brightwing connection","who is mayara"},it="ties"},{q="Where can Count Remington Ridgewell be found?",a="Count Remington Ridgewell can be found in the Petitioner's Chamber inside Stormwind Keep, among nobles and dignitaries seeking an audience with the royal court.",al={"where is count ridgewell","ridgewell location","petitioner's chamber noble"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Count Remington Ridgewell on?",a="Count Ridgewell is a loyal noble of the Kingdom of Stormwind and a member of the House of Nobles. He stands firmly with the Alliance, conducting his high-society patronage and private affairs right from the Royal Keep.",al={"count ridgewell faction","ridgewell loyalty","who does ridgewell serve"},it="side",add="7bd2f97e"},{q="Why is Count Remington Ridgewell in Stormwind Keep?",a="As an influential aristocrat and member of the House of Nobles, Count Ridgewell attends court in the Petitioner's Chamber of Stormwind Keep. From here, he maintains his family's prestige, conducts courtly business, and hires daring adventurers to recover precious relics across Azeroth.",al={"why is ridgewell here","why is count ridgewell in stormwind keep","ridgewell petitioners chamber"},it="why_here",add="ecd2a567"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance mercenary, you may find Count Ridgewell a lucrative patron; he pays well for relics recovered from fallen northern kingdoms and lost dwarven cities.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you can see how Stormwind’s House of Nobles prizes cultural standing and art collecting, even amid the kingdom’s political instability."},kw={"house of nobles","mayara brightwing","museum","perenolde tiara","petitioner's chamber","remington ridgewell","ridgewell","stormwind keep"},rel={"subzone:petitioner-s-chamber","subzone:stormwind-keep","quest:543","topic:house-of-nobles","topic:alterac-kingdom","subzone:ruins-of-thaurissan","subzone:ruins-of-alterac","zone:burningsteppes"},src={"Count Remington Ridgewell"}}
E["npc:dashel-stonefist"] = {t="npc",n="Dashel Stonefist",z="stormwind",s="In Old Town, Dashel Stonefist is known for his quick temper and heavy hands. The dwarf called Fist keeps to Stormwind City's rougher alleys, where dangerous connections draw the attention of covert investigators.",h="In Old Town, Dashel Stonefist is known for his quick temper and heavy hands.",sec={{t="A Brawler in Old Town",b="In Old Town, Dashel Stonefist is known as Fist for the street fights that have earned him the name. Locals and city guards see a drunken, combative dwarf ready to throw a punch outside a tavern. His place in the district puts him at the nexus of Stormwind's underworld, where smugglers, cutpurses, and political agitators trade coin and rumors beyond the eyes of Cathedral Square.",sp=0},{t="The Diplomat's Disappearance",b="A missing diplomat draws covert royal investigators to Dashel Stonefist. Whispers of treachery lead them to the dwarf, a street-level contact for the Defias Brotherhood within Stormwind's walls. He knows about the abduction, but refuses to speak until investigators beat him into submission. What he reveals reaches deeper into the kingdom's politics than a simple kidnapping.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Dashel Stonefist?",a="In Stormwind City's Old Town, Dashel Stonefist is a low-level cutthroat and informant in the capital's shadowy quarters. The dwarf known as Fist has a violent reputation and a habit of brawling.",al={"who is dashel","who is fist","dashel stonefist lore"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Dashel Stonefist?",a="You can find Dashel Stonefist standing outside in Old Town, among its back alleys near the city's rogue and warrior haunts.",al={"dashel location","where is dashel stonefist","find dashel"},gp=true},{q="Why do investigators need to fight him?",a="Investigators fight Dashel Stonefist because leads in the search for the missing royal diplomat point to him as a collaborator. Fiercely loyal to his shady employers, he respects only force and will not reveal what he knows until beaten in a bare-knuckle brawl.",al={"why attack dashel","subdue dashel stonefist","fight dashel"},sp=1},{q="What is his connection to the Defias Brotherhood?",a="Dashel Stonefist is an inside operative and messenger for the Defias Brotherhood in Stormwind. He coordinates local contacts and street muscle to conceal the Brotherhood's plans from the City Guard.",al={"is dashel defias","dashel stonefist defias","defias in stormwind"},sp=1,it="ties"},{q="Who is the missing diplomat connected to Dashel?",a="Royal agents pursue the story of an unnamed diplomat who vanished en route to Theramore.",al={"who is the missing diplomat","missing diplomat questline","king varian missing"},sp=2},{q="Is Dashel related to any other known dwarves?",a="No relatives of Dashel Stonefist are recorded. His criminal ties in Stormwind set him apart from reputable dwarven society.",al={"telda stonefist relative","dashel stonefist family","stonefist family"}},{q="Whose side is Dashel Stonefist on?",a="Dashel Stonefist walks a dangerous line between Old Town's criminal underbelly and open treason. While he masquerades as just another roughneck brawler in the city alleys, his clandestine allegiances lie with the Defias Brotherhood, passing information and helping coordinate their subversive activities right under the Stormwind City Guard's noses.",al={"dashel stonefist faction","who does dashel work for","is dashel defias"},sp=1,it="side",add="06e53778"},{q="Why is Dashel Stonefist in Old Town?",a="Dashel lingers in Old Town because its crowded, shadowed streets provide the ideal cover for illicit business. Far from the polished oversight of Cathedral Square or the royal court, Old Town allows him to maintain contact with shadowy conspirators, orchestrate back-alley deals, and keep tabs on city movements without drawing premature attention from the authorities.",al={"why is dashel in stormwind","dashel stonefist location why","what is dashel doing in old town"},it="why_here",add="388c2391"},{q="Why is Dashel Stonefist known as Fist?",a="Locals and thugs throughout Old Town know Dashel simply as 'Fist,' an earned moniker rooted in his notorious temper and eagerness to settle any dispute with raw violence. He has a fearsome reputation for brutal back-alley brawling, making most citizens and pickpockets think twice before crossing him or poking into his affairs.",al={"why is dashel called fist","dashel stonefist nickname","dashel reputation"},it="fame",add="329088a4"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="For rogues moving through Old Town's criminal web, Dashel Stonefist shows how an operative can talk too much once his jaw is rattled. Trusting brute muscle with delicate secrets is a poor wager.",["race:Dwarf"]="Many Ironforge dwarves in Stormwind work as honored smiths, mountaineers, or emissaries. Stonefist shows that a dwarf can also fall into street-corner thuggery and treason.",["faction:Alliance"]="Dashel Stonefist represents the quiet rot inside Stormwind's capital. The Defias Brotherhood's reach stretches past Westfall's farms and into the sovereign city."},kw={"brawler","dashel","defias","fist","missing diplomat","old town","stonefist","stormwind"},rel={"quest:1241","subzone:old-town","zone:stormwind","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:dwarf"},src={"Dashel Stonefist"}}
E["npc:demisette-cloyce"] = {t="npc",n="Demisette Cloyce",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind's Mage Quarter, Demisette Cloyce teaches warlocks beneath the Slaughtered Lamb. She guides students in fel magic and sends those ready for more toward other summoners.",h="In Stormwind's Mage Quarter, Demisette Cloyce teaches warlocks beneath the Slaughtered Lamb.",sec={{t="The Crypts of the Slaughtered Lamb",b="Warlocks gather in the cellar beneath the Slaughtered Lamb in Stormwind's Mage Quarter, while the city's authorities uphold order and the Holy Light. Demisette Cloyce lives in the catacombs below, teaching those willing to study forbidden arts. She warns that dark energies corrupt only those without the discipline to master them.",sp=0},{t="Connecting the Covens",b="Demisette guides warlocks beyond Stormwind when they have gained enough mastery. She connects them with summoners such as Menara Voidrender in the Barrens, where they can seek potent artifacts and learn to bind formidable fel steeds.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Demisette Cloyce?",a="Demisette Cloyce trains warlocks beneath the Slaughtered Lamb in Stormwind's Mage Quarter. She teaches demonic summoning and dark spells.",al={"who is demisette","demisette cloyce lore","who is demisette cloyce"},it="identity"},{q="Why is she hiding in a tavern cellar?",a="Warlocks gather in the cellar beneath the Slaughtered Lamb, away from public view. Its cellar offers a discreet place for their dark practices.",al={"why is she in the cellar","why slaughtered lamb","slaughtered lamb basement"},it="why_here"},{q="What is her connection to the Barrens?",a="Demisette sends experienced warlocks across the sea to Menara Voidrender in Ratchet, on the coast of the Barrens. They seek advanced rituals, powerful orbs, and binding rites.",al={"demisette barrens","in search of menara voidrender","menara voidrender connection"},it="ties"},{q="How does she react to non-warlocks?",a="Demisette has contempt for outsiders. Unless you follow the path of a warlock, she warns that darkness does not embrace you and orders you to stop talking and leave.",al={"demisette dialogue","talking to demisette"}},{q="Whose side is Demisette Cloyce on?",a="Demisette Cloyce is aligned with the Alliance and resides safely within Stormwind City. While she operates hidden in the catacombs beneath the Slaughtered Lamb alongside fellow warlocks, her loyalties lie with instructing and empowering practitioners loyal to Stormwind rather than enemy cults or the Burning Blade.",al={"demisette cloyce faction","is demisette cloyce alliance","who does demisette serve"},it="side",add="9bf7bbcc"},{q="What does Demisette Cloyce want?",a="Demisette seeks to guide promising warlocks in mastering dangerous fel magic without succumbing to corruption. She directs practitioners to ancient artifacts and powerful mentors across the world—even reaching toward Kalimdor—believing that only strong-willed disciples can harness dark sorcery effectively without meeting an untimely, ruinous end.",al={"demisette cloyce motive","demisette cloyce goal","what does demisette want"},it="wants",add="5142027a"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock in Stormwind, you can learn fundamental spellcraft from Demisette. She later points you toward claiming a felsteed and binding demonic orbs.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you can find Demisette beneath Stormwind, where she has turned from the Holy Light to demonic power."},kw={"cloyce","demisette","mage quarter","menara voidrender","slaughtered lamb","stormwind","warlock trainer"},rel={"subzone:slaughtered-lamb","subzone:mage-quarter","npc:menara-voidrender","quest:4736","zone:stormwind","zone:barrens"},src={"Demisette Cloyce"}}
E["npc:donyal-tovald"] = {t="npc",n="Donyal Tovald",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind Keep, Donyal Tovald tends the Royal Library’s historical works. Under an initiative sponsored by young King Anduin Wrynn, he preserves and copies books for wider public use.",h="In Stormwind Keep, Donyal Tovald tends the Royal Library’s historical works.",sec={{t="Steward of Stormwind's History",b="Donyal Tovald tends the Royal Library’s collection in Stormwind Keep. The library holds historical accounts, scrolls, and scholarly volumes, chiefly for the nobility and royal court. Young King Anduin Wrynn has sponsored an effort to make that knowledge more accessible to ordinary citizens. Tovald preserves and copies the texts, helping keep the Alliance’s lessons and triumphs recorded amid the kingdom’s political troubles.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Donyal Tovald?",a="Donyal Tovald is a human librarian in Stormwind Keep’s Royal Library. He tends the kingdom’s archives and oversees King Anduin Wrynn’s effort to share copies of historical books with the public.",al={"who is tovald","royal librarian","donyal tovald lore"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Donyal Tovald?",a="You can find Donyal Tovald in the Royal Library wing on the eastern side of Stormwind Keep, among bookshelves and historical scrolls.",al={"donyal tovald location","where is tovald","how to find tovald"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is he handing out books to citizens?",a="Young King Anduin Wrynn sponsored a royal project to share knowledge with the public. Donyal Tovald oversees the copying and distribution of royal manuscripts.",al={"anduin book initiative","stormwind library project","why does he give books"},it="motive"},{q="Is he affiliated with the House of Nobles or the clergy?",a="Tovald works directly under the crown as a keeper of royal archives in Stormwind Keep. He focuses on historical and scholarly texts rather than ecclesiastical or political doctrine.",al={"is tovald church of light","tovald faction"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Donyal Tovald on?",a="Tovald is a loyal servant of the Kingdom of Stormwind and the Alliance. Stationed within Stormwind Keep itself, he answers to the royal administration and directly supports the educational efforts championed by the young King Anduin Wrynn.",al={"donyal tovald allegiance","donyal tovald faction","who does donyal serve"},it="side",add="18ed48d6"},{q="What does Donyal Tovald want?",a="Tovald wants to preserve the kingdom's history and foster literacy among its people. He tends the archives within the Royal Library and works to place educational copies into the hands of ordinary citizens across Stormwind.",al={"donyal tovald goal","what is donyal trying to do","donyal tovald purpose"},it="wants",add="6c9214b5"},{q="Why is Donyal Tovald here in the Royal Library?",a="Tovald is stationed in Stormwind Keep's Royal Library wing to serve as one of its stewards. From this post, he safeguards the realm's accumulated knowledge and manages the distribution of texts authorized by the crown.",al={"why is donyal tovald in stormwind keep","donyal tovald library duties","why is donyal here"},it="why_here",add="715728b5"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human of Stormwind, you see Tovald’s work as part of preserving and rebuilding your culture and recorded history after the First War and the capital’s reconstruction.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage visiting Stormwind Keep, you may value Tovald’s care for written knowledge, though these texts are mainly historical rather than arcane."},kw={"anduin wrynn","books","donyal tovald","history","librarian","royal library","stormwind keep"},rel={"subzone:royal-library","subzone:stormwind-keep","quest:579","zone:stormwind","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Donyal Tovald"}}
E["npc:duthorian-rall"] = {t="npc",n="Duthorian Rall",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind's Cathedral of Light, Duthorian Rall guides new holy warriors through their trials. The respected human knight of the Silver Hand is one of the Alliance's most influential paladins, overseeing their training and spiritual tests. He teaches charity, valor, and devotion as they prepare to defend Azeroth from the Scourge and threats within the kingdom.",h="In Stormwind's Cathedral of Light, Duthorian Rall guides new holy warriors through their trials.",sec={{t="A Pillar of the Silver Hand",b="In the Cathedral of Light, Duthorian Rall upholds the traditions of the Knights of the Silver Hand. The kingdom is unsettled by internal strife, and King Varian Wrynn is missing. Duthorian carries the duty of teaching discipline to new initiates. Respected paladins in the field send promising recruits to him: Brother Wilhelm in Goldshire and Brandur Ironhammer in Ironforge, so they can begin their sacred trials.",sp=0},{t="Trials of Compassion and Life",b="Duthorian teaches that martial power without a moral foundation is hollow. In the Tome of Divinity trials, he tests an initiate's empathy through acts of mercy and selfless service across Stormwind. Only after these tests does he entrust candidates with deeper mysteries. Near Heroes' Vigil, he tests them with the Symbol of Life, then sends them to aid wounded allies and learn to channel the Light's power to restore fallen comrades from death.",sp=0},{t="The Price of Valor",b="Duthorian's trials of valor demand courage in the face of peril. He warns aspirants that their vows may cost them their lives. To test their resolve, he sends initiates into danger, including to defend Daphne Stilwell from Defias renegades in Westfall. He then directs them to master smith Jordan Stilwell outside Ironforge and grants them holy steeds worthy of their station.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Duthorian Rall?",a="Duthorian Rall is a prominent knight of the Silver Hand who resides in Stormwind City's Cathedral of Light. He instructs and guides new paladins, testing their devotion and courage in service to the Church of the Holy Light.",al={"duthorian rall lore","who is duthorian","cathedral paladin duthorian"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Duthorian Rall be found?",a="Duthorian Rall can be found in the eastern wing of the Cathedral of Light, at the heart of Stormwind City's Cathedral Square.",al={"where is duthorian rall","duthorian rall location","how to find duthorian"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is his connection to the Tome of Divinity?",a="Duthorian gives paladins the Book of Divinity and guides them through trials of humility, compassion, and rescue. Completing the trials proves an initiate worthy to wield the Light's power to resurrect the dead.",al={"tome of divinity duthorian","redemption quest duthorian","symbol of life quest"}},{q="Why does Duthorian send paladins to Westfall?",a="Duthorian sends paladins to protect Daphne Stilwell from Defias bandits on her farm in Westfall during the Tome of Valor trial. The danger tests their willingness to sacrifice themselves to defend the innocent.",al={"daphne stilwell quest","tome of valor westfall","westfall paladin quest"},it="target"},{q="What rewards does Duthorian grant to paladins who pass his trials?",a="Through Duthorian's guidance, successful paladins earn key holy capabilities, including the sacred gift of resurrection, the ability to sense undead, protective armaments such as the Bastion of Stormwind, and eventually a summoned warhorse.",al={"duthorian quest rewards","what do you get from duthorian"},gp=true},{q="Who sends adventurers to Duthorian initially?",a="Paladin trainers, including Brother Wilhelm in Goldshire and Brandur Ironhammer in Ironforge, typically direct aspirants to Duthorian.",al={"who sends you to duthorian","duthorian breadcrumb quest"},it="arrival",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Duthorian Rall on?",a="Duthorian Rall is staunchly devoted to the Grand Alliance, the kingdom of Stormwind, and the Knights of the Silver Hand. Operating within the Cathedral of Light, he serves the Holy Light and works alongside the kingdom's leadership and priesthood to train paladins dedicated to protecting Azeroth from perils like the Scourge and Defias Brotherhood.",al={"duthorian rall faction","who does duthorian serve","is duthorian rall alliance"},it="side",add="adc9c2ec"},{q="What does Duthorian Rall want?",a="Duthorian seeks to test, temper, and guide aspiring paladins so they embody true virtue, compassion, and valor. Through trials of charity, penance, and martial duty, he ensures new holy warriors are prepared to wield the Light's greatest gifts—such as resurrection—to defend the realm against growing threats.",al={"what is duthorian rall goal","what does duthorian want","duthorian rall motives"},it="wants",add="5fa6dad6"},{q="Why is Duthorian Rall here?",a="Stationed within Stormwind's Cathedral of Light, Duthorian serves as a chief mentor for the Silver Hand in the southern kingdoms. Instructors across the realm direct promising initiates to him so he can oversee their spiritual devotion, test their resolve in the field, and officially induct them into higher ranks.",al={"why is duthorian in stormwind","duthorian rall role cathedral","why is duthorian rall here"},it="why_here",add="091b91cc"},{q="Who is Duthorian Rall tied to?",a="Duthorian works closely with regional mentors like Brother Wilhelm in Goldshire and Brandur Ironhammer in Ironforge, who refer prospective paladins to him. He also maintains close ties with friends in need across Elwynn, such as Gazin Tenorm, and coordinates with allies like the Stilwells in Westfall.",al={"duthorian rall allies","duthorian rall connections","who does duthorian know"},it="ties",add="6e7325c8"},{q="Why is Duthorian Rall famous?",a="Duthorian is renowned as one of the most influential paladins of the Alliance. Within the Silver Hand, he commands deep respect for his unwavering piety, his role in molding the next generation of holy champions, and his authority to bestow great sacred honors upon worthy knights.",al={"is duthorian rall famous","duthorian rall reputation","how well known is duthorian rall"},it="fame",add="46aa8798"}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you receive Duthorian Rall's guidance in Stormwind. His foundational trials test your compassion and valor, unlocking resurrection, divine senses, and your warhorse.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance defender, you rely on Duthorian, an influential Silver Hand leader, to keep the Alliance's defenders morally upright and able to defend the realm against bandits and undead.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you find Duthorian anchored in Stormwind's Cathedral of Light, where he represents the devotion and chivalric discipline central to human faith and society."},kw={"cathedral of light","daphne stilwell","duthorian rall","jordan stilwell","paladin trainer","silver hand","stormwind","symbol of life","tome of divinity","tome of valor"},rel={"subzone:cathedral-of-light","quest:1641","quest:1649","quest:1653","npc:brother-wilhelm","npc:brandur-ironhammer","npc:daphne-stilwell","npc:jordan-stilwell"},src={"Duthorian Rall"}}
E["npc:elling-trias"] = {t="npc",n="Elling Trias",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind's Trade District, Elling Trias runs a cheese shop with his family. He welcomes customers with easy talk, while his quiet work as an information broker reaches across continents.",h="In Stormwind's Trade District, Elling Trias runs a cheese shop with his family.",sec={{t="The Master Cheesemonger",b="Elling Trias sells fine cheese in the Trade District, working beside his wife Elaine and son Ben. He cheerfully offers wheels of cheese and chats with the townsfolk. To those who know better, Trias' Cheese is one of Stormwind's most reliable fronts. The city's steady trade gives operatives, courtiers and adventurers a place to exchange quiet words beyond the city watch's notice.",sp=0},{t="A Web of Whispers",b="Elling Trias has informants and allies far beyond what most shopkeepers can claim. He keeps ties with Master Mathias Shaw of SI:7, works with Church contacts such as Bishop DeLavey, and corresponds with agents in Darkshire, Theramore Isle and the distant Plaguelands near Hearthglen. When rumors surface about highway bandits or quiet movements in the countryside, Trias often pieces them together before the royal court takes notice.",sp=0},{t="The Missing Diplomat",b="Elling Trias helps investigators untangle the disappearance of a high-ranking diplomat during a voyage to Theramore. He points them toward his contacts, including an estranged operative named Jorgen and an old friend, Tyrion. Their trail exposes the Defias Brotherhood's part in the abduction. Beneath his sharp wit and cynical banter, Elling sees that the plot reaches deep into Stormwind's aristocracy.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Elling Trias?",a="Elling Trias runs a cheese shop in Stormwind's Trade District with his family. He also works as an experienced information broker, with ties to SI:7, the Church and distant outposts across Azeroth.",al={"who is elling","elling trias identity","trias cheese guy"},it="identity"},{q="Where is his cheese shop located?",a="Trias' Cheese is in Stormwind City's Trade District, along the outer canal wall near the border with Old Town.",al={"trias cheese location","where is elling trias","trias shop stormwind"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is his connection to the Defias Brotherhood?",a="Elling Trias is not a member of the Defias Brotherhood. He tracks their movements through his informant network and helps Alliance adventurers trace their part in plots, including the kidnapping of a royal diplomat.",al={"trias defias","is trias in the defias"},sp=1,it="conflict"},{q="How does he know Mathias Shaw?",a="Mathias Shaw has known Elling Trias for years and turns to him when official channels fail. Shaw hates asking, and Elling grumbles when his work helps Shaw and SI:7. The shop offers a place to make discreet inquiries outside royal channels.",al={"trias and shaw","trias si7","is trias si7"},it="ties"},{q="Who runs the shop with him?",a="Elling runs Trias' Cheese with his wife, Elaine Trias, and son, Ben Trias. Together, they keep the shop looking like an ordinary family trade.",al={"trias family","elling trias wife"},it="people"},{q="What is his involvement in the Missing Diplomat investigation?",a="Bishop DeLavey sends investigators to Elling Trias, whose contacts include old associates Jorgen and Tyrion. Their leads trace Defias movements and reveal who seized the diplomat bound for Theramore.",al={"missing diplomat trias","why visit trias cheese"},sp=1,it="purpose"},{q="Whose side is Elling Trias on?",a="Elling stands firmly with Stormwind and the Alliance, despite operating in shadows. Though he often masks his activities behind the humble front of a Trade District cheesemonger, his covert ties connect directly to Master Mathias Shaw and SI:7. He actively works against subversives like the Defias Brotherhood to keep the realm secure.",al={"is elling trias loyal to stormwind","who does elling trias work for","is elling trias alliance"},it="side",add="f0ad15b5"},{q="What does Elling Trias want?",a="Publicly, Elling seeks nothing more than to sell fine cheese alongside his family. In truth, he wants to maintain the safety of Stormwind by gathering intelligence and rooting out threats to the crown. When crises arise, he uses his far-reaching network of contacts to quietly unravel conspiracies without causing public panic.",al={"elling trias motive","what is elling trias goal","why does elling trias help"},it="wants",add="fc385e9b"},{q="Why is Elling Trias here in Stormwind?",a="Elling operates out of Stormwind's bustling Trade District because a popular cheese shop offers the perfect cover for espionage. From behind his counter, he can seamlessly exchange whispers, receive couriers, and coordinate with intelligence operatives across the kingdom while appearing to be an ordinary merchant tending shop with his wife and son.",al={"why is elling trias in stormwind","why does elling stay in stormwind","elling trias purpose in city"},it="why_here",add="e76b2a1d"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you know a cheese shop can make an ideal drop point. Elling's place near Old Town and his close ties to Mathias Shaw make it a fixture in Stormwind's underworld.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can count on Elling to quietly gather rumors from Theramore to Hearthglen and help guard the realm against threats within."},kw={"elaine trias","elling trias","mathias shaw","missing diplomat","si:7","stormwind","trade district","trias cheese","tyrion"},rel={"subzone:trade-district","zone:stormwind","npc:mathias-shaw","quest:1241","npc:tyrion","npc:bishop-delavey","topic:defias-brotherhood","quest:2300"},src={"Elling Trias"}}
E["npc:farthing"] = {t="npc",n="Farthing",z="stormwind",s="Farthing serves the faithful from Stormwind's Cathedral of Light. The kind and wise human clergyman guides parishioners and directs aid to settlements across the kingdom.",h="Farthing serves the faithful from Stormwind's Cathedral of Light.",sec={{t="A Bishop in Stormwind",b="Bishop Farthing tends to the spiritual needs of Stormwind City from the Cathedral of Light. Alongside Archbishop Benedictus and the gathered clergy, he counsels travelers, assists those pursuing the holy arts, and attends to the Church of the Holy Light's civic and pastoral duties.",sp=0},{t="Aid to the Plagued Lands",b="From the capital, Farthing directs earnest travelers toward parts of the kingdom in need of holy aid. Reports tell of the necromancer Morbent Fel and an undead blight spreading through Duskwood. Farthing advises on ways to overcome dark sorceries and cleanse the blighted frontier.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can Bishop Farthing be found?",a="Bishop Farthing resides inside the Cathedral of Light, at the center of Cathedral Square in Stormwind City.",al={"farthing location","where is farthing","farthing map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What role does Farthing play in the Cathedral?",a="Farthing is an ordained bishop in the Church of the Holy Light. He guides visiting faithful, priests in training, and adventurers seeking holy wisdom for distant settlements.",al={"what does farthing do","who is farthing"},it="purpose"},{q="How is Farthing involved with Duskwood?",a="Adventurers dealing with Duskwood's undead menace seek Farthing's advice on the dark arts sustaining the necromancer Morbent Fel. He directs them toward purification.",al={"farthing duskwood","farthing morbent fel"},it="ties"},{q="Is Farthing related to other citizens bearing the same name?",a="Several people across human lands share the Farthing surname, including Coleman and Yvette Farthing. Bishop Farthing does not speak of any direct family ties.",al={"coleman farthing relative","farthing family"},it="people"},{q="Who is Bishop Farthing?",a="Bishop Farthing is a human priest of the Church of the Holy Light who serves within Stormwind City's grand Cathedral of Light. Kind and wise, he attends to cathedral business and offers guidance to the faithful.",al={"who is farthing","bishop farthing","farthing lore"},it="identity",add="e622858b"},{q="Whose side is Bishop Farthing on?",a="Farthing stands firmly with the Grand Alliance and the Church of the Holy Light under Archbishop Benedictus. He represents the priesthood within Stormwind's holy sanctuary, guiding petitioners and tending to matters of the faith.",al={"farthing allegiance","who does farthing serve","is farthing alliance"},it="side",add="6481fc58"},{q="What does Bishop Farthing want?",a="Farthing wants to aid travelers and uphold the virtues of the Light. He shows particular concern for lands threatened by darkness, such as advising adventurers on how to assist the beleaguered people of Duskwood against dark necromancy.",al={"farthing motive","what does farthing want","farthing goal"},it="wants",add="e4f9a584"},{q="Why is Bishop Farthing in the Cathedral of Light?",a="Farthing is stationed in Stormwind's Cathedral of Light to perform his clerical duties as a bishop, counseling visitors, supporting the priesthood, and helping direct church affairs on behalf of the high clergy.",al={"why is farthing here","why is farthing in stormwind","farthing purpose cathedral"},it="why_here",add="1783acb6"}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest visiting the Cathedral of Light, you can look to Farthing for the hierarchy and scholarly wisdom of Stormwind's human clergy.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance adventurer fighting corruption in southern territories such as Duskwood, you can seek divine insight and spiritual resolve from Farthing and his fellow clergy."},kw={"benedictus","bishop farthing","cathedral of light","farthing","morbent fel","seeking wisdom","stormwind"},rel={"subzone:cathedral-of-light","npc:archbishop-benedictus","quest:269","quest:55","quest:270","zone:stormwind","zone:duskwood","topic:church-of-the-holy-light"},src={"Farthing"}}
E["npc:field-marshal-stonebridge"] = {t="npc",n="Field Marshal Stonebridge",z="stormwind",s="At Stormwind's gates, Field Marshal Stonebridge helps oversee the city's defenses with General Marcus Jonathan. She also receives reports and trophies from major victories.",h="At Stormwind's gates, Field Marshal Stonebridge helps oversee the city's defenses with General Marcus...",sec={{t="A Bulwark at the Gates",b="Field Marshal Stonebridge watches the eastern archway at the entrance to the Valley of Heroes, beside Stormwind's main gates. A senior officer in the Grand Alliance, she works closely with General Marcus Jonathan. From the gate, she watches defenders, travelers, and returning champions enter the capital, ready to organize the garrison if danger breaches the outer defenses.",sp=0},{t="Bearer of Trophies",b="Field Marshal Stonebridge also receives reports and spoils from campaigns against great threats to the kingdom. Senior commanders rely on officers like her to confirm important intelligence and mark victories in the field, including the defeat of warlords and monsters in the crags of Blackrock Mountain.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Field Marshal Stonebridge located?",a="She stands beneath an archway in the northeastern Valley of Heroes in Stormwind City, just to the right of General Marcus Jonathan as you enter through the city gates.",al={"stonebridge location","where is field marshal stonebridge","find stonebridge"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Field Marshal Stonebridge's role in Stormwind?",a="She is a senior Alliance officer who helps General Marcus Jonathan defend Stormwind's main gate. She also receives important military reports and trophies from Alliance champions returning with great victories.",al={"what does stonebridge do","stonebridge purpose","who is field marshal stonebridge"},it="purpose"},{q="What rank is a Field Marshal in the Alliance?",a="Field Marshal is one of the Grand Alliance's highest officer ranks, just below Grand Marshal. Officers of this rank oversee major tactical deployments, city defense sectors, and strategic garrisons.",al={"alliance field marshal rank","how high rank is stonebridge"}},{q="What major quests involve Field Marshal Stonebridge?",a="Field Marshal Stonebridge receives the report and trophy for 'The Lord of Blackrock', confirming Nefarian's defeat when Alliance adventurers bring the dragon's head back to Stormwind's gates.",al={"stonebridge quests","the lord of blackrock quest ender"},sp=1,gp=true},{q="Who is Field Marshal Stonebridge?",a="Field Marshal Stonebridge is a high-ranking human commander of the Alliance military, stationed at the gates of Stormwind City. Standing alongside the city's leadership in the Valley of Heroes, she oversees critical defenses and serves as one of the kingdom's senior military authorities.",al={"who is stonebridge","field marshal stonebridge identity","stonebridge lore"},it="identity",add="63c0e4ac"},{q="Whose side is Field Marshal Stonebridge on?",a="Field Marshal Stonebridge is utterly loyal to the Kingdom of Stormwind and the Grand Alliance. She serves directly beneath the kingdom's supreme commanders, helping safeguard the capital from external threats.",al={"stonebridge faction","stonebridge allegiance","who does stonebridge serve"},it="side",add="05caa28c"},{q="Why is Field Marshal Stonebridge here?",a="She is posted at the Valley of Heroes to stand guard at the capital's grand entrance, assisting General Marcus Jonathan with the coordination of Stormwind's forces and receiving high-priority military reports and trophies brought back by Alliance champions.",al={"why is stonebridge in stormwind","why is stonebridge at the gates","stonebridge valley of heroes"},it="why_here",add="d0356b7c"},{q="What does Field Marshal Stonebridge want?",a="Stonebridge seeks the complete defense of Stormwind and the defeat of the realm's greatest adversaries, eagerly verifying proof of major victories brought by adventurers to ensure the kingdom's safety.",al={"stonebridge goals","what does field marshal stonebridge want","stonebridge motives"},it="wants",add="a46f624c"},{q="Who is Field Marshal Stonebridge tied to?",a="She works closely with General Marcus Jonathan, the commander of Stormwind's city defense, and stands as part of Highlord Bolvar Fordragon's wider military apparatus protecting the young King Anduin Wrynn's realm.",al={"stonebridge connections","who does stonebridge work with","stonebridge marcus jonathan"},it="ties",add="af024441"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you can earn the respect of frontline soldiers by striving for high martial standing in the Alliance. Field Marshal Stonebridge is one of the senior commanders at Stormwind's gates.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you share the defense of Stormwind with officers such as Field Marshal Stonebridge and General Marcus Jonathan."},kw={"field marshal","gates","lord of blackrock","marcus jonathan","nefarian","stonebridge","stormwind","valley of heroes"},rel={"subzone:valley-of-heroes","npc:general-marcus-jonathan","quest:7781","zone:stormwind","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:alliance"},src={"Field Marshal Stonebridge"}}
E["npc:furen-longbeard"] = {t="npc",n="Furen Longbeard",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind's Dwarven District, warriors seek Furen Longbeard's skill to forge specialized, battle-ready armor. Apprenticed to Grimand Elmore, the master armorer is known for his metallurgical expertise and heavy protective gear.",h="In Stormwind's Dwarven District, warriors seek Furen Longbeard's skill to forge specialized, battle-ready...",sec={{t="A Dwarven Smith in the Human Capital",b="Furen Longbeard works far from Ironforge's great forges, among the cobblestones and soot of Stormwind's Dwarven District. Like many dwarves, he brought traditional metallurgy south to help rebuild and defend the kingdom. His work keeps him connected with artisans throughout the city and beyond.",sp=0},{t="Mastery of Fire-Hardened Mail",b="Grimand Elmore taught Furen Longbeard his craft. Furen has perfected ways to treat heavy mail and plate so they can withstand the punishment of battle. Young warriors seeking durable protection turn to him, and he requires rare ores, specialized components, and exotic reagents from distant corners of the world to fashion his signature fire-hardened armor.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Furen Longbeard?",a="Furen Longbeard is a dwarven armorer in Stormwind City's Dwarven District. Alliance warriors seek him as an essential contact and mentor when they need mastercrafted mail armor.",al={"who is furen","furen longbeard lore","dwarf armorer stormwind"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Furen Longbeard be found?",a="Furen Longbeard can be found in Stormwind City's Dwarven District, near the neighborhood's forges and smithing workshops.",al={"where is furen longbeard","furen longbeard location","furen stormwind"},it="why_here",gp=true},{q="Who taught Furen his smithing craft?",a="Grimand Elmore, a respected veteran craftsman who also lives in the Dwarven District, taught Furen Longbeard armorcraft and metallurgy.",al={"furen teacher","furen mentor","who trained furen"},it="ties"},{q="What armor is Furen famous for crafting?",a="Furen Longbeard is known for crafting Fire Hardened Mail, resilient armor made through exacting metallurgical work with rare components gathered across the continent.",al={"fire hardened mail","furen armor quest","warrior mail quest stormwind"},it="fame"},{q="Is Furen Longbeard related to other Longbeards?",a="Furen Longbeard shares his clan name with other prominent dwarves across the Eastern Kingdoms, including Pilot Longbeard, an Ironforge siege engine pilot. Furen focuses on smithing.",al={"furen family","longbeard clan","pilot longbeard relative"},it="ties"},{q="Why do warriors seek out Furen Longbeard?",a="Warriors who have proven their basic martial prowess are directed to Furen Longbeard for heavy, durable armor that can endure front-line combat against deadlier threats.",al={"why do warriors visit furen","warrior quest dwarven district","furen warrior trainer"},it="purpose"},{q="Whose side is Furen Longbeard on?",a="Furen Longbeard is a loyal member of the Alliance, plying his trade from the bustling Dwarven District in Stormwind City. Working closely with Ironforge kin, fellow smiths, and the Stormpike clan, he dedicates his craftsmanship to outfitting the defenders of the Alliance.",al={"furen longbeard faction","furen longbeard alliance","who does furen longbeard serve"},it="side",add="269e0799"},{q="What does Furen Longbeard want?",a="Furen seeks rare materials and capable allies to craft exceptional armor, particularly for promising warriors seeking sturdy gear like fire-hardened mail. He also works to fulfill crucial military contracts, including specialized orders for the Stormpike guard.",al={"what does furen want","furen longbeard motive","furen longbeard goals"},it="wants",add="d8add91c"},{q="Why is Furen Longbeard in Stormwind?",a="Furen works out of Stormwind City's Dwarven District, serving as a vital connection between dwarven craftsmanship and the human capital's martial needs. Here, near the city's great forges, he can collaborate with apprentices, master smiths, and gnomish engineers while providing heavy armor to frontline defenders.",al={"why is furen longbeard here","why is furen in stormwind","furen longbeard location lore"},it="why_here",add="316ead5d"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As an Alliance warrior, you can turn to Furen Longbeard for fire-hardened armor made from gathered reagents and his smithing skill.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="As a blacksmith, you can see the high standards of dwarven smithing in Stormwind and the advanced techniques Grimand Elmore passed down to Furen Longbeard.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you can see Furen Longbeard keeping dwarven metallurgical traditions alive in the heart of the human capital."},kw={"armorer","blacksmith","dwarven district","fire hardened mail","furen longbeard","grimand elmore","stormwind","warrior"},rel={"quest:1701","quest:1782","quest:1700","subzone:dwarven-district","zone:stormwind","topic:dwarf","npc:pilot-longbeard","quest:1338"},src={"Furen Longbeard"}}
E["npc:gakin-the-darkbinder"] = {t="npc",n="Gakin the Darkbinder",z="stormwind",s="Beneath The Slaughtered Lamb in Stormwind, Gakin the Darkbinder teaches the warlock arts in secret. He tests aspiring Alliance warlocks before they attempt to summon and bind demons.",h="Beneath The Slaughtered Lamb in Stormwind, Gakin the Darkbinder teaches the warlock arts in secret.",sec={{t="A Secret Gathering Place",b="Below The Slaughtered Lamb's taproom, a cellar shelters those who study shadow and fel. The crypt-like room holds summoning circles and grim tomes, hidden from the eyes that watch Stormwind's open mage sanctuaries. Gakin guides young warlocks there, teaching discipline and restraint before they summon forces they cannot control.",sp=0},{t="Master of Demons",b="Gakin teaches demonology and the rites used to bind demons. Those who earn his notice travel across the kingdom to gather rare things, including stolen bloodstone talismans and corrupt wood from dark forests. When the materials are ready, Gakin oversees their work in the crypt's summoning circle. Novices must master voidwalkers and succubi in trials that test their will and put their lives at risk.",sp=0},{t="Betrayals and Loose Ends",b="Surena Caledon, a former apprentice of Gakin, fled into the wilds with a valuable Bloodstone Choker. Her betrayal could expose the warlock circle to Stormwind's guards. Gakin sends loyal followers to recover lost artifacts and silence loose ends before the authorities take notice.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where can I find Gakin the Darkbinder?",a="Gakin waits beneath The Slaughtered Lamb in Stormwind's Mage Quarter. Enter the tavern and take the downward ramp at the back. Follow the stone tunnels to the summoning circle in the lowest crypt.",al={"where is gakin","gakin location","slaughtered lamb basement"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What does Gakin the Darkbinder do?",a="Gakin mentors Alliance warlocks and tests novices with trials across Azeroth. He teaches them to summon and bind demons such as the Voidwalker and Succubus.",al={"what does gakin do","gakin role","gakin quests"},it="purpose"},{q="Why are warlocks allowed under The Slaughtered Lamb?",a="Stormwind forbids demonic magic and deeply mistrusts it. The warlocks beneath The Slaughtered Lamb work in secrecy, hidden from guards and citizens and tolerated as a dangerous covert asset.",al={"why are warlocks allowed","are warlocks legal in stormwind","slaughtered lamb lore"},it="why_here"},{q="Who is Surena Caledon?",a="Surena Caledon was Gakin's former student, and she stole a powerful Bloodstone Choker from him. Her betrayal threatens the hidden order, so Gakin sends warlocks to track her down.",al={"surena caledon","gakin student","who stole from gakin"},it="ties"},{q="Which demons does Gakin help summon?",a="Gakin oversees rites to bind Voidwalkers and Succubi. He guides warlocks as they summon the demons into the underground circle and subdue them.",al={"gakin demons","gakin voidwalker","gakin succubus"},it="power",gp=true},{q="Who is Strahad and why does Gakin mention him?",a="Strahad Farsan is an experienced warlock in the Ratchet hills of Kalimdor. After a student masters Gakin's basic binding rites, Gakin sends them across the sea to continue their dark studies with Strahad.",al={"strahad","seeking strahad","where does gakin send me next"},it="allies"},{q="Who is Gakin the Darkbinder?",a="Gakin the Darkbinder is a powerful human warlock hiding deep within the crypts beneath The Slaughtered Lamb in Stormwind's Mage Quarter. Far from the prying eyes of the city watch and the kirin tor, he guides fledgling practitioners of the fel arts, instructing them on the perilous rites required to bend otherworldly demons to their will.",al={"who is gakin","gakin identity","gakin lore"},it="identity",add="5c1d997e"},{q="Whose side is Gakin the Darkbinder on?",a="Gakin operates loosely in service to the Alliance, training human and gnome practitioners to weaponize demonic forces for their own survival. However, like most masters of the dark arts, his ultimate loyalties remain guarded, steeped in shadows, secrecy, and the pursuit of forbidden knowledge beyond the scrutiny of Stormwind's rulers.",al={"is gakin alliance","gakin loyalty","who does gakin serve"},it="side",add="a5302178"},{q="What does Gakin the Darkbinder want?",a="Gakin seeks to expand his mastery over fel magic and ensure aspiring warlocks possess the resolve to bind greater demons rather than be consumed by them. He also works quietly to recover stolen artifacts of power, such as a stolen Bloodstone Choker taken by his wayward former pupil.",al={"what does gakin want","gakin goals","gakin motives"},it="wants",add="503bf85b"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a human or gnome warlock, you can learn the rites to summon and bind a voidwalker and succubus from Gakin in Stormwind's crypts.",["faction:Alliance"]="Gakin's hidden circle beneath the capital reveals the compromises made in the heart of the Alliance."},kw={"darkbinder","gakin","mage quarter","slaughtered lamb","succubus","surena caledon","voidwalker","warlock"},rel={"subzone:slaughtered-lamb","subzone:mage-quarter","zone:stormwind","quest:1471","quest:1472","quest:1688","quest:1715","quest:1798"},src={"Gakin the Darkbinder"}}
E["npc:gazin-tenorm"] = {t="npc",n="Gazin Tenorm",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind's Cathedral of Light, Gazin Tenorm keeps watch near the altar after a dangerous scouting mission in Elwynn Forest.",h="In Stormwind's Cathedral of Light, Gazin Tenorm keeps watch near the altar after a dangerous scouting mission...",sec={{t="A Scout in the Cathedral",b="Gazin Tenorm stays in the Cathedral of Light, though his thoughts remain in Elwynn Forest. He and his close friend Henze Faulk went into the woods to gather proof of the Defias Brotherhood's movements for the royal court. Defias forces ambushed them. Gazin escaped to Stormwind, but Henze was left in mortal danger. Now Gazin seeks a hero of the Light to help his companion.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Gazin Tenorm?",a="Gazin Tenorm stands near the back altar inside the Cathedral of Light in Stormwind City, among high-ranking clergy and paladin mentors.",al={"gazin location","where is gazin tenorm","where is gazin"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happened to Gazin Tenorm in Elwynn Forest?",a="Gazin and his companion Henze Faulk were ambushed by Defias forces while investigating the Brotherhood. Gazin escaped to Stormwind City, but Henze was stranded in the forest.",al={"gazin story","what happened to gazin","why is gazin hurt"},it="history"},{q="Why was Gazin investigating the Defias Brotherhood?",a="Gazin and Henze went into Elwynn Forest to gather proof of the Defias Brotherhood's illicit activities for the king's advisors in Stormwind.",al={"why investigate defias","gazin mission","gazin henze defias"},it="purpose"},{q="How does Gazin connect to the Paladin trials?",a="Duthorian Rall sends aspiring human paladins pursuing the Tome of Divinity to Gazin. Gazin points them toward rescuing Henze Faulk, testing their valor and mercy.",al={"gazin tome of divinity","paladin quest gazin","henze faulk quest"}},{q="Who is Gazin Tenorm?",a="Gazin Tenorm is a dwarven investigator currently sheltering inside Stormwind's Cathedral of Light. Working in coordination with royal contacts, he and his partner sought evidence to confirm the growing Defias threat stirring just outside the capital's gates.",al={"who is gazin","who is gazin tenorm","gazin tenorm identity"},it="identity",add="d8d56684"},{q="Whose side is Gazin Tenorm on?",a="Gazin is entirely loyal to the Alliance and the Kingdom of Stormwind. He works alongside the priesthood and paladins of the Cathedral of Light, striving to gather hard intelligence for the king's court regarding rebel subversion in Elwynn.",al={"gazin tenorm faction","is gazin alliance","who does gazin serve"},it="side",add="e9ee1d11"},{q="What does Gazin Tenorm want?",a="Having barely survived an ambush by Defias thugs, Gazin desperately wants his companion Henze Faulk rescued from Elwynn Forest. Beyond that, he seeks to expose the Defias Brotherhood's schemes to the king's advisors before their insurrection gains further ground.",al={"what does gazin want","gazin tenorm goal","what is gazin looking for"},it="wants",add="22d0c57e"},{q="Why is Gazin Tenorm in the Cathedral of Light?",a="After a violent confrontation with the Defias left him shaken and fleeing for his life, Gazin sought the holy sanctuary of the Cathedral of Light. Here, near the altar, he recuperates under the watchful protection of Duthorian Rall and the Silver Hand.",al={"why is gazin in cathedral","why is gazin tenorm here","gazin cathedral of light"},it="why_here",add="6cef862e"},{q="Who is Gazin Tenorm tied to?",a="Gazin works in close partnership with Henze Faulk, his fellow investigator. He also shares a strong bond of trust with Duthorian Rall, who directs promising young paladins to Gazin's aid in their shared duty to safeguard the realm.",al={"gazin tenorm allies","gazin connections","who does gazin work with"},it="ties",add="2ec8b348"}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As an initiate learning compassion and redemption, you meet Gazin in the Cathedral of Light and help his fallen comrade, Henze Faulk.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you see Gazin's solidarity with Stormwind. He faces Elwynn's brigands on behalf of the kingdom's advisors."},kw={"cathedral of light","defias","duthorian rall","gazin tenorm","henze faulk","paladin","tome of divinity"},rel={"npc:henze-faulk","npc:duthorian-rall","quest:1641","subzone:cathedral-of-light","zone:stormwind","topic:defias-brotherhood","zone:elwynn"},src={"Gazin Tenorm"}}
E["npc:harlan-bagley"] = {t="npc",n="Harlan Bagley",z="stormwind",s="At the Lionheart Armory in Stormwind City, Harlan Bagley tends to the arms and equipment his customers need. He is a human merchant in the Trade District, serving citizens and visiting adventurers from his shop on the district's northern side.",h="At the Lionheart Armory in Stormwind City, Harlan Bagley tends to the arms and equipment his customers need.",sec={{t="The Lionheart Armory",b="Harlan Bagley keeps the Lionheart Armory on the northern side of Stormwind's Trade District. He tends its stock and sells defensive gear from behind the counter. Trade and regional couriers bring supplies to the shop as the capital faces distant border conflicts and shortages.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Harlan Bagley?",a="Harlan Bagley is a human shopkeeper and tradesman who runs the Lionheart Armory, an equipment shop in Stormwind City's Trade District.",al={"who is harlan","harlan bagley lore","lionheart armory vendor"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Harlan Bagley?",a="You can find Harlan Bagley inside the Lionheart Armory, on the northern side of the central square in Stormwind City's Trade District.",al={"harlan bagley location","where is harlan","lionheart armory location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What role does he play in Stormwind's commerce?",a="As a merchant in the kingdom's capital, Harlan Bagley supplies armor and gear. He sometimes hires adventurers to carry deliveries and secure supply shipments that keep his armory open.",al={"what does harlan sell","harlan bagley business"},it="purpose"},{q="Whose side is Harlan Bagley on?",a="Harlan Bagley is an ordinary citizen and tradesman of the Alliance, loyal to the Kingdom of Stormwind. He conducts his business openly within the Trade District, serving the adventurers, guards, and defenders who pass through the capital.",al={"harlan bagley faction","is harlan bagley alliance"},it="side",add="13bd1b18"},{q="What does Harlan Bagley want?",a="Running the Lionheart Armory requires a reliable flow of raw materials and craftsmanship. Harlan is focused on keeping his armory fully stocked and ready to serve customers, frequently seeking help from travelers to secure goods and restock his shelves.",al={"what does harlan want","harlan bagley motive","harlan needs a resupply why"},it="wants",add="d342d373"},{q="Why is Harlan Bagley here?",a="Harlan operates Lionheart Armory, situated on the northern side of Stormwind City's bustling Trade District. He stays here to cater to the heavy foot traffic of shoppers, smiths, and soldiers outfitting themselves for travel across Azeroth.",al={"why is harlan bagley in stormwind","why is harlan in trade district"},it="why_here",add="0eb71712"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance merchant, Harlan Bagley helps supply the kingdom's capital with gear and goods while threats across the surrounding territories put regular supply lines at risk."},kw={"armorer","harlan bagley","lionheart armory","merchant","stormwind","trade district"},rel={"subzone:trade-district","zone:stormwind","quest:333","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Harlan Bagley"}}
E["npc:high-priestess-laurena"] = {t="npc",n="High Priestess Laurena",z="stormwind",s="At Stormwind's Cathedral of Light, High Priestess Laurena trains human priests in devotion and arcane wards.",h="At Stormwind's Cathedral of Light, High Priestess Laurena trains human priests in devotion and arcane wards.",sec={{t="A High Priestess of the Cathedral",b="High Priestess Laurena holds a senior post in the Church of the Holy Light. She serves in Stormwind City's Cathedral of Light, the heart of the faith, where Archbishop Benedictus leads the Church.",sp=0},{t="Tending the Faithful",b="Behind the central altar in the cathedral sanctuary, High Priestess Laurena mentors aspiring priests. Acolytes who show dedication and piety are sent to her for deeper study. She teaches sacred boons such as Desperate Prayer and defensive spells that turn enemy arcane magic against its wielders. When her students have learned all she can teach, she sends them to other master priests across the Alliance.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find High Priestess Laurena?",a="High Priestess Laurena stands behind the main altar inside the Cathedral of Light in Cathedral Square, Stormwind City.",al={"laurena location","where is priestess laurena","find laurena"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What does High Priestess Laurena teach?",a="High Priestess Laurena trains human priests in foundational prayers, including Desperate Prayer, and wards such as Arcane Feedback against hostile spellcasters.",al={"laurena spells","priest trainer laurena","what does laurena teach"},it="for_you",gp=true},{q="Where did Laurena come from before Stormwind?",a="Nothing is recorded of High Priestess Laurena's life before she took up her post at Stormwind City's Cathedral of Light.",al={"laurena backstory","is laurena from stormwind","laurena lordaeron"},it="origin"},{q="Does she serve under Archbishop Benedictus?",a="Yes. Archbishop Benedictus leads the Church of the Holy Light and presides over the Cathedral of Light, where High Priestess Laurena holds a senior post.",al={"laurena and benedictus","who is laurena's boss","benedictus laurena"},it="ties"},{q="Why does she direct me to other priest trainers?",a="Once High Priestess Laurena has taught the foundational prayers of the Holy Light, she sends students to master priests of other disciplines, such as dwarven masters in Ironforge or night elf priestesses in Darnassus, to broaden their spiritual learning.",al={"laurena sends me away","a lack of fear quest","elunes grace quest"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Did Laurena lose her family to the undead?",a="Nothing is recorded of High Priestess Laurena's family.",al={"laurena family dead","what happened to laurena family"},it="history"},{q="Who is High Priestess Laurena?",a="High Priestess Laurena is a prominent senior priestess within the Church of the Holy Light. She serves behind the main altar in Stormwind City's Cathedral of Light, guiding promising acolytes in their holy duties.",al={"who is laurena","high priestess laurena identity","who is high priestess laurena"},it="identity",add="7a5d626d"},{q="Whose side is High Priestess Laurena on?",a="She is devoted entirely to the Church of the Holy Light and the Alliance. Stationed within Stormwind's Cathedral of Light, she works to minister to the kingdom's faithful, nurture new priests, and support the surviving peoples who have sought refuge from the devastation across Azeroth.",al={"laurena allegiance","what faction is laurena","who does laurena serve"},it="side",add="f0ff80a5"},{q="What does High Priestess Laurena want?",a="Laurena strives to shepherd the faithful and prepare newly dedicated priests to withstand dark magic and the threats plaguing Azeroth.",al={"laurena goals","what is laurena trying to do","laurena motive"},it="wants",add="15a925ad"},{q="Why is High Priestess Laurena in the Cathedral of Light?",a="As a High Priestess of the Church of the Holy Light, Laurena serves in the Cathedral of Light, the heart of the faith in Stormwind, where she instructs promising initiates and helps the Church protect the realm.",al={"why is laurena here","why is laurena in stormwind","why cathedral of light laurena"},it="why_here",add="8a1c100b"}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you can learn from High Priestess Laurena in Stormwind. She guides human acolytes, teaches Desperate Prayer, and shows them how to disrupt enemy spellcasters.",["race:Human"]="As a human of Stormwind, you can look to High Priestess Laurena as a spiritual guide at the Cathedral of Light through troubled times.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance champion, you can find High Priestess Laurena strengthening the faith of the Alliance from the Cathedral of Light, teaching defenses against dark magic and undead horrors."},kw={"arcane feedback","benedictus","cathedral of light","desperate prayer","high priestess","holy light","laurena","priest trainer","stormwind"},rel={"subzone:cathedral-of-light","npc:archbishop-benedictus","topic:church-of-the-holy-light","quest:5634","quest:5676","quest:5645","quest:5672","zone:stormwind"},src={"High Priestess Laurena"}}
E["npc:innkeeper-allison"] = {t="npc",n="Innkeeper Allison",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind's Trade District, Innkeeper Allison keeps the Gilded Rose ready for travelers and merchants. The busy inn stands between the bank and auction house, where she offers hearthstone bindings, drinks, and shelter.",h="In Stormwind's Trade District, Innkeeper Allison keeps the Gilded Rose ready for travelers and merchants.",sec={{t="Hospitality in the Trade District",b="Innkeeper Allison welcomes travelers at the Gilded Rose in Stormwind. The inn stands between the Trade District auction house and the city's main vaults, and its ground floor sees a steady flow of peddlers, mercenaries, and visiting diplomats. She keeps order behind the main counter and offers lodging and hearthstone services. Allison also joins local holiday festivities and coordinates small errands for traveling heroes seeking rest in the capital.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Innkeeper Allison?",a="Innkeeper Allison stands behind the counter on the ground floor of the Gilded Rose. The inn is in Stormwind City's Trade District, between the central bank and the auction house.",al={"allison location","where is innkeeper allison","gilded rose innkeeper"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What services does Innkeeper Allison offer?",a="Innkeeper Allison lets travelers bind their hearthstones to the Gilded Rose and offers food and drink. She also takes part in seasonal events and holidays.",al={"what does allison do","allison services","can i bind hearthstone here"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Does Innkeeper Allison offer any quests?",a="Yes. Innkeeper Allison takes part in seasonal festivities and can sometimes help with city errands for travelers seeking aid across the realm.",al={"allison quests","innkeeper allison quest"},gp=true},{q="Who is Innkeeper Allison?",a="Allison is the proprietor and innkeeper of the Gilded Rose, one of the most prominent resting spots in Stormwind City. Operating right in the heart of the bustling Trade District, she welcomes weary adventurers, merchants, and travelers seeking hearth and comfort amid the crowded capital.",al={"who is allison","innkeeper allison lore","who is innkeeper allison"},it="identity",add="681a398f"},{q="Whose side is Innkeeper Allison on?",a="Allison is a loyal subject of the Kingdom of Stormwind and is devoted to the Alliance. Her inn serves as a safe haven and home base for Alliance champions and citizens passing through the city.",al={"innkeeper allison faction","is allison alliance","who does innkeeper allison serve"},it="side",add="4fce5435"},{q="Why is Innkeeper Allison here?",a="Allison manages the Gilded Rose, situated directly between Stormwind's busy bank and auction house. She remains at her post on the ground floor to provide rooms, bind hearthstones, and tend to the endless stream of travelers trading and doing business in the district.",al={"why is innkeeper allison in the trade district","innkeeper allison purpose here","why is allison here"},it="why_here",add="3063ebee"},{q="What does Innkeeper Allison want?",a="Allison wants nothing more than to run a successful, hospitable establishment and keep the Gilded Rose running smoothly. Beyond tending to her daily patrons, she gladly takes part in civic festivities and seasonal celebrations across the capital.",al={"innkeeper allison motives","what does allison want","what are innkeeper allison's goals"},it="wants",add="735a1673"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance champion, you can rest at the Gilded Rose after returning from the front lines and bank your spoils there."},kw={"allison","gilded rose","hearthstone","innkeeper allison","stormwind","trade district"},rel={"subzone:trade-district","zone:stormwind","topic:alliance","topic:stormwind-kingdom","quest:8356"},src={"Innkeeper Allison"}}
E["npc:jasper-fel"] = {t="npc",n="Jasper Fel",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind's Old Town, Jasper Fel supplies daggers and vials from SI:7 headquarters. He keeps watch on visitors and warns them to mind their speech.",h="In Stormwind's Old Town, Jasper Fel supplies daggers and vials from SI:7 headquarters.",sec={{t="Supplies for the Shadows",b="Inside SI:7 headquarters in Old Town, Jasper Fel supplies the agents who work there. He offers simple daggers and empty vials for brewing and applying poisons. Jasper works under Mathias Shaw's intelligence division and warns visitors to mind their speech. In a place built for espionage, careless words can put people in danger.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Jasper Fel?",a="Jasper Fel can be found inside SI:7 headquarters in the eastern part of Old Town, Stormwind City.",al={"jasper fel location","where is jasper fel","jasper fel stormwind"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What does Jasper Fel sell?",a="Jasper Fel supplies simple daggers and various grades of empty vials for operatives.",al={"jasper fel vendor","what does fel sell","jasper fel wares"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Is Jasper Fel related to Morbent Fel?",a="Jasper Fel and Morbent Fel share a surname, but Jasper keeps silent about his personal matters.",al={"jasper fel morbent fel","is jasper fel related to morbent","fel family duskwood"},it="ties"},{q="Why does Jasper Fel warn people to speak quietly?",a="Jasper Fel warns visitors to mind their speech because he works inside SI:7, Stormwind's espionage headquarters, where loose talk is dangerous.",al={"why speak quietly","jasper fel warning","wrong word throat cut"}},{q="Who is Jasper Fel?",a="Jasper Fel is a discreet human merchant operating out of Stormwind City. Embedded within the secretive confines of Old Town and closely rubbing shoulders with SI:7 operatives, he provides covert supplies, vials, and simple weaponry to rogues and clandestine agents navigating the city's murky underworld.",al={"jasper fel lore","who is jasper fel","jasper fel identity"},it="identity",add="4d6e97a5"},{q="Whose side is Jasper Fel on?",a="Jasper Fel is loyal to Stormwind and the Alliance, operating in close coordination with the covert intelligence network of SI:7. While his shadowy persona and dangerous warnings might suggest a rogue element, his trade directly supports operatives serving the kingdom's interests from within Old Town.",al={"jasper fel alliance","who does jasper fel serve","jasper fel faction"},it="side",add="0dbc34cf"},{q="Why is Jasper Fel here?",a="Stationed within SI:7's territory in Old Town, Jasper Fel serves as an unobtrusive supplier for operatives requiring tools of the trade. Whether providing empty vials for concocting poisons or basic blades for quiet work, he remains on hand to support covert activities away from prying eyes.",al={"why is jasper fel in old town","jasper fel purpose","why is jasper fel here"},it="why_here",add="50a88541"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you can find vials and spare blades from Jasper Fel for your covert work in Stormwind.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can rely on SI:7 headquarters to supply the agents who defend the kingdom from the shadows."},kw={"daggers","jasper fel","morbent fel","old town","rogue supplies","si:7","stormwind","vials"},rel={"quest:2300","subzone:old-town","zone:stormwind","quest:55","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:alliance"},src={"Jasper Fel"}}
E["npc:jennea-cannon"] = {t="npc",n="Jennea Cannon",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind, Jennea Cannon guides new mages through their first studies. From the Wizard's Sanctum in the Mage Quarter, she teaches caution and self-control, and investigates disturbances in local arcane energies.",h="In Stormwind, Jennea Cannon guides new mages through their first studies.",sec={{t="A Guide in the Sanctum",b="At the top of the Wizard's Sanctum's spiral walkway, Jennea Cannon guides those who come to Stormwind to study the arcane. She teaches more than spells, insisting that students learn caution and self-control. Even those who do not study magic hear her warning: without training, magic can burn its wielder.",sp=0},{t="Fieldwork and Foundation",b="Jennea sends promising apprentices beyond the city walls to test what they have learned. At Mirror Lake in Elwynn Forest, they study how natural water sources meet arcane resonance. As they advance, she sends them to investigate disturbances at the Blue Recluse or gather volatile reagents for their first true wizard's implements.",sp=0},{t="Ties to Greater Masters",b="When an apprentice outgrows Jennea's lessons, she points the way to greater masters. Those who show true potential may continue up the Sanctum's hierarchy with High Sorcerer Andromath, or travel beyond the kingdom to practitioners such as Tabetha, deep in the Dustwallow Marsh.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Jennea Cannon?",a="Jennea Cannon guides new mages and directs early magical research from the Wizard's Sanctum in Stormwind's Mage Quarter.",al={"jennea cannon","who is jennea","stormwind mage trainer"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Jennea Cannon?",a="You can find Jennea Cannon inside the Wizard's Sanctum, the spiral tower at the center of Stormwind City's Mage Quarter.",al={"jennea cannon location","where is jennea","find jennea"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What quests does Jennea Cannon offer?",a="Jennea offers Alliance mages early studies that include examining Mirror Lake in Elwynn Forest, investigating strange happenings at the Blue Recluse, and gathering materials for novice mage gear.",al={"jennea quests","jennea cannon questline"},gp=true},{q="Why does she send mages to Mirror Lake?",a="Jennea sends apprentices to fetch a sample from the base of Mirror Lake's waterfall so she can test it for magical taints. She fears altered magic around Stormwind and Elwynn may be seeping into the water.",al={"why mirror lake","mirror lake quest jennea"},it="purpose"},{q="Does Jennea Cannon interact with non-mage classes?",a="Non-mages can speak with Jennea, who warns them to be cautious around magic because it burns those without proper training.",al={"can non mages talk to jennea","jennea for other classes"}},{q="Who does Jennea Cannon report to?",a="Jennea guides students within the Wizard's Sanctum until they are ready to study with senior figures such as High Sorcerer Andromath.",al={"jennea superior","wizards sanctum leaders"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Jennea Cannon on?",a="Jennea serves the Kingdom of Stormwind and the Alliance. Stationed within the Wizard's Sanctum, she works alongside Stormwind's circle of sorcerers to strengthen the city's magical defenses and train fledgling mages loyal to the realm.",al={"jennea cannon faction","who does jennea cannon serve","jennea cannon allegiance"},it="side",add="b57d5dda"},{q="What does Jennea Cannon want?",a="Jennea is dedicated to guiding and preparing emerging spellcasters. She seeks to ensure that novices understand the dangerous, volatile nature of the arcane, cautioning travelers that raw magic will burn the untrained while directing promising students toward vital studies across the realm.",al={"jennea cannon goal","what does jennea want","jennea cannon purpose"},it="wants",add="d154dff8"},{q="Why is Jennea Cannon here?",a="She resides in the Wizard's Sanctum in Stormwind's Mage Quarter to act as a mentor for Alliance mages. From this tower, she oversees initial arcane instruction, examines disturbances nearby, and directs practitioners to higher authorities like High Sorcerer Andromath or tutors abroad.",al={"why is jennea cannon in stormwind","jennea cannon wizard's sanctum","why is jennea in mage quarter"},it="why_here",add="d5352518"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you can look to Jennea for your first field investigations and guidance toward crafting your formal wizard robes and staff.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can find Jennea in Stormwind's Mage Quarter, where she trains new sorcerers to serve the Alliance safely."},kw={"andromath","blue recluse","jennea cannon","mage quarter","mage trainer","mirror lake","stormwind","wizard's sanctum"},rel={"subzone:mage-quarter","zone:stormwind","quest:1860","quest:1861","quest:1939","quest:1961","npc:tabetha","topic:alliance"},src={"Jennea Cannon"}}
E["npc:jorgen"] = {t="npc",n="Jorgen",z="stormwind",s="Jorgen keeps watch beside the water at Stormwind's Valley of Heroes entrance. His quiet perch draws people with matters they cannot discuss openly.",h="Jorgen keeps watch beside the water at Stormwind's Valley of Heroes entrance.",sec={{t="Eyes by the Water",b="Jorgen keeps to the water just right of Stormwind's great entrance. Above him, statues of heroes look over the bridge, while he watches those who come and go below. People seeking information they want kept off the record can find a quiet contact there.",sp=0},{t="A Tangled History",b="Jorgen's past ties him to Elling Trias, a master cheese merchant who gathers intelligence, and Bishop DeLavey of the Cathedral of Light. When investigators seek a diplomat who disappeared after being sent to Theramore, Jorgen can point them in the right direction. Few local contacts know the way through such delicate inquiries, and Jorgen helps only when approached with care.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where can I find Jorgen?",a="Jorgen waits beside the water in Stormwind's Valley of Heroes. Enter through the gates from Elwynn Forest, then head down to the water on the right side of the main bridge.",al={"jorgen location","where is jorgen","find jorgen"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Jorgen connected to in Stormwind?",a="Jorgen has a history with Elling Trias, a prominent cheesemonger in the Trade District with covert connections, and Bishop DeLavey of the Cathedral of Light.",al={"jorgen connections","jorgen ties","who does jorgen know"},it="ties"},{q="What role does Jorgen play in the investigation of the missing diplomat?",a="Bishop DeLavey sends investigators to his old friend Jorgen with a letter during the search for the missing envoy. Jorgen grudgingly agrees to help, makes them swear to secrecy, and sends them to Elling Trias at Trias' Cheese with a sealed note.",al={"jorgen missing diplomat","jorgen quest"},it="purpose"},{q="Is Jorgen affiliated with the Stormwind City Guard?",a="No. Jorgen works independently, away from the Stormwind City Guard's patrols along the canal banks, where people can speak out of earshot.",al={"is jorgen a guard","jorgen faction"},it="side"},{q="Who is Jorgen?",a="Jorgen is a shadowy figure who lingers quietly down by the water in the Valley of Heroes, just past Stormwind's grand front gates. Rather than serving in any official civic capacity, he operates on the fringes of the capital's affairs, possessing deep connections and an unrevealed past tied closely to Master Elling Trias and Bishop DeLavey.",al={"who is jorgen","jorgen stormwind","jorgen identity"},it="identity",add="536f8488"},{q="Why is Jorgen here?",a="Jorgen keeps to the outskirts of the Valley of Heroes to act as a discreet point of contact within Stormwind. Positioned right near the city gates and away from prying eyes, he remains available to assist trusted contacts like Elling Trias whenever delicate, covert inquiries need to be handled quietly.",al={"why is jorgen here","jorgen location reason","why is jorgen in stormwind"},it="why_here",add="846a3fb1"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="Jorgen shows how whispers travel through Stormwind beneath its marble streets, with close ties to the covert work run through Trias' Cheese.",["faction:Alliance"]="When official channels in Stormwind meet bureaucratic walls, street informants like Jorgen help track threats to the kingdom."},kw={"bishop delavey","elling trias","informant","jorgen","missing diplomat","stormwind","valley of heroes"},rel={"quest:1241","npc:elling-trias","npc:bishop-delavey","subzone:valley-of-heroes","zone:stormwind","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Jorgen"}}
E["npc:katrana-prestor"] = {t="npc",n="Lady Katrana Prestor",z="stormwind",s="Lady Katrana Prestor is a noblewoman of Stormwind and one of the most influential voices at court. With King Varian missing, she stands beside the boy-king Anduin and Highlord Bolvar Fordragon in Stormwind Keep as a trusted advisor.",h="Lady Katrana Prestor is a noblewoman of Stormwind and one of the most influential voices at court.",sec={{t="Voice of the Court",b="Lady Prestor arrived at court some years ago and quickly rose to become one of its most trusted figures. The nobles of Stormwind seek her favor, and her counsel shapes many of the decisions made in the young king's name while Highlord Bolvar Fordragon rules as regent. Petitioners who come to Stormwind Keep asking for soldiers or aid often find that her opinion carries as much weight as the regent's.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Lady Katrana Prestor?",a="Lady Katrana Prestor is a Stormwind noblewoman and a trusted advisor at court. With King Varian missing, she stands beside the boy-king Anduin and Highlord Bolvar Fordragon in Stormwind Keep, and her voice carries great weight with the nobles.",al={"who is katrana prestor","who is lady prestor","katrana prestor lore"}},{q="Why is she advising the king?",a="King Varian's disappearance left his young son Anduin on the throne, with Highlord Bolvar Fordragon ruling as regent. Lady Prestor sits at their side as an advisor. Many of the court's decisions, including how Stormwind answers requests for help from its outlying lands, pass through her counsel.",al={"why is prestor at court","what does katrana do"}},{q="Where can I find Lady Prestor?",a="She is usually found in the throne room of Stormwind Keep, standing near Highlord Bolvar Fordragon and the young King Anduin.",al={"where is katrana prestor","katrana prestor location"}}},kw={"katrana","prestor","katrana prestor","lady prestor","advisor","stormwind keep","court"},rel={"zone:stormwind","npc:bolvar-fordragon","npc:anduin-wrynn"},src={"Katrana Prestor"}}
E["npc:keryn-sylvius"] = {t="npc",n="Keryn Sylvius",z="stormwind",s="On the second floor of Goldshire’s Lion’s Pride Inn, Keryn Sylvius trains young rogues. In the reading room, she teaches stealth and bladecraft and quietly guides promising operatives toward Stormwind’s intelligence service.",h="On the second floor of Goldshire’s Lion’s Pride Inn, Keryn Sylvius trains young rogues.",sec={{t="A Quiet Presence in Goldshire",b="Keryn Sylvius keeps to the reading room above the Lion’s Pride Inn. Downstairs, travelers crowd the floor with town guards, while upstairs she watches the steady flow of road gossip. She mentors rogues learning their trade in Elwynn Forest. When promising operatives outgrow petty theft and roadside skulduggery, Sylvius discreetly sends them to Stormwind City to contact SI:7.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Keryn Sylvius?",a="Find Keryn Sylvius in the small reading room on the second floor of the Lion’s Pride Inn in Goldshire.",al={"keryn sylvius location","where is keryn","goldshire rogue trainer location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What services does she offer?",a="Keryn Sylvius trains rogues, teaching new abilities, resetting talent specializations, and guiding their progress.",al={"what does keryn do","can she train me","keryn sylvius role"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="What connection does she have to SI:7?",a="Once operatives prove their abilities, Sylvius directs them to seek out Master Mathias Shaw and SI:7 in Old Town, where Stormwind’s covert intelligence network is based.",al={"keryn si7","is she si:7","does she work for stormwind"},it="ties"},{q="Who is Keryn Sylvius?",a="Keryn Sylvius is a rogue trainer who makes her home on the upper floor of Goldshire's Lion's Pride Inn. Tucked away in the quiet reading room, she observes the comings and goings of Elwynn Forest while passing on the subtle arts of stealth, lockpicking, and subterfuge to promising rogues under the banner of the Alliance.",al={"who is keryn","keryn sylvius lore","who is sylvius"},it="identity",add="74741391"},{q="Whose side is Keryn Sylvius on?",a="Keryn stands firmly with the Kingdom of Stormwind and the Alliance. Her craft serves the realm's interests, quietly directing talented agents to Stormwind's clandestine intelligence network so they can aid the kingdom against internal unrest and outside threats alike.",al={"keryn sylvius alliance or horde","keryn sylvius allegiance","who does keryn sylvius serve"},it="side",add="017a68dc"},{q="What does Keryn Sylvius want?",a="Keryn aims to scout and instruct raw talent in the quiet heart of Elwynn before they run afoul of the law or misuse their deadly skills. Once an apprentice proves capable, her goal is to channel their abilities into organized service by directing them onward to SI:7 headquarters in Old Town.",al={"what does keryn want","keryn sylvius goals","why train rogues"},it="wants",add="90e34396"},{q="Why is Keryn Sylvius here in Goldshire?",a="The Lion's Pride Inn serves as the bustling crossroads of Elwynn Forest, making it an ideal place to quietly identify rogues finding their footing outside Northshire Valley. Stationing herself upstairs gives her a discreet perch to mentor fledglings without drawing undue attention from the local guards or townspeople below.",al={"why is keryn in lions pride inn","why is keryn sylvius in goldshire","keryn goldshire why"},it="why_here",add="f8e496c4"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you can learn from Sylvius in Elwynn Forest. When you are ready, she can point you toward SI:7 headquarters in Stormwind City.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can count on Sylvius to keep covert eyes on Elwynn’s main roads from her post above Goldshire’s crossroads."},kw={"elwynn forest","goldshire","keryn sylvius","lion's pride inn","rogue trainer","si:7"},rel={"subzone:lion-s-pride-inn","subzone:goldshire","zone:elwynn","quest:2205","quest:2300"},src={"Keryn Sylvius"}}
E["npc:lieutenant-orrin"] = {t="npc",n="Lieutenant Orrin",z="stormwind",s="At Stormwind's gates, Lieutenant Orrin watches for Scourge incursions and calls for scouts. The Argent Dawn officer stands in the Valley of Heroes, where he directs recruits to investigate undead threats beyond the capital.",h="At Stormwind's gates, Lieutenant Orrin watches for Scourge incursions and calls for scouts.",sec={{t="A Sentinel at the Gates",b="Lieutenant Orrin watches the road from the Valley of Heroes. The Argent Dawn is known for holding the front lines in the ruined north, but it also guards strongholds farther south, including Stormwind City. When necromantic magic stirs beyond the capital, Orrin sounds the alarm and rallies adventurers before the undead can threaten the people within.",sp=0},{t="Eyes on the Unliving",b="Lieutenant Orrin connects the Argent Dawn with volunteers in the southern kingdom. When signs of the Scourge appear beyond Stormwind's gates, he sends scouts to gather intelligence and secure hazardous artifacts. Cracked necrotic crystals are among the objects they recover, helping the order understand and repel the undead threat.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Lieutenant Orrin?",a="Lieutenant Orrin is a human officer of the Argent Dawn, stationed in the Valley of Heroes at Stormwind City's entrance. He coordinates defenses and recruits scouts when the Scourge threatens the surrounding lands.",al={"who is orrin","lieutenant orrin lore","who is the argent dawn officer"},it="identity"},{q="Why is the Argent Dawn in Stormwind City?",a="The Argent Dawn keeps watch in Stormwind because the Scourge threatens lands beyond the Plaguelands. Its officers at the capital's gates watch for necromantic incursions and recruit fighters to stem the undead.",al={"why is argent dawn in stormwind","argent dawn stormwind","what is argent dawn doing here"},it="why_here"},{q="What does Lieutenant Orrin ask adventurers to do?",a="Lieutenant Orrin sends recruits to scout beyond Stormwind City, investigate signs of Scourge activity, and recover artifacts such as cracked necrotic crystals. The order studies these objects to understand the unholy magic behind the incursions.",al={"orrin quests","investigate the scourge of stormwind","what does orrin want"},it="wants"},{q="Whose side is Lieutenant Orrin on?",a="Lieutenant Orrin serves the Argent Dawn, a dedicated neutral coalition formed to fight the Scourge wherever it threatens Azeroth. While he is stationed within Stormwind's Valley of Heroes among human defenders, his primary allegiance remains to the Dawn's holy mission rather than the politics of the Alliance.",al={"lieutenant orrin faction","who does orrin serve","is lieutenant orrin alliance"},it="side",add="3ede5d84"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance champions returning to Stormwind, Lieutenant Orrin's watch shows that the southern heartlands face danger from the Lich King's reach.",["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you share the Argent Dawn's effort to purge necromancy wherever it festers."},kw={"argent dawn","lieutenant orrin","necrotic crystal","orrin","scourge","stormwind","undead","valley of heroes"},rel={"topic:argent-dawn","topic:scourge","subzone:valley-of-heroes","zone:stormwind","quest:9260","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Lieutenant Orrin"}}
E["npc:lord-baurles-k-wishock"] = {t="npc",n="Lord Baurles K. Wishock",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind Keep, Lord Baurles K. Wishock lives among the petitioners and dignitaries. Barkeeps know him for unpaid tabs and a taste for strong drink, but his nights in the city’s underbelly brought him near darker dealings.",h="In Stormwind Keep, Lord Baurles K.",sec={{t="A Nobleman's Dangerous Curiosity",b="Lord Baurles K. Wishock moves among petitioners and dignitaries in Stormwind Keep, where he belongs to the influential House of Nobles. Though his station is high, he often drinks in the Mage Quarter’s dive bars, especially the Slaughtered Lamb, and leaves large bills unpaid. There, he hears of a warlock coven practicing dark arts in cellars beneath the floorboards. Wishock sets out to have the tavern closed and asks fellow nobles for a formal investigation. Uncovering demonic cabals in Stormwind rarely goes unpunished.",sp=0},{t="A Poisoned Cup",b="Lord Baurles K. Wishock’s efforts put him in the warlocks’ sights. To avoid royal scrutiny and an inquiry into their underground sanctum, Zardeth of the Black Claw arranges the nobleman’s quiet killing. The coven exploits Wishock’s thirst for luxury vintages, preparing a lethal drink disguised as fine ale. A hired adventurer is arranged to carry it to Wishock beneath the Keep guards’ noses.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Lord Baurles K. Wishock?",a="Lord Baurles K. Wishock belongs to the House of Nobles and spends his days in the Petitioner's Chamber inside Stormwind Keep. In the Mage Quarter, barkeeps know him for large, unpaid drinking tabs.",al={"baurles wishock","who is wishock","noble petitioner"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Lord Wishock be found?",a="Lord Baurles K. Wishock can be found in the Petitioner's Chamber on the eastern side of Stormwind Keep, among courtiers, diplomats, and supplicants awaiting royal attention.",al={"wishock location","where is wishock","find lord wishock"},it="why_here",gp=true},{q="Why do the warlocks beneath the Slaughtered Lamb want him dead?",a="At the Slaughtered Lamb, Lord Baurles K. Wishock learns that a warlock coven operates beneath the tavern. He seeks a formal inquiry from the House of Nobles and wants the establishment closed, threatening to expose their operations.",al={"why kill wishock","zardeth wishock","why poison wishock"},sp=1,it="motive"},{q="How is he assassinated?",a="Zardeth of the Black Claw prepares a deadly poison disguised as an exquisite drink. An agent brings the poisoned cask to Lord Baurles K. Wishock in Stormwind Keep, where his taste for fine alcohol and free drinks makes him an easy target.",al={"how does wishock die","wishock poison","a noble brew"},sp=1,it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Lord Baurles K. Wishock on?",a="Lord Wishock serves the Kingdom of Stormwind as a sitting member of the House of Nobles. He operates strictly within the royal aristocracy, using his political influence to champion civic and noble authority against subversive elements lurking within the city's borders.",al={"lord wishock side","lord wishock faction","who does wishock serve"},it="side",add="255656dc"},{q="What does Lord Baurles K. Wishock want?",a="Lord Wishock is determined to expose and shut down the dark coven operating in the cellar beneath the Slaughtered Lamb. Having discovered their foul rites, he is actively lobbying his peers in the House of Nobles to launch a full-scale official investigation into the tavern and purge the warlocks from Stormwind.",al={"wishock goal","what does wishock want","lord wishock plan"},it="wants",add="59c1fa27"},{q="Why is Lord Baurles K. Wishock in Stormwind Keep?",a="You will find Lord Wishock standing in the Petitioner's Chamber within Stormwind Keep, where he attends to his aristocratic duties. As a member of the House of Nobles, he frequents the keep to confer with fellow lords and petition the royal court.",al={"why is wishock in stormwind keep","why is lord wishock here","wishock petitioners chamber"},it="why_here",add="3d37be28"},{q="Who is Lord Baurles K. Wishock tied to?",a="Lord Wishock belongs to the House of Nobles, the influential governing assembly of Stormwind's aristocracy. Outside the court, he was a regular patron of the Slaughtered Lamb in the Mage Quarter—where he accumulated an enormous unpaid tab before uncovering the warlock coven practicing dark arts in its hidden crypts.",al={"wishock ties","lord wishock connections","wishock house of nobles"},it="ties",add="83d2fff3"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you know Wishock’s investigation of the Slaughtered Lamb threatens Stormwind’s shadow coven. His quiet death becomes a priority for its members.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you see the House of Nobles’ decadent, self-serving reputation reflected in the Petitioner's Chamber during the boy-king Anduin’s early reign."},kw={"baurles","house of nobles","petitioner's chamber","slaughtered lamb","stormwind keep","wishock","zardeth"},rel={"quest:335","quest:397","npc:zardeth-of-the-black-claw","subzone:slaughtered-lamb","subzone:petitioner-s-chamber","subzone:stormwind-keep","topic:house-of-nobles"},src={"Lord Baurles K. Wishock"}}
E["npc:lucius"] = {t="npc",n="Lucius",z="stormwind",s="At the Lakeshire docks, Lucius watches the Redridge waterfront. The dwarf works undercover for Stormwind’s SI:7, helping agents with reconnaissance and trade skills.",h="At the Lakeshire docks, Lucius watches the Redridge waterfront.",sec={{t="Eyes in the Mountains",b="Lucius watches the Lakeshire docks for SI:7, Stormwind’s intelligence service. He keeps an eye on trade, unusual traffic, and threats moving into the Redridge Mountains. Agents sent east from Stormwind come to him to coordinate covert work and practice field skills such as lockpicking. Through Lucius, Stormwind keeps a hidden reach beyond Elwynn Forest.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Lucius?",a="Lucius is a dwarf agent in Lakeshire who works for SI:7, Stormwind’s intelligence service.",al={"lucius identity","who is the dwarf on the docks","lucius npc"},it="identity"},{q="What does Lucius do in Lakeshire?",a="Lucius helps covert agents with local instruction in thievery and lockpicking, while watching movements across the Redridge Mountains.",al={"what is lucius doing here","lucius purpose","why is lucius on the docks"},it="why_here"},{q="Which quests involve Lucius?",a="Lucius handles the SI:7 mission ‘Redridge Rendezvous’ and sends young rogues to pick the locks of chests at Alther’s Mill for their Certificate of Thievery.",al={"lucius quests","redridge rendezvous quest","alther's mill"},gp=true},{q="Whose side is Lucius on?",a="Lucius stands firmly with the Alliance and specifically answers to SI:7, Stormwind's elite intelligence and covert operations agency. While he keeps a humble profile working around the pier in Lakeshire, his loyalties lie directly with the spymasters in the capital.",al={"lucius faction","lucius allegiance","who does lucius serve"},it="side",add="f414b59e"},{q="What does Lucius want?",a="Lucius serves as an unassuming field operative for SI:7. He keeps a sharp eye on activities around Lake Everstill and the Redridge frontier, liaising with visiting agents and guiding promising operatives sent to carry out sensitive tasks across the mountains.",al={"what is lucius doing","what does lucius need","lucius goals"},it="wants",add="db7d3191"},{q="Who is Lucius tied to?",a="Lucius is directly tied to SI:7, the intelligence network based out of Stormwind City. He acts as their quiet local contact in Redridge, working alongside fellow operatives dispatched into the region to handle covert reconnaissance and specialized operations.",al={"who is lucius affiliated with","lucius connections","lucius si7"},it="ties",add="2f7f1e59"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue sent east from Stormwind, you can turn to Lucius for instruction in lockpicking and reconnaissance.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, Lucius shows how your people’s talents can serve Stormwind’s covert operations as well as the forge and front line."},kw={"docks","dwarf","lakeshire","lockpick","lucius","redridge","rogue","si:7"},rel={"quest:2281","quest:2282","quest:2300","subzone:lakeshire","zone:redridge","topic:dwarf"},src={"Lucius"}}
E["npc:major-mattingly"] = {t="npc",n="Major Mattingly",z="stormwind",s="At Stormwind’s main gates, Major Mattingly helps guard the capital and advises crafters on protection from dragons.",h="At Stormwind’s main gates, Major Mattingly helps guard the capital and advises crafters on protection from...",sec={{t="Sentinel of the Capital Gates",b="Major Mattingly is a high-ranking officer responsible for Stormwind City's landward defense. He stands watch in the Valley of Heroes under General Marcus Jonathan, alongside the city's garrison. His duties include overseeing gate patrols and travelers entering the city. Mattingly also knows the lethal nature of dragons and guides skilled crafters who seek to make protective dragonscale gear for facing dangerous lairs.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can Major Mattingly be found?",a="Major Mattingly keeps watch just inside Stormwind City's main gates, in the Valley of Heroes, alongside the garrison.",al={"mattingly location","where is major mattingly","find major mattingly"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Major Mattingly's rank and role in Stormwind?",a="Major Mattingly is a Stormwind Army officer under General Marcus Jonathan. He helps oversee the city's gate defenses and gives military guidance to adventurers.",al={"who is mattingly","mattingly job","what does mattingly do"},it="identity"},{q="Why do leatherworkers seek out Major Mattingly?",a="Leatherworkers seek Major Mattingly for instructions on treating black dragonhide and crafting scale cloaks that protect allies from dragonfire.",al={"onyxia scale cloak mattingly","mattingly quest","the journey has just begun mattingly"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Is Major Mattingly involved in any broader conflicts?",a="Major Mattingly is a battle-hardened veteran of the Kingdom of Stormwind. He devotes himself to defending the realm while King Varian Wrynn is missing and the kingdom faces lingering threats.",al={"mattingly background","mattingly lore"},it="conflict"},{q="Whose side is Major Mattingly on?",a="Major Mattingly is wholly devoted to the Kingdom of Stormwind and the Alliance. As an officer in the Stormwind Army, he answers directly to General Marcus Jonathan and stands vigil over the grand entrance of the capital, loyal to the throne and the realm's defense.",al={"mattingly faction","who does mattingly serve","major mattingly allegiance"},it="side",add="3133ea98"},{q="Why is Major Mattingly stationed at the Valley of Heroes?",a="He is stationed at the gates within the Valley of Heroes to oversee the capital's foremost line of defense. Beneath the towering monuments to the heroes of the Second War, Mattingly helps command the gatehouse watch, ensuring that no hostile forces march through the gates unchallenged.",al={"why is mattingly here","mattingly valley of heroes why","what is mattingly doing in stormwind"},it="why_here",add="3a90c3f3"},{q="Who is Major Mattingly tied to?",a="Major Mattingly serves directly beneath General Marcus Jonathan within the chain of command of the Stormwind Army. He also shares a surname with Janice Mattingly, a resident of the city, though his daily duties remain tied strictly to his military post and commanding officer.",al={"mattingly commander","who does mattingly report to","major mattingly connections"},it="ties",add="728996ed"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance champions challenging great dragons like Onyxia, Major Mattingly offers guidance on crafting protective cloaks from dragon scales.",["class:Warrior"]="As a disciplined veteran with a longsword at Stormwind's gates, Major Mattingly reflects the steadfast resolve of the Stormwind Army's infantry officers."},kw={"dragonscale cloak","marcus jonathan","major mattingly","mattingly","stormwind army","valley of heroes"},rel={"subzone:valley-of-heroes","zone:stormwind","topic:stormwind-army","quest:7493","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:alliance"},src={"Major Mattingly"}}
E["npc:major-samuelson"] = {t="npc",n="Major Samuelson",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind Keep, Major Samuelson commands the city guard and its personnel. The high-ranking veteran officer serves in the throne room and once mentored Lieutenant Farren Orinelle.",h="In Stormwind Keep, Major Samuelson commands the city guard and its personnel.",sec={{t="A Pillar of Stormwind's Guard",b="Before Stormwind's royal court, Major Samuelson leads the Stormwind City Guard. He oversees officer postings and military orders across the realm. He mentored Lieutenant Farren Orinelle, who serves at Southshore in the Hillsbrad Foothills. When junior commanders struggle or seek transfer from distant frontier garrisons, their requests and official reports travel across the kingdom to Samuelson's desk in the capital.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Major Samuelson?",a="Major Samuelson is a Stormwind City Guard officer stationed in the throne room of Stormwind Keep. As an administrative commander, he oversees officer deployments and personnel.",al={"samuelson","major samuelson identity","who is the major in keep"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Major Samuelson be found?",a="Major Samuelson stands in the throne room of Stormwind Keep, inside Stormwind City, near the boy-king Anduin Wrynn and Highlord Bolvar Fordragon.",al={"samuelson location","where is major samuelson","find samuelson"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is his connection to Southshore?",a="Major Samuelson mentored Lieutenant Farren Orinelle, stationed at Southshore in the Hillsbrad Foothills. Orinelle seeks reassignment from his stressful northern post through Samuelson.",al={"samuelson southshore","lieutenant farren orinelle mentor","samuelson hillsbrad"},it="ties"},{q="Why do adventurers seek him out?",a="Adventurers traveling from the northern front in Hillsbrad bring Lieutenant Farren Orinelle's official reassignment request to Major Samuelson in Stormwind Keep.",al={"stormwind ho quest turnin","reassignment quest","why talk to samuelson"},it="purpose"},{q="Whose side is Major Samuelson on?",a="Major Samuelson serves the Kingdom of Stormwind and the Alliance. As an officer within the Stormwind City Guard stationed directly inside Stormwind Keep, his duty is to defend the capital, maintain military order, and carry out the commands of the city's leadership.",al={"samuelson faction","who does major samuelson serve","is samuelson alliance"},it="side",add="75428c69"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Major Samuelson serves in the royal throne room and directs Stormwind's military personnel across contested lands such as Hillsbrad."},kw={"farren orinelle","major samuelson","reassignment","samuelson","southshore","stormwind guard","stormwind keep"},rel={"subzone:stormwind-keep","zone:stormwind","npc:lieutenant-farren-orinelle","quest:562","quest:563","zone:hillsbrad","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Major Samuelson"}}
E["npc:milton-sheaf"] = {t="npc",n="Milton Sheaf",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind Keep, Milton Sheaf guards the kingdom's written history. He tends the Royal Library and calls on Alliance travelers to recover lost books and records.",h="In Stormwind Keep, Milton Sheaf guards the kingdom's written history.",sec={{t="The Caretaker of Stormwind's History",b="Milton Sheaf tends the Royal Library inside Stormwind Keep. While the court handles politics, noble disputes, and military concerns, he preserves the written record. He sees accurate histories of the Alliance and the Eastern Kingdoms as a duty, especially amid war, loss, and instability.",sp=0},{t="Recovering Lost Tomes",b="Milton Sheaf sends travelers to recover books scattered across the realm. Volumes wear with use, while records lie in monastic archives, distant outposts, and forgotten ruins. He sends Alliance adventurers from Northshire Abbey to Southshore in the north to retrieve misplaced books, examine ancient texts, and return rare manuscripts safely to the keep.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Milton Sheaf?",a="Milton Sheaf is a human scholar who cares for the Royal Library inside Stormwind Keep in Stormwind City. He manages the kingdom's books and chronicles.",al={"who is milton sheaf","milton sheaf role","stormwind librarian"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Milton Sheaf?",a="You can find Milton Sheaf in the Royal Library wing of Stormwind Keep, just off the main palace corridors.",al={"milton sheaf location","where is milton sheaf","stormwind library location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Milton Sheaf need adventurers?",a="Milton Sheaf relies on traveling Alliance adventurers to find historical manuscripts, replace damaged books, and work with scholars and priests across the kingdom to grow the Royal Library's archives.",al={"milton sheaf quests","what does milton want","why give quests"},it="wants"},{q="Does Milton Sheaf interact with other scholars in the kingdom?",a="Yes. Milton Sheaf keeps ties with monastic archivists and religious scholars, including Brother Paxton in Northshire Valley, to preserve sacred teachings and historical records.",al={"milton northshire","milton brother paxton","milton connections"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Milton Sheaf on?",a="Milton Sheaf serves the Kingdom of Stormwind and the Alliance. Stationed within Stormwind Keep itself, he works directly on behalf of the crown's royal archives, cataloging history and preserving knowledge for the kingdom's scholars and leadership.",al={"milton sheaf faction","who does milton sheaf serve","milton sheaf alliance"},it="side",add="440d1fb9"},{q="Why is Milton Sheaf here in Stormwind Keep?",a="Milton is tasked with the stewardship and upkeep of the Royal Library. He tends the kingdom's vast collection of scrolls, tomes, and historical records, ensuring that vital accounts of Azeroth's past remain protected and accessible to the court.",al={"why is milton sheaf in the royal library","milton sheaf purpose here","why is milton in stormwind"},it="why_here",add="1fad6188"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you can help Milton Sheaf preserve the recorded heritage of the human kingdoms and the wider Alliance.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you share a history Milton Sheaf safeguards, preserving chronicles that survived Stormwind's fall and rebuilding."},kw={"books","history","librarian","milton sheaf","royal library","stormwind keep","tomes"},rel={"subzone:royal-library","subzone:stormwind-keep","zone:stormwind","quest:337","quest:343","quest:344","subzone:southshore","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Milton Sheaf"}}
E["npc:morgan-pestle"] = {t="npc",n="Morgan Pestle",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind, Morgan Pestle runs Pestle's Apothecary in the Trade District. He works with his brother William Pestle in Goldshire, handling supplies and alchemical research for the capital.",h="In Stormwind, Morgan Pestle runs Pestle's Apothecary in the Trade District.",sec={{t="The City Apothecary",b="Morgan Pestle sells alchemical goods, reagents, and practical remedies at Pestle's Apothecary in Stormwind's Trade District. His brother William keeps a workshop at the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire, while Morgan tends their family trade in the capital. He receives supplies from the rural heartlands, including candles sent by William.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Morgan Pestle?",a="You can find Morgan Pestle inside Pestle's Apothecary in Stormwind City's Trade District.",al={"morgan pestle location","where is morgan pestle","pestle apothecary stormwind"},it="place",gp=true},{q="How is Morgan Pestle related to William Pestle?",a="Morgan Pestle and William Pestle are brothers who both work as alchemists in Elwynn. Morgan runs their shop in Stormwind, while William works in Goldshire.",al={"william pestle brother","are william and morgan related","pestle brothers"},it="ties"},{q="What role does he play in Elwynn quests?",a="Morgan receives the candles William sends north from Goldshire to Pestle's Apothecary and pays the courier well for delivering them.",al={"shipment to stormwind morgan","morgan pestle quest"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Who is Morgan Pestle?",a="Morgan Pestle is a human alchemist and shopkeeper operating out of the Trade District in Stormwind City. He owns and runs Pestle's Apothecary, dealing in reagents, remedies, and various alchemical mixtures for the city's inhabitants.",al={"who is morgan pestle","morgan pestle lore","who is pestle"},it="identity",add="2e5b0856"},{q="Whose side is Morgan Pestle on?",a="Morgan Pestle is a loyal citizen of the Alliance. Based in the heart of Stormwind City's Trade District, his trade supports the local populace and the broader kingdom.",al={"morgan pestle faction","is morgan pestle alliance","morgan pestle allegiance"},it="side",add="ae642a6d"},{q="Why is Morgan Pestle here?",a="Morgan Pestle resides in Stormwind City to manage his shop, Pestle's Apothecary. From his storefront in the bustling Trade District, he sells potions and trinkets and receives shipments from his brother William, who works out of Goldshire.",al={"why is morgan pestle in stormwind","morgan pestle trade district"},it="why_here",add="2ef8a55a"}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="Morgan relies on fresh ingredients gathered across Elwynn Forest and beyond to supply his apothecary in Stormwind's Trade District.",["faction:Alliance"]="If you arrive in Stormwind from Elwynn as an Alliance adventurer, Morgan's shop offers practical alchemical supplies and local city deliveries."},kw={"alchemist","morgan pestle","pestle apothecary","shipment to stormwind","stormwind","trade district","william pestle"},rel={"npc:william-pestle","subzone:trade-district","zone:stormwind","quest:61","zone:elwynn"},src={"Morgan Pestle"}}
E["npc:nara-meideros"] = {t="npc",n="Nara Meideros",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind's Park, Nara Meideros guides young seekers in Elune's teachings. As a night elf priestess in the human capital, she offers a familiar spiritual presence to her kin.",h="In Stormwind's Park, Nara Meideros guides young seekers in Elune's teachings.",sec={{t="A Priestess in Stormwind",b="Nara Meideros serves Elune far from Kalimdor, across the Great Sea in Stormwind City. In the Park, night elf druids and priests have tended a green refuge. Nara guides young seekers in devotion to the Moon Goddess. Human priests serve the Holy Light in nearby Cathedral Square, while Nara gives night elves visiting or living in the Eastern Kingdoms a connection to their own faith.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Nara Meideros?",a="Find Nara Meideros in the Park district of Stormwind City, among moonwells and towering trees that recall home to night elf travelers.",al={"nara meideros location","where is nara meideros","park priest trainer"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What role does Nara Meideros serve?",a="Nara trains priests, helping novices and growing priests. She directs human priests to the Cathedral of Light to learn devotional spells such as Desperate Prayer.",al={"what does nara do","nara meideros purpose","who is nara meideros"},it="purpose"},{q="Why is a night elf priestess residing in Stormwind?",a="Night elf ties with the Grand Alliance are growing stronger. Emissaries, druids, and priests from Darnassus keep an active presence in the Park to aid their kin and represent their spiritual traditions.",al={"why is she in stormwind","night elf in stormwind"},it="why_here"},{q="Who is Nara Meideros?",a="Nara Meideros is a night elf priestess of the moon serving the Sisterhood of Elune. Stationed abroad among the mortal allies of the Alliance, she guides devoted acolytes in the spiritual traditions and holy disciplines of her people.",al={"who is nara meideros","who is nara","nara meideros lore"},it="identity",add="07f550b7"},{q="Whose side is Nara Meideros on?",a="She is wholly loyal to the Kaldorei and the Alliance, serving as an ambassador of night elven faith and providing guidance to priests who seek communion with the divine Light and the teachings of Elune.",al={"nara meideros faction","who does nara meideros serve","nara meideros alliance"},it="side",add="6f64ae70"}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a night elf priest traveling in the Eastern Kingdoms, you can seek Nara's guidance in important racial devotions without returning to Kalimdor.",["race:NightElf"]="Far from Ashenvale and Teldrassil, you can find a comforting piece of home with Nara Meideros in the Park, amid Stormwind's stone walls."},kw={"elune","nara meideros","night elf priest","priest trainer","stormwind","the park"},rel={"subzone:park","zone:stormwind","quest:5634","quest:5628","topic:night-elf","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Nara Meideros"}}
E["npc:nikova-raskol"] = {t="npc",n="Nikova Raskol",z="stormwind",s="In Old Town, Nikova Raskol grieves for her murdered grandson. The elderly Stormwind townswoman seeks justice against the Defias Brotherhood rioters held in the Stockade.",h="In Old Town, Nikova Raskol grieves for her murdered grandson.",sec={{t="A Grandmother's Grief",b="Nikova Raskol wanders Old Town, carrying the grief of a recent loss. Her beloved grandson, Mac, was slain by Defias Brotherhood brigands. While the kingdom faces treason on a grand scale, Nikova bears the private cost of the Brotherhood's lawless rampage.",sp=0},{t="Vengeance in the Stockade",b="Many criminals who wrecked havoc were captured and locked in the Stockade, but a violent inmate rebellion has seized the prison. The guards have failed to restore order, and Nikova turns to adventurers heading inside. She asks them to bring back red Defias bandanas as proof that her grandson's killers have faced retribution.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Nikova Raskol?",a="Nikova Raskol is an elderly Stormwind resident who walks Old Town's oval road. She mourns her grandson Mac, murdered by Defias thugs.",al={"who is nikova","nikova raskol role","nikova raskol lore"},it="identity"},{q="What happened to her grandson Mac?",a="Mac was fourteen. When the army marched to the front, he took up arms as a guard in the Stockade, where the Defias are locked up. After he reprimanded prisoners for tearing their wool blankets into gang scarves, they stabbed him in the back.",al={"who is mac","what happened to mac","how did mac die"},it="ties"},{q="Why does she want red bandanas from the Stockade?",a="The red bandana marks the Defias Brotherhood. Nikova asks fighters entering the rebellious Stockade to bring back the neckerchiefs as proof that the criminals who took innocent lives have been dealt with.",al={"color of blood","why red bandanas","defias bandanas"},it="wants"},{q="Where can Nikova Raskol be found?",a="Nikova paces along Old Town's main thoroughfare, near the Pig and Whistle Tavern and Stormwind City's training grounds.",al={"where is nikova","nikova location","nikova raskol path"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Nikova Raskol on?",a="Nikova Raskol stands firmly with Stormwind and the Alliance. As an elderly resident living within the heart of the capital, her hatred is directed entirely at the Defias Brotherhood, whom she holds responsible for murdering her family.",al={"is nikova alliance","nikova raskol faction","whose side is nikova on"},it="side",add="dc3813b4"},{q="Why is Nikova Raskol in Old Town?",a="Nikova wanders the stone streets of Old Town because Stormwind is her home. Consumed by grief and a thirst for justice, she paces the city looking for capable heroes to strike back at the criminal conspirators confined beneath the streets.",al={"why is nikova here","why is nikova raskol in stormwind","nikova raskol old town why"},it="why_here",add="cb2616e5"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance champions in Stormwind, helping Nikova is a reminder that defending the kingdom means protecting ordinary townsfolk whose families have been torn apart by civil unrest."},kw={"defias bandana","mac","nikova raskol","old town","stockade","stormwind","the color of blood"},rel={"quest:388","subzone:stormwind-stockade","subzone:old-town","topic:defias-brotherhood","zone:stormwind","quest:65"},src={"Nikova Raskol"}}
E["npc:orphan-matron-nightingale"] = {t="npc",n="Orphan Matron Nightingale",z="stormwind",s="In Cathedral Square, Orphan Matron Nightingale cares for Stormwind’s orphaned children. She and Matron Shellene give them shelter and guidance, and invite Alliance adventurers to spend Children's Week with them.",h="In Cathedral Square, Orphan Matron Nightingale cares for Stormwind’s orphaned children.",sec={{t="Guardian of the Displaced",b="Outside the orphanage, south-east of the Cathedral of Light, Orphan Matron Nightingale cares for Stormwind’s most vulnerable children. Recent wars, gnoll attacks, and the rise of the Defias Brotherhood have left many without homes or parents. Nightingale and Matron Shellene give them shelter, basic care, and guidance under the Church of the Holy Light’s watch.",sp=0},{t="Children's Week Patron",b="Matron Nightingale believes children need hope as well as food and shelter. Each Children's Week, she asks Alliance heroes to take an orphan on journeys across Azeroth. She hopes meeting celebrated champions will build their confidence, show them the wider world beyond the city walls, and remind them they are not forgotten.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can Orphan Matron Nightingale be found?",a="Orphan Matron Nightingale can be found outside the Stormwind Orphanage in Cathedral Square, south-east of the Cathedral of Light.",al={"matron nightingale location","stormwind orphanage location","where is nightingale"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why are there so many orphans in Stormwind?",a="Stormwind has many orphans because devastating wars, including the Third War, and ongoing skirmishes with the Defias Brotherhood, orc remnants, and hostile beasts have killed many city residents and frontier farmers, leaving children without homes.",al={"why are there orphans","stormwind orphans origin","who are these kids"},it="history"},{q="What is Children's Week?",a="Children's Week is an annual Stormwind celebration organized by Matron Nightingale. Alliance adventurers chaperone an orphan on journeys to see the wonders and heroes of the wider world.",al={"childrens week stormwind","what is children's week","orphan event"}},{q="Who helps Matron Nightingale run the orphanage?",a="Matron Shellene helps Nightingale raise, feed, and shelter the children in and around the orphanage.",al={"other orphan matron","who runs the orphanage","matron shellene"},it="allies"},{q="Who is Orphan Matron Nightingale?",a="Orphan Matron Nightingale is the compassionate caretaker who oversees the Stormwind City orphanage alongside Matron Shellene. Positioned in the heart of Cathedral Square, she devotes her days to sheltering and nurturing children who have lost their families to the relentless wars and hardships threatening the kingdom.",al={"who is matron nightingale","orphan matron nightingale lore","who runs stormwind orphanage"},it="identity",add="9dba66e4"},{q="Whose side is Orphan Matron Nightingale on?",a="She is entirely loyal to the Grand Alliance and the people of Stormwind. Her duties place her under the protective shadow of the Cathedral of Light, working tirelessly to support the kingdom's most vulnerable young citizens and relying on Alliance heroes to enrich the children's lives.",al={"nightingale faction","is nightingale alliance","matron nightingale allegiance"},it="side",add="e8925ab2"},{q="What does Orphan Matron Nightingale want?",a="Her primary concern is the welfare, happiness, and upbringing of the orphans under her watch. She seeks to provide them with a safe haven amidst troubled times, even enlisting experienced travelers during Children's Week to give the youngsters hope and a glimpse of the wider world outside the city walls.",al={"matron nightingale goal","what does nightingale want","nightingale purpose"},it="wants",add="1cac5069"},{q="Why is Orphan Matron Nightingale here?",a="She stays just outside the orphanage steps in Cathedral Square to look after the children in her care and greet visitors. From this bustling, sacred corner of the city, she coordinates the orphanage's daily routines and reaches out to benevolent adventurers willing to help her young charges.",al={"why is matron nightingale in cathedral square","why is nightingale outside orphanage","nightingale location reason"},it="why_here",add="e192fa2f"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance champion, you see in Nightingale the quiet cost of war and the duty to protect the realm’s future generations.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you can recognize the compassion and service Nightingale shows outside the Cathedral of Light, virtues that priests of the Holy Light uphold."},kw={"cathedral square","children's week","matron shellene","nightingale","orphan matron nightingale","stormwind","stormwind orphanage"},rel={"subzone:cathedral-square","subzone:cathedral-of-light","zone:stormwind","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:light","topic:alliance"},src={"Orphan Matron Nightingale"}}
E["npc:osric-strang"] = {t="npc",n="Osric Strang",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind's Old Town, veteran armor merchant Osric Strang supplies weary travelers and Alliance defenders with sturdy gear. His shop, Limited Immunity, specializes in heavy mail and plate armor, along with shields.",h="In Stormwind's Old Town, veteran armor merchant Osric Strang supplies weary travelers and Alliance defenders...",sec={{t="Shopkeeper of Limited Immunity",b="Osric Strang runs Limited Immunity, where fighters find heavy armor and shields. He also helps arriving couriers who need a point of contact in the capital, including those coming from nearby settlements such as Sentinel Hill in Westfall.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What does Osric Strang sell?",a="Osric sells heavy protective armor, including augmented chain, polished scale, solid platemail suits, bucklers, and heater shields.",al={"osric items","what does osric strang have","limited immunity goods"},gp=true},{q="Where can I find Osric Strang?",a="You can find Osric inside Limited Immunity, an armor shop in Old Town near Stormwind's southern district.",al={"osric location","where is osric strang","limited immunity location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why am I sent to Osric Strang on a quest?",a="Couriers carrying goods across the kingdom, including shipments arriving by gryphon master from Westfall, are directed to Osric's shop in Old Town to deliver them and receive return messages.",al={"why talk to osric","osric strang quest","delivery to osric"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Who is Osric Strang?",a="Osric Strang is an armor merchant working out of Limited Immunity, a shop nestled in Stormwind's bustling Old Town. He makes a living outfitting adventurers and city guards with heavy suits of mail, plate, and sturdy shields.",al={"who is osric","osric strang lore","osric strang background"},it="identity",add="a4d8c3b8"},{q="Whose side is Osric Strang on?",a="Osric Strang is a loyal citizen of the Kingdom of Stormwind and stands firmly with the Alliance, proudly providing protective wargear to those who defend the realm.",al={"osric strang faction","osric strang loyalty","is osric alliance"},it="side",add="66b236b5"},{q="Why is Osric Strang in Stormwind?",a="Osric Strang operates Limited Immunity in the heart of Old Town, a district known for its seasoned warriors, craftsmen, and armories. Stormwind offers him a steady stream of recruits, travelers, and defenders looking for dependable heavy armor.",al={"why is osric strang here","osric strang shop","osric strang limited immunity"},it="why_here",add="9aee9a9e"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior visiting Old Town, you can find reliable chain, scale, plate, and shields from Osric, offering dependable bulk protection.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can rely on Stormwind resident Osric to equip the kingdom's defenders and help couriers maintain supply links between Stormwind and outlying settlements."},kw={"dungar longdrink","heavy armor","limited immunity","old town","osric strang","shields","stormwind vendor"},rel={"subzone:old-town","quest:6281","quest:6261","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Osric Strang"}}
E["npc:randis"] = {t="npc",n="Randis",z="stormwind",s="In Cathedral Square, Randis waits for a chance to see the world beyond Stormwind. During Children's Week, he eagerly joins willing adventurers across Alliance lands.",h="In Cathedral Square, Randis waits for a chance to see the world beyond Stormwind.",sec={{t="A Ward of Stormwind",b="Randis lives in the orphanage near Stormwind's Cathedral of Light, one of many children left without family by the realm's conflicts. When Children's Week comes each year, Orphan Matron Nightingale gives sympathetic heroes a whistle and entrusts them with his care. Curious and full of questions, Randis dreams of adventure, asks riddles, and declares that he wants to be king of Stormwind when he grows up.",sp=0},{t="Eyes on the World",b="For Randis, who spends most days in Cathedral Square, leaving the capital is a grand adventure. He remarks that places like Ironforge smell odd, and his wonder shows what Alliance heroes fight to protect.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Randis?",a="Randis is a human child living at the Stormwind Orphanage in Cathedral Square. During Children's Week, willing adventurers can look after him and take him across Alliance lands.",al={"randis npc","who is the human orphan","human orphan stormwind"},it="identity"},{q="How do you meet Randis?",a="During Children's Week, Orphan Matron Nightingale gives adventurers an orphan whistle in Cathedral Square. Blow it, and Randis comes along on your travels.",al={"how to get randis","summon randis","orphan whistle stormwind"},it="arrival",gp=true},{q="What places does Randis want to visit?",a="Randis wants to visit anywhere beyond Stormwind's walls with the hero who takes him along. He has visited Ironforge and says it smells funny there.",al={"randis places","randis sights","childrens week human orphan locations"},it="wants"},{q="Why is Randis living in an orphanage?",a="Randis lost his parents to the constant wars, invasions, and hardships that have struck Stormwind and the wider lands of Azeroth. Many children under Matron Nightingale's care share that loss.",al={"randis parents","why is randis an orphan","stormwind orphanage lore"},it="origin"},{q="Whose side is Randis on?",a="Randis is a young human boy raised in Stormwind City, placing his loyalties entirely with the Alliance. Having spent his childhood under the care of the city's orphanage, he looks up to the great heroes and leaders of the Alliance and even dreams of one day growing up to become the King of Stormwind himself.",al={"randis alliance","is randis alliance","randis faction"},it="side",add="5920bd8f"},{q="Why is Randis in Stormwind?",a="Randis resides in Stormwind City because he is an orphan under the charge of Orphan Matron Nightingale at the local orphanage in Cathedral Square. During the annual celebration of Children's Week, he waits eagerly for traveling adventurers who answer the Matron's call to take him out of the city and show him the wonders of the wider world.",al={"why is randis here","why is randis in stormwind","randis stormwind location"},it="why_here",add="ece316b6"},{q="Who is Randis tied to?",a="Randis is cared for by Orphan Matron Nightingale, who oversees the human orphans living in Stormwind's Cathedral Square. During Children's Week, he relies on compassionate Alliance adventurers to take him along on their travels beyond the city walls.",al={"who looks after randis","randis connections","who is randis associated with"},it="ties",add="33179f48"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance champion, caring for Randis during Children's Week reminds you that your battles protect the next generation of civilians and dreamers."},kw={"cathedral square","children's week","human orphan","matron nightingale","randis","stormwind"},rel={"npc:orphan-matron-nightingale","subzone:cathedral-square","zone:stormwind","zone:ironforge","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Randis"}}
E["npc:rema-schneider"] = {t="npc",n="Rema Schneider",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind City, Rema Schneider works from the Canal Tailor and Fit Shop. She is a human citizen who often helps local shopkeepers and artisans with trade deliveries.",h="In Stormwind City, Rema Schneider works from the Canal Tailor and Fit Shop.",sec={{t="Shopkeeper of the Canals",b="Rema Schneider manages daily trade from the Canal Tailor and Fit Shop. The shop stands just west of the stone bridge into Cathedral Square, along Stormwind's canals. Cloth and finished garments move between local craftsmen, and Rema relies on helpful couriers to carry supplies between workshops.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Rema Schneider located?",a="Rema Schneider works inside the Canal Tailor and Fit Shop in Stormwind City. It sits along the Canals, just west of the bridge into Cathedral Square.",al={"rema schneider location","where is rema","find rema schneider"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What role does Rema play in Stormwind?",a="Rema coordinates local trade errands, supply packages, and resupply orders between merchants and craftspeople across the city.",al={"who is rema schneider","what does rema do","rema schneider purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Does Rema teach tailoring?",a="No. Rema works from the Canal Tailor and Fit Shop and handles shipments of tailor goods, but she is neither a profession trainer nor a primary vendor.",al={"is rema a tailor trainer","rema tailoring training"},gp=true},{q="Who is Rema Schneider?",a="Rema Schneider is a human citizen and tailor working in Stormwind City. You can find her attending to business inside the Canal Tailor and Fit Shop, situated along the Canals just west of the bridge leading toward Cathedral Square.",al={"who is rema schneider","rema schneider identity","rema schneider"},it="identity",add="080a82f0"},{q="Whose side is Rema Schneider on?",a="Rema Schneider is a loyal subject of the Kingdom of Stormwind and firmly allied with the Grand Alliance. She conducts her tailoring trade within the capital and assists local couriers and merchants across the kingdom.",al={"rema schneider faction","is rema schneider alliance","rema schneider allegiance"},it="side",add="37d985b5"},{q="What does Rema Schneider want?",a="Rema is focused on running her tailoring business and maintaining trade connections throughout the realm. She relies on passing couriers and adventurers to carry packages and resupply local craftsmen who depend on her materials.",al={"what does rema want","rema schneider goal","rema schneider quests"},it="wants",add="c7f62ca5"},{q="Why is Rema Schneider here?",a="Rema works as a resident tailor at the Canal Tailor and Fit Shop. The Canals offer a bustling route for commerce between the districts of Stormwind, making it an ideal post for managing her goods and deliveries.",al={"why is rema in stormwind","why is rema schneider here","rema schneider canal tailor"},it="why_here",add="d4111a95"}},ang={["profession:Tailoring"]="Rema works inside the Canal Tailor and Fit Shop, an everyday part of Stormwind's clothworking trade.",["faction:Alliance"]="As a traveler or new recruit in Stormwind, you may run simple courier tasks for Rema while getting your bearings in the capital."},kw={"canal tailor","harlan needs a resupply","package for thurman","rema schneider","stormwind canals"},rel={"quest:333","quest:334","zone:stormwind","subzone:canals-stormwind-city","subzone:cathedral-square","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Rema Schneider"}}
E["npc:renato-gallina"] = {t="npc",n="Renato Gallina",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind's Trade District, Renato Gallina calls travelers toward his family's winery.",h="In Stormwind's Trade District, Renato Gallina calls travelers toward his family's winery.",sec={{t="Voice of the Gallina Winery",b="Renato Gallina calls to passers-by among the Trade District stalls, proclaiming his family's vintages the finest in Stormwind. The Gallina family runs a winery along the Canals, and Renato promotes it with pamphlets. Travelers can bring one to his sister Suzetta at the shop for a free bottle of wine.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Renato Gallina?",a="Renato Gallina is a human barker in Stormwind City's Trade District. He belongs to the Gallina family and promotes their winery to locals and visiting travelers.",al={"renato gallina","who is renato","wine barker stormwind"},it="identity"},{q="Where is the Gallina Winery located?",a="The Gallina Winery is along the Canals of Stormwind City, just off the main commercial quarters.",al={"where is gallina winery","stormwind wine shop location","gallina winery"},it="place"},{q="What does Renato ask adventurers to do?",a="Renato gives travelers a pamphlet for his family's wine shop and asks them to bring it to his sister, Suzetta Gallina, at the winery along the Canals. The pamphlet earns them a free bottle of wine.",al={"renato gallina quest","wine shop advert quest","what does renato want"},it="wants"},{q="Whose side is Renato Gallina on?",a="Renato is a loyal citizen of Stormwind and a member of the Alliance. His heart belongs to his city, his trade, and above all, the success of the Gallina family's commercial ambitions.",al={"renato gallina faction","renato gallina allegiance","is renato alliance"},it="side",add="fce75f2a"},{q="Why is Renato Gallina in the Trade District?",a="Renato stands in the bustling Trade District square to drum up business for his family's vintner trade. Rather than sitting behind a counter, he spends his days advertising Gallina Winery directly to travelers and townsfolk passing through Stormwind.",al={"why is renato here","renato gallina trade district","what is renato doing here"},it="why_here",add="c03f1140"},{q="Who is Renato Gallina tied to?",a="Renato is bound closely to the Gallina family, the proprietors of the Gallina Winery situated along Stormwind's Canals. His daily efforts are devoted entirely to promoting their vintage and expanding their clientele across the city.",al={"renato gallina ties","renato gallina family","who does renato work with"},it="ties",add="9e1708f4"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler arriving in the capital, you can see Renato at work promoting Stormwind's local commerce and domestic trades."},kw={"canals","gallina winery","renato gallina","stormwind wine","trade district","wine shop advert"},rel={"subzone:trade-district","subzone:canals-stormwind-city","quest:332","zone:stormwind","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Renato Gallina"}}
E["npc:suzetta-gallina"] = {t="npc",n="Suzetta Gallina",z="stormwind",s="At the Gallina Winery in Stormwind City, Suzetta Gallina tends the family wine business.",h="At the Gallina Winery in Stormwind City, Suzetta Gallina tends the family wine business.",sec={{t="A Taste of the Canals",b="Suzetta Gallina helps run the Gallina Winery along Stormwind's Canals. The shop offers wines imported from across the kingdom or crafted there. Her family supplies taverns, nobles, and common folk. Suzetta is no figure in high politics, but her work keeps the capital's trade moving through troubled times.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Suzetta Gallina?",a="Suzetta Gallina belongs to the family that runs the Gallina Winery along Stormwind City's Canals.",al={"suzetta gallina","who is suzetta","gallina winery woman"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Suzetta Gallina?",a="Find Suzetta inside the Gallina Winery, along the canals between the Trade District and Cathedral Square in Stormwind City.",al={"suzetta gallina location","where is suzetta","gallina winery location"},it="why_here",gp=true},{q="Does Suzetta offer any work for travelers?",a="Suzetta does not offer work directly. Her brother Renato gives out Wine Tickets; bring one to her at the Gallina Winery to receive a complimentary bottle of the family's special pinot noir.",al={"suzetta quests","gallina wine quest","wine shop advert"},it="wants",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Suzetta Gallina on?",a="Suzetta Gallina is a loyal citizen of the Alliance. Living and working peacefully in the heart of Stormwind City, she and her family cater to the capital's tavern keeps, nobles, and common folk alike.",al={"suzetta gallina faction","is suzetta gallina alliance","who does suzetta serve"},it="side",add="f0d37e75"},{q="What does Suzetta Gallina want?",a="Suzetta wants to keep her family's wine business flourishing. Alongside her kin, she tends to the Gallina Winery, ensuring their casks and bottles find eager buyers across the city and spreading word of their vintage to thirsty travelers.",al={"suzetta gallina goal","what does suzetta want","what is suzetta gallina doing"},it="wants",add="44c42184"},{q="Why is Suzetta Gallina here in Stormwind?",a="Suzetta stays in the Canal District because it houses the Gallina Winery, the center of her family's trade. From here, she helps manage the business and stays close to the bustling taverns and trade thoroughfares of Stormwind.",al={"why is suzetta gallina here","why is suzetta in the canals","suzetta gallina location lore"},it="why_here",add="290e58c2"},{q="Who is Suzetta Gallina tied to?",a="Suzetta is part of the wine-selling Gallina family, working alongside her kin within the family shop to produce and sell vintage wines throughout Stormwind City.",al={"suzetta gallina family","who is suzetta related to","gallina winery family"},it="ties",add="c1c3d801"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler returning from the dangers of Elwynn or Westfall, a stop at Suzetta's shop offers a reminder of peaceful life in the capital."},kw={"gallina winery","stormwind canals","stormwind wine","suzetta gallina","wine shop advert"},rel={"quest:332","zone:stormwind","subzone:canals-stormwind-city","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Suzetta Gallina"}}
E["npc:tyrion"] = {t="npc",n="Tyrion",z="stormwind",s="Inside Stormwind Keep, Tyrion watches the court and aids covert work. The gnome works with Elling Trias to gather intelligence and counter plots against the kingdom.",h="Inside Stormwind Keep, Tyrion watches the court and aids covert work.",sec={{t="A Quiet Presence in the Keep",b="Tyrion keeps to the halls of Stormwind Keep, watching the palace and staying in touch with contacts beyond official oversight.",sp=0},{t="Shadows and Espionage",b="Elling Trias, a cheese merchant in the Trade District, trusts Tyrion with sensitive matters. Trias runs a discreet information network and sends reliable operatives to Tyrion when the House of Nobles' bureaucracy must be bypassed.",sp=0},{t="Uncovering the Threat",b="Tyrion helps investigators enter guarded places and secure sensitive goods in the city. His work reveals danger within the royal heart of the kingdom, and he warns his allies before an organized strike can threaten Stormwind's leaders.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Tyrion?",a="Tyrion is a gnome operative inside Stormwind Keep. He handles covert work and intelligence gathering beyond the usual royal channels.",al={"who is this gnome","tyrion identity","what does tyrion do"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Tyrion?",a="Tyrion is inside Stormwind Keep in Stormwind City, watching for agents sent by his trusted contacts.",al={"tyrion location","where is tyrion","find tyrion"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is his connection to Elling Trias?",a="Tyrion and Elling Trias are longtime friends and collaborators. Trias gathers whispers through his trade connections and sends reliable adventurers to Tyrion when covert work inside the Keep is needed.",al={"tyrion and elling trias","does tyrion know trias","trias connection"},it="ties"},{q="What quests does Tyrion offer?",a="Tyrion is involved in covert operations including 'Infiltrating the Castle', 'Items of Some Consequence', and warning allies during 'The Attack!'.",al={"tyrion quests","what quests does he give"},gp=true},{q="Why is a gnome handling secret operations in the human court?",a="Gnomes are key allies of the Alliance. Tyrion brings sharp intellect, stealth, and technical resourcefulness to secret work in the human court.",al={"why is a gnome in stormwind keep","gnome operative keep"},it="why_here"},{q="What is the nature of the plot Tyrion is investigating?",a="Tyrion tracks stolen intelligence and hidden plots within the royal court, leading to an armed ambush inside the city.",al={"tyrion conspiracy","what is tyrion investigating"},sp=1,it="wants"},{q="Whose side is Tyrion on?",a="Tyrion works quietly from within Stormwind Keep alongside his old friend, the master cheese merchant and rogue informant Elling Trias. Though operating through shadows, whispers, and clandestine spycraft, his loyalty lies with the integrity of Stormwind and the Alliance, quietly looking out for the kingdom's safety against unseen domestic threats.",al={"is tyrion loyal to stormwind","tyrion faction","who does tyrion work for"},it="side",add="f469be85"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, Tyrion shows the subtlety and intellect gnomes bring to Alliance espionage, working beneath the notice of human nobility.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue involved in Elling Trias's covert work, you can rely on Tyrion as an ally inside Stormwind Keep.",["faction:Alliance"]="Tyrion's intelligence work helps protect the crown from covert threats in the kingdom's capital."},kw={"elling trias","gnome","infiltrating the castle","items of some consequence","spy","stormwind keep","the attack","tyrion"},rel={"npc:elling-trias","subzone:stormwind-keep","zone:stormwind","quest:2745","quest:2746","quest:434","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:gnome"},src={"Tyrion"}}
E["npc:watcher-backus"] = {t="npc",n="Watcher Backus",z="stormwind",s="Along Duskwood's road, Watcher Backus keeps watch for danger and suspicious traffic tied to Stormwind's political intrigues. He patrols between Darkshire and Manor Mistmantle, watching for undead and strange travelers.",h="Along Duskwood's road, Watcher Backus keeps watch for danger and suspicious traffic tied to Stormwind's...",sec={{t="A Patrol in the Shadows",b="Watcher Backus walks a solitary beat north of Darkshire, passing near Manor Mistmantle. Like the rest of the Night Watch, he struggles against Duskwood's curse. Stormwind's garrison gives the region little support, so local volunteers guard its misty paths on their own. Backus keeps beast and ghoul at bay along the road.",sp=0},{t="Eyes on the Road",b="Watcher Backus sees much of the traffic skirting Darkshire from his isolated route. When royal investigators follow the disappearance of a high-ranking diplomat down south, he recalls odd Defias activity around Addle's Stead.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Watcher Backus?",a="Watcher Backus is a human guard in the beleaguered Night Watch, the militia defending Darkshire and Duskwood's roads.",al={"who is backus","watcher backus role","backus duskwood"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Watcher Backus be found?",a="Watcher Backus patrols the main road north from Darkshire toward Manor Mistmantle in Duskwood.",al={"where is backus","backus location","backus patrol route"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the Night Watch?",a="The Night Watch is a local volunteer militia formed by Duskwood's citizens to defend against undead, worgen, and feral beasts after Stormwind withdrew its official military presence.",al={"what is the night watch","night watch duskwood","darkshire guards"}},{q="How is Backus involved with The Missing Diplomat?",a="During the search for a missing Stormwind diplomat, clues lead adventurers to Duskwood. Watcher Backus recalls recent Defias activity around Addle's Stead and helps examine documents recovered from their hideout there.",al={"backus missing diplomat","missing diplomat quest backus"},sp=1,it="purpose"},{q="Does Watcher Backus have any town gossip surrounding him?",a="Darkshire's fellow guard Watcher Brownell is known to harbor an unspoken crush on Backus, a rare piece of lighthearted town gossip amid the gloom.",al={"backus brownell","watcher brownell crush"}},{q="Why does Backus patrol alone near Manor Mistmantle?",a="The Night Watch is stretched thin across the entire territory, leaving few able-bodied defenders to spare. Watchers like Backus must handle long, dangerous patrol routes alone.",al={"why alone","backus danger"},it="why_here"},{q="Whose side is Watcher Backus on?",a="Watcher Backus stands squarely with the Night Watch and the beleaguered people of Darkshire. As one of Duskwood's dedicated local defenders, he serves the Alliance and answers to the town's leadership, braving the shadowed roads day and night to protect travelers and residents from the ravenous horrors prowling the gloom.",al={"backus faction","who does watcher backus serve","watcher backus allegiance"},it="side",add="cd7ae440"},{q="What does Watcher Backus want?",a="Backus wants to keep the roads of Duskwood safe and see that justice is done in a land abandoned by Stormwind's army. When travelers or investigators bring trouble his way, he focuses on clearing dangerous suspects, keeping his patrol route clear of undead, and ensuring the survival of Darkshire's beleaguered folk.",al={"watcher backus goal","what is backus trying to do","backus motive"},it="wants",add="f48ed911"},{q="Who is Watcher Backus tied to?",a="Beyond his comrades in the Night Watch who patrol the gloomy woods beside him, Backus has caught the eye of fellow guard Watcher Brownell, who harbors an unmistakable crush on him. He also coordinates with agents investigating suspicious activity along the roads, linking him directly to broader inquiries concerning Stormwind.",al={"watcher backus connections","who knows watcher backus","watcher backus relations"},it="ties",add="8919f8c2"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance agents tracking a missing diplomat, Backus is a vital contact with ground-level intelligence on the frontier.",["race:Human"]="As a human, Backus shows the grit of Duskwood's defenders, abandoned by the capital yet determined to hold the roads."},kw={"backus","darkshire","duskwood","manor mistmantle","night watch","the missing diplomat","watcher backus"},rel={"quest:1241","zone:duskwood","subzone:darkshire","subzone:manor-mistmantle"},src={"Watcher Backus"}}
E["npc:wynne-larson"] = {t="npc",n="Wynne Larson",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind's Mage Quarter, Wynne Larson supplies mages across the kingdom with robes. Human clothier Wynne relies on local craftsmen since Dalaran and Quel'Thalas fell in the Third War, and points spellcasters toward rare materials for enchanted garments.",h="In Stormwind's Mage Quarter, Wynne Larson supplies mages across the kingdom with robes.",sec={{t="A New Arcane Market",b="Before the Third War, Dalaran and Quel'Thalas supplied the finest woven fabrics and enchanted vestments. Their destruction crippled the old trade routes and arcane textile production. In Stormwind's Mage Quarter, Wynne Larson now works with local tailors and enchanters such as Lucan Cordell. Together, they meet the city's growing demand for robes and spellwoven gear.",sp=0},{t="Crafting Sorcerous Robes",b="Novice and journeyman mages seeking arcane garments come to Wynne's shop. She knows what materials are needed for vestments such as Manaweave Robes and Astral Knot Garments. To find those materials, she sends arcane practitioners into dangerous places to recover rare reagents like pristine spider silk. Her work helps keep Stormwind's mages outfitted despite shortages from the north.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Wynne Larson?",a="You can find Wynne Larson in Stormwind City's Mage Quarter, where she sells arcane cloth chestpieces and garments to spellcasters.",al={"wynne larson location","where is wynne larson","mage robe vendor stormwind"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Wynne mention Dalaran and Quel'Thalas?",a="Before the Third War, Dalaran and Quel'Thalas were the Eastern Kingdoms' main sources of enchanted fabrics. Their destruction cut off imports, so Stormwind's merchants rely on local craftsmen and rare materials from farther afield.",al={"wynne dalaran dialogue","quelthalas robes","why are robes hard to find"},it="history"},{q="What quests involve Wynne Larson?",a="Wynne helps mages obtain tailored arcane garments through Gathering Materials, Manaweave Robe, Pristine Spider Silk, and Astral Knot Garment.",al={"wynne larson quests","robe quests stormwind","manaweave robe quest"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="What does Wynne Larson sell?",a="Wynne sells basic and intermediate cloth robes, including Burning Robes, Chromatic Robes, Double-Stitched Robes, and Silver Dress Robes.",al={"wynne larson goods","what robes does wynne sell"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Who does Wynne rely on for crafting supplies in Stormwind?",a="Wynne relies on local artisans, especially enchanter Lucan Cordell and other Stormwind tradesmen, to weave and enchant the goods she sells.",al={"who makes wynnes robes","lucan cordell connection"},it="ties"},{q="Is Wynne Larson related to other Larsons in Stormwind?",a="Wynne shares her surname with Evan Larson, a Stormwind clothier, and Jenny Larson. The shared name suggests a family of tradesfolk in the city's garment trade.",al={"larson family stormwind","evan larson","jenny larson"},it="ties"},{q="Who is Wynne Larson?",a="Wynne Larson is a respected human robe merchant doing business in the Mage Quarter of Stormwind City. She caters primarily to spellcasters and tailoring apprentices, dealing in high-quality cloth garments and arcane materials sourced from local artisans.",al={"who is wynne larson","wynne larson identity","who is wynne"},it="identity",add="61901341"},{q="Whose side is Wynne Larson on?",a="Wynne Larson is a loyal citizen of Stormwind and a proud member of the Alliance. She works closely with local human craftsmen and the city's mage community to supply Alliance casters with fine garments.",al={"wynne larson faction","who does wynne larson serve","wynne larson alliance"},it="side",add="f66b818d"},{q="Why is Wynne Larson in the Mage Quarter?",a="Wynne sets up her shop in the Mage Quarter because that is where Stormwind's scholars, arcanists, and enchanters congregate. Selling robes and assisting apprentice spellcasters makes the district the natural home for her trade.",al={"why is wynne here","why is wynne in mage quarter","wynne larson location purpose"},it="why_here",add="3ea6d1a4"},{q="What does Wynne Larson want?",a="With Dalaran destroyed and Quel'Thalas ruined, fine magical textiles are rare. Wynne wants to keep Stormwind's spellcasters outfitted in premium attire by procuring exotic materials—such as pristine spider silk—and supporting local tradesmen.",al={"what does wynne want","wynne larson goals","wynne larson motive"},it="wants",add="d20d9bb4"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you can turn to Wynne early in your arcane path for help tailoring Manaweave and Astral Knot garments.",["profession:Tailoring"]="As a tailor, you can see how clothiers and tailors help Stormwind after the northern textile centers fell.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can see Stormwind stepping forward to provide self-sufficient arcane craftsmanship for the surviving Alliance races."},kw={"astral knot garment","dalaran","mage quarter","manaweave robe","quel'thalas","robe vendor","stormwind","wynne larson"},rel={"subzone:mage-quarter","zone:stormwind","quest:1941","quest:1942","quest:1961","quest:1940","subzone:dalaran","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Wynne Larson"}}
E["npc:zardeth-of-the-black-claw"] = {t="npc",n="Zardeth of the Black Claw",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind's Mage Quarter, Zardeth of the Black Claw protects a hidden warlock cabal from scrutiny. He dwells in the chambers beneath the Slaughtered Lamb and poses as an ordinary patron. When curious nobles look too closely, he makes sure their inquiries end for good.",h="In Stormwind's Mage Quarter, Zardeth of the Black Claw protects a hidden warlock cabal from scrutiny.",sec={{t="A Shadow Beneath the Lamb",b="Beneath the Slaughtered Lamb, tunnels shelter those who practice darker arts while the Mage Quarter's spires study arcane discipline in the open. Zardeth of the Black Claw works from these crypts, guarding warlocks who hide right beneath the city guard's nose. The Alliance condemns fel magic, so the cabal survives by keeping its presence secret and removing threats before royal investigators arrive.",sp=0},{t="Silencing the Nobility",b="Lord Baurles K. Wishock learned whispers of the hidden warlock coven and began urging the House of Nobles to launch a full investigation. Zardeth feared that scrutiny would destroy the enclave beneath the Slaughtered Lamb, so he arranged a secret response. Knowing the lord favored fine liquor, Zardeth sent an operative across the eastern kingdoms to collect two rare, lethal plants: the Tear of Tilloa from Duskwood and Musquash Root from beneath the Stonewrought Dam.",sp=1},{t="A Noble Brew",b="Zardeth mixed the gathered plants with stout ale to make Black Claw Stout, a lethal drink disguised as an ordinary luxury gift. The poisoned brew reached Wishock's estate and killed him swiftly and quietly. With the lord dead and his campaign ended before the crown could intervene, Zardeth and the other warlocks kept their hidden enclave beneath the Slaughtered Lamb safe.",sp=2}},faq={{q="Who is Zardeth of the Black Claw?",a="Zardeth is a human warlock who keeps watch over the hidden brotherhood in the crypts beneath the Slaughtered Lamb in Stormwind's Mage Quarter. He deflects suspicion and handles threats to the warlocks' secret presence in the city.",al={"zardeth","who is zardeth","zardeth stormwind"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Zardeth?",a="Zardeth can be found beneath the Slaughtered Lamb in the southern half of Stormwind City's Mage Quarter. Enter the tavern, find the passage descending at the back, and follow the winding catacombs to the warlock enclave.",al={"zardeth location","where is zardeth","zardeth slaughter lamb"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Zardeth want Lord Wishock dead?",a="Lord Baurles K. Wishock found evidence of warlocks beneath Stormwind and urged the city's nobility to investigate. An official inquiry could have led the authorities to root out and execute the Slaughtered Lamb coven.",al={"why kill wishock","lord wishock target","noble brew reason"},it="motive"},{q="What is Black Claw Stout?",a="Black Claw Stout is a lethal drink Zardeth brewed from stout and two rare poisonous plants, the Tear of Tilloa from Darkshire and Musquash Root from the Wetlands. He made it look like an expensive vintage to quietly kill Lord Wishock.",al={"black claw stout","what is the brew","wishock poison"},it="item"},{q="What is the Black Claw?",a="The Black Claw is Zardeth's affiliation or title within Stormwind's hidden warlock network. Its members evade the Stormwind guard and the Kirin Tor, using lethal measures to protect their secrecy.",al={"black claw meaning","who are the black claw","black claw warlock"},it="origin"},{q="Why are warlocks allowed in Stormwind at all?",a="Warlocks are not openly tolerated in Stormwind, so they hide in the cellars beneath the Slaughtered Lamb. The authorities may turn a blind eye for pragmatic reasons, or remain unaware because agents like Zardeth kill those who prepare to expose the warlocks.",al={"are warlocks legal","stormwind warlock lore","why warlock in city"},it="history"},{q="Whose side is Zardeth of the Black Claw on?",a="Zardeth looks after the survival of Stormwind's hidden warlocks rather than the crown's laws. While he operates under the banner of the Alliance from beneath the Mage Quarter, his loyalty belongs strictly to the coven secluded within the Slaughtered Lamb, ready to remove any noble or official who threatens to expose their dark studies.",al={"zardeth faction","who does zardeth serve","is zardeth loyal to stormwind"},it="side",add="ec5a54de"},{q="What does Zardeth of the Black Claw want?",a="Zardeth aims to protect his enclave of warlocks from scrutiny by the Stormwind nobility. When Lord Wishock caught wind of their subterranean establishment and pushed for a formal investigation, Zardeth immediately sought to orchestrate the meddling nobleman's quiet and permanent removal.",al={"what is zardeths goal","zardeth plan","what does zardeth want"},sp=1,it="wants",add="212e3858"},{q="Why is Zardeth of the Black Claw here in Stormwind?",a="Zardeth operates from the catacombs of the Slaughtered Lamb, using the tavern's unassuming facade to practice fel magic in secret. He remains on watch to intercept external threats, ensuring the practitioners gathered below can pursue their forbidden arts unhindered by city authorities.",al={"why is zardeth here","zardeth slaughtered lamb purpose","why did zardeth come to stormwind"},it="why_here",add="f970876d"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a human warlock, Zardeth shows the cold pragmatism some rely on to survive in the heart of the Alliance, where survival can depend on pre-emptive killings.",["faction:Alliance"]="For an Alliance loyalist, Zardeth reveals a corrupt underbelly beneath Stormwind's gleaming streets.",["profession:Herbalism"]="As a herbalist, you can see how Zardeth's plot turns poisonous plants like the Tear of Tilloa and Musquash Root into lethal tools."},kw={"a noble brew","baurles wishock","black claw","mage quarter","musquash root","slaughtered lamb","tear of tilloa","warlock","zardeth"},rel={"subzone:slaughtered-lamb","npc:lord-baurles-k-wishock","quest:335","quest:397","subzone:mage-quarter","zone:stormwind","subzone:darkshire","subzone:stonewrought-dam"},src={"Zardeth of the Black Claw"}}
E["quest:1075"] = {t="quest",n="A Scroll from Mauren",z="stormwind",s="Gaxim Rustfizzle needs arcane help to trigger his NG-5 explosives from afar. He sends you to Collin Mauren in Stormwind, where gnomish ingenuity meets human arcane craft.",h="Gaxim Rustfizzle needs arcane help to trigger his NG-5 explosives from afar.",sec={{t="A Spark Across Distances",b="Gaxim Rustfizzle seeks a safer way to set off his NG-5 explosives. Mechanical fuses cannot give him the remote trigger he wants: one button should ignite the charges while he stays at a safe distance. He turns to arcane magic to bridge that gap.",sp=0},{t="The Mage Quarter Connection",b="Gaxim sends you to Collin Mauren in Stormwind's Mage Quarter for the needed spellwork. Mauren is a human spellcaster whose practical knowledge of the arcane may help bind an explosive ignition to a distant command. His work begins the incantation Gaxim needs for his dangerous project.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends me to Collin Mauren?",a="Gaxim Rustfizzle sends you to Collin Mauren. He needs an arcane formula from his human acquaintance to finish a remote detonator.",al={"quest giver","who gives a scroll from mauren","gaxim quest"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Collin Mauren be found?",a="Collin Mauren is in Stormwind City's Mage Quarter. Look for him among the instructors, apprentices, and arcane researchers around the district's towers and shops.",al={"collin mauren location","where is collin mauren","find mauren"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Gaxim need a spell for an explosive device?",a="Gaxim wants to set off his NG-5 explosives with one button from a safe distance. He seeks Mauren's arcane knowledge for an instant remote trigger because mechanical means can be cumbersome or unreliable over long ranges.",al={"why magic for bombs","remote detonation lore","why see a mage"},it="motive"},{q="What is the NG-5?",a="NG-5, or Nitromirglyceronium, is a volatile explosive brewed by Gaxim's old colleague Lomac Gearstrip in Ironforge. Gaxim needs a remote detonation system so the person setting it off can stay well beyond the blast radius.",al={"ng-5","what is ng5","gaxim explosive"},it="item"},{q="What comes next after speaking with Collin Mauren?",a="After Collin Mauren considers the request for a distant detonation spell, he asks you to help him in Westfall in Devils in Westfall.",al={"next quest","what follows a scroll from mauren","collin mauren follow up"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Is Collin Mauren a gnome or a human?",a="Collin Mauren is a human mage. Gaxim notes that Mauren should be easy to spot among the crowds in Stormwind because he is human.",al={"collin mauren race","what race is mauren","is mauren a human"},it="identity"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you know that the Kirin Tor and Stormwind's arcane practitioners work with engineers. They apply evocation and transmutation to mechanical problems.",["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you are never shy about joining technology with sorcery when it promises a more catastrophic explosion from a comfortable distance.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you know that volatile black powder and arcane catalysts can solve problems such as remote ignition.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you see gnomish tinkerers working with the human wizards who study in Stormwind's Mage Quarter."},kw={"collin mauren","devils in westfall","explosives","gaxim rustfizzle","mage quarter","ng-5","remote detonator","stormwind"},rel={"npc:collin-mauren","npc:gaxim-rustfizzle","subzone:mage-quarter","quest:1076","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Gaxim Rustfizzle",["end"]="Collin Mauren",level="21",faction="Alliance",id=1075},src={"A Scroll from Mauren"}}
E["quest:1076"] = {t="quest",n="Devils in Westfall",z="stormwind",s="Dust devils roam Westfall, and Collin Mauren needs their remains for a spell. The Mage Quarter wizard is helping Gaxim Rustfizzle with an unusual experiment. Their work calls for a messaging scroll, and the dust holds what Mauren needs to enchant it.",h="Dust devils roam Westfall, and Collin Mauren needs their remains for a spell.",sec={{t="A Messenger's Components",b="Collin Mauren is preparing a messaging scroll for Gaxim Rustfizzle. The wizard is helping the tinkerer with an unusual venture, but the spell needs more than ink and vellum. Dust devils roam Westfall with elemental magic swirling within them. Their remains provide the volatile medium Mauren needs to bind Gaxim's spell to parchment.",sp=0},{t="The Elemental Wastes",b="Westfall was once Stormwind's fertile breadbasket. Drought, banditry, and neglect have left its fields arid and wild. Dust devils roam there, threatening travelers and lone homesteaders. Their residue holds the focused elemental essence Mauren needs to complete the enchantment.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Collin Mauren?",a="Collin Mauren is a human mage in Stormwind's Mage Quarter. He works with spellcasters in the city and sometimes helps outside researchers such as Gaxim Rustfizzle prepare enchanted scrolls and arcane components.",al={"collin mauren","who is the quest giver","mage in stormwind"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Collin Mauren need dust devil debris?",a="Collin Mauren needs dust devil debris to enchant a messaging scroll for Gaxim Rustfizzle. The remains hold elemental energy that helps bind the spell to parchment.",al={"why dust devil debris","what is dust devil debris for","why go to westfall"},it="motive"},{q="Where are dust devils found?",a="Dust devils roam Westfall's dry plains and barren fields, especially the dusty stretches between neglected farmsteads south of the Sentinel Hill road.",al={"dust devil location","where are dust devils","westfall dust devils"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Gaxim Rustfizzle?",a="Gaxim Rustfizzle is an ambitious gnome inventor working on esoteric engineering projects. Collin Mauren helps him prepare enchanted scrolls for his experiments.",al={"gaxim","gaxim rustfizzle","who is gaxim"},it="identity"},{q="What happens after bringing the debris to Mauren?",a="With the debris, Collin Mauren completes the messaging scroll and asks you to take it to Gaxim Rustfizzle, so the inventor can continue his experiments.",al={"quest reward","what comes next","after devils in westfall"},it="next_step"},{q="Are dust devils magical or natural creatures?",a="Dust devils are minor air elementals that appear as living whirlwinds of sand and grit. They thrive in Westfall's dry, unsettled landscape.",al={"are dust devils elementals","dust devil lore"},it="origin"},{q="What is the Dust Devil Debris used for?",a="Collin Mauren requires the remnant debris of a dust devil as a crucial reagent to enchant a specialized scroll. Gaxim Rustfizzle requires a messaging spell for his odd experiments, and the elemental material gathered from the whirlwind creature allows Mauren to impress the magical enchantment into parchment.",al={"dust devil debris use","what is debris for","why dust devil debris"},it="item",add="b0d4cd5a"},{q="What are the dust devils you are hunting?",a="Dust devils are chaotic air elementals that roam the barren plains and farmlands of Westfall. Stirred up by the turbulent winds and wild magic across the region, these miniature whirlwinds lash out at any travelers who cross their path, making them a lethal hazard to local farmers and wanderers alike.",al={"what are dust devils","dust devil targets","who are the dust devils"},it="target",add="9b2ec5a3"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you see how enchanting can harness wild elemental resonance to bind a complex communication spell into a scroll.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you see Gaxim Rustfizzle's work draw on arcane scrollcraft to solve a communication problem.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you cross from Stormwind's towers to Westfall's neglected fields, where the kingdom's frontier lies in ruin."},kw={"collin mauren","dust devil","dust devil debris","gaxim rustfizzle","mage quarter","messaging spell","scroll","stormwind","westfall"},rel={"npc:collin-mauren","quest:1075","zone:westfall","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Collin Mauren",level="21",faction="Alliance",id=1076,ri={"Dust Devil Debris"}},src={"Devils in Westfall"}}
E["quest:1097"] = {t="quest",n="Elmore's Task",z="stormwind",s="Smith Argus sends you from Goldshire to Stormwind to help Grimand Elmore. The dwarven weaponsmith needs help with a delivery bound for his kin in Khaz Modan, and Argus trusts you to make the journey.",h="Smith Argus sends you from Goldshire to Stormwind to help Grimand Elmore.",sec={{t="A Word from the Forge",b="In Goldshire, blacksmith Smith Argus watches for travelers he can trust with work beyond clearing wolves and kobolds. Grimand Elmore, a skilled dwarven weaponsmith in Stormwind, has asked for help with a delivery to his kin in Khaz Modan. Argus sees you as fit for the journey and sends you toward the city gates to answer Elmore's call.",sp=0},{t="The Ties That Bind",b="Stormwind and Ironforge depend on open trade and goodwill to keep both realms supplied and united. Argus says Elwynn Forest needs defenders, but honoring promises to the dwarves matters too. In northeastern Stormwind, the Dwarven District leads you to Elmore's shop, where a journey beyond the forest begins.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who starts the quest Elmore's Task?",a="Smith Argus, the blacksmith in Goldshire, sends you to help Grimand Elmore.",al={"where do i get elmore's task","who gives elmore's task","elmore task quest giver"},gp=true},{q="Where can Grimand Elmore be found?",a="Grimand Elmore works in a weapon shop in the northeastern Dwarven District of Stormwind.",al={"grimand elmore location","where is grimand elmore","find elmore stormwind"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the purpose of this task?",a="Argus sends you to Elmore, who needs a trustworthy courier to carry a delivery north to his homeland. The journey takes you beyond Elwynn and through Alliance lands.",al={"why send me to elmore","elmore's task purpose","what does elmore want"},it="purpose"},{q="What quest follows Elmore's Task?",a="Speaking with Grimand Elmore completes the errand and opens Stormpike's Delivery, which asks you to carry his shipment north to Loch Modan.",al={"elmore's task next quest","followup to elmore's task","what comes after elmore's task"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does Smith Argus care about dwarven deliveries?",a="Argus says strong trade ties with the dwarves of Khaz Modan help protect Stormwind and keep its supplies moving, even as Elwynn needs defenders.",al={"why does argus help dwarves","smith argus dwarven ties"},it="motive"},{q="Do you need to be a blacksmith to take this quest?",a="No. Any Alliance traveler ready to go to Stormwind can take the delivery, whether or not they know blacksmithing.",al={"is elmore's task blacksmith only","blacksmithing required elmore task"},gp=true},{q="Why does Smith Argus send you instead of going himself?",a="Smith Argus is anchored to his forge in Goldshire, keeping Elwynn Forest's defenders and travelers armed and repaired. While he could make use of more hands locally, he recognizes you as a sturdy traveler capable of handling the footwork between Elwynn Forest and Stormwind. Recommending an adventurer allows him to support his dwarven counterpart without abandoning his own vital smithing work in Goldshire.",al={"why send me elmores task","why doesnt argus deliver it","smith argus why me"},it="why_me",add="4799d1e0"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you help keep trade and trust strong between Stormwind and the dwarven clans of Khaz Modan.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you may recognize how human smiths honor Ironforge's craft and help send supplies north to the mountains.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="As a blacksmith, you see two smiths joined by their craft: Smith Argus in Goldshire and Grimand Elmore in Stormwind."},kw={"blacksmith","delivery","dwarven district","elmore","goldshire","grimand elmore","smith argus","stormwind"},rel={"npc:smith-argus","quest:1700","subzone:dwarven-district","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Smith Argus",["end"]="Grimand Elmore",faction="Alliance",id=1097},src={"Elmore's Task"}}
E["quest:121"] = {t="quest",n="Messenger to Stormwind",z="stormwind",s="You carry General Marcus Jonathan's reply from Stormwind to Lakeshire, where Blackrock orcs and gnolls threaten the town. The capital offers no troops, leaving the settlement to face danger while Stormwind's leaders delay.",h="You carry General Marcus Jonathan's reply from Stormwind to Lakeshire, where Blackrock orcs and gnolls...",sec={{t="A Dispatch to Lakeshire",b="You brought Magistrate Solomon's plea for reinforcements to General Marcus Jonathan in Stormwind. Now you carry his preliminary reply back to Redridge while he waits for approval from the throne. Without royal authorization, the General cannot commit the army. Lakeshire's citizens remain without city guards, and each day brings the settlement closer to falling under the Blackrock clan.",sp=0},{t="Unease in the Kingdom",b="Magistrate Solomon finds no promised battalions marching east along the Elwynn border in Jonathan's reply. The letter offers evasive procedure instead of troops, and Solomon senses something is wrong in the royal court. King Varian Wrynn is missing, and the regency is deadlocked. Outlying towns such as Lakeshire are left to defend themselves.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is in General Marcus Jonathan's response?",a="General Marcus Jonathan's letter says he cannot send the Stormwind army without formal authorization from the King or royal court. He says the matter has been raised with the crown, leaving Lakeshire to wait.",al={"what does the letter say","general response","marcus jonathan letter"},it="item"},{q="Why can't Stormwind just send soldiers to Redridge?",a="With King Varian Wrynn missing, governing decisions rest with young King Anduin, Regent Lord Bolvar Fordragon, and the House of Nobles. Division and delay in the capital keep General Jonathan from marching without royal approval.",al={"why no stormwind help","why won't stormwind help lakeshire","stormwind army redridge"},it="conflict"},{q="Who is Magistrate Solomon?",a="Magistrate Solomon governs Lakeshire and the Redridge Mountains. He leads the settlement and coordinates its scant defenses against Blackrock orcs, gnolls, and local brigands.",al={"magistrate solomon","who is solomon","lakeshire magistrate"},it="identity"},{q="Who is General Marcus Jonathan?",a="General Marcus Jonathan commands the Stormwind City Guard and the capital's standing armed forces. He is stationed at the Valley of Heroes, just inside Stormwind City's main gates.",al={"who is marcus jonathan","general jonathan","stormwind general"},it="identity"},{q="What does Solomon do next after reading the letter?",a="After reading the letter, Solomon seeks help from neighboring regions and sends you to learn the state of Westfall.",al={"what happens next","quest after messenger to stormwind","where to go next"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Solomon say 'something is amiss in our Kingdom'?",a="Solomon sees no military sense in refusing or delaying aid to a border town under attack. The delay warns him that Stormwind's political leaders are being manipulated or paralyzed from within.",al={"something is amiss","why is solomon worried","stormwind conspiracy"},it="danger"},{q="Why does General Marcus Jonathan send you back to Lakeshire?",a="Magistrate Solomon urgently petitioned Stormwind for military reinforcements to fend off the gnoll and orc threats encircling Lakeshire. While General Jonathan petitioned the throne for aid, he cannot dispatch royal troops without authorization from the Crown. He sends you back with his official response so Lakeshire's leadership isn't left in the dark while royal deliberation stalls in the capital.",al={"why marcus jonathan send letter","marcus jonathan lakeshire reply","why general jonathan needs this done"},it="motive",add="53d96341"},{q="Why does General Jonathan entrust this letter to you instead of a royal courier?",a="You were the one who carried Solomon's original petition from Redridge into the Valley of Heroes. With Stormwind's city garrison already spread thin maintaining order and guarding the capital gates, General Jonathan finds it far more practical to send an able adventurer who knows the road back to Lakeshire than to pull one of his own stationed guards away from duty.",al={"why send me marcus jonathan","why not royal guard messenger","why adventurer delivery lakeshire"},it="why_me",add="64d074bd"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human of the kingdom, you carry this correspondence between Stormwind City's guarded comfort and the crumbling borders of its Elwynn neighbors.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you see how political deadlock leaves the kingdom's human territories exposed to regional threats."},kw={"blackrock orcs","bolvar","lakeshire","magistrate solomon","marcus jonathan","messenger to stormwind","redridge mountains","stormwind"},rel={"quest:120","quest:143","npc:magistrate-solomon","npc:general-marcus-jonathan","subzone:lakeshire","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="General Marcus Jonathan",["end"]="Magistrate Solomon",level="14",faction="Alliance",id=121},src={"Messenger to Stormwind (2)"}}
E["quest:1241"] = {t="quest",n="The Missing Diplomat",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind, an urgent inquiry begins after a diplomat fails to reach Theramore Isle. Bishop DeLavey suspects Defias foul play and sends trusted operatives to Jorgen, a discreet contact in the Valley of Heroes.",h="In Stormwind, an urgent inquiry begins after a diplomat fails to reach Theramore Isle.",sec={{t="A Vanishing in the Shadows",b="A high-ranking diplomat sailed from the Eastern Kingdoms to meet Lady Jaina Proudmoore in Theramore Isle for sensitive talks, but never arrived. Royal investigators search Stormwind for clues. The disappearance remains secret to prevent panic and keep conspirators from learning that the crown is watching.",sp=0},{t="Private Inquiries",b="Bishop DeLavey believes the Defias Brotherhood abducted the diplomat, but does not rely only on the king’s guard. He turns to discreet contacts and seeks out Jorgen, an old acquaintance who keeps a low profile fishing in the Valley of Heroes, just inside the city gates.",sp=0},{t="A Reluctant Informant",b="Jorgen keeps a gruff manner and an unassuming post by the city waters, but honors old obligations to DeLavey. He warns that tracing the diplomat’s path carries deadly risks. Anyone drawn into the inquiry must keep silent.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is the missing diplomat?",a="The Church of the Light and the Stormwind throne guard the diplomat’s identity, referring to them only as a key diplomat sent across the Great Sea to Theramore.",al={"missing diplomat identity","who disappeared","who vanished","diplomat identity"},it="target"},{q="Why was the diplomat traveling to Theramore?",a="The diplomat was sent to meet Lady Jaina Proudmoore for critical talks about the security and state of the Alliance between the Eastern Kingdoms and Kalimdor.",al={"why theramore","diplomat purpose","what was diplomat doing"},it="purpose"},{q="Who does Bishop DeLavey suspect?",a="Bishop DeLavey suspects the Defias Brotherhood abducted the diplomat, though their methods and accomplices in the city remain unknown.",al={"who took the diplomat","delavey suspect","who kidnapped the diplomat"},it="threat"},{q="Who is Jorgen?",a="Jorgen is an operative and longtime personal contact of Bishop DeLavey who fishes in Stormwind’s Valley of Heroes, just inside the city gates.",al={"where is jorgen","jorgen identity","who is the fisherman"},it="identity"},{q="Why is the matter kept secret from the public?",a="The authorities keep the matter quiet because revealing that a vital envoy was abducted under the throne’s nose could cause chaos and alert the conspirators that royal agents are hunting them.",al={"why secrecy","why keep it secret","why not tell the city"},it="motive"},{q="Where does this investigation lead?",a="Jorgen directs the inquiry toward Stormwind’s underworld and hidden networks to uncover where the diplomat was intercepted.",al={"what happens next","where to go after jorgen"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Bishop DeLavey need an adventurer instead of the royal guard?",a="King's agents are already scouring Stormwind, but Bishop DeLavey prefers to pursue his own discreet avenues outside the official royal oversight. Entrusting a private courier allows him to involve independent contacts like Jorgen without drawing the eye of the general public or alerting conspirators within the city.",al={"why me missing diplomat","why not city guards missing diplomat","bishop delavey why me"},it="why_me",add="02dad4d3"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The missing royal diplomat puts delicate negotiations between Stormwind and Lady Jaina Proudmoore’s outpost in Theramore at risk.",["class:Priest"]="Bishop DeLavey uses church connections to investigate state crimes quietly when the usual royal channels may be compromised.",["class:Rogue"]="Jorgen is a longtime contact whose low profile helps trace missing envoys through the underground espionage beneath Stormwind’s spotless streets.",["race:Human"]="The Defias Brotherhood’s threat reaches beyond Westfall into the capital, putting the stability of the human kingdom at risk."},kw={"defias","delavey","jaina","jorgen","missing diplomat","stormwind","theramore","valley of heroes"},rel={"npc:bishop-delavey","npc:jorgen","npc:jaina-proudmoore","subzone:valley-of-heroes","zone:stormwind","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Bishop DeLavey",["end"]="Jorgen",level="28",faction="Alliance",id=1241},src={"The Missing Diplomat (2)"}}
E["quest:1242"] = {t="quest",n="The Missing Diplomat",z="stormwind",s="Jorgen sends trusted operatives across Stormwind with a sealed note for Elling Trias. The delivery carries the search for the missing diplomat from the Valley of Heroes to Trias' Cheese in the Trade District.",h="Jorgen sends trusted operatives across Stormwind with a sealed note for Elling Trias.",sec={{t="A Discreet Delivery",b="After the first inquiries into the diplomat's disappearance, Jorgen asks trusted operatives to keep silent and carry a sealed note across the city. It is meant for Trias' Cheese in Stormwind's Trade District, not a barracks or magistrate's office. The handoff avoids ordinary guard channels as concern over the missing diplomat reaches beyond the palace.",sp=0},{t="Behind the Shopfront",b="Elling Trias is a jovial, hardworking cheesemonger and respected merchant at Trias' Cheese. His history with Jorgen and his own contacts reach beyond the shop. With Jorgen's note delivered, the search for the missing diplomat passes quietly into Trias' hands.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Elling Trias?",a="Elling Trias is a respected merchant who runs Trias' Cheese in Stormwind's Trade District. He shares some history with Jorgen and has contacts he can use in delicate matters.",al={"who is trias","cheese vendor","elling trias identity"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Jorgen tell me to keep quiet?",a="Jorgen demands silence because the diplomat's disappearance is a state secret. Word could stir panic or alert whoever orchestrated the abduction, betraying that an investigation is underway.",al={"why silence","jorgens warning","keep your yapper shut"}},{q="Where can I find Trias' Cheese?",a="Trias' Cheese is in Stormwind City's Trade District, along the main avenues among merchants and craftsmen.",al={"trias location","cheese shop location","where is elling trias"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is in the sealed note to Elling?",a="Jorgen's sealed note briefs Elling Trias about the missing diplomat and calls on him to use his contacts and underground ears to find tracks conventional authorities cannot trace.",al={"note contents","what does note say","sealed note to elling"},it="item"},{q="Who is the missing diplomat mentioned in the quest?",a="The royal court guards the diplomat's identity at this stage. The secrecy and concern point to someone of immense political significance to the Kingdom of Stormwind.",al={"who is missing","who is the diplomat","missing person identity"},it="target"},{q="Why would the investigation use a cheesemonger instead of the city guard?",a="The city guard is bound by protocol, jurisdiction, and political ties. Elling Trias can reach street whispers and quiet contacts beyond the soldiers' reach.",al={"why a cheesemonger","why trias not guards","guards vs trias"},it="why_me"},{q="Why does Jorgen want this letter delivered to Elling Trias?",a="Jorgen knows the search for the missing diplomat is a delicate, secretive affair far beyond the scope of a simple field agent. Elling Trias may appear to be an ordinary cheesemonger in the Trade District, but he possesses underground connections and intelligence essential to the investigation. Jorgen needs to pass his findings safely into Trias's hands without tipping off anyone watching.",al={"why send note to elling trias","jorgen motive missing diplomat","why deliver sealed note"},it="motive",add="c433039c"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you may suspect Trias' Cheese is more than a dairy storefront. Its owner keeps quiet contacts well beyond the Trade District.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can see how the quiet pursuit of the missing envoy reveals subtle vulnerabilities in Stormwind's leadership."},kw={"elling trias","jorgen","missing diplomat","sealed note","stormwind","trade district","trias cheese"},rel={"npc:elling-trias","npc:jorgen","subzone:trade-district","zone:stormwind","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Jorgen",["end"]="Elling Trias",level="28",faction="Alliance",id=1242},src={"The Missing Diplomat (3)"}}
E["quest:1243"] = {t="quest",n="The Missing Diplomat",z="stormwind",s="Elling Trias sends you south to seek news of the missing diplomat. Leads in Stormwind point toward Duskwood and Watcher Backus, a contact near Darkshire who may know of Defias activity.",h="Elling Trias sends you south to seek news of the missing diplomat.",sec={{t="Footwork in the Gloom",b="After a frustrating exchange with Jorgen, cheesemonger Elling Trias turns to his wider circle of informants. To save his own coin, he sends you to do the fieldwork instead of hiring agents. You carry a sealed missive across the border into Duskwood, where beasts and the undead make travel dangerous.",sp=0},{t="A Friendly Ear in the Night Watch",b="Watcher Backus serves in the Night Watch and patrols the northern approach to Darkshire. Trias trusts him to report illicit movements through Duskwood, despite the dangers on its roads. Show Backus the sealed dispatch, and he can share guard records and local gossip about Defias Brotherhood operations in the south.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Elling Trias sending me to Duskwood?",a="Elling Trias is following leads on the missing diplomat and suspected Defias Brotherhood activity. To use his contacts without spending coin on agents, he sends you to ask Watcher Backus what is happening in Duskwood.",al={"why go to duskwood","trias duskwood errand","why darkshire"},it="purpose"},{q="Where can I find Watcher Backus?",a="Watcher Backus patrols the northern dirt road just outside Darkshire in Duskwood, along the road toward Redridge and Elwynn Forest.",al={"watcher backus location","where is backus","find backus"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Watcher Backus?",a="Watcher Backus is a soldier in Darkshire's civic militia, the Night Watch. He knows Elling Trias personally and shares what he sees of suspicious travelers and criminal movements.",al={"backus lore","who is backus"},it="identity"},{q="What is in the sealed note given to Backus?",a="Elling Trias's sealed note asks Watcher Backus for intelligence about local sightings or movements of the Defias Brotherhood through Duskwood.",al={"contents of sealed note","what does the note say","sealed note to watcher backus"},it="item"},{q="What does Duskwood have to do with the Defias Brotherhood?",a="The Defias Brotherhood is centered in Westfall and hides beneath the Deadmines. Its cells, couriers, and hideouts also reach through the southern human provinces, including Duskwood's shadowed fringes.",al={"defias in duskwood","are defias in duskwood"},it="threat"},{q="Why does Trias complain about Jorgen?",a="Jorgen stonewalled Trias or drove a hard bargain during the investigation. Trias was so irritated that he cursed Jorgen to the Twisting Nether before turning to other contacts in the field.",al={"who is jorgen","trias and jorgen"},it="conflict"},{q="Why does Elling Trias want this done?",a="Elling Trias may look like a humble master of fine cheeses, but he keeps a wide web of contacts and has agreed to look into the disappearance of the missing diplomat. Any sign of Defias Brotherhood involvement could be the lead that breaks the case, so he puts you on the trail to Duskwood while he works his own sources in the city.",al={"why does trias care","trias motivation","elling trias motive"},it="motive",add="8b2965b1"},{q="Why does Elling Trias have you do the footwork instead of doing it himself?",a="Trias makes no secret of his practicality: sending an adventurer saves him substantial coin and keeps him free to work his discreet contacts within Stormwind City. A high-profile merchant wandering into gloomy Duskwood would draw needless attention, whereas an itinerant investigator can quietly press local guards like Watcher Backus without tipping off Defias eyes.",al={"why send me","why does trias need me","why not go himself"},it="why_me",add="c3fdc8e2"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance hero, you help pursue a disappearance that concerns Stormwind's royal interests. The search brings together royal spymasters, independent crooks, and regional militias.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you see how Elling Trias works through a network. He relies on independent foot soldiers to gather information while keeping his own hands clean."},kw={"darkshire","defias","duskwood","elling trias","jorgen","missing diplomat","night watch","watcher backus"},rel={"quest:1241","npc:elling-trias","npc:watcher-backus","npc:jorgen","subzone:darkshire","zone:duskwood"},m={start="Elling Trias",["end"]="Watcher Backus",level="28",faction="Alliance",id=1243},src={"The Missing Diplomat (4)"}}
E["quest:1244"] = {t="quest",n="The Missing Diplomat",z="stormwind",s="In Duskwood, the search for Stormwind's missing diplomat follows a lead from Watcher Backus to Defias papers at Addle's Stead.",h="In Duskwood, the search for Stormwind's missing diplomat follows a lead from Watcher Backus to Defias papers...",sec={{t="A Lead in the Gloom",b="Watcher Backus of the Night Watch brings the search to Duskwood. He says an unusually large gathering of Defias bandits came to Addle's Stead several weeks ago. The bandits usually keep to themselves across the border in Westfall, so their gathering in the dark woods marks an unusual move. Now you search the abandoned farmstead for the papers they left behind.",sp=0},{t="The Defias Docket",b="At the overrun farmstead, you find a locked footbox holding a Defias Docket. The papers confirm the brotherhood's involvement, but Watcher Backus warns you to be cautious. The Defias could have forged them to mislead investigators.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is Addle's Stead located?",a="Addle's Stead lies in western Duskwood, just south of the main road from Westfall. Hostile Defias agents occupy the run-down farmhouse.",al={"addle's stead location","where is addles stead","find addle's stead"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the Defias Docket?",a="The Defias Docket is a collection of official-looking papers in a footbox at Addle's Stead. It details some of the Brotherhood's recent covert operations in the region.",al={"defias docket","what is the docket","addle stead document"},it="item"},{q="Who is Watcher Backus?",a="Watcher Backus is a member of the Night Watch stationed in Duskwood. His contacts in town and watch over border threats help him track unusual Defias movements along the Westfall border.",al={"watcher backus","who is backus","backus duskwood"},it="identity"},{q="Why are Defias operating inside Duskwood?",a="Defias operatives make quiet incursions into western Duskwood, though their stronghold lies across the border in Westfall. Addle's Stead is an isolated waypoint away from Stormwind patrols.",al={"why are defias in duskwood","defias at addle's stead"},it="why_here"},{q="Can the contents of the Defias Docket be trusted?",a="Watcher Backus warns that the Defias may have planted false leads to throw investigators off their trail. The docket looks authentic, but its contents may be misdirection.",al={"is the docket real","docket forgery","is it a dupe"},it="power"},{q="Who originally pointed investigators toward Watcher Backus?",a="Watcher Backus says Elling Trias, a cheese merchant and covert information broker in Stormwind, directed the investigation to the Night Watch in Duskwood.",al={"who sent me to backus","trias connection"},it="history"},{q="Why does Watcher Backus send you to Addle's Stead?",a="Watcher Backus considers any Defias presence in Duskwood a looming threat to Darkshire's borders, even when they keep quiet. A couple of weeks ago, an unusual gathering of their agents at Addle's Stead caught the Night Watch's attention. Backus suspected something major occurred there, making it the most promising lead for your investigation into the brotherhood's covert movements.",al={"why does backus want this done","watcher backus motive","why investigate addle's stead"},it="motive",add="860270d2"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The kingdom's missing emissary puts Stormwind's security at risk. Defias intrigue reaches far beyond petty highway robbery in Westfall.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you must navigate criminal networks and tell genuine intelligence from Defias misdirection."},kw={"addle's stead","defias docket","duskwood","footbox","night watch","the missing diplomat","watcher backus"},rel={"npc:watcher-backus","subzone:addle-s-stead","zone:duskwood","zone:westfall"},m={start="Watcher Backus",level="30",faction="Alliance",id=1244,ri={"Defias Docket"}},src={"The Missing Diplomat (5)"}}
E["quest:1245"] = {t="quest",n="The Missing Diplomat",z="stormwind",s="You carry the recovered Defias Docket back to Stormwind as the search for a missing diplomat grows more dangerous.",h="You carry the recovered Defias Docket back to Stormwind as the search for a missing diplomat grows more...",sec={{t="Too Heavy for the Night Watch",b="In Duskwood, Watcher Backus wants no part of the Defias Docket you recovered. Its papers describe plans too intricate to be simple banditry or a diversion. Afraid of royal punishment and wary of his Night Watch superiors, Backus asks you to keep his involvement quiet. The papers point to schemes dangerous enough to end careers or cost lives, so you carry them to Stormwind.",sp=0},{t="A Cheesemonger's True Trade",b="Back in Stormwind's Trade District, Master Cheesemonger Elling Trias drops his shopkeeper's pretense when you return. He studies the docket as a handler in the kingdom's covert intelligence network. The papers describe careful planning by the Defias Brotherhood and name an ominous codename: 'Fist.' The missing diplomat was targeted by a careful, well-connected network with reach deep inside the kingdom.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Defias Docket?",a="The Defias Docket is a collection of sensitive papers you recovered in Duskwood, outlining plans by the Defias Brotherhood. Their complexity frightens local watchmen and gives Master Trias new leads in the search for the missing diplomat.",al={"defias docket","what are the papers","docket contents"},it="item"},{q="Why is Watcher Backus so afraid to keep the docket?",a="Watcher Backus fears the docket contains information beyond a Duskwood Night Watchman's authority. He worries that if his commanders or Stormwind superiors learn he handled or withheld such intelligence, he could be hanged for treason.",al={"why backus scared","watcher backus fear"},it="motive"},{q="Why take the papers to a cheese shop owner in Stormwind?",a="Elling Trias poses as a cheesemonger, but he is a Stormwind spymaster and a key figure in the kingdom's covert intelligence network. His knowledge and connections help him decipher the Defias plans.",al={"why elling trias","why trias cheese"},it="identity"},{q="Who is 'Fist' mentioned in the docket?",a="Elling Trias recognizes 'Fist' in the docket as a codename for someone tied to the Defias Brotherhood's coordination of the abduction plot.",al={"who is fist","the fist defias","fist codename"},it="target"},{q="Where does this investigation lead next?",a="The docket's details let Trias trace the conspirators further. He sends you to question contacts and pursue 'Fist' to learn where the diplomat was taken.",al={"next step","what after docket","where do i go next"},it="next_step"},{q="What does this have to do with King Varian Wrynn?",a="The docket does not name King Varian Wrynn. You are searching for an unnamed diplomat who never arrived in Theramore, and Trias's reading of the papers does not reveal the target's identity.",al={"is varian the diplomat","king varian connection"},sp=1,it="purpose"},{q="Why does Watcher Backus need you instead of taking the docket himself?",a="Watcher Backus is terrified of what is written in the Defias Docket. As a member of the Night Watch, he is bound by duty to report matters of state to his commanders, but he knows that handling treasonous conspiracy documents outside official channels could cost him his life. If his superiors discover he held this information and withheld it, he fears he would be hanged. You are an independent investigator already working with Trias, allowing Backus to wash his hands of the lethal intrigue while ensuring the papers reach someone capable of deciphering them.",al={"why me","why doesn't backus deliver the docket","why send me to trias"},it="why_me",add="74ee0470"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="Elling Trias shows how roguecraft can trade daggers for information networks. As a rogue, you see how a spymaster deciphers Defias cipher-work in the crown's shadow wars.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you see how deeply Stormwind's security has eroded since the Third War, with Defias plans threatening the kingdom from within."},kw={"defias docket","duskwood","elling trias","fist","missing diplomat","stormwind","watcher backus"},rel={"npc:elling-trias","npc:watcher-backus","zone:duskwood","npc:jorgen","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Watcher Backus",["end"]="Elling Trias",level="30",faction="Alliance",id=1245},src={"The Missing Diplomat (6)"}}
E["quest:1246"] = {t="quest",n="The Missing Diplomat",z="stormwind",s="In Old Town, a lead in the missing diplomat's case points to a street fighter. Elling Trias sends you to find Dashel Stonefist and get answers about the suspicious papers. The investigation reaches Stormwind's rough streets.",h="In Old Town, a lead in the missing diplomat's case points to a street fighter.",sec={{t="A Lead in Old Town",b="Elling Trias recalls a name tied to the coded notes and leads: Dashel Stonefist, known as Fist. He is a rough street fighter, far from the nobility around Cathedral Square. Stonefist keeps to Old Town's cramped alleys. Finding him draws the search out of Stormwind Keep's grand halls and into the city's criminal circles.",sp=0},{t="Persuasion by the Fist",b="Elling Trias warns that Dashel Stonefist will not speak freely to curious strangers, especially when treason and kidnappings are involved. If questions fail, Trias says force will have to speak. Stonefist treats the alleyways as his domain and resents outsiders probing matters that could cost him his livelihood or his neck.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Dashel Stonefist?",a="Dashel Stonefist is a notorious brawler who frequents the central alleys of Stormwind's Old Town. Trias links him to incriminating papers found during the search for the missing diplomat.",al={"dashel stonefist","who is fist","dashel"},it="target"},{q="Where can I find Dashel Stonefist?",a="Dashel Stonefist lingers outdoors in the alleys near the center of Old Town, away from its main streets.",al={"dashel stonefist location","where is dashel","where is stonefist"},gp=true},{q="Why is Elling Trias sending me after him?",a="Trias links Dashel's name to papers about the King's envoy's disappearance. Dashel may know names, places, or orders tied to whoever organized the abduction.",al={"why fight dashel","trias reason"},it="motive"},{q="Will Dashel cooperate willingly?",a="No. Stonefist is hostile to strangers meddling in his business. Trias expects him to resist and advises you to use a weapon or your fists to make him talk.",al={"does dashel talk","stonefist friendly"},it="threat"},{q="What happens after finding Dashel?",a="Confronting Dashel leads to a brawl. Once subdued, he gives you leads on the network behind the diplomat's abduction and points toward other conspirators within the kingdom.",al={"missing diplomat next step","what after dashel"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Who is the missing diplomat mentioned in the quest?",a="Stormwind authorities speak only of an unnamed diplomat who vanished while traveling to Theramore to meet Jaina Proudmoore. The envoy's identity remains a closely guarded secret at this stage of the investigation.",al={"who is missing diplomat","which diplomat"},sp=2,it="identity"},{q="Why does Elling Trias send you instead of the city guards?",a="Elling operates in secrets, rumors, and delicate political ties rather than overt authority. The disappearance of a high-profile diplomat is an explosive matter, and involving the Stormwind city guard would invite public panic and alert the conspirators that someone is onto them. Trias needs an independent investigator who can slip quietly through Old Town's back alleys, ask dangerous questions, and crack knuckles without bringing the heavy hand—and loud notice—of the law.",al={"why send me","why not stormwind guards","why not city guard"},it="why_me",add="8d360f6b"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you are at home in Old Town, among informants like Trias and thuggish enforcers like Stonefist.",["race:Human"]="As a human of Stormwind, you see troubling proof that local street scum are aiding high treason against the kingdom's leadership.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you know that unraveling the conspiracy behind the missing diplomat matters to the Alliance's stability and to the kingdom at its heart."},kw={"dashel stonefist","elling trias","fist","missing diplomat","old town","stormwind"},rel={"npc:dashel-stonefist","npc:elling-trias","subzone:old-town","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Elling Trias",["end"]="Dashel Stonefist",level="31",faction="Alliance",id=1246},src={"The Missing Diplomat (7)"}}
E["quest:1247"] = {t="quest",n="The Missing Diplomat",z="stormwind",s="Dashel Stonefist has confessed in Old Town, and you carry his warning to Elling Trias. The thug names a backup abduction plot and a contact in Menethil Harbor.",h="Dashel Stonefist has confessed in Old Town, and you carry his warning to Elling Trias.",sec={{t="A Crack in the Wall",b="Dashel Stonefist gives up when he fears for his health. In an Old Town alley, he admits the conspirators' first kidnapping plan fell apart, leaving his part in the plot in ruins. To shift blame, he tells you of a secret meeting weeks ago at Addle's Stead in Duskwood. He also names one lead in their backup plan: an insider in Menethil Harbor known only as Slim.",sp=0},{t="Reporting to the Fromager",b="Elling Trias gathers secrets for the Crown from behind the counter of Trias' Cheese in the Trade District. While you questioned Dashel, Trias studied captured messages about the plot. The confession matches what they reveal: the conspirators targeted an unnamed diplomat, their first ambush failed, and a backup plan began through the Wetlands. With Slim's name, the search turns north from Stormwind toward the marshes.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Dashel Stonefist?",a="Dashel Stonefist is a fixer and strong arm in Stormwind's Old Town. Linked to the Defias underworld, he helped carry out the first plan to capture Stormwind's envoy, then gave information when confronted.",al={"dashel stonefist","who is dashel","stonefist stormwind"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Elling Trias involved in this investigation?",a="Elling Trias gathers secrets for Stormwind while posing as a master of fine cheeses. His Trade District shop lets him coordinate discreet inquiries beyond the city guard's reach.",al={"why elling trias","cheese vendor spy","trias intelligence"}},{q="What happened at Addle's Stead?",a="The conspirators met weeks ago at Addle's Stead, an abandoned farm in western Duskwood, to plan their kidnappings after their first attempt was disrupted.",al={"addle's stead meeting","addles stead","westfall meeting"},it="history"},{q="Who is the diplomat they were trying to abduct?",a="The conspirators' documents and street thugs identify their target only as an unnamed diplomat bound for Theramore. The envoy's identity remains closely guarded at this point in the investigation.",al={"who is missing diplomat","who got kidnapped","the diplomat identity"},sp=2,it="identity"},{q="Who is Slim?",a="Slim is the name Dashel Stonefist gives for the contact handling the backup plan from Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands. The contact represents the conspirators' second route for moving people and supplies.",al={"who is slim","slim menethil","menethil contact"},it="identity"},{q="Where does the trail lead after this?",a="The trail leads north to Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands, where Slim is said to be. Elling Trias confirms Dashel's information.",al={"next step missing diplomat","where to go after dashel","what next"},it="next_step"},{q="Why is Dashel Stonefist talking now?",a="Dashel is only talking because you just beat him into submission. Realizing his thugs could not protect him from you, he is scrambling to save his own skin by giving up what little he knows about the conspiracy's backup plan and pointing you away from himself.",al={"why does dashel talk","dashel stonefist motive","why did dashel confess"},it="motive",add="a7b1abaf"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you know how closely street crime and state secrets can meet, from Dashel's back-alley muscle to Trias's quiet intelligence work.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you see a conspiracy unfolding within Stormwind's borders while the boy-king sits on the throne.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you know the missing envoy matters to the Alliance's stability, with sabotage threatening Stormwind's leadership."},kw={"addle's stead","dashel stonefist","elling trias","menethil","missing diplomat","slim","stormwind"},rel={"npc:dashel-stonefist","npc:elling-trias","subzone:addle-s-stead","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Dashel Stonefist",["end"]="Elling Trias",level="31",faction="Alliance",id=1247},src={"The Missing Diplomat (9)"}}
E["quest:1274"] = {t="quest",n="The Missing Diplomat",z="stormwind",s="A quiet request in Stormwind draws you to Bishop DeLavey in Stormwind Keep. The Church and crown need help with a matter too perilous for public channels.",h="A quiet request in Stormwind draws you to Bishop DeLavey in Stormwind Keep.",sec={{t="A Quiet Summons",b="As you travel through Stormwind, Thomas, an altar boy, approaches with a quiet request. Bishop DeLavey, a respected cleric of the Church of the Holy Light, needs an outsider's help at Stormwind Keep. He calls the matter delicate and urgent. You must keep it discreet, lest the people panic.",sp=0},{t="Whispers in the Keep",b="At Stormwind Keep, Bishop DeLavey tells you why the matter must stay secret: a high-ranking kingdom dignitary has vanished under mysterious circumstances. Domestic unrest is brewing, and King Varian Wrynn is missing. Any sign of foul play among the kingdom's highest ranks could threaten its fragile peace.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Thomas?",a="Thomas is an altar boy at the Cathedral of Light who runs errands for Bishop DeLavey. He watches for capable adventurers on Stormwind's streets and directs them to the keep when Church or state affairs need discreet help.",al={"who is thomas","thomas stormwind","thomas quest giver"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Bishop DeLavey?",a="Bishop DeLavey is a senior cleric of the Church of the Holy Light at Stormwind Keep. He works with the royal court on discreet security concerns and sensitive inquiries that city guards cannot openly pursue.",al={"who is bishop delavey","delavey","bishop delavey"},it="target"},{q="Why is this matter handled in secret?",a="Stormwind is already uneasy: King Varian Wrynn is missing, and the Defias Brotherhood is stirring rebellion across Westfall. News that another prominent diplomat or official has vanished could spread panic or expose weaknesses at court.",al={"why discreet","why secrecy","why secret"}},{q="Where does this investigation lead?",a="The inquiry begins with Bishop DeLavey in Stormwind Keep. It leads through Stormwind and the surrounding human territories, then into dangerous lands across the sea.",al={"where does missing diplomat go","missing diplomat next"},it="next_step"},{q="Who is the missing diplomat?",a="Bishop DeLavey keeps the diplomat's identity secret at the start of the inquiry. Revealing it could threaten the investigation and endanger the missing official and the kingdom.",al={"who is the diplomat","identity of missing diplomat"}},{q="Why does Thomas want you to see Bishop DeLavey?",a="Young Thomas is acting directly on Bishop DeLavey's orders. DeLavey tasked him with quietly scouting capable adventurers throughout Stormwind who could handle a delicate and pressing matter for the kingdom. Thomas has no personal stake beyond diligently serving the bishop and seeing that you reach the keep without raising alarms.",al={"why does thomas send you","thomas motive missing diplomat","why see bishop delavey"},it="motive",add="46e2b0bf"},{q="Why does Bishop DeLavey recruit adventurers instead of the city guard?",a="The mission involves a matter of grave importance that must remain strictly confidential. Mobilizing the Stormwind city guard or drawing official military attention risks leaking sensitive information across the city. By having Thomas discreetly approach independent adventurers like you, the bishop can pursue his quiet inquiries without alerting potential enemies or unsettling the public.",al={"why not the city guard","why recruit adventurers missing diplomat","why does bishop delavey need you"},it="why_me",add="227c4a3f"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Finding the missing diplomat matters to the Alliance's integrity and defense. The inquiry may expose threats within Stormwind's own court.",["race:Human"]="As a human of Stormwind, you face a matter tied to your homeland's stability during a fragile regency."},kw={"bishop delavey","diplomat","investigation","stormwind keep","the missing diplomat","thomas"},rel={"quest:1241","subzone:stormwind-keep","npc:bishop-delavey","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Thomas",["end"]="Bishop DeLavey",level="28",faction="Alliance",id=1274},src={"The Missing Diplomat"}}
E["quest:1338"] = {t="quest",n="Stormpike's Order",z="stormwind",s="In Loch Modan, Mountaineer Stormpike is arranging a shield from Furen Longbeard. The armorsmith works far south in Stormwind City, so Stormpike asks a traveler to carry his order there.",h="In Loch Modan, Mountaineer Stormpike is arranging a shield from Furen Longbeard.",sec={{t="A Shield Worth the Journey",b="Mountaineer Stormpike wants a new shield, and he trusts only Furen Longbeard to forge it. The mountaineer is willing to pay well to place the commission in the smith’s hands, though Loch Modan and Stormwind City lie far apart.",sp=0},{t="From Ironforge to the Dwarven District",b="Stormpike wonders why Furen works so far from Ironforge and the Great Forge, where many dwarves make their home. He suspects Stormwind’s humans pay the smith a king’s ransom. When the order reaches Furen at his anvil, the armorsmith takes pride in hearing from the prestigious Stormpike clan and eagerly prepares to forge the shield.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Mountaineer Stormpike?",a="Mountaineer Stormpike is an Alliance sentry stationed in Loch Modan. He belongs to the proud and influential Stormpike clan and serves among the dwarven mountaineers who protect the mountain passes and valleys.",al={"mountaineer stormpike","who gives the quest","quest giver"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Furen Longbeard?",a="Furen Longbeard is an accomplished dwarven armorsmith who lives in Stormwind City's Dwarven District. His reputation for forging superior shields and armor reaches north to Khaz Modan.",al={"furen longbeard","who is furen","the armorsmith"},it="people"},{q="Why does Furen live in Stormwind instead of Ironforge?",a="Furen Longbeard works in Stormwind's Dwarven District, where he caters to human nobility, city guards, and traveling adventurers. Mountaineer Stormpike wonders why a master dwarf would leave Ironforge, but Furen likely earns a lucrative income in human coin.",al={"why is furen in stormwind","why dwarven district","furen leaving ironforge"},it="why_here"},{q="What is the Deeprun Tram's role in delivering this order?",a="Travelers carrying Stormpike's missive usually go west from Loch Modan to Ironforge, then ride the Deeprun Tram underground into Stormwind City's Dwarven District, where Furen's forge is located.",al={"travel to stormwind","how to get to stormwind","deeprun tram"},gp=true},{q="What comes before this quest?",a="Before entrusting you with the delivery to Stormwind, Mountaineer Stormpike tests your mettle and reliability in Loch Modan with 'Mountaineer Stormpike's Task'.",al={"prerequisites","previous quest","mountaineer stormpike's task"},it="history"},{q="Does Furen Longbeard forge the shield immediately?",a="When Furen Longbeard receives the letter and recognizes the prestige of the Stormpike name, he accepts the commission and promises to start hammering out the shield before the end of the day.",al={"what happens next","followup quest","furen reaction"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Mountaineer Stormpike want this done?",a="Mountaineer Stormpike needs a new shield and holds Furen Longbeard's craftsmanship in exceptionally high esteem, viewing the armorsmith's skill as unmatched. Despite his bewilderment that a master dwarven smith would dwell so far away among the humans of Stormwind rather than near Ironforge, Stormpike is unwilling to settle for inferior defense and insists on having a shield forged by Furen's own hands.",al={"why does stormpike need a shield","mountaineer stormpike motive","why order from furen"},it="motive",add="317873dc"},{q="Why does Mountaineer Stormpike ask you instead of going himself?",a="As an active Mountaineer stationed in the high passes of Loch Modan, Stormpike cannot simply abandon his post guarding the dwarven frontiers to trek south into human lands. Delivering a commission to the Dwarven District in Stormwind requires a long journey, so he turns to traveling adventurers with time to spare and a willingness to carry his missive in exchange for honest coin.",al={"why send an adventurer to furen","why can't stormpike deliver the order","why me stormpike order"},it="why_me",add="02c191af"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you see how far a clan's reputation can reach. Stormpike's order also raises the question of why a master armorsmith would choose human stone over Ironforge.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="As a blacksmith, you may take note of Furen Longbeard, an exceptional armorsmith recognized even across kingdoms, as you travel through Stormwind.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you can see the trade and cultural ties between the dwarven holds of Khaz Modan and Stormwind, joined by the Deeprun Tram."},kw={"armorsmith","dwarven district","furen longbeard","ironforge","loch modan","shield","stormpike","stormwind"},rel={"npc:furen-longbeard","npc:mountaineer-stormpike","quest:1339","subzone:dwarven-district","zone:ironforge","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Mountaineer Stormpike",["end"]="Furen Longbeard",level="14",faction="Alliance",id=1338},src={"Stormpike's Order"}}
E["quest:1447"] = {t="quest",n="The Missing Diplomat",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind, the search for the missing diplomat brings you face to face with Dashel Stonefist in Old Town. You need answers from a man who would rather keep them to himself.",h="In Stormwind, the search for the missing diplomat brings you face to face with Dashel Stonefist in Old Town.",sec={{t="A Friendly Chat in Old Town",b="In Old Town, your search for the missing diplomat leads among cutpurses and shady brokers, beyond the Cathedral's watchful eye. Dashel Stonefist is a local contact with ties to Stormwind's criminal factions, and he knows about the abduction. He has no wish to share what he knows with investigators asking sensitive questions.",sp=0},{t="Brawl in the Alley",b="Dashel Stonefist refuses to cooperate when you approach him. His loyal Old Town thugs back him as he tries to beat you down and end the investigation. Once you subdue Dashel and his men, he changes his tune and opens the way to the next lead in the conspiracy.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Dashel Stonefist?",a="Dashel Stonefist is a shady local contact in Old Town with ties to Stormwind's criminal underworld. He knows more than he lets on about illicit movements through the city.",al={"dashel stonefist","who is stonefist","dashel"},it="identity"},{q="Why do I have to fight Dashel instead of just talking to him?",a="Dashel has no interest in cooperating with investigators. When you ask about the missing diplomat, he assumes you can be easily intimidated and calls in his thugs to silence you. Only a sound thrashing convinces him to talk.",al={"why fight dashel","can i talk to stonefist","why beat up dashel"},it="conflict"},{q="Do I have to kill Dashel Stonefist?",a="No. You need to beat Dashel into submission, not kill him. When his health falls low enough, he yields, calls off his cronies, and agrees to answer your questions.",al={"do i kill dashel","stonefist alive","is dashel dead"},gp=true},{q="Where does this fight take place?",a="The fight takes place in the open in Old Town, near the alleys behind the Pig and Whistle tavern and local training halls where Dashel Stonefist usually hangs around.",al={"stonefist location","where is dashel","old town brawl"},it="place"},{q="What happens after beating Dashel?",a="Once you best Dashel, he apologizes and agrees to tell you what he knows about the conspiracy. He points the investigation toward the next link outside the capital.",al={"what next after dashel","stonefist next quest","diplomat chain next"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="What is 'The Missing Diplomat' chain really about?",a="The search for a lost ambassador uncovers a web of deceit around the diplomat's abduction and the shadowy figures behind it.",al={"missing diplomat lore","who is the diplomat","missing king"},sp=2,it="purpose"},{q="Who are you fighting in this confrontation?",a="You are fighting Dashel Stonefist and a pair of his brawny Old Town thugs. Dashel operates out of the rough alleys of Old Town, surrounded by local ruffians who handle his dirty work and intimidate anyone poking their noses into matters that don't concern them. Rather than answer questions about his illicit ties, Dashel calls on his friends to beat you into silence so you will never leave the city.",al={"who do i fight missing diplomat","who attacks with dashel","target of missing diplomat 8"},it="target",add="c22a58c4"},{q="Why does Dashel Stonefist attack you?",a="Dashel does not want anyone asking questions about the missing diplomat or his own shady connections. Operating in the shadows of Old Town, he survives on secrecy, intimidation, and muscle. When you press him for answers, he views you as an unwelcome snoop and an easy mark, expecting his thugs to silence you permanently before his involvement in darker plots can come to light.",al={"why does dashel stonefist fight you","why does dashel attack","dashel stonefist motive"},it="motive",add="15b1a9ee"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a Rogue, you handle brutes like Dashel Stonefist when shaking down contacts for street-level intelligence.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you see Stormwind thugs hindering the search for the missing diplomat, a threat to the kingdom's security.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, every lead on the diplomat's disappearance may expose the treachery threatening the leadership's stability."},kw={"brawl","conspiracy","dashel","missing diplomat","old town","stonefist","stormwind","thugs"},rel={"npc:dashel-stonefist","subzone:old-town","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Dashel Stonefist",level="31",faction="Alliance",id=1447},src={"The Missing Diplomat (8)"}}
E["quest:1638"] = {t="quest",n="A Warrior's Training",z="stormwind",s="In Goldshire, A Warrior's Training sends young warriors to Stormwind for lessons in battlefield endurance. Lyria Du Lac directs them to the Pig and Whistle Tavern in Old Town, where veteran Harry Burlguard offers seasoned instruction.",h="In Goldshire, A Warrior's Training sends young warriors to Stormwind for lessons in battlefield endurance.",sec={{t="From Elwynn to Old Town",b="After aspiring fighters show reliable command of the fundamentals against threats across Elwynn Forest, their trainers see little more for Goldshire drillmasters to teach. Lyria Du Lac sends recruits into Stormwind, toward the gritty district of Old Town. Veteran fighters gather there to share combat experience far from the royal garrison’s rigid ways.",sp=0},{t="Lessons of the Veteran",b="Harry Burlguard, an aged battle veteran, keeps his quarters at the Pig and Whistle Tavern. He tests a warrior’s mettle with tavern grit and practical stamina instead of parade-ground drills. Before teaching defensive maneuvers that help soldiers survive dangerous campaigns, Harry expects new arrivals to match his appetite for drink and face local brawlers in the tavern.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives this quest?",a="Lyria Du Lac, the warrior trainer behind the blacksmith in Goldshire, offers this training after a fighter proves their early combat skill.",al={"quest giver","who starts a warriors training","lyria du lac quest"},gp=true},{q="Where can Harry Burlguard be found?",a="Harry Burlguard can be found inside the Pig and Whistle Tavern in Stormwind City’s Old Town district.",al={"where is harry burlguard","harry burlguard location","pig and whistle tavern"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What does Harry Burlguard teach?",a="Harry teaches practical moves and stances that help warriors endure longer in the field, beginning with tests of stamina.",al={"what do you learn","warrior quest reward level 10","harry burlguard lesson"},it="power"},{q="Why is training held in a tavern instead of the barracks?",a="Old Town is Stormwind’s traditional, rough heart, where retired soldiers and hardened veterans gather. Harry teaches over ale and with bare-knuckle discipline instead of the barracks’ formal military ways.",al={"why pig and whistle","why train in tavern","stormwind barracks"},it="why_here"},{q="What comes after speaking to Harry?",a="After speaking with Harry, the recruit faces a challenge involving Bartleby the Drunk, a local brawler, to test their physical resilience before training is complete.",al={"what is next quest","after a warriors training","next step"},sp=1,it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Can non-warriors receive this quest?",a="Only warriors can receive this training. It belongs to the dedicated warrior training line.",al={"is this warrior only","can paladins do this","warrior class quest"},it="for_you",gp=true},{q="Why does Lyria Du Lac send you to Harry Burlguard?",a="Lyria Du Lac recognizes that you have proven yourself a capable warrior, but she knows raw enthusiasm only gets you so far on the battlefield. To ensure your survival against deadlier threats, she directs you to Harry Burlguard. As an experienced veteran, Harry possesses seasoned martial techniques and practical battlefield wisdom that newer recruits desperately need if they hope to stay alive.",al={"why does lyria want this","lyria du lac motive","why send to harry burlguard"},it="motive",add="7596c61a"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, this rite marks your passage from local militia recruit to an officially recognized soldier of the Alliance. It opens the way to advanced stances and defensive techniques.",["race:Human"]="As a human fighter, your path leads from Elwynn’s pastoral defenses into Old Town, the ancestral, working-class cradle of Stormwind’s martial heritage.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance recruit, you can carry practical brawling wisdom from veterans like Harry Burlguard toward contested borders, alongside book-learned tactics."},kw={"bartleby","goldshire","harry burlguard","lyria du lac","old town","pig and whistle","stormwind","training","warrior"},rel={"npc:lyria-du-lac","subzone:pig-and-whistle-tavern","subzone:old-town","quest:1639","npc:bartleby","quest:1640","quest:1665","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Lyria Du Lac",["end"]="Harry Burlguard",level="10",faction="Alliance",id=1638},src={"A Warrior's Training"}}
E["quest:1639"] = {t="quest",n="Bartleby the Drunk",z="stormwind",s="In the Pig and Whistle Tavern, Bartleby the Drunk faces a test set by Harry Burlguard. An aspiring Alliance warrior must take Bartleby's prized mug before Harry will teach deeper combat skills.",h="In the Pig and Whistle Tavern, Bartleby the Drunk faces a test set by Harry Burlguard.",sec={{t="A Tavernhouse Test",b="Harry Burlguard asks for proof of a novice's backbone before teaching deeper combat skills in the Pig and Whistle Tavern. Across the room, Bartleby nurses his drinks at the far end of the counter. Harry wants you to take the man's mug, knowing Bartleby would rather fight than surrender his ale. The challenge puts a warrior's resolve to the test.",sp=0},{t="Old Town Etiquette",b="Soldiers, laborers, and rough locals fill the Pig and Whistle, where polished manners count for little. Bartleby mocks newcomers as too prissy for a tavern scuffle instead of answering politely. The exchange leads to a brawl on the floorboards, where a warrior's training in Stormwind begins with a test of basic barroom fighting.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Bartleby?",a="Bartleby is an obstinate, heavy-drinking patron at the bar in the Pig and Whistle Tavern in Stormwind's Old Town.",al={"who is bartleby","bartleby npc","bartleby the drunk"},it="target"},{q="Why does Harry Burlguard send me to Bartleby?",a="Harry Burlguard wants to see what moves you have before teaching advanced warrior techniques. Taking Bartleby's mug guarantees a fight and tests whether you can take a punch and hold your ground.",al={"why fight bartleby","harry burlguard test","why get the mug"},it="motive"},{q="Where does this encounter take place?",a="The encounter takes place inside the Pig and Whistle Tavern in Old Town, on the eastern side of Stormwind City.",al={"where is bartleby","pig and whistle location"},it="place"},{q="What happens when you speak to Bartleby?",a="Bartleby insults you as fancy and prissy, then warns you not to break a nail in the Pig and Whistle. His words quickly spark a fight.",al={"what does bartleby say","bartleby dialogue"}},{q="What comes after talking to Bartleby?",a="After you speak to Bartleby, a tavern brawl begins. You must defeat him to claim his mug and return it to Harry Burlguard.",al={"next quest after bartleby","what follows bartleby the drunk"},it="next_step"},{q="Is this quest available to any class?",a="No. This class training is for Alliance warriors who have reached level ten.",al={"can anyone do bartleby","warrior only"},gp=true},{q="Why does Harry Burlguard send you instead of confronting Bartleby himself?",a="Harry Burlguard has nothing personal to settle with the local sot—he is a warrior trainer testing your mettle. Before he wastes his time teaching you advanced martial techniques, he wants to see if you have the grit to handle yourself in a rough brawl. Sending you to wrest a mug from a stubborn tavern drunk is simply his practical entrance exam.",al={"why me","why send me bartleby","why doesn't harry fight bartleby"},it="why_me",add="1d302574"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you face a practical test from Stormwind's trainers before they teach defensive tactics and stance mastery.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you see the rough, unglamorous side of Stormwind's Old Town, far from the royal court of the Keep."},kw={"bartleby","drunk","harry burlguard","mug","old town","pig and whistle","stormwind","training","warrior"},rel={"quest:1638","quest:1640","quest:1665","npc:bartleby"},m={start="Harry Burlguard",["end"]="Bartleby",level="10",faction="Alliance",id=1639},src={"Bartleby the Drunk"}}
E["quest:1640"] = {t="quest",n="Beat Bartleby",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind, Bartleby guards the mug a young warrior must claim. The instructors send recruits to face him in a bare-knuckle fight and earn the vessel for their training.",h="In Stormwind, Bartleby guards the mug a young warrior must claim.",sec={{t="A Brawler's Challenge",b="Stormwind's warrior instructors expect recruits to face combat without excuses or grand ceremony. As part of their formal training, young warriors must retrieve a particular mug from Bartleby, a notorious drunkard who lounges in the city. He scoffs at polite requests and swears no one will take his prized drinkware without prying it from his cold, dead fingers. For a fledgling warrior, words soon give way to a fistfight.",sp=0},{t="A Drunken Lesson",b="Bartleby boasts that he will fight to the death, but a thorough thrashing is enough to sober him. Once beaten, his bravado gives way to bruised admiration. He recognizes that his opponent is tougher than they appear and yields peacefully, letting the victor claim the mug and complete the trial at the training hall.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Bartleby?",a="Bartleby is a belligerent drunkard who frequents Stormwind City. He clings to a beloved drinking vessel and tests novice warriors sent to prove their physical resolve.",al={"bartleby","who is bartleby","bartleby npc"},it="identity"},{q="Why do I have to fight Bartleby?",a="Alliance warrior trainers send recruits to recover a mug in Bartleby's possession. He refuses to give it up without a brawl, so the trainee must defeat him hand to hand to claim it.",al={"why fight bartleby","beat bartleby reason","why beat him"},it="conflict"},{q="Do I actually kill Bartleby in this quest?",a="No. Bartleby boasts that you must pry the mug from his cold, dead fingers, but he surrenders when beaten and admits you are tougher than he expected.",al={"does bartleby die","kill bartleby","is bartleby dead"}},{q="Where does this quest take place?",a="The confrontation takes place in Stormwind, where Bartleby drinks and loiters.",al={"beat bartleby location","where is bartleby","bartleby spot"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens after I defeat him?",a="After you beat him, Bartleby yields and speaks to you amicably. You can take his mug back to the warrior trainers to complete your initiation.",al={"after beat bartleby","what next bartleby"},it="next_step"},{q="What level of training does this trial represent?",a="This brawl is an early milestone for fledgling warriors around their tenth season of experience, a practical test of basic melee endurance.",al={"bartleby quest level","when do i fight bartleby"}},{q="Why does Bartleby fight you?",a="Bartleby does not want this brawl to happen at all; rather, you initiated the fight by demanding his mug. Stubborn, intoxicated, and attached to his drink, he refuses to hand it over willingly, declaring you will have to pry it from his cold, dead fingers. For Bartleby, fighting you is purely a drunken matter of pride and keeping hold of his ale.",al={"why does bartleby attack","bartleby motive","why is bartleby fighting"},it="motive",add="14f26138"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As an Alliance warrior, you face this early tavern brawl and learn that force of will and a heavy fist can settle disputes when diplomacy fails.",["faction:Alliance"]="In Stormwind's capital streets, you glimpse the city's rough underbelly alongside its stately stone walls."},kw={"bartleby","brawl","drunk","mug","stormwind","training","trial","warrior"},rel={"npc:bartleby","quest:1639","quest:1665","quest:1638"},m={start="Bartleby",level="10",faction="Alliance",id=1640},src={"Beat Bartleby"}}
E["quest:1641"] = {t="quest",n="The Tome of Divinity",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind, The Tome of Divinity guides young paladins through a solemn rite. Under Duthorian Rall's care in the Cathedral of Light, you face teachings on virtue, devotion, and the duties that come with the Holy Light.",h="In Stormwind, The Tome of Divinity guides young paladins through a solemn rite.",sec={{t="A Paladin's Calling",b="Duthorian Rall guides those who answer the paladin's calling in the Cathedral of Light. Early training teaches martial discipline and the order's rites, but advancement asks for a deeper commitment to the spirit. The trials ask you to look beyond battle and weigh the moral duties of a paladin. Stormwind faces dangers within its borders and beyond, and its people need defenders who understand that duty.",sp=0},{t="The Path of Virtue",b="Receiving the Book of Divinity binds you to service and self-sacrifice. Duthorian asks you to study the holy text and learn what the Light demands of its defenders. Its lessons prepare paladins to oppose the Scourge's creeping horrors and protect common folk. Righteous power must answer to virtue and compassion.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Tome of Divinity?",a="The Tome of Divinity tests a developing paladin's grasp of sacred principles. Before greater divine abilities are entrusted to an initiate, their strength must be grounded in devotion and virtue, not martial force alone.",al={"why tome of divinity","what is tome of divinity","paladin book quest"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Duthorian Rall?",a="Duthorian Rall is a senior paladin trainer in Stormwind's Cathedral of Light. He guides new paladins, gives them the Book of Divinity, and directs their trials across the kingdom.",al={"duthorian rall","paladin trainer stormwind","who is duthorian"},it="identity"},{q="Where does this trial take place?",a="The trial begins in Stormwind City's Cathedral Square, inside the Cathedral of Light. After preliminary duties in outer townships such as Goldshire, initiates report to Duthorian Rall.",al={"where is duthorian","cathedral of light quest","where start tome of divinity"},it="place"},{q="Why is the Scourge mentioned in Stormwind's teachings?",a="The Scourge devastated Lordaeron to the north, but its undead remain a threat to all living mortals. Stormwind's paladins learn to recognize and fight the Scourge's unholy corruption wherever it appears across Azeroth.",al={"scourge threat stormwind","why scourge here","paladins vs scourge"},it="threat"},{q="What comes after reading the Book of Divinity?",a="Reading the Book of Divinity is only the first step. Duthorian Rall tests whether you have taken its lessons to heart by sending you to aid those in dire need, where deeds must prove your compassion and resilience.",al={"next step tome of divinity","after reading book","what does duthorian want next"},it="next_step"},{q="Who normally directs candidates to Duthorian Rall?",a="Local instructors and clergy in Elwynn's outlying settlements can direct candidates to Duthorian Rall. Brother Wilhelm in Goldshire is one such guide, sending initiates to the capital when they are ready for formal trials.",al={"who sent me to duthorian","previous quest tome of divinity","brother wilhelm"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Duthorian Rall want you to undertake this trial?",a="Duthorian Rall bears the duty in Stormwind of guiding fledgling paladins toward true virtue and devotion to the Holy Light. With Azeroth menaced by the Scourge and countless other perils, the order requires stalwart defenders of steadfast faith and capability. By presenting you with the Book of Divinity, he seeks to test your comprehension of a paladin's sacred vows, ensuring you possess the spiritual foundation required before granting you greater sacred blessings.",al={"why does Duthorian Rall want this done","duthorian rall motive","why study book of divinity"},it="motive",add="f1eda7dc"},{q="Why does Duthorian Rall choose you for this task?",a="This trial is an internal, spiritual rite of passage that only you can walk. Ordinary guards or established knights cannot study the tenets of the Light on your behalf. Duthorian Rall oversees your personal growth as an aspiring paladin; to earn the honor and abilities of the order, you must prove your own dedication and readiness to shoulder the sacred responsibilities ahead.",al={"why me Duthorian Rall","why does Duthorian pick you","why not send guards"},it="why_me",add="e0af06a7"}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, this rite marks your passage from an apprentice of arms to a servant of the Holy Light. It sets out the sacrifice and mercy at the heart of the order.",["race:Human"]="As a human of Stormwind, you honor the fallen knights of Lordaeron and carry on the Silver Hand's proud tradition in the southern kingdom.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, your training strengthens Stormwind's heart and prepares its paladins to shield the Alliance from rising darkness."},kw={"book of divinity","brother wilhelm","cathedral of light","duthorian rall","holy light","paladin","stormwind","tome of divinity","virtue"},rel={"npc:duthorian-rall","topic:light","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:scourge"},m={start="Duthorian Rall",level="12",faction="Alliance",id=1641},src={"The Tome of Divinity (human 1)"}}
E["quest:1649"] = {t="quest",n="The Tome of Valor",z="stormwind",s="Duthorian Rall awaits paladins seeking trials of faith and courage in Stormwind. The Tome of Valor guides their first steps toward proving their devotion to the Church.",h="Duthorian Rall awaits paladins seeking trials of faith and courage in Stormwind.",sec={{t="Tempering the Spirit",b="The Tome of Valor teaches that valor must be forged through hardship. Its sacred text compares virtues to precious ores, valuable when found but needing refinement to endure. Through hard trials and true commitment, a paladin binds faith, compassion, and courage into a strength that can resist the evils threatening Azeroth.",sp=0},{t="Petitioning the Church",b="After reading the Tome of Valor, you are directed to Duthorian Rall, a respected leader among the paladins in Stormwind's Cathedral of Light. He hears petitions from those seeking the trials of valor. The tests are no mere ritual: defending the innocent and upholding the Church may demand your life, and only the steadfast earn recognition in the order.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this quest?",a="The Tome of Valor guides an initiate from holy doctrine toward perilous trials. After reading it, aspiring paladins petition Duthorian Rall in the Cathedral of Light for tests of faith and courage.",al={"what is the tome of valor quest","why do i need this quest","tome of valor purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Duthorian Rall?",a="Duthorian Rall is a high-ranking paladin and teacher in Stormwind's Cathedral of Light. He oversees the training of promising defenders and the trials that prove an initiate's worth to the Church.",al={"who is duthorian rall","duthorian rall lore","cathedral paladin trainer"},it="identity"},{q="Why does the Church test its paladins so severely?",a="The Church of the Holy Light tests paladins so they can stand firm against despair and violence. Weak resolve or fragile faith could cost lives in battle, so instructors test and temper each initiate before critical holy missions.",al={"why are paladin trials dangerous","why test valor"},it="motive"},{q="Where does this trial take place?",a="You bring your petition to Duthorian Rall in the Cathedral of Light, at the heart of Cathedral Square in Stormwind City.",al={"where to turn in tome of valor","duthorian rall location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does the Tome of Valor direct you to Duthorian Rall?",a="The text of the Tome of Valor acts as a spiritual and moral guide, emphasizing that virtues like faith and courage must be actively tested and forged into an unbreakable resolve. It sends you to Duthorian Rall in Stormwind because trials cannot simply be read; a prospective paladin must petition the leadership of the Cathedral of Light directly to demonstrate that their devotion can withstand deadly sacrifice.",al={"why must i speak to duthorian rall","why duthorian rall tome of valor","why send me to rall"},it="why_me",add="5e1febd2"}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, this trial marks a defining step in your growth. It binds your martial skill to disciplined faith and selfless service.",["faction:Alliance"]="As a member of the Alliance, you share in the strength these Stormwind trials preserve, both in defense and in spirit during turbulent times."},kw={"cathedral of light","church of the holy light","duthorian rall","faith","paladin","stormwind","tome of valor","valor"},rel={"npc:duthorian-rall","topic:light","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Tome of Valor (Classic)",["end"]="Duthorian Rall",level="25",faction="Alliance",id=1649},src={"The Tome of Valor (2)"}}
E["quest:1650"] = {t="quest",n="The Tome of Valor",z="stormwind",s="Duthorian Rall sends a paladin to protect Daphne Stilwell on Westfall's distant shore. With her husband away, Defias bandits threaten her homestead.",h="Duthorian Rall sends a paladin to protect Daphne Stilwell on Westfall's distant shore.",sec={{t="A Call to Arms",b="At Stormwind's Cathedral of Light, Duthorian Rall tests aspiring paladins by asking them to defend the realm's people. After accepting the mantle of valor, you put those ideals to work where law and authority have failed.",sp=0},{t="Peril on the Longshore",b="Daphne Stilwell and her husband Jordan keep an outpost at Westfall's isolated Longshore. Jordan is away in Ironforge, consulting dwarven blacksmiths, and Defias Brotherhood activity is rampant. Duthorian sends you west to protect Daphne before the thieves overwhelm her homestead.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Daphne Stilwell alone in Westfall?",a="Her husband, Jordan Stilwell, traveled to Ironforge to consult fellow blacksmiths. While he is away, Daphne faces growing Defias attacks on their coastal property alone.",al={"where is daphnes husband","why is jordan stilwell gone","daphne stilwell alone"},it="why_here"},{q="Who assigns this task to the paladin?",a="Duthorian Rall assigns it. He trains paladins at Stormwind's Cathedral of Light and gives the order once you prove ready for the trials of valor.",al={"who gives tome of valor 1650","quest giver tome of valor","duthorian rall quest"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Daphne Stilwell be found?",a="Daphne lives in a small cottage on the far southern Longshore, along the coast of southwestern Westfall.",al={"where is daphne stilwell","daphne stilwell location","find daphne stilwell"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Is Daphne completely helpless when you arrive?",a="No. By the time you reach her porch, Daphne has already killed half a dozen Defias bandits with her own weapon while defending the homestead.",al={"can daphne fight","is daphne defenseless","daphne stilwell fighting"},it="threat"},{q="What threat is menacing the Stilwell home?",a="The Defias Brotherhood threatens the Stilwell home. The Brotherhood has overrun much of Westfall and keeps harassing the isolated coastal homestead, seeking to claim the land and plunder what remains.",al={"who is attacking daphne","defias in westfall","enemies at stilwell farm"},it="conflict"},{q="How does this task fit into the Tome of Valor chain?",a="The paladin's valor is measured by sacrifice and defense of the defenseless. Protecting Daphne from marauding bandits puts righteousness into action.",al={"why do i have to help daphne","tome of valor trial purpose","meaning of this quest"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does Duthorian Rall send you to Daphne Stilwell?",a="Duthorian Rall aims to test your resolve and devotion to the virtues of the Light. While her husband Jordan travels to Ironforge to trade smithing knowledge, Daphne Stilwell has been left alone in Westfall just as the Defias Brotherhood overruns the coast. Dispatching you to defend an unprotected civilian serves both as righteous duty and a true trial of valor.",al={"why does Duthorian Rall want this","duthorian rall motive","why send paladin to daphne"},it="motive",add="ef242344"},{q="Why does Duthorian Rall need you instead of the Stormwind city guard?",a="Westfall lies far outside the safety of Stormwind's walls, neglected by the Crown and overrun by bandits. The city guard is stretched thin defending Elwynn and managing urban unrest. For the Church of the Holy Light, shielding defenseless homesteaders is the solemn calling of paladins, making this perilous mission the ideal crucible to prove you are worthy of the Tome of Valor.",al={"why me Duthorian Rall","why not send guards to daphne","why send an initiate"},it="why_me",add="49096f91"}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you leave the safety of Stormwind's Cathedral to protect the defenseless and prove your valor.",["faction:Alliance"]="The Stilwell homestead shows how far Westfall has fallen from Stormwind's protection, leaving rural people to face the Defias alone."},kw={"daphne stilwell","defias brotherhood","duthorian rall","jordan stilwell","longshore","stormwind","tome of valor","westfall"},rel={"npc:duthorian-rall","npc:daphne-stilwell","subzone:longshore","zone:westfall","zone:ironforge","quest:1649"},m={start="Duthorian Rall",["end"]="Daphne Stilwell",level="25",faction="Alliance",id=1650},src={"The Tome of Valor (3)"}}
E["quest:1652"] = {t="quest",n="The Tome of Valor",z="stormwind",s="At the Cathedral of Light in Stormwind, word returns that Daphne Stilwell is safe. After defending her Westfall homestead from bandits, an aspiring paladin reports to Duthorian Rall, completing the Church of the Holy Light's trials of valor. The Church's charge is to shield the innocent without thought for oneself.",h="At the Cathedral of Light in Stormwind, word returns that Daphne Stilwell is safe.",sec={{t="A Sacred Shield",b="Daphne Stilwell's homestead in Westfall is safe after an initiate of the Church of the Holy Light defended it from bandits. Back at the Cathedral of Light in Stormwind, the aspiring paladin reports her safety to Duthorian Rall. The defense shows the courage and conviction expected of one who stands between danger and the defenseless.",sp=0},{t="Ties Between Kingdoms",b="Daphne's husband, Jordan Stilwell, is in Ironforge, where he lends his renowned craftsmanship to the Alliance. With Daphne safe and the homestead guarded, Duthorian Rall prepares to send word north to Jordan. Reassured that his family is protected, the artisan can focus on his work. Their distant homes are bound by the aid the Alliance gives across its lands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Duthorian Rall?",a="Duthorian Rall is a senior paladin trainer at Stormwind's Cathedral of Light. He guides young paladins through spiritual and martial trials, teaching valor, righteousness, and humility.",al={"duthorian rall","who is duthorian","paladin trainer stormwind"},it="identity"},{q="Why was Daphne Stilwell in danger?",a="Daphne Stilwell was in danger because bandits besieged her isolated Westfall farm. Her husband, Jordan, was away working in Ironforge.",al={"daphne stilwell","stilwell farm","who attacked daphne"},it="conflict"},{q="Who is Jordan Stilwell?",a="Jordan Stilwell is Daphne's husband, a skilled blacksmith and craftsman. He is in Ironforge, helping the Alliance with his work while the Church protects his wife at home.",al={"jordan stilwell","daphne husband","jordan ironforge"},it="identity"},{q="What is the Tome of Valor?",a="The Tome of Valor is a holy book of lessons tied to practical trials given by the Cathedral of Light. Through them, paladins prove their courage in facing darkness and protecting the vulnerable at personal risk.",al={"tome of valor meaning","what is tome of valor"},it="item"},{q="What comes after completing this trial?",a="After Duthorian Rall acknowledges your defense of Daphne Stilwell, he guides you toward the Test of Righteousness, the next step in your spiritual and martial progression.",al={"next quest after tome of valor","what is next"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does the Church care about the Stilwell homestead?",a="The Church cares about the Stilwell homestead because Daphne and Jordan have aided it through faithful service and craftsmanship. Protecting Daphne while Jordan is away honors the Church's promise to care for its own.",al={"why church help daphne","church and stilwells"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does Daphne Stilwell want you to report back to Duthorian Rall?",a="Daphne wants Duthorian Rall to know that she is safe and the homestead has survived the assault, but her deepest concern is her husband, Jordan. Jordan is away working in Ironforge, and Daphne knows he will worry endlessly until he hears news from home. By reporting back to the Church of the Light in Stormwind, Duthorian can send word to Ironforge to reassure Jordan that his wife and home are secure.",al={"why send to duthorian","daphne stilwell motive","why talk to duthorian rall"},it="motive",add="9332b34b"}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, reporting to Duthorian Rall completes your lesson in valor and shows the selflessness expected of a holy protector of the Alliance.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can see how the Stilwell family's troubles connect Westfall's human farmlands with Ironforge's dwarven workshops. Their story shows how the Alliance depends on aid between distant lands."},kw={"cathedral of light","daphne stilwell","duthorian rall","ironforge","jordan stilwell","stormwind","tome of valor","westfall"},rel={"npc:duthorian-rall","npc:daphne-stilwell","quest:1653","topic:stormwind-kingdom","zone:ironforge"},m={start="Daphne Stilwell",["end"]="Duthorian Rall",level="25",faction="Alliance",id=1652},src={"The Tome of Valor (5)"}}
E["quest:1653"] = {t="quest",n="The Test of Righteousness",z="stormwind",s="In Ironforge, glad tidings bring Jordan Stilwell news of his wife. Duthorian Rall sends you from Westfall to tell the devout smith that Daphne survived the Defias attack.",h="In Ironforge, glad tidings bring Jordan Stilwell news of his wife.",sec={{t="A Messenger of Good News",b="Duthorian Rall sends you from Cathedral Square with news for Jordan Stilwell. You have guarded Daphne Stilwell through a Defias ambush at her Westfall homestead, and she survived. Her husband left for Ironforge believing his family was in danger. Rall asks you to carry the news in person, so Jordan can know his wife is safe.",sp=0},{t="The Smith of Dun Morogh",b="Jordan Stilwell was once destined to join the paladins, but chose to follow his father's craft as a master weaponsmith. He works at his anvil outside Ironforge's gates, keeping his faith as he shapes weapons. When you tell him Daphne survived the Defias attack, gratitude moves him to help you forge a blessed weapon of righteousness.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Jordan Stilwell?",a="Jordan Stilwell is a devout weaponsmith who works outside Ironforge's gates. He once studied the ways of the Light alongside paladins, then chose to continue his father's smithing craft.",al={"jordan stilwell","who is jordan","the smith in ironforge"},it="identity"},{q="Why was Jordan's wife in danger?",a="Daphne Stilwell lives on a farmstead in Westfall, where Defias Brotherhood outlaws threaten the people. Jordan feared an attack when he left for Ironforge. Bandits stormed the farm, but paladin initiates drove them off.",al={"daphne stilwell danger","what happened to jordan's wife","why defias attacked"},it="conflict"},{q="Where can Jordan Stilwell be found?",a="Jordan Stilwell works outside Ironforge's main gates in Dun Morogh. He prefers the mountain air to the Great Forge inside the city.",al={"where is jordan stilwell","stilwell location","jordan ironforge location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Duthorian Rall send the player to Ironforge?",a="Duthorian Rall sends you to tell Jordan that Daphne survived the Defias attack. The journey also brings you to a master smith who can guide you in making a sacred paladin weapon.",al={"why go to ironforge","duthorian rall errand","reason for message"},it="purpose"},{q="What comes after speaking with Jordan?",a="After hearing the news, Jordan offers to help you forge a holy warhammer. He asks you to gather rare materials and sanctified relics from distant lands.",al={"test of righteousness next","what does jordan want","after talking to jordan"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="How does Jordan feel about the Defias threat?",a="Jordan is angered by Stormwind's council and its neglect. The Defias Brotherhood has plagued Westfall for a long time, and he hopes attacks on honest homesteads will force the boy-king's regents to face the crisis.",al={"jordan defias opinion","stilwell king advisors","defias in westfall"},it="threat"},{q="Why does Duthorian Rall send you to Jordan Stilwell?",a="Jordan Stilwell departed for Ironforge unaware of whether his home and wife survived the Defias onslaught in Westfall. Having tested your valor by defending his family, Duthorian Rall wants to grant the smith peace of mind. Sending you delivers the joyful news directly from the paladin who answered the call.",al={"why send me to jordan","duthorian rall motive","why visit jordan stilwell"},it="motive",add="c7e3478b",nx={8}},{q="Why does Duthorian Rall pick you for this errand instead of an ordinary messenger?",a="You are the one who actually fought off the Defias to rescue Jordan's wife. Rather than trusting an impersonal courier, Duthorian believes Jordan deserves to hear the good tidings directly from his family's savior, continuing your mentorship under the Light with an ally deeply sympathetic to the paladin order.",al={"why send me instead of messenger","why am i delivering the message","why me test of righteousness"},it="why_me",add="26f62cea"}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you move from protecting the weak to crafting sacred tools to purge evil across Alliance lands.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you see Westfall's common folk struggling against the Defias while royal advisors in Stormwind delay action.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="As a blacksmith, you can see how Jordan's work at the anvil expresses his devotion as surely as wielding a consecrated blade in battle."},kw={"daphne stilwell","defias brotherhood","dun morogh","duthorian rall","ironforge","jordan stilwell","stormwind","test of righteousness"},rel={"npc:jordan-stilwell","npc:duthorian-rall","zone:ironforge","topic:light"},m={start="Duthorian Rall",["end"]="Jordan Stilwell",level="21",faction="Alliance",id=1653},src={"The Test of Righteousness"}}
E["quest:1665"] = {t="quest",n="Bartleby's Mug",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind, Bartleby's Mug marks a young warrior's trial of grit. After besting Bartleby in the Pig and Whistle Tavern, you claim his drinking mug for your trainer, Harry Burlguard.",h="In Stormwind, Bartleby's Mug marks a young warrior's trial of grit.",sec={{t="Trophy of a Tavern Brawl",b="Harry Burlguard tests young warriors with a brawl in Old Town. He asks you to take down Bartleby, a stubborn drunk at the bar of the Pig and Whistle Tavern. Once subdued, Bartleby reluctantly gives up his prized drinking mug, but first takes one final swig to drain the dregs.",sp=0},{t="A Step Toward Mastery",b="Returning the mug to Harry Burlguard completes your novice trial. Burlguard sees that you can persuade through sheer force and recognizes your readiness for defensive mastery. He points you onward to further battlefield instruction with Marshal Haggard, a seasoned veteran in Elwynn Forest.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Harry Burlguard want Bartleby's mug?",a="Harry Burlguard wants Bartleby's mug as proof that you fought and bested him. Bartleby is fiercely attached to his drink, so giving up his personal mug shows he was soundly beaten into submission.",al={"why bartleby mug","burlguard mug purpose","proof of beating bartleby"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who is Bartleby?",a="Bartleby is an unruly patron at the bar of the Pig and Whistle in Stormwind's Old Town. Drunken and foul-tempered, he gives local warrior trainers an informal test for up-and-coming fighters.",al={"bartleby lore","who is bartleby the drunk","bartleby old town"},it="identity"},{q="Where does this fight take place?",a="The brawl takes place inside the Pig and Whistle Tavern in Stormwind's Old Town.",al={"where is bartleby","bartleby location","pig and whistle fight"},it="place"},{q="What comes after returning the mug to Burlguard?",a="After Burlguard inspects the mug and confirms your victory, he teaches you advanced defensive combat stances. He then sends you outside the city gates to seek Marshal Haggard in Elwynn Forest.",al={"what next after bartleby mug","quest after bartleby mug","haggard quest"},it="next_step"},{q="Does Bartleby get hurt permanently in the brawl?",a="No. The brawl is non-lethal. Bartleby yields, finishes his drink, hands over his mug, and remains in the tavern with bruises and wounded pride.",al={"is bartleby dead","did bartleby die","bartleby survived"}},{q="Can any Alliance class do this quest?",a="Only Alliance warriors undertake this trial as part of their level ten class training in combat stances and defensive maneuvers.",al={"is bartlebys mug warrior only","who can do bartleby quest","mug quest classes"},gp=true},{q="Why does Bartleby give up his mug?",a="Bartleby only hands over his prized mug because you bested him fair and square in a tavern brawl. He was unwilling to part with it voluntarily, but having been battered into submission, he concedes honorably—though not before hastily finishing whatever drink was left inside.",al={"why does bartleby give his mug","bartleby motive","why give up mug"},it="motive",add="2bbd1f99"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior in Stormwind, you prove you can stand toe-to-toe with unruly foes by taking Bartleby's mug.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you know disorderly patrons in Old Town are a familiar headache for Stormwind's martial instructors."},kw={"bartleby","burlguard","mug","old town","pig and whistle","stormwind","warrior"},rel={"quest:1640","quest:1639","quest:1638","npc:bartleby"},m={start="Bartleby",["end"]="Harry Burlguard",level="10",faction="Alliance",id=1665},src={"Bartleby's Mug (quest)"}}
E["quest:1666"] = {t="quest",n="Marshal Haggard",z="stormwind",s="At Eastvale, Marshal Haggard keeps the arms he gathered over a lifetime of service. Harry Burlguard sends novice warriors from Stormwind City to meet the retired marshal and seek better weapons.",h="At Eastvale, Marshal Haggard keeps the arms he gathered over a lifetime of service.",sec={{t="A Veteran's Armory",b="Stormwind's novice warriors need more than skill to face danger beyond the city. Harry Burlguard sends promising fighters east through Elwynn Forest to find Marshal Haggard, a retired officer who served the realm for years. Haggard gathered a personal armory over a lifetime in the field, and his home near the Eastvale Logging Camp holds weapons for young warriors seeking better arms.",sp=0},{t="Retirement at Eastvale",b="Marshal Haggard lives in a secluded manor near the Eastvale Logging Camp. Years of service have weakened his failing sight, and he sometimes mistakes approaching travelers for prowling riverpaw gnolls. Though age keeps him in this quiet corner of eastern Elwynn, Stormwind's guards and trainers still respect the old marshal.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who starts this quest?",a="Harry Burlguard, a warrior trainer in Stormwind City, sends promising young warriors to Marshal Haggard.",al={"where do i get marshal haggard quest","who gives marshal haggard","quest giver marshal haggard"},gp=true},{q="Where is Marshal Haggard located?",a="Marshal Haggard lives in a manor just east of the Eastvale Logging Camp, in far eastern Elwynn Forest near the Redridge Mountains border.",al={"marshal haggard location","where is haggard","eastvale lumber camp manor"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Harry Burlguard send you to Haggard?",a="Harry Burlguard sends you to Marshal Haggard because young warriors need better arms than their training blades. Haggard gathered weapons and armor during his long career and may share them with those who prove their worth.",al={"why marshal haggard","why go to eastvale warrior","purpose of marshal haggard quest"},it="motive"},{q="Why does Haggard mistake visitors for gnolls?",a="Marshal Haggard's eyesight has worsened with age. Gnolls harass Elwynn Forest's eastern timber operations and outskirts, leaving the old veteran wary of sudden visitors.",al={"haggard eyesight","is haggard blind","haggard gnoll dialogue"},it="identity"},{q="What comes after completing this quest?",a="After you greet Marshal Haggard, he tests your mettle by sending you to deal with Dead-tooth Jack before he considers sharing weapons from his stores.",al={"marshal haggard next quest","follow up to marshal haggard"},sp=1,it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Is this quest available to classes other than warriors?",a="No. This path is for warriors, as part of their training around level ten and their preparation for dangers beyond Elwynn Forest.",al={"can paladins do marshal haggard","warrior only quest haggard"},gp=true}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As an Alliance warrior, you leave Stormwind's formal training and venture into the wilderness in search of arms.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance fighter, you follow Stormwind's reliance on retired veterans and their private stores to prepare the next generation of defenders."},kw={"eastvale","eastvale logging camp","elwynn forest","harry burlguard","marshal haggard","stormwind","warrior"},rel={"quest:1667","zone:elwynn","topic:gnoll"},m={start="Harry Burlguard",["end"]="Marshal Haggard",level="10",faction="Alliance",id=1666},src={"Marshal Haggard (quest)"}}
E["quest:1685"] = {t="quest",n="Gakin's Summons",z="stormwind",s="A summons delivered to promising Alliance warlocks by Remen Marcot on behalf of Gakin the Darkbinder. It directs fledgling practitioners down into the crypts beneath the Slaughtered Lamb in Stormwind's Mage Quarter to begin their next stage of dark occult training.",h="A summons delivered to promising Alliance warlocks by Remen Marcot on behalf of Gakin the Darkbinder.",sec={{t="A Discrete Message",b="Demonology is strictly outlawed across the civilized districts of Stormwind, yet dark arts persist right under the noses of the city guard. When a warlock displays sufficient proficiency with their introductory imps, word quietly travels to senior practitioners. Remen Marcot delivers the message with deliberate discretion, urging initiates to keep the meeting place quiet and head into the shadowy recesses beneath the Mage Quarter.",sp=0},{t="The Crypts of the Slaughtered Lamb",b="Behind the modest facade of the Slaughtered Lamb tavern lies a network of damp cellars and hidden catacombs. Here, shielded from prying Kirin Tor mages and the Cathedral's inquisitors, Gakin the Darkbinder oversees the instruction of Stormwind's warlocks. The summons serves as the gateway to commanding a voidwalker, a rite requiring dangerous stolen reagents and perilous summoning circles.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Gakin the Darkbinder summon warlocks?",a="Gakin summons budding warlocks once they reach a suitable level of experience. He considers untrained warlocks a liability prone to losing their heads, and aims to instruct them in the complex ritual of binding a voidwalker to their service.",al={"why gakin summons","what is gakin summons for","voidwalker quest start"},it="purpose"},{q="Where is Gakin the Darkbinder located?",a="Gakin is hidden in the deep underground crypts beneath the Slaughtered Lamb, a tavern situated in the Mage Quarter of Stormwind.",al={"where is gakin","gakin location","slaughtered lamb basement"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Remen Marcot?",a="Remen Marcot is an associate of Stormwind's warlock coven who keeps to the cellar of the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire, tracking down promising candidates to quietly direct them to Gakin's hidden enclave.",al={"remen marcot","who starts gakin summons"},it="identity"},{q="Why must the location be kept secret?",a="Fel magic and demon summoning are forbidden in the Kingdom of Stormwind. Discovery by the Silver Hand, the Cathedral of Light, or the city guards would result in imprisonment or execution.",al={"why secret","warlock secrecy stormwind"},it="why_here"},{q="What comes after answering Gakin's summons?",a="After reporting to Gakin, he tasks the warlock with venturing to the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch in Elwynn Forest to recover a bloodstone choker from Surena Caledon, an essential component for the voidwalker binding ritual.",al={"next quest after gakins summons","what happens next"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Can non-warlocks receive this summons?",a="No. The summons is strictly restricted to warlocks who have mastered their basic imp companion and require advanced occult instruction.",al={"can mages get this","who can do gakins summons"},gp=true},{q="Why does Remen Marcot want you to see Gakin?",a="Remen Marcot is acting purely on orders from Master Gakin the Darkbinder. He spent all day scouring the city to track you down, growing thoroughly frustrated in the process. His only stake is fulfilling his task so he can stop chasing after you and return to his own business, warning you to report quickly before your master loses patience.",al={"why does remen send you to gakin","remen marcot motive","why is remen looking for you"},it="motive",add="0d517c2f"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="This summons marks your progression beyond parlor tricks and minor imps, initiating the trials necessary to enslave a voidwalker to shield you in battle.",["faction:Alliance"]="Even within the heart of Stormwind, the Alliance tolerates a subterranean cabal of shadow-weavers whose fel expertise provides a shadowy edge against their enemies."},kw={"demonology","gakin the darkbinder","mage quarter","remen marcot","slaughtered lamb","stormwind","voidwalker","warlock"},rel={"npc:gakin-the-darkbinder","subzone:slaughtered-lamb","quest:1688","quest:1471","subzone:mage-quarter","quest:1715","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Remen Marcot",["end"]="Gakin the Darkbinder",level="10",faction="Alliance",id=1685},src={"Gakin's Summons (Voidwalker)"}}
E["quest:1689"] = {t="quest",n="The Binding",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind, Gakin the Darkbinder puts a novice warlock through a final trial. With his recovered Bloodstone Choker, you draw a voidwalker into a hidden circle and force it to submit.",h="In Stormwind, Gakin the Darkbinder puts a novice warlock through a final trial.",sec={{t="Subjugation in the Crypts",b="Beneath the Slaughtered Lamb in Stormwind's Mage Quarter, forgotten catacombs run beyond the watchful gaze of the Silver Hand and Kirin Tor magistrates. Gakin the Darkbinder teaches novice warlocks that dark magic demands more than channeling power; they must also dominate otherworldly beings. You have recovered Gakin's stolen Bloodstone Choker from Surena Caledon. Now he asks you to call a voidwalker into the summoning circle beneath the tavern.",sp=0},{t="Asserting Will over the Void",b="A voidwalker will not bargain with you. The power in the Bloodstone Choker opens a rift and draws the shadow creature into the mortal world. You must batter it with magic and force until its will breaks, proving you can command it. Once defeated, the voidwalker's essence binds to you, giving you a durable, shadowy protector that can endure punishment in the battles ahead.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the summoning circle located?",a="The summoning circle lies deep in the basement catacombs beneath The Slaughtered Lamb in Stormwind's Mage Quarter. Follow the stairs from Gakin the Darkbinder into the underground passages, down to the lowest chamber, where a glowing purple ritual rune marks the stone floor.",al={"summoning circle location","where do i summon the voidwalker","where is the circle"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Gakin the Darkbinder?",a="Gakin the Darkbinder is a warlock trainer who works beneath The Slaughtered Lamb in Stormwind. He secretly teaches promising human and gnome practitioners to summon and control demonic and void-touched beings, away from the city guard and church authorities.",al={"who is gakin","gakin the darkbinder lore","gakin"},it="identity"},{q="What is the Bloodstone Choker used for?",a="Surena Caledon stole the Bloodstone Choker before you recovered it for Gakin. Its focused magic helps a novice warlock breach the veil and draw a voidwalker into the summoning circle.",al={"bloodstone choker use","why do i need the choker","choker"},it="item"},{q="Why do warlocks have to fight their demons to bind them?",a="Demons and void creatures do not willingly serve mortal masters. A warlock must break one in combat with strength and will before binding it to serve.",al={"why fight the voidwalker","why subdue demons","demon subjugation"},it="purpose"},{q="What happens after completing the ritual?",a="After you defeat the creature and return the choker to Gakin, you gain the knowledge and technique to summon and command a loyal voidwalker to shield you on your travels.",al={"what reward do i get","voidwalker spell","after the binding"},it="next_step"},{q="Why is this ritual performed in secret beneath a tavern?",a="Demonology and void magic are taboo, and the Church of the Holy Light and the Alliance's magi view them with hostility. Warlocks in Stormwind practice in concealed basements and catacombs, away from the authorities.",al={"why hidden under tavern","is fel magic illegal","slaughtered lamb basement"},it="place"},{q="Why does Gakin the Darkbinder want you to bind a voidwalker?",a="Gakin sees raw potential in you after you recovered his Bloodstone Choker, but he considers your magical training incomplete. Being a true warlock requires far more than channeling shadowy energies; it demands the will to dominate creatures of the Nether. Before he can teach you how to properly command a voidwalker in battle, you must prove your supremacy over one with your own might.",al={"why does gakin want this","gakin motive","why bind voidwalker"},it="motive",add="bc8c924d"},{q="What is the voidwalker you summon?",a="You are conjuring a hostile entity from the Twisting Nether into the summoning circle beneath the tavern. Voidwalkers are shadowy, resilient beings driven by chaotic malice. Drawn across the threshold by the power of the Bloodstone Choker, this creature will lash out instantly, seeking to destroy its summoner unless forced into submission through physical and magical combat.",al={"what voidwalker","who do you fight","summoned voidwalker"},it="target",add="8fb1392b"},{q="Why does Gakin make you summon the voidwalker yourself?",a="A demon cannot be bound to a warlock by proxy. If Gakin or an assistant were to tame the beast, it would answer only to them. To earn the power and protection of a voidwalker, you must personally draw it into the circle and break its will. Only by overpowering it yourself can you forge the mystical bond required to summon and command it in the future.",al={"why do i have to summon it","why cant gakin do it","why me voidwalker"},it="why_me",add="b41bc1ad"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you gain a voidwalker to defend you. The rite marks your passage from novice summoner to commander of otherworldly forces.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you serve a cause that champions the Holy Light and arcane order. In perilous times, pragmatic leaders turn a blind eye to dark practitioners beneath the Mage Quarter.",["race:Human"]="As a human warlock, you face close scrutiny from Stormwind's priesthood. You master dangerous beings in the shadows and keep your power hidden from the city above.",["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome warlock, you bring a precise, curious mind to dark summoning. Under Gakin's guidance, you study the subjugation of void beings as a metaphysical experiment."},kw={"binding","bloodstone choker","gakin the darkbinder","mage quarter","slaughtered lamb","stormwind","summoning circle","voidwalker"},rel={"npc:gakin-the-darkbinder","quest:1688","quest:1685","zone:stormwind","quest:1471","zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Gakin the Darkbinder",level="10",faction="Alliance",id=1689},src={"The Binding (Voidwalker, Stormwind)"}}
E["quest:1698"] = {t="quest",n="Yorus Barleybrew",z="stormwind",s="At the Lakeshire Inn, Yorus Barleybrew awaits Alliance warriors bold enough to answer his challenge. Trainers across Alliance capitals send seasoned fighters from Stormwind toward the Redridge borderlands to meet the eccentric dwarf and face his test of arms.",h="At the Lakeshire Inn, Yorus Barleybrew awaits Alliance warriors bold enough to answer his challenge.",sec={{t="A Call to the Strong",b="Across Alliance capitals, warrior trainers watch fighters who have outgrown their first drills. When an apprentice proves their mettle around their twentieth season, trainers such as Kelv Sternhammer, Wu Shen, and Darnath Bladesinger pass along word of Yorus Barleybrew. The dwarf offers no standard military order. Instead, he has issued an open wager and a test of arms to any Alliance warrior bold enough to answer.",sp=0},{t="Waiting in Lakeshire",b="Yorus Barleybrew waits at the tavern in Lakeshire, on the front lines of Redridge's struggle against encroaching gnolls and Blackrock orcs. Those who find him meet a boastful dwarf with a hearty drink in hand, ready to judge any challenger who claims true fighting spirit. For warriors seeking to prove themselves beyond the capital's safe cobbled streets, his trial opens onto the harsher battles of the frontier.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Yorus Barleybrew?",a="Yorus Barleybrew is a dwarf of the famous Barleybrew brewing clan who has issued an open martial challenge to Alliance warriors. He waits at the Lakeshire Inn, where he tests fighters who believe they are ready for the brutal frontier of Redridge Mountains.",al={"yorus barleybrew","who is barleybrew","dwarf in lakeshire inn"},it="identity"},{q="Why do the trainers send warriors to Redridge?",a="When a warrior has gained sufficient skill in Stormwind, local weapon masters send them toward practical, high-stakes combat. Yorus Barleybrew's trial takes trainees beyond the city walls, where they prove their endurance against real wilderness threats.",al={"why lakeshire","warrior trainer quest redridge","why go to yorus"},it="motive"},{q="Where can I find Yorus Barleybrew?",a="Yorus Barleybrew waits inside the Lakeshire Inn, in the town of Lakeshire in the Redridge Mountains, just east of Elwynn Forest.",al={"yorus barleybrew location","where is yorus","find barleybrew"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens after speaking with Yorus?",a="Speaking with Yorus begins his martial trial: the Rethban Gauntlet, a perilous test against the vicious beasts and gnolls in the surrounding hills.",al={"after yorus","barleybrew trial","next quest"},it="next_step"},{q="Who offers the quest to find him?",a="Warrior trainers in the Alliance capitals, including Kelv Sternhammer, Wu Shen, and Darnath Bladesinger, send warriors to find Yorus once they have proven basic competence.",al={"who gives quest","quest starter","trainers for yorus"},it="people",gp=true},{q="Is this trial open to classes other than warriors?",a="No. Yorus Barleybrew offers this challenge only to warriors, martial combatants who rely on physical endurance and arms.",al={"can paladins do this","is this warrior only","class restrictions"},it="why_me",gp=true},{q="Why are the trainers sending you to Yorus Barleybrew?",a="Your trainers recognize that you have outgrown basic drills and require trials that test your mettle in the field. Yorus Barleybrew issued an open challenge specifically to able Alliance warriors, promising a grand reward to anyone strong enough to overcome it. Rather than keeping you sheltered in capital training halls, your mentors send you to Redridge to prove your prowess against a real test.",al={"why send me to yorus","why me yorus barleybrew","why warrior trial redridge"},it="why_me",add="f43b4090"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As an Alliance warrior, you face a rite of passage from introductory drills to dangerous trials on the Redridge frontier.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance recruit, you may be sent to Lakeshire, a vulnerable settlement beset by gnolls and Blackrock orcs."},kw={"kelv sternhammer","lakeshire","lakeshire inn","redridge","rethban","stormwind","warrior","wu shen","yorus barleybrew"},rel={"quest:1699","subzone:lakeshire-inn","subzone:lakeshire","topic:alliance"},m={start="Kelv Sternhammer,Wu Shen, orDarnath Bladesinger",["end"]="Yorus Barleybrew",level="20",faction="Alliance",id=1698},src={"Yorus Barleybrew (quest)"}}
E["quest:1700"] = {t="quest",n="Grimand Elmore",z="stormwind",s="Following the creation of specialized armor, the dwarven smith Furen Longbeard sends a copy of his findings across the district to Grimand Elmore. The brief errand carries technical notes between two headstrong weaponsmiths sharing space in Stormwind City.",h="Following the creation of specialized armor, the dwarven smith Furen Longbeard sends a copy of his findings...",sec={{t="A Message Across the District",b="Having forged the specialized Fire Hardened Mail, Furen Longbeard documents the intricate heat-treating techniques and elemental principles he uncovered during the process. Rather than keeping the knowledge entirely to himself, he commits the notes to parchment and tasks an adventurer with delivering them straight to Grimand Elmore, a seasoned crafter operating out of a nearby weapon shop.",sp=0},{t="Professional Pride and Curiosity",b="Grimand Elmore's immediate reaction upon receiving the manuscript is wounded pride. Adamant that he taught Furen everything the younger dwarf knows, Grimand bristles at the notion that his former pupil could offer him instruction. Despite his outward indignation, the craftsman cannot resist perusing the text, quickly finding an intriguing idea hidden within the notes that he is eager to test for himself.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Grimand Elmore?",a="Grimand Elmore is a respected weaponsmith who maintains a shop in Stormwind City's Dwarven District. He is known for his immense professional pride and his past role in teaching craft skills to other local smiths, including Furen Longbeard.",al={"grimand elmore","who is grimand","elmore stormwind"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Furen send notes to Grimand?",a="While crafting the Fire Hardened Mail, Furen discovered new techniques and recorded his methods. He wanted to share the breakthroughs with Grimand, even while knowing Grimand's fiery temper and stubborn ego would make him react defensively to being taught something new.",al={"why send notes","furen notes","furen to grimand"},it="motive"},{q="Where can Grimand Elmore be found?",a="He can be found working inside the weapon shop located within the Dwarven District of Stormwind City, only a short walk from Furen Longbeard's forge.",al={"where is grimand","grimand location","grimand elmore shop"},it="place",gp=true},{q="How does Grimand react to the notes?",a="Grimand is initially outraged, declaring that he taught Furen everything the dwarf knows. However, his curiosity as a master smith quickly takes over when he spots an intriguing technique in the text that he wants to experiment with.",al={"grimand reaction","is grimand mad"}},{q="What happens after Grimand reads the notes?",a="Intrigued by Furen's work on fire-tempering metal, Grimand decides to pursue his own ambitious craft project, which leads into further tasks to gather rare components with elemental heat.",al={"what next grimand","after grimand elmore quest"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Furen warn to duck when handing over the notes?",a="Furen knows Grimand's fiery temper and excessive pride firsthand. He anticipates that Grimand might throw a tantrum—or an object—at the mere implication that an apprentice could teach the master a new technique.",al={"why duck","furen duck warning"}},{q="Why does Furen send you instead of going to Grimand himself?",a="Furen knows Grimand Elmore's prickly temper all too well. Grimand claims to have taught Furen everything he knows, and having his former student stroll into his shop to lecture him on new smithing techniques would ignite a fiery row. By having you deliver the notes instead, Furen avoids a direct confrontation and lets his stubborn mentor swallow his pride in private.",al={"why send me grimand elmore","why not deliver notes himself furen","why does furen need me"},it="why_me",add="7d98159c"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="This delivery bridges the gap between armoring yourself and seeking out martial weapons forged through the very same elemental experiments.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="The exchange between Furen and Grimand illustrates the intense professional rivalry and sharing of trade secrets common among master metalworkers.",["race:Dwarf"]="The hot-headed, prideful banter between Grimand and Furen reflects the deeply competitive yet cooperative traditions of Khaz Modan's smithing culture."},kw={"blacksmithing","dwarven district","fire hardened mail","furen longbeard","furen's notes","grimand elmore","stormwind"},rel={"npc:furen-longbeard","quest:1701","subzone:dwarven-district"},m={start="Furen Longbeard",["end"]="Grimand Elmore",level="28",faction="Alliance",id=1700},src={"Grimand Elmore (quest)"}}
E["quest:1701"] = {t="quest",n="Fire Hardened Mail",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind, Furen Longbeard has a new armor design for an Alliance warrior. The dwarf armorer offers to forge Fire Hardened Mail if the warrior brings him rare materials from both continents.",h="In Stormwind, Furen Longbeard has a new armor design for an Alliance warrior.",sec={{t="A Master Armorer's Ambition",b="Furen Longbeard has forged an exceptional buckler for the aspiring warrior and now proposes a greater work: mail made to withstand fierce blows. His craft calls for more than iron or steel. He needs rare materials touched by elemental heat and natural resilience. Furen cannot leave his Stormwind forge, so the warrior seeking the armor must gather these dangerous ingredients.",sp=0},{t="A Cross-Continental Expedition",b="Furen sends the warrior to distant wilds and dangerous depths for the parts he needs. The recipe calls for fangs from venomous spiders in the damp crevices of the Wetlands, along with scorched and galvanized horns from fierce chimaeras in the Stonetalon Mountains. To bind and temper those beast parts into mail, Furen also needs volatile phlogiston from Roogug, a geomancer deep within Razorfen Kraul's thorny maze in the Barrens.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Furen Longbeard?",a="Furen Longbeard is a veteran dwarf armorer and shieldsmith in Stormwind City's Dwarven District. He crafts tailored defenses for promising warriors willing to help him.",al={"furen","who gives fire hardened mail","who is the smith"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Furen require such strange ingredients?",a="Furen needs unusual ingredients to temper the metal beyond ordinary dwarven methods. His secret craft uses organic materials conditioned by natural venom, mountain winds, and breath weapons, together with volatile phlogiston.",al={"why spider fangs","why horns","what is phlogiston"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where do the chimaera horns come from?",a="The scorched and galvanized horns come from chimaeras in Kalimdor's Stonetalon Mountains. The younger beasts and the formidable Chimaera Matriarch who leads them carry the horns.",al={"where to find chimaera horns","charred horn location","galvanized horn"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Where can phlogiston be found?",a="Roogug, a quilboar geomancer, carries a vial of phlogiston in his lair at Razorfen Kraul, near the southern tip of the Barrens in Kalimdor.",al={"vial of phlogiston","who drops phlogiston","roogug"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Which spiders carry scorched spider fangs?",a="Leech Stalkers and Cave Stalkers carry the scorched spider fangs. These giant arachnids lurk in the Wetlands' marshes and caverns in the Eastern Kingdoms.",al={"scorched spider fangs","where are the spiders","wetlands spiders"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens after all the materials are gathered?",a="Once Furen receives the fangs, horns, and phlogiston, he begins forging a custom breastplate for the warrior. He makes it in his forge as part of Furen's Armor.",al={"what comes next","fire hardened mail follow up","reward"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Furen Longbeard want this done?",a="Furen takes fierce pride in his smithcraft. Having already crafted your shield, he wants to prove his mastery by forging an exceptionally tough suit of mail. He knows the secret techniques required to work these exotic, fire-tempered reagents, and he offers to craft the mail for you simply to see such extraordinary armor brought into being—provided you are willing to brave the perils of gathering the components.",al={"furen longbeard motivation","why make fire hardened mail","why does furen want materials"},it="motive",add="cecd81db"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you prove your mettle by braving Kalimdor's wilds and deep dungeons to earn a piece of masterwork armor.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you know true armor calls for unyielding materials taken straight from nature's harshest predators.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance soldier, you venture deep into the Barrens and Stonetalon Mountains, where the Horde contests the land."},kw={"charred horn","fire hardened mail","furen longbeard","galvanized horn","phlogiston","razorfen kraul","roogug","scorched spider fang","stonetalon","wetlands"},rel={"npc:furen-longbeard","quest:1782","quest:1702","zone:razorfenkraul","zone:stonetalon","zone:wetlands","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:razorfen"},m={start="Furen Longbeard",level="28",faction="Alliance",id=1701,ri={"Charred Horn","Galvanized Horn","Scorched Spider Fang","Vial of Phlogiston"}},src={"Fire Hardened Mail"}}
E["quest:1702"] = {t="quest",n="The Shieldsmith",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind, Yorus Barleybrew sends warriors back after a harrowing trial in the Redridge Mountains. He gives them a cask of Barleybrew Scalder to take to Furen Longbeard, who will fashion a stout shield.",h="In Stormwind, Yorus Barleybrew sends warriors back after a harrowing trial in the Redridge Mountains.",sec={{t="A Promise Kept",b="After you prove your mettle against the gnolls and perils of the Rethban Gauntlet, Yorus Barleybrew honors his bargain. The promised reward cannot be hammered out in Lakeshire, so he directs promising fighters back to Stormwind City. A dwarven armorer there stands ready to repay a personal debt.",sp=0},{t="Barleybrew's Finest",b="Yorus gives you a heavy cask of Barleybrew Scalder instead of a letter of credit. Take it to Furen Longbeard in Stormwind's Dwarven District, where soot and hammer-clatter fill the air. The seasoned smith recognizes the name behind the delivery and lends his craft to a warrior seeking a stout shield.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Furen Longbeard?",a="Furen Longbeard is a master dwarven armorer and shieldsmith stationed in Stormwind City's Dwarven District. Alliance warriors know his skill, and he crafts specialized defensive gear for martial veterans who earn his respect.",al={"furen longbeard","who is furen","who is the shieldsmith"},it="target"},{q="Why does Yorus send you to Stormwind?",a="Yorus Barleybrew sends you to Stormwind because he promised a martial shield but lacks the specialized smithing skills to forge one himself. His friend Furen Longbeard owes him a significant favor.",al={"why go to stormwind","why stormwind","yorus reward location"},it="motive"},{q="What is Barleybrew Scalder?",a="Barleybrew Scalder is an exceptionally potent dwarven drink made by the Barleybrew family. Yorus sends a fresh cask to Furen Longbeard to slake the smith's thirst and grease the wheels of their arrangement.",al={"cask of scalder","barleybrew scalder","what is the scalder"},it="item"},{q="Where can Furen Longbeard be found?",a="Furen Longbeard tends his forge in the heart of Stormwind City's Dwarven District, among the soot, anvils, and workshops of dwarven crafters.",al={"furen location","where is furen longbeard","find furen"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens after giving Furen the cask?",a="The cask confirms that Yorus sent you. Furen acknowledges his debt and immediately offers to construct defensive armor suited to seasoned battle, beginning the path to fire-hardened gear.",al={"what comes next","furen follow up quest"},it="next_step"},{q="Why is this errand important for Alliance warriors?",a="This delivery introduces an Alliance warrior to one of the kingdom's most capable armorers. It opens the way to tailored martial gear and further instruction in defensive warfare.",al={"warrior quest importance","why warriors care"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why does Yorus Barleybrew send you on this delivery instead of a courier?",a="Yorus is making good on his promise after you braved the Rethban Gauntlet. Rather than handling a routine delivery, he is sending you to collect your promised reward in person. Since the shield he promised is with his friend Furen Longbeard in Stormwind, having you carry a cask of his famous Scalder lets him honor his word and call in an old favor directly on your behalf.",al={"why send me shieldsmith","why does yorus send me","why me yorus barleybrew"},it="why_me",add="23250e3d"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you carry the grit of Redridge to Stormwind and prove your right to bear a shield forged by a legendary dwarven armorer.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you know that trading a cask of fine Barleybrew ale for forged iron in Stormwind's Dwarven District is familiar business.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="As a blacksmith, you meet Furen Longbeard, whose specialized defensive armor work is celebrated throughout the Alliance."},kw={"barleybrew scalder","cask","dwarven district","furen longbeard","rethban","shieldsmith","stormwind","warrior","yorus barleybrew"},rel={"npc:furen-longbeard","quest:1699","quest:1701","quest:1698","subzone:dwarven-district","topic:stormwind-kingdom","quest:116"},m={start="Yorus Barleybrew",["end"]="Furen Longbeard",level="22",faction="Alliance",id=1702},src={"The Shieldsmith"}}
E["quest:1705"] = {t="quest",n="Burning Blood",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind, Grimand Elmore turns to Furen Longbeard’s smithing methods. He needs burning blood and a burning rock from Duskwood to test the armorcrafting technique himself.",h="In Stormwind, Grimand Elmore turns to Furen Longbeard’s smithing methods.",sec={{t="A Reluctant Experiment",b="Grimand Elmore is one of the Alliance’s accomplished armorers, and he rarely accepts that another smith might surpass his methods. Hearing of Furen Longbeard’s unusual smithing discoveries stirs his professional curiosity. Grimand agrees to test Furen’s methods by making a piece of armor. He needs strange, volatile components from the dark reaches of the south to quench and temper the metal to his exact requirements; ordinary water and common coals will not do.",sp=0},{t="The Horrors of Roland's Doom",b="Grimand sends you to Duskwood, to the abandoned mine called Roland’s Doom. Savage Nightbane worgen have overrun its tunnels, their cursed veins pulsing with burning ichor. He needs vials of their burning blood and a rare, flaming core called a burning rock, carried by the pack’s leader, Gutspill. Bring these scorching materials back so Grimand can test Furen’s methods at the forge.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Grimand Elmore?",a="Grimand Elmore is a respected master armorer in Stormwind’s Dwarven District. He works with other craftsmen to equip the city’s defenders and trains aspiring warriors in the weight and strength of proper battle plate.",al={"grimand","grimand elmore","stormwind armorer"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Grimand want burning blood and a burning rock?",a="Grimand wants to test an armorcrafting technique developed by Furen Longbeard. The burning blood and burning rock provide the supernatural heat needed to forge and temper specialized armor plates.",al={"why burning blood","what is burning rock for","quest purpose"},it="motive"},{q="Where do I find the Nightbane worgen carrying these materials?",a="You can find the materials in Duskwood at Roland’s Doom, an abandoned mine in southeastern Duskwood, southwest of Darkshire. Nightbane worgen fill its tunnels and carry the burning blood.",al={"where are the worgen","roland's doom location","where is burning blood"},gp=true},{q="Who holds the burning rock?",a="Gutspill, a powerful leader among the Nightbane worgen, carries the burning rock deep within Roland’s Doom.",al={"who has burning rock","gutspill","gutspill location"},it="target"},{q="What is the relationship between Grimand Elmore and Furen Longbeard?",a="Furen Longbeard is Grimand Elmore’s former student. Grimand is usually skeptical of outside ideas, but Furen’s latest armorcrafting methods have persuaded him to test them firsthand.",al={"grimand and furen","who is furen longbeard"},it="ties"},{q="What happens after returning the blood and rock?",a="Grimand begins forging armor after receiving the fiery reagents, to test Furen’s methods. He promises the finished piece to the adventurer who gathered the materials.",al={"next quest","reward","what does grimand make"},it="next_step"},{q="What is the Burning Blood for?",a="Grimand Elmore needs the burning blood to test an exotic smithing technique pioneered by his former student, Furen Longbeard. Drawing on the unnatural, fiery heat running through the veins of Duskwood's worgen, Grimand intends to temper a specialized suit of armor to see if Furen's metallurgy holds genuine merit.",al={"burning blood quest item","what is burning blood used for","why burning blood"},it="item",add="50895b50"},{q="What is the Burning Rock for?",a="Grimand requires the burning rock as an essential component for testing Furen Longbeard's armor-crafting methods. Sourced from the worgen pack leader Gutspill deep within Roland's Doom, the scorching stone provides the raw elemental heat and arcane properties necessary to forge the Fire Hardened Coif.",al={"burning rock use","why burning rock","what does grimand do with burning rock"},it="item",add="8a0ab7ce"},{q="Who are the Nightbane worgen in Duskwood?",a="The Nightbane are feral, wolf-like humanoids that haunt the dark forests of Duskwood. A contingent of them has taken shelter inside the abandoned mine of Roland's Doom, commanded by the fearsome Gutspill. Their unnaturally hot blood and fiery treasures make them the target of ambitious armorers like Grimand.",al={"who are nightbane worgen","rolands doom worgen","nightbane rolands doom"},it="target",add="0438723a"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you can brave Duskwood’s cursed beasts for Grimand’s experiment and earn uniquely tempered armor made for the front lines.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="As a blacksmith, you can see Grimand test the methods of his former student, Furen, with rare metals and quenching agents.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can recover reagents from Roland’s Doom, helping check the worgen threat in Duskwood and supply Stormwind’s armories with new defensive methods."},kw={"burning blood","burning rock","duskwood","furen longbeard","grimand elmore","gutspill","nightbane worgen","roland's doom"},rel={"quest:1700","quest:1706","subzone:roland-s-doom","zone:duskwood","topic:worgen","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Grimand Elmore",level="28",faction="Alliance",id=1705,ri={"Burning Blood (quest item)","Burning Rock"}},src={"Burning Blood (quest)"}}
E["quest:1706"] = {t="quest",n="Grimand's Armor",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind, Grimand's Armor takes shape through a test of Furen Longbeard's methods. Grimand Elmore crafts a helm from rare materials, meant to endure punishing blows in battle. For an Alliance warrior, it marks a step toward mastery.",h="In Stormwind, Grimand's Armor takes shape through a test of Furen Longbeard's methods.",sec={{t="A Master's Innovation Proven",b="Grimand Elmore tests Furen Longbeard's daring smithing methods at his forge in Stormwind's Dwarven District. Grimand had doubted the dwarven master armorer's theories. To put them to the test, a warrior gathers rare elemental and beast components in hostile territory and brings them to Grimand. He uses the materials to forge a reinforced helm built to endure crushing impacts.",sp=0},{t="Forging the Aegis",b="Grimand's finished coif shows that Furen's metallurgic insights were sound. He treats the metal to withstand pressure and physical blows that would warp ordinary steel. Grimand gives the coif to the warrior who helped him, honoring Furen's craft and the warrior's resolve. The armor can help them hold the frontline against Azeroth's greatest threats.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this quest?",a="Grimand Elmore finishes a specially treated coif with the rare materials you gathered, testing Furen Longbeard's experimental smithing methods. This is the final handoff in a major warrior training line.",al={"grimand armor purpose","why do grimands armor","what does grimand give me"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Grimand Elmore?",a="Grimand Elmore is a skilled dwarven weaponsmith in Stormwind's Dwarven District. He works with colleagues in Ironforge to help rising warriors obtain specialized armor.",al={"who is grimand","grimand elmore role","where is grimand"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Furen Longbeard and why is he mentioned?",a="Furen Longbeard is a dwarven master armorer in Stormwind's Dwarven District. He devised a method to fortify armor against immense stress, but Grimand doubted his claims until you brought materials to test it.",al={"who is furen","furen technique","furen longbeard"},it="ties"},{q="What quest leads directly into this one?",a="This follows 'Burning Blood'. There, the warrior brings Grimand the final rare reagent, Burning Blood from the Nightbane worgen of Roland's Doom in Duskwood, so he can quench and temper the metal.",al={"prereq for grimands armor","burning blood quest","what quest comes before this"},gp=true},{q="Can any class complete this quest?",a="No. This chain is for Alliance warriors around their thirtieth season, and marks a rite of passage toward durable mail armor.",al={"is grimand's armor warrior only","who can do grimand armor"},gp=true},{q="Where does this turn-in take place?",a="You bring the coif to Grimand Elmore at his anvil in Stormwind City's Dwarven District.",al={"where turn in grimand armor","grimand location stormwind"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Grimand Elmore want this done?",a="Grimand Elmore is putting Furen Longbeard's radical smithing techniques to the ultimate test. Initially skeptical that Furen's methods could yield superior results, Grimand needed rare and potent components to forge the set himself. By finishing the suit of armor and proving it can withstand incredible punishment, he confirms his fellow smith's breakthrough while equipping an accomplished warrior for battle.",al={"why craft grimands armor","grimand elmore motive","why forge the armor"},it="motive",add="c92a0d61"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As an Alliance warrior, you reach a defining step in your training: a resilient coif forged to withstand the hard blows of frontline combat.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="The exchange brings together two dwarven smiths in Stormwind's Dwarven District, using unusual reagents to temper metal.",["faction:Alliance"]="Grimand Elmore draws on Furen Longbeard's designs, as the dwarven smiths of Stormwind's Dwarven District pool discoveries to arm Alliance warriors."},kw={"armor","coif","burning blood","dwarven district","furen longbeard","grimand elmore","stormwind","warrior quest"},rel={"quest:1700"},m={start="Grimand Elmore",level="30",faction="Alliance",id=1706},src={"Grimand's Armor"}}
E["quest:1782"] = {t="quest",n="Furen's Armor",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind, Furen Longbeard seeks help testing new armor. An aspiring warrior gathers spider fangs, chimaera horns, and phlogiston so the master smith can forge fire-hardened mail. Furen gives the finished armor to the warrior and promises to share what he learned with Alliance smiths.",h="In Stormwind, Furen Longbeard seeks help testing new armor.",sec={{t="A Master's Breakthrough",b="Furen Longbeard, a dwarven armorer in Stormwind, works to improve how Alliance armor withstands heat and crushing blows. He asks an aspiring warrior to gather rare materials for his tests. The resulting mail proves a success and strengthens Furen's standing among Alliance armorers.",sp=0},{t="Sharing the Craft",b="Furen gives the finished fire-hardened mail to the warrior who gathered the materials, grateful for their help. The experiments also deepen his knowledge of protective smithing. He plans to send his notes and findings to other Alliance smiths, so they can put the new methods to use.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Furen Longbeard?",a="Furen Longbeard is a master dwarven armorer in Stormwind who works extensively with the Alliance's martial orders, especially warriors seeking specialized armor.",al={"who is furen","furen longbeard","stormwind smith furen"},it="identity"},{q="What kind of armor did Furen create?",a="Furen forged a Fire Hardened Hauberk, a mail chest piece made with rare fangs, horns, and phlogiston. It is designed to withstand fierce attacks and extreme heat.",al={"what armor does furen make","fire hardened mail","furen's reward"},it="item"},{q="Where does Furen Longbeard send his smithing discoveries?",a="Furen promises to send his findings and notes to fellow blacksmiths across the Alliance, sharing the tested tempering methods with forges throughout the realm.",al={"furen's notes","who gets furen's designs","alliance blacksmiths"}},{q="Why was the warrior asked to gather reagents for Furen?",a="Furen needed rare, volatile materials to test new smithing techniques. Unable to leave his forge to hunt spiders in the Wetlands and chimaeras in Stonetalon, he relied on an ambitious warrior to gather them.",al={"why gather reagents for furen","fire hardened mail quest materials"},it="motive"},{q="Where is this armor forged and delivered?",a="Furen forges and delivers the armor at his forge in Stormwind, where he completes the mail suit.",al={"where is furen longbeard","turn in location","furen location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Does this work benefit other Alliance fighters?",a="Yes. Furen plans to share what he learned with other Alliance armorers, hoping they will use the methods to make strong equipment for Alliance soldiers.",al={"alliance benefit","furen's breakthrough"},it="allies"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As an Alliance warrior, earning Furen's custom-tempered armor marks a passage into frontline service and offers protection for early campaigns.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="Furen's experiment reflects how Alliance smiths share metallurgical findings to improve their craft in Stormwind and Ironforge.",["faction:Alliance"]="Strong arms help keep Alliance forces alive against threats from the Defias, gnolls, and hostile elemental forces."},kw={"alliance warrior","blacksmithing","fire hardened mail","furen longbeard","furen's armor","mail armor","stormwind"},rel={"npc:furen-longbeard","quest:1701","topic:alliance"},m={start="Furen Longbeard",level="28",faction="Alliance",id=1782},src={"Furen's Armor"}}
E["quest:1860"] = {t="quest",n="Speak with Jennea",z="stormwind",s="In Goldshire, Zaldimar Wefhellt sends novice mages to Stormwind for further instruction. He directs apprentices who have advanced beyond basic training in Elwynn Forest to Jennea Cannon in the Wizard's Sanctum.",h="In Goldshire, Zaldimar Wefhellt sends novice mages to Stormwind for further instruction.",sec={{t="A Call to the Wizard's Sanctum",b="Zaldimar Wefhellt sends you from Goldshire to Stormwind City as your training advances. Your time learning elementary spells from local tutors in Elwynn's hamlets has run its course. In the Mage Quarter, the Wizard's Sanctum is where the kingdom's senior mages pursue arcane study and instruction. They coordinate magical matters across the realm.",sp=0},{t="Matters of Kingdom Security",b="Zaldimar says your report concerns the security of Elwynn Forest and Stormwind, not only your studies. In Stormwind, you report to Jennea Cannon, a mage who oversees local assignments. She is cautious about sharing grand secrets with a newly arrived apprentice, but your report begins your service to the wizarding order.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends me on this quest?",a="Zaldimar Wefhellt, the mage trainer at the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire, sends you once your arcane skills have advanced enough.",al={"quest giver","who gives quest","zaldimar"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Jennea Cannon?",a="Jennea Cannon is in the Wizard's Sanctum, in the center of Stormwind City's Mage Quarter.",al={"jennea cannon location","where is jennea","find jennea"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the Wizard's Sanctum?",a="The Wizard's Sanctum is a prominent magical spire in Stormwind's Mage Quarter. The kingdom's mages and arcane scholars use it as an academy, library, and base of operations.",al={"what is wizards sanctum","mage tower stormwind"},it="place"},{q="Why does Zaldimar send me to Jennea instead of handling it himself?",a="Zaldimar teaches young mages the fundamentals in Goldshire. Higher-ranking scholars such as Jennea Cannon oversee larger regional threats and specialized work affecting the realm from the capital.",al={"why go to stormwind","why jennea"},it="why_me"},{q="What happens after reporting to Jennea Cannon?",a="Jennea sends you to investigate mysterious magical anomalies around Mirror Lake in Elwynn Forest.",al={"what next","follow up quest","next step"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Is this quest available to any class?",a="No. Only mages receive this rite of passage from village training into Stormwind's arcane society.",al={"can non mages do this","mage only","class requirement"},gp=true},{q="Why does Zaldimar Wefhellt want you to speak with Jennea?",a="Zaldimar Wefhellt acts out of concern for the safety of both Stormwind City and Elwynn Forest. An urgent matter has arisen that requires the attention of capable mages, but rather than managing it directly, he directs promising apprentices to Jennea Cannon in the Wizard's Sanctum, who oversees the details of this delicate mission.",al={"zaldimar motive","why see jennea","why send to jennea"},it="motive",add="8f9ffa7f"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you leave rural spellcasting in Goldshire for formal work with the high mages at Stormwind's Wizard's Sanctum.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you rely on arcane vigilance from the capital to help protect Elwynn Forest and Stormwind."},kw={"elwynn forest","goldshire","jennea cannon","mage quarter","speak with jennea","stormwind","wizard's sanctum","zaldimar wefhellt"},rel={"npc:jennea-cannon","npc:zaldimar-wefhellt","quest:1861","zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Zaldimar Wefhellt",["end"]="Jennea Cannon",level="10",faction="Alliance",id=1860},src={"Speak with Jennea"}}
E["quest:1938"] = {t="quest",n="Ur's Treatise on Shadow Magic",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind, High Sorcerer Andromath seeks the forbidden tome Morganth stole and carried to the Tower of Ilgalar in the Redridge Mountains.",h="In Stormwind, High Sorcerer Andromath seeks the forbidden tome Morganth stole and carried to the Tower of...",sec={{t="A Schism in the Tower",b="Three promising mages once studied together in Stormwind's Wizard's Sanctum. Morganth turned to dark arts and shadow magic, despite his peers' desperate warnings to abandon those corrupting powers. The city's magical order formally banished him. Before leaving, he stole a dangerous work by Ur, an infamous archmage whose studies reached beyond orthodox arcana.",sp=0},{t="The Fallen Mage's Lair",b="Morganth seized the Tower of Ilgalar in the heights of the Redridge Mountains, far from Stormwind's scrutiny. High Sorcerer Andromath considers the tome's knowledge hazardous in the hands of an outcast practicing forbidden sorcery. He sends Alliance adventurers to breach the tower and recover it before its wards fall.",sp=0},{t="Intact Wards",b="After the treatise is recovered from Ilgalar's library and returned to the Wizard's Sanctum, High Sorcerer Andromath is greatly relieved. He feared Morganth had already unraveled its protective enchantments or hidden the book beyond reach. The magical seals on Ur's treatise held firm, keeping the catastrophic secrets in its pages from the rogue sorcerer.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who wrote the treatise?",a="Ur wrote the treatise. The legendary Dalaran mage was renowned for esoteric research into extra-planar entities and shadow magic.",al={"who is ur","author of the treatise","urs treatise author"},it="origin"},{q="Who stole Ur's Treatise on Shadow Magic?",a="Morganth stole Ur's Treatise on Shadow Magic. He was a Stormwind mage who fell to dark magic and was banished from the Wizard's Sanctum.",al={"who stole the book","who took the treatise","morganth book"},it="target"},{q="Where is the book kept?",a="The book is in the library of the Tower of Ilgalar, high in the Redridge Mountains, where Morganth established his new sanctuary.",al={"where is the treatise","tower of ilgalar book location","where is urs treatise found"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Did Morganth manage to read the book?",a="No. High Sorcerer Andromath confirms that the book's protective seals held firm when it was returned, so Morganth never opened it.",al={"did morganth open the book","was the treatise opened","are the seals broken"},sp=1},{q="Why do the mages of Stormwind want the book back?",a="The tome holds profound secrets of shadow magic that can bring ruin to the untrained. Stormwind's mages consider it too perilous to leave with Morganth, an outcast practicing forbidden sorcery.",al={"why recover the book","why is the treatise dangerous","andromath goal"},it="motive"},{q="Who gives this quest?",a="High Sorcerer Andromath offers it from the Wizard's Sanctum in Stormwind's Mage Quarter.",al={"quest giver","where to get urs treatise quest","andromath quest"},it="in_charge"},{q="What is Ur's Treatise on Shadow Magic?",a="It is a potent and dangerous tome exploring the dark mysteries of shadow magic. Written by the Kirin Tor wizard Ur, its depths are not meant for the untrained, as delving into its forbidden knowledge can lead directly to doom and ruin. To prevent its misuse, the mages of Stormwind bound the volume beneath magical seals.",al={"urs treatise on shadow magic","what is the treatise","what does ur treatise do"},it="item",add="705e1c6d"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you see Stormwind's mages take internal discipline seriously. They entrust practitioners with containing the danger left by a peer who turned to forbidden shadow magic.",["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you may covet the powers of extra-planar summoning and dark casting sealed in Ur's treatises, though the Kirin Tor and Stormwind's mages fear them.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help protect Redridge from Morganth's growing magical menace and Stormwind from rogue arcana by recovering the stolen tome."},kw={"andromath","ilgalar","morganth","shadow magic","stormwind","treatise","ur","wizards sanctum"},rel={"quest:1939","quest:249","subzone:tower-of-ilgalar","quest:115","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:alliance"},m={start="High Sorcerer Andromath",level="28",faction="Alliance",id=1938,ri={"Ur's Treatise on Shadow Magic"}},src={"Ur's Treatise on Shadow Magic (quest)"}}
E["quest:1939"] = {t="quest",n="High Sorcerer Andromath",z="stormwind",s="At Stormwind's Wizard's Sanctum, a summons calls promising Alliance mages to the tower's summit. Andromath works among the kingdom's foremost archmages beyond ruined Dalaran.",h="At Stormwind's Wizard's Sanctum, a summons calls promising Alliance mages to the tower's summit.",sec={{t="Summons to the Tower",b="Jennea Cannon, the apprentice coordinator in Stormwind's Mage Quarter, sends promising casters up to the Wizard's Sanctum summit. High Sorcerer Andromath, among the southern kingdoms' most senior active practitioners of the arcane, has asked to meet magi ready for greater responsibilities.",sp=0},{t="A Master Outside Dalaran",b="Dalaran's magocracy was ruined in the Third War, and its surviving wizards are occupied with rebuilding. Without easy access to the Violet Citadel's libraries, the Alliance depends on senior archmages in Stormwind to study ancient threats and guide research into shadowy, forbidden arts.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is High Sorcerer Andromath?",a="High Sorcerer Andromath is a senior mage at the top of Stormwind's Wizard's Sanctum. Beyond Dalaran, his peers count him among the world's most powerful and knowledgeable spellcasters.",al={"who is andromath","andromath lore","stormwind high sorcerer"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find High Sorcerer Andromath?",a="Andromath is at the summit of the Wizard's Sanctum, the spiraling tower in Stormwind's Mage Quarter.",al={"andromath location","where is andromath","find high sorcerer andromath"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Jennea Cannon send me to see him?",a="Jennea Cannon sends promising casters who have outgrown basic instruction to Andromath for higher counsel and specialized, hazardous research.",al={"why speak to andromath","jennea cannon referral"},it="motive"},{q="What does Andromath need help with?",a="Andromath calls on capable mages to investigate dark arcane secrets, including retrieving the dangerous historical volume Ur's Treatise on Shadow Magic.",al={"andromath questline","what does andromath want"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why is Dalaran described as 'locked away'?",a="Jennea's words reflect how withdrawn the Kirin Tor have been since the Third War. After the Scourge and Burning Legion devastated Dalaran, its surviving wizards turned inward to rebuild, leaving few involved in outside affairs.",al={"why is dalaran locked away","dalaran status","what happened to dalaran"},it="history"},{q="Is this quest exclusive to mages?",a="Yes. The summons belongs to the training path for Alliance mages advancing their craft.",al={"can non mages do this","mage only quest"},gp=true},{q="Why is Jennea Cannon sending me instead of handling it herself?",a="Jennea Cannon serves as an instructor within the Wizard's Sanctum, guiding developing practitioners of the arcane. High Sorcerer Andromath specifically asked to speak with you, an accomplished and rising mage ready for more advanced matters, rather than taking the academy's mentors away from their teaching duties.",al={"why send me","why doesn't jennea go","why does andromath want me"},it="why_me",add="56d3f2e8"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you move from routine spellcraft exercises with Jennea Cannon to dangerous, specialized lore alongside one of Stormwind's foremost archmages.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you depend on Stormwind's Sanctum to train mages and counter supernatural threats while Dalaran's surviving magi rebuild their ruined city."},kw={"andromath","arcane","dalaran","jennea cannon","mage quarter","stormwind","wizard's sanctum"},rel={"npc:jennea-cannon","subzone:dalaran","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:alliance"},m={start="Jennea Cannon",["end"]="High Sorcerer Andromath",level="26",faction="Alliance",id=1939},src={"High Sorcerer Andromath (quest)"}}
E["quest:1940"] = {t="quest",n="Pristine Spider Silk",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind, High Sorcerer Andromath sends rising Alliance mages to Duskwood for pristine spider silk. They bring eight samples to Wynne Larson in the Mage Quarter, where she makes a robe for an adept.",h="In Stormwind, High Sorcerer Andromath sends rising Alliance mages to Duskwood for pristine spider silk.",sec={{t="Vestments of the Adept",b="High Sorcerer Andromath marks a mage’s passage beyond apprenticeship with vestments fit for an adept. In the Wizard’s Sanctum, arcane mastery is matched by the robes its practitioners wear. Rather than buy finished garments, the mage must show field skill and discernment by taking pristine, unblemished silk from dangerous spiders.",sp=0},{t="The Loom of Duskwood",b="Venomous carrion recluse spiders haunt Duskwood’s gloomy woods, and their silk is not sold at ordinary stalls. You gather eight prime samples and carry them across Stormwind to Larson Clothiers in the Mage Quarter. There, Wynne Larson uses the delicate threads to weave a robe with arcane significance.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends mages on this assignment?",a="High Sorcerer Andromath, who presides over the Wizard's Sanctum in Stormwind City, sends spellcasters who have proved their dedication.",al={"who gives pristine spider silk","quest giver pristine spider silk","andromath quest"},it="identity"},{q="Where is the silk harvested?",a="You gather the silk from carrion recluse spiders in Duskwood’s haunted forests and webbed clearings.",al={"where do i get pristine silk","spider location","carrion recluse location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who crafts the robe from the silk?",a="Wynne Larson, a tailor at Larson Clothiers in Stormwind’s Mage Quarter, weaves and tailors the robe.",al={"who weaves the silk","wynne larson","larson clothiers"},it="identity"},{q="Why do mages use spider silk for garments?",a="Pristine spider silk is naturally resilient and finely woven, making lightweight fabric that can hold subtle enchantments without weighing down a spellcaster.",al={"why spider silk","spider silk magic robes"},it="item"},{q="What comes after delivering the silk?",a="After Wynne inspects the silk and works at her loom, she presents the mage with the finished Astral Knot Garment.",al={"next quest after pristine spider silk","what happens next"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Is any spider silk from Duskwood acceptable?",a="No. Larson Clothiers needs pristine samples carefully taken from carrion recluses for its delicate enchantments; coarser webbing will not do.",al={"can i use regular spider silk","pristine vs normal silk"},gp=true},{q="Why does High Sorcerer Andromath send you to gather silk?",a="High Sorcerer Andromath sees your unwavering dedication to the arcane arts and believes it is time your attire reflected your growing mastery. Rather than handing you a finished robe, the Wizard's Sanctum expects you to earn it by braving the perils of Duskwood to gather the rare materials needed for an adept's garment.",al={"why andromath wants silk","andromath motive","why does andromath give this quest"},it="motive",add="a495a13a"},{q="What creatures must you hunt for the silk?",a="You are sent to hunt the carrion recluse spiders lurking in the dark woods of Duskwood. These venomous arachnids spin an exceptionally durable and resonant thread, though only their finest, unblemished strands are suitable for weaving an enchanted garment.",al={"who do i hunt for pristine silk","what spiders drop the silk","carrion recluse duskwood"},it="target",add="8d44c073"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you pass from apprenticeship to adept status through this rite. Every Stormwind mage wears robes woven from hazards they have faced themselves.",["profession:Tailoring"]="As a tailor, you can see how Wynne Larson turns high-grade wild monster fibers into fabric that takes enchantments better than common wool or linen.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance subject, you leave Stormwind’s sanctuary for dangerous Duskwood to gather a rare resource from the region."},kw={"andromath","carrion recluse","duskwood","larson clothiers","mage robes","pristine spider silk","wizard's sanctum","wynne larson"},rel={"npc:wynne-larson","quest:1942","zone:duskwood","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:alliance"},m={start="High Sorcerer Andromath",["end"]="Wynne Larson",level="26",faction="Alliance",id=1940,ri={"Pristine Spider Silk"}},src={"Pristine Spider Silk (quest)"}}
E["quest:1941"] = {t="quest",n="Manaweave Robe",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind, Wynne Larson presents the Manaweave Robe as a proud showcase for her family’s shop. She has woven the enchanted garment from fine materials for a commission that is now complete.",h="In Stormwind, Wynne Larson presents the Manaweave Robe as a proud showcase for her family’s shop.",sec={{t="Larson Clothiers",b="Larson Clothiers serves spellcasters in Stormwind’s Mage Quarter with garments made to channel volatile energies. Fine magical robes call for rare materials, careful needlework, and threadwork that holds through mystic resonance. Wynne Larson takes pride in each piece that leaves her shop, where every robe worn into the field carries the Larson name.",sp=0},{t="Woven Sorcery",b="The manaweave robe offers comfort, mobility, and practical resilience for travel through contested lands. Once the needed components are delivered, Wynne Larson weaves the final stitch herself and presents the finished garment as a fine example of Larson tailoring, meant to draw admiration and spread the shop’s name across the kingdom.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who crafts the Manaweave Robe?",a="Wynne Larson crafts the Manaweave Robe at Larson Clothiers in Stormwind City’s Mage Quarter.",al={"who makes manaweave robe","wynne larson robe","larson clothiers"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Wynne Larson want you to wear the robe with pride?",a="Wynne considers the robe one of her finest creations and asks adventurers to spread the word about Larson Clothiers when others admire its craftsmanship. Their praise brings living promotion to her shop.",al={"why tell people larson","larson advertising","wynne dialogue"},it="motive"},{q="Where is Larson Clothiers located?",a="Larson Clothiers is in Stormwind City’s Mage Quarter, close to the academies and sanctums where Alliance spellcasters gather.",al={"larson shop location","where is wynne larson","mage quarter tailoring shop"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What kind of garment is a Manaweave Robe?",a="The Manaweave Robe is an enchanted cloth garment for practitioners of magic, tailored to channel mystic energies and remain practical on dangerous journeys.",al={"manaweave robe lore","what is manaweave robe","what does the robe do"},it="item"},{q="Is this part of a longer questline?",a="Yes. It concludes a mage chain begun by Jennea Cannon. After investigating a mana rift at the Blue Recluse, you gather linen and charged rift gems for Wynne Larson to make your robe.",al={"manaweave chain","robe quest chain","questline end"},it="history",gp=true},{q="What faction can undertake this quest?",a="Only members of the Alliance can undertake it. Wynne Larson works entirely within Stormwind, the Alliance capital.",al={"alliance or horde robe","can horde get manaweave robe","faction requirement"},it="side",gp=true}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage studying in Stormwind’s towers, you wear a tailored manaweave robe as a sign of graduation into serious field research and independent spellcraft.",["profession:Tailoring"]="Wynne Larson’s work shows the high standard of human tailoring, weaving worldly materials to harness and temper volatile arcane power.",["faction:Alliance"]="When you outfit a promising champion through a local shop in the capital, you help carry Stormwind’s prestige and self-sufficiency across troubled territories."},kw={"apprentice robe","clothier","larson clothiers","mage quarter","manaweave robe","stormwind","tailor","wynne larson"},rel={"npc:wynne-larson"},m={start="Wynne Larson",["end"]="Wynne Larson",level="15",faction="Alliance",id=1941},src={"Manaweave Robe (quest)"}}
E["quest:1942"] = {t="quest",n="Astral Knot Garment",z="stormwind",s="Wynne Larson works fine spider silk into a garment in Stormwind City. An adventurer brings her rare silk gathered from the wilds, and she tailors it into a magical weave for dangerous journeys and high-society gatherings.",h="Wynne Larson works fine spider silk into a garment in Stormwind City.",sec={{t="A Weaver's Wit",b="In Stormwind's Mage Quarter, tailors serve arcane elites and visiting nobles. Wynne Larson is known for weaving pristine spider silk into durable, enchanted garments. Her playful humor comes through when she jokes about saving a few precious scraps for her own wardrobe before handing over her finished work.",sp=0},{t="Versatile Elegance",b="Spellcasters who wear cloth prize the Astral Knot Garment for its resilience and refinement. Its silk comes from dangerous spiders, and its weave is made to endure combat while keeping the polished look expected at formal banquets in Stormwind Keep.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Astral Knot Garment?",a="Wynne Larson crafts the Astral Knot Garment in Stormwind City from pristine spider silk. It is made for cloth-wearing practitioners facing combat or attending high-society affairs.",al={"what is astral knot garment","astral knot robe","astral knot vestments"},it="item"},{q="Who crafts the Astral Knot Garment?",a="Wynne Larson, a tailor in Stormwind's Mage Quarter, crafts the garment when given the needed exotic materials.",al={"who makes astral knot","wynne larson quest","astral knot tailor"},it="identity"},{q="What materials are required to complete this garment?",a="The garment requires pristine spider silk gathered from deadly spiders in the wild regions of the world. Tailoring preserves the silk's natural strength and enchantability.",al={"materials for astral knot","spider silk needed","how is it made"},gp=true},{q="Why does Wynne Larson tease about keeping leftover silk?",a="Wynne jokes about making the garment short so she can keep a few scraps of the rare, prized spider silk. She delivers the finished work in full.",al={"did she steal my silk","wynne larson joke","short robe"}},{q="Where in Stormwind does this tailoring take place?",a="The tailoring takes place in Stormwind's Mage Quarter, a district of scholars, arcanists, and clothiers skilled in enchanted textiles.",al={"where is wynne larson","astral knot location","where to turn in astral knot"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who typically wears the Astral Knot Garment?",a="Alliance mages favor the Astral Knot Garment for its light, protective weave and dignified appearance.",al={"who uses astral knot","what class is this for","who wears it"},it="for_you"},{q="Why does Wynne Larson craft the Astral Knot Garment?",a="Wynne Larson is a skilled tailor in Stormwind who agrees to weave the garment as the culmination of your efforts. Having sent you across perilous lands to gather rare components like pristine spider silk, she takes pride in fashioning exceptional vestments tailored for practitioners of magic, combining practical protection with exquisite formal elegance.",al={"why does wynne larson make the garment","wynne larson motive astral knot garment","why does wynne craft the robe"},it="motive",add="96918ee1"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you can see Stormwind's arcane dignity in this garment, with practical enchantments for travel beyond the kingdom's fortified walls.",["profession:Tailoring"]="Wynne Larson's work shows how pristine spider silk can be refined into grand fashion.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance champion, you can find Stormwind craftsmanship suited to royal halls and dangerous frontlines alike."},kw={"astral knot garment","cloth armor","mage quarter","pristine spider silk","silk robe","stormwind","tailoring","wynne larson"},rel={"npc:wynne-larson","quest:1940","topic:alliance"},m={start="Wynne Larson",level="26",faction="Alliance",id=1942},src={"Astral Knot Garment"}}
E["quest:2205"] = {t="quest",n="Seek out SI: 7",z="stormwind",s="In Goldshire, Keryn Sylvius sends new rogues toward SI: 7. A sealed package carried to Stormwind City brings them before Master Mathias Shaw, who leads the crown's covert intelligence network.",h="In Goldshire, Keryn Sylvius sends new rogues toward SI: 7.",sec={{t="A Courier's Test",b="At the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire, rogue trainer Keryn Sylvius wastes no time praising newcomers. She thinks fresh initiates look more like cheese delivery hands than covert agents, yet gives them a sealed delivery for the capital. The trip tests their reliability as couriers and quietly vets scouts for wider service to the realm.",sp=0},{t="Behind Closed Doors in Old Town",b="SI: 7 works from the southeastern corner of Old Town in Stormwind City. The worn district holds the command center of Stormwind Intelligence, Section 7, where Master Mathias Shaw oversees the kingdom's covert operations. Shaw receives the package with dry skepticism and judges whether the traveler has the grit for real espionage.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is SI:7?",a="SI: 7 means Stormwind Intelligence, Section 7. Led by Master Mathias Shaw from its Old Town headquarters, it handles the Kingdom of Stormwind's secret intelligence and covert operations.",al={"what does si 7 mean","what is si7","si:7 lore"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Keryn Sylvius?",a="Keryn Sylvius trains rogues at the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire. She works with SI: 7, evaluates local recruits, and directs promising scouts to Master Mathias Shaw in Stormwind City.",al={"keryn sylvius","goldshire rogue trainer"},it="people"},{q="Where is Mathias Shaw located in Stormwind?",a="Master Mathias Shaw is on the upper floor of SI: 7 headquarters, in the southeastern corner of Old Town in Stormwind City, past the city's rogue trainers.",al={"where is shaw","find mathias shaw","mathias shaw location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens after delivering the package to Shaw?",a="After you report to Mathias Shaw, he tests your rogue skills by sending you to Jerod's Landing to steal a shipping schedule from a Defias dockmaster.",al={"next quest after seek out si 7","what does shaw want"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Keryn mock the player before handing over the delivery?",a="SI: 7 operatives prize competence and sharp instincts. Keryn Sylvius treats new recruits harshly to judge their temperament and see whether they have the resolve to approach Master Shaw.",al={"why does keryn insult me","cheese delivery insult"}},{q="Why does Keryn Sylvius want this package delivered to Mathias Shaw?",a="Keryn made a formal commitment to deliver the parcel to Master Mathias Shaw as part of an official assignment. While she clearly disdains running standard courier errands herself, sending you serves a dual purpose: it honors her obligation to the agency while putting your fledgling rogue talents to the test before her superiors in Stormwind.",al={"why deliver to mathias","keryn sylvius motive","why send package to si7"},it="motive",add="5aa3ad9f"},{q="Why does Keryn send an unproven rogue instead of delivering the package herself?",a="Keryn is stationed out in Goldshire scouting and mentoring new talent, leaving her little interest in walking minor deliveries back to Old Town. Handing the task off to an eager novice like you spares her the legwork while serving as a practical audition to see if you are sharp enough to locate the headquarters of Stormwind's secret service.",al={"why does keryn send me","why me seek out si7","why not deliver it herself"},it="why_me",add="6bd14f9c"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you enter Stormwind's foremost espionage agency, moving from back-alley tricks to royal reconnaissance.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you rely on SI: 7 to guard the realm against threats within and beyond its borders while King Varian Wrynn remains missing."},kw={"goldshire","keryn sylvius","mathias shaw","old town","rogue","seek out si: 7","si:7","stormwind"},rel={"quest:2206","npc:mathias-shaw","npc:keryn-sylvius","subzone:old-town","zone:stormwind","subzone:goldshire","quest:2300"},m={start="Keryn Sylvius",["end"]="Mathias Shaw",level="10",faction="Alliance",id=2205},src={"Seek out SI: 7"}}
E["quest:2206"] = {t="quest",n="Snatch and Grab",z="stormwind",s="Master Mathias Shaw sends agents to Jerod's Landing for shipping intelligence. The Defias Brotherhood uses the river dock to move supplies in secret.",h="Master Mathias Shaw sends agents to Jerod's Landing for shipping intelligence.",sec={{t="A Test of Tradecraft",b="Master Mathias Shaw tests aspiring operatives who seek a place in Stormwind's covert intelligence wing. He asks for finesse and stealth, not brute force. SI:7 agents take down key figures quietly and recover important papers without drawing the realm into open scandal. Each new operative must prove they can work unseen.",sp=0},{t="Smugglers on the River",b="Jerod's Landing lies on the river in southern Elwynn, south of Goldshire and just east of the Maclure Vineyards. The Defias Brotherhood seized the once-quiet dock and made it an illicit route. Smuggled arms, supplies, and contraband cross the water from Redridge toward Westfall, beyond the reach of royal road patrols.",sp=0},{t="Plausible Deniability",b="Master Mathias Shaw warns agents that capture, compromise, or death leaves them without the Crown's support. Stormwind and its spymasters will deny knowing they ever existed. Recovering the Defias Dockmaster's schedule gives SI:7 proof of the Brotherhood's supply lines while keeping Stormwind's official involvement hidden.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who assigns the quest Snatch and Grab?",a="Master Mathias Shaw, leader of Stormwind's intelligence service SI:7, assigns the work from its headquarters in Old Town.",al={"who gives snatch and grab","quest giver snatch grab"},gp=true},{q="Where is Jerod's Landing?",a="Jerod's Landing is a river dock in southern Elwynn Forest, south of Goldshire and just east of the Maclure Vineyards. The Defias Brotherhood has taken control of the docks and dock house.",al={"jerods landing location","where is jerod's landing","dockmaster location"},gp=true},{q="What are the Defias smuggling through Jerod's Landing?",a="The Defias move contraband and supplies across the water between Redridge and Westfall, beyond kingdom watchposts and road checkpoints.",al={"what are they smuggling","defias contraband"}},{q="Who carries the Defias Shipping Schedule?",a="The Defias Dockmaster carries the shipping schedule and guards the dock house at Jerod's Landing.",al={"where is shipping schedule","who drops schedule","defias dockmaster"},gp=true},{q="What happens if an operative is captured during this mission?",a="Master Mathias Shaw warns that SI:7 will deny any connection to an operative who is exposed or captured.",al={"what happens if i fail","disavowed by si7"}},{q="Why does SI:7 care about this shipping schedule?",a="The schedule details how the Defias Brotherhood moves contraband between Redridge and Westfall. It lets Stormwind's intelligence network map the enemy's supply lines without alerting the syndicate.",al={"why need schedule","si7 shipping schedule"},it="motive"},{q="What is the Defias Shipping Schedule?",a="The schedule details the transport of illicit goods across the waterways of Elwynn Forest. The Defias Brotherhood has commandeered Jerod's Landing to run large amounts of contraband between Redridge and Westfall right under the nose of the realm. Recovering these timetables provides SI:7 with concrete intelligence on Defias movement corridors and logistical routes.",al={"defias shipping schedule","what is shipping schedule","shipping schedule use"},it="item",add="170a7301"},{q="Who is the Defias Dockmaster?",a="The Dockmaster oversees the Brotherhood's covert operations at Jerod's Landing, a dockhouse on the river south of Goldshire. From this vantage, he coordinates the flow of smuggled supplies, weapons, and stolen cargo moving between Redridge and Westfall, keeping the contraband manifests on his person to direct the Defias riverrunners.",al={"defias dockmaster","who is the dockmaster","dockmaster jerods landing"},it="target",add="5dd0ffd3"},{q="Why does Mathias Shaw send you instead of senior SI:7 agents?",a="You were sent to Mathias Shaw as a promising new rogue recruit scouted by Keryn Sylvius. Infiltrating Jerod's Landing serves as both a live operational test of your stealth and thievery and a deniable field mission. Because SI:7 plans to disavow all knowledge of you if caught, using a green operative keeps Stormwind's premier intelligence network shielded from public exposure.",al={"why send me","why recruit for si7","why mathias shaw needs you"},it="why_me",add="a07026c6"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you are introduced to SI:7 and tested in stealth and cutpurse instincts. Earn Mathias Shaw's recognition and a signature blade.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help intercept Defias supply lines at Jerod's Landing, protecting Elwynn Forest and weakening the criminal syndicate that threatens Stormwind's surrounding territories."},kw={"crystal lake","defias","dockmaster","goldshire","jerod's landing","mathias shaw","shipping schedule","si:7","snatch and grab"},rel={"quest:2205","npc:mathias-shaw","subzone:jerod-s-landing","subzone:goldshire","zone:westfall","quest:2300"},m={start="Master Mathias Shaw",level="10",faction="Alliance",id=2206,ri={"Defias Shipping Schedule"}},src={"Snatch and Grab"}}
E["quest:2281"] = {t="quest",n="Redridge Rendezvous",z="stormwind",s="Promising Alliance rogues are sent east from Stormwind’s intelligence headquarters to train in Lakeshire. SI:7 wants them ready for dangerous field work under seasoned operatives.",h="Promising Alliance rogues are sent east from Stormwind’s intelligence headquarters to train in Lakeshire.",sec={{t="A Measure of Survival",b="Renzik 'The Shiv', SI:7’s second-in-command in Stormwind, warns that untrained rogues rarely survive dangerous operations. Sending raw recruits into hostile territory brings casualties instead of intelligence. SI:7 sends promising agents east to the Redridge Mountains, where they train under Lucius, stationed among Lakeshire’s docks.",sp=0},{t="Eyes in Lakeshire",b="Lakeshire offers an ideal ground for clandestine training. Gnolls and Blackrock orcs threaten the frontier town, while its piers give Lucius cover to test a rogue’s stealth, reflexes, and lockpicking without attracting townspeople or guards.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Redridge Rendezvous?",a="Renzik 'The Shiv', a goblin spymaster in Stormwind’s Old Town, gives the assignment from SI:7 headquarters to rogues who report to intelligence command.",al={"who starts redridge rendezvous","redridge rendezvous questgiver","who gives quest"},it="identity",gp=true},{q="Where is Lucius located?",a="Lucius waits along Lakeshire’s wooden docks in the Redridge Mountains, among local loafers and fishermen by the water.",al={"where is lucius","lucius location","find lucius"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does SI:7 send rogues to Redridge?",a="Renzik considers inexperienced rogues unfit for dangerous intelligence work. Lucius sharpens their rough edges and tests skills such as pickpocketing and lockpicking under frontier conditions.",al={"why lakeshire","purpose of redridge rendezvous","why redridge"},it="motive"},{q="What comes after completing Redridge Rendezvous?",a="Reporting to Lucius leads to training exercises that begin at Alther's Mill, where the agent tests stealth and manual dexterity.",al={"next quest","redridge rendezvous followup","after redridge rendezvous"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Is this quest available to classes other than rogues?",a="No. Redridge Rendezvous is for Alliance rogues, as part of their SI:7 field training.",al={"can warriors do redridge rendezvous","is this rogue only","class requirement"},gp=true},{q="Why does Renzik work for Stormwind intelligence?",a="Though a goblin, Renzik 'The Shiv' is a trusted lieutenant of Spymaster Mathias Shaw. He oversees operative intake and training from within SI:7’s stronghold.",al={"why is a goblin in si7","renzik lore","goblin in stormwind"},it="history"},{q="Why does Renzik need me for this assignment?",a="SI:7 needs fresh operatives capable of handling dangerous covert work, but Renzik knows tossing an unpolished rogue straight into active field operations is essentially a death sentence. Rather than waste promising talent, he dispatches you specifically so you can sharpen your tradecraft under Lucius before tackling missions that could get you killed.",al={"why me renzik","why pick me redridge","why send me to lucius"},it="why_me",add="da1ebf68"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you begin formal SI:7 field work here, moving from backstreet thievery to calculated state espionage.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you see Stormwind’s clandestine arm reaching outer settlements such as Lakeshire, where quiet operatives are stationed."},kw={"lakeshire","lucius","redridge rendezvous","renzik the shiv","rogue quest","si:7","stormwind"},rel={"npc:lucius","npc:renzik-the-shiv","quest:2300","quest:2282","subzone:lakeshire","zone:redridge"},m={start="Renzik \"The Shiv\"",["end"]="Lucius",level="16",faction="Alliance",id=2281},src={"Redridge Rendezvous"}}
E["quest:2300"] = {t="quest",n="SI:7",z="stormwind",s="In Goldshire, Keryn Sylvius sends promising young rogues toward Stormwind's hidden ranks. Recruits report to Renzik \"The Shiv\" in Old Town, where they enter Master Mathias Shaw's service.",h="In Goldshire, Keryn Sylvius sends promising young rogues toward Stormwind's hidden ranks.",sec={{t="A Summons to Old Town",b="Keryn Sylvius watches local recruits from the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire. When a rogue proves cunning and capable against the growing Defias threat, Sylvius passes along a message from headquarters. The order is plain: report to Renzik \"The Shiv\" without delay. The recruit leaves Elwynn's fields for the covert heart of Stormwind.",sp=0},{t="Stormwind's Hidden Eyes",b="Behind an unassuming barracks in Old Town, SI:7 keeps its headquarters. Master Mathias Shaw commands the agency, whose work includes covert operations, reconnaissance, and assassination across the kingdom and beyond. Renzik \"The Shiv,\" Shaw's sharp-tongued second-in-command, assesses promising agents before sending them into dangerous work beyond the reach of the kingdom's formal military.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends me to report to SI:7?",a="Keryn Sylvius, the rogue trainer at the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire, sends you to report to SI:7. After you prove your skill in the field, Sylvius gives you orders to report to Stormwind headquarters.",al={"who gives quest","quest giver","keryn sylvius"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Renzik \"The Shiv\"?",a="Renzik \"The Shiv\" is a goblin operative and SI:7's second-in-command under Master Mathias Shaw. He evaluates field agents and coordinates covert intelligence assignments from the headquarters in Old Town.",al={"renzik the shiv","who is renzik","renzik"},it="identity"},{q="What is SI:7?",a="SI:7, or Stormwind Intelligence, handles covert espionage, reconnaissance, and assassination for the Kingdom of Stormwind. Led by Mathias Shaw, its operatives gather intelligence on threats the kingdom's guards and soldiers cannot address.",al={"what is si7","what does si7 do","stormwind intelligence"},it="purpose"},{q="Where is the SI:7 headquarters located?",a="SI:7's headquarters is in eastern Old Town in Stormwind City. The agency operates from a fortified guildhall and training barracks set away from the main streets.",al={"where is si7","si7 location","where is renzik"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens after reporting to Renzik?",a="After you report to Renzik, he tests your readiness, then sends you beyond the city walls to meet an operative stationed in Redridge.",al={"next quest","what comes after","redridge rendezvous"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Keryn Sylvius call me 'fish'?",a="“Fish” is slang for an untested novice or new recruit. Agency operatives use colorful, abrasive nicknames to keep rookies grounded until they prove themselves on real assignments.",al={"why called fish","fish meaning"}},{q="Why does Keryn Sylvius send me to SI:7?",a="Keryn Sylvius is acting on orders from high above. Renzik \"The Shiv\" specifically sent word that he was looking for you, and Keryn knows better than to ignore a summons from Mathias Shaw's second-in-command. In the covert hierarchy of Stormwind's intelligence service, when Renzik calls for an operative, intermediaries like Keryn promptly pass along the command without keeping headquarters waiting.",al={"why does keryn send me","keryn sylvius motive","why report to si7"},it="motive",add="d2c94cb8"},{q="Why does SI:7 need me instead of their own agents?",a="Renzik \"The Shiv\" specifically asked for you by name. As an up-and-coming rogue working within the Alliance's network, you represent fresh talent outside the immediate gaze of local adversaries. Master Shaw and Renzik frequently rely on capable, newly proven field agents to take on discreet assignments across the kingdom where seasoned, well-known faces might draw unwanted attention.",al={"why me si7","why does renzik want me","why call on me"},it="why_me",add="fe886311"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, this summons takes you from local work into service as an operative for Stormwind's official intelligence branch.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can look to SI:7 for dangerous espionage beyond the reach of regular marshals and infantry."},kw={"keryn sylvius","mathias shaw","old town","renzik the shiv","rogue","sentinel hill","si:7","stormwind"},rel={"npc:renzik-the-shiv","npc:keryn-sylvius","quest:2281","quest:2282","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Keryn Sylvius",["end"]="Renzik \"The Shiv\"",level="16",faction="Alliance",id=2300},src={"SI:7 (quest)"}}
E["quest:2359"] = {t="quest",n="Klaven's Tower",z="stormwind",s="Agent Kearnen watches Klaven's Tower from a camp in Westfall. Strange shipments and altered guards point to a threat inside the Defias Brotherhood.",h="Agent Kearnen watches Klaven's Tower from a camp in Westfall.",sec={{t="A Stakeout in Westfall",b="Near the river at Westfall's southeastern edge, Klaven's Tower rises north of the Dagger Hills. The Defias Brotherhood claims the stone spire, though its human thieves and brigands are common across the plains. Agent Kearnen has watched it alone for weeks and noticed strange developments. A bizarre shipment recently came straight from Duskwood's shadowed woods. Monstrous, deformed sentries escorted it, unlike any ordinary highwaymen.",sp=0},{t="The Spire and the Spiked Guard",b="Klaven Mortwake commands the tower, where oddly altered sentries breathe in harsh, labored gasps. A hulking zombie among the shambling guards carries the Defias Tower Key, and taking it calls for silence and finesse. With the key, an operative can bypass the ground defenses, reach the stronghold's upper levels, and open the padlocked Duskwood Chest.",sp=1},{t="Zanzil's Concoction",b="Klaven Mortwake's personal journal links the Defias, the Venture Company, and the jungle trolls of Stranglethorn. The writings say the witch doctor Zanzil discovered an alchemical poison that can raise unthinking, obedient undead drones. For Master Mathias Shaw and SI:7, the discovery reveals the Defias's widening ambitions. Its agents need a firm understanding of poisons.",sp=2}},faq={{q="Where is Klaven's Tower located?",a="Klaven's Tower stands at Westfall's southeastern edge, near the river and north of the Dagger Hills. The Defias Brotherhood holds the fortified spire.",al={"klavens tower location","where is klavens tower","defias tower location westfall"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Agent Kearnen?",a="Agent Kearnen works for Stormwind's intelligence service, SI:7. She has watched Klaven's Tower in secret for weeks from a nearby camp, tracking strange shipments and planning an infiltration.",al={"agent kearnen","who gives klaven's tower quest","who is the rogue in westfall"},it="identity"},{q="What makes the guards at Klaven's Tower unusual?",a="The tower's sentries are altered undead, unlike the Defias's usual human bandits. An exotic alchemical concoction shipped into Westfall made them mindless laborers.",al={"why are guards zombies","klaven tower guards","what are the tower guards"},sp=1,it="threat"},{q="How does the Defias have undead servants?",a="The Defias obtained a specialized toxic brew from Zanzil, a jungle troll witch doctor in Stranglethorn Vale. The poison came through dealings with the Venture Company and turns living subjects into obedient drones.",al={"how did defias get zombies","why defias have undead","zanzil defias connection"},sp=1,it="origin"},{q="Who is Klaven Mortwake?",a="Klaven Mortwake is a high-ranking Defias overseer at the tower. He oversaw dark shipments from Duskwood and kept a private journal about their sinister alchemy.",al={"klaven mortwake lore","who is klaven mortwake","klaven"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Mathias Shaw care about the recovered journal?",a="Master Mathias Shaw needs useful intelligence on Defias alliances and dangerous foreign agents. Word that Zanzil's trolls can create undead through poison warns SI:7 of a grave threat to Stormwind, so the agency must train its operatives in venomcraft.",al={"why mathias shaw wants journal","si7 zanzil poison","mathias shaw klaven"},sp=1,it="why_wanted"},{q="Why does Agent Kearnen want this done?",a="Agent Kearnen has staked out Klaven's Tower for weeks tracking Defias activity. When an eerie shipment arrived from Duskwood under the guard of inhuman creatures, she knew the Brotherhood was harboring something dangerous. Her duty to SI:7 is surveillance and intelligence gathering; uncovering what lies locked inside that chest will expose whatever sinister venture the Defias are concocting right under Stormwind's nose.",al={"kearnen motive","why does agent kearnen need this","kearnen reason"},it="motive",add="af44437f"},{q="What is the Defias Tower Key for?",a="The Defias Tower Key grants access to the heavily fortified stronghold and the Duskwood chest guarded within. Carried by one of the grotesque, spiked monstrosities patrolling the perimeter, the key is your only way to bypass the Defias locks and investigate what their strange allies have smuggled into Westfall.",al={"defias tower key","what opens klaven tower","tower key use"},it="item",add="043ff283"},{q="What is Klaven Mortwake's Journal?",a="Locked away inside the Duskwood chest atop the tower, this journal contains the records and secrets of Klaven Mortwake. It details how the Defias Brotherhood partnered with outside forces to brew vile concoctions, revealing that strange potions from Zanzil's trolls can induce a state of living death to create unquestioning drones.",al={"klaven mortwake journal","klaven's journal","what is in the journal"},sp=1,it="item",add="d5d17d25"},{q="Why does Agent Kearnen send you instead of going herself?",a="Agent Kearnen is an SI:7 scout whose primary assignment is long-term reconnaissance. Breaking her cover to breach a fortified outpost crawling with unnatural guards would compromise her post and alert the Defias before SI:7 learns what they are planning. She needs a capable operative to slip past the sentries, secure the intelligence, and deliver it directly to Mathias Shaw.",al={"why me klaven tower","why doesn't kearnen infiltrate","why send me"},it="why_me",add="738a266c"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As an Alliance rogue, you face a covert infiltration that calls for stealth, pickpocketing, lockpicking, and finding an enemy's physical weakness.",["faction:Alliance"]="The Defias at Klaven's Tower have joined with jungle trolls and dark alchemy to threaten the kingdom. They are more than aggrieved masons.",["race:Human"]="As a human defender of Stormwind, you may be horrified to find former countrymen turned into mindless undead drones in Westfall."},kw={"agent kearnen","defias brotherhood","duskwood chest","klaven mortwake","klaven's tower","mathias shaw","poisons","si:7","westfall","zanzil"},rel={"npc:mathias-shaw","quest:2300","topic:stormwind-kingdom","zone:duskwood","topic:troll","topic:venture-company"},m={start="Agent Kearnen",["end"]="Master Mathias Shaw",level="24",faction="Alliance",id=2359,ri={"Defias Tower Key","Klaven Mortwake's Journal"}},src={"Klaven's Tower (quest)"}}
E["quest:269"] = {t="quest",n="Seeking Wisdom",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind, Sven Yorgen seeks holy counsel for Duskwood. He sends Jitters' Completed Journal to Bishop Farthing at the Cathedral of Light, hoping the bishop can reveal how to destroy Morbent Fel's shield.",h="In Stormwind, Sven Yorgen seeks holy counsel for Duskwood.",sec={{t="A Plea from the Shadows",b="Duskwood suffers beneath lingering curses and ravenous undead, while Stormwind's royal court grows indifferent. Sven Yorgen, a broken-hearted survivor at a camp near the borders, knows ordinary strength cannot pierce Morbent Fel's dark wards. With Jitters' assembled journal, Sven asks you to seek the church's counsel. The road north leads to the Cathedral of Light.",sp=0},{t="Counsel in the Cathedral",b="Bishop Farthing hears Duskwood's pleas at Stormwind's Cathedral. Jitters' account confirms Morbent Fel's dread power: vile sorcery shields the necromancer from ordinary blows. Courage alone cannot overcome those wards. To defeat him, an enchanted holy instrument must be found.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Sven send you to Bishop Farthing instead of King Anduin?",a="Sven trusts Bishop Farthing, a compassionate and learned man of the Holy Light who understands foul magic. Stormwind's nobility and army have largely left Darkshire and the surrounding lands to fend for themselves amid political paralysis, so Sven expects no soldiers from official channels.",al={"why farthing","why not stormwind nobles","stormwind ignored duskwood"},it="motive"},{q="What is Jitters' journal and why does the Bishop need it?",a="Jitters recorded what happened around the attack on Sven's farm. Sven sends the completed account to Bishop Farthing so he can advise the adventurer preparing to face Morbent Fel.",al={"what is jitters journal","why jitters journal","jitters completed journal"},it="item"},{q="Who is Morbent Fel?",a="Morbent Fel is a powerful necromancer seen at the Forlorn Rowe in Duskwood. He commands hordes of skeletal minions and shields himself with potent wards that turn aside normal weapons.",al={"who is morbent fel","morbent fel lore"},it="target"},{q="Where is Bishop Farthing located?",a="Bishop Farthing resides in the Cathedral of Light, the grand human cathedral in Stormwind City's Cathedral Square district.",al={"where is farthing","farthing location","bishop farthing map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens after Bishop Farthing reads the journal?",a="Bishop Farthing explains that ordinary blows cannot harm Morbent Fel. He points you toward a sanctified relic that can dispel the necromancer's wards, beginning the search for the Doomed Fleet.",al={"what next seeking wisdom","seeking wisdom followup","after seeking wisdom"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Where does Sven Yorgen stay in Duskwood?",a="Sven Yorgen shelters at a small camp in northwestern Duskwood, near the river border, south of Elwynn Forest and west of the haunted Raven Hill Cemetery.",al={"where is sven","sven yorgen location","sven's camp"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Sven Yorgen need you to deliver the journal?",a="Sven is holding out alone in Duskwood, consumed by vengeance and grief while surviving in a camp surrounded by horrors. Stormwind has abandoned Darkshire and the surrounding lands to fend for themselves, leaving no royal guards to assist him. Sven cannot leave Duskwood unguarded, nor does he possess the means to break Morbent Fel's dark sorcery alone. Having proven your mettle against the local threats, you represent his only reliable hope to carry Jitters' uncovered truth to someone with the wisdom and holy power to help.",al={"why me sven","why send player to bishop farthing","why doesnt sven go to stormwind"},it="why_me",add="12ed4f38"}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, carrying pleas for holy aid from the abandoned borderlands to the Cathedral of Light tests the Silver Hand's duty to protect the forgotten and purge necromancy.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, Bishop Farthing offers guidance on how dark wards corrupt body and soul. Shadow sorcery calls for focused sanctification as well as the blade.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, the journey reveals the divide between Stormwind City's guarded marble halls and Duskwood's forsaken towns, which receive no garrison support."},kw={"bishop farthing","cathedral of light","darkshire","duskwood","jitters","morbent fel","seeking wisdom","stormwind","sven yorgen"},rel={"npc:farthing","npc:sven-yorgen","npc:jitters","quest:55","quest:270","subzone:cathedral-of-light","zone:duskwood","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Sven Yorgen",["end"]="Bishop Farthing",level="29",faction="Alliance",id=269},src={"Seeking Wisdom"}}
E["quest:2745"] = {t="quest",n="Infiltrating the Castle",z="stormwind",s="Master cheese monger and intelligence broker Elling Trias directs you into the royal seat of Stormwind Keep. Your objective is to rendezvous with his fellow operative Tyrion, who has spent weeks watching the corrupt nobleman Lord Gregor Lescovar from the keep's gardens.",h="Master cheese monger and intelligence broker Elling Trias directs you into the royal seat of Stormwind Keep.",sec={{t="A Matter Outside the Law",b="When you bring your findings to Elling Trias in his Trade District cheese shop, he quickly grasps the gravity of the Defias threat nestled deep inside the kingdom's governance. Legal channels will not suffice to expose or punish someone as deeply entrenched and protected as Lord Gregor Lescovar. Trias offers a dangerous route forward: delivering extrajudicial justice within the very walls of Stormwind Keep to permanently sever the conspiracy.",sp=0},{t="Eyes in the Shrubbery",b="Trias does not work alone in the high halls. For weeks, an operative named Tyrion—a clever gnome adept at concealment—has staked out the keep's courtyards and manicured royal gardens. Tyrion has watched Lescovar's movements, noting who enters his chambers and when the traitor confers with his covert Defias contacts. Reaching Tyrion without arousing the suspicion of the Royal Guard is the vital next link in the chain.",sp=0},{t="Treason in the Court",b="The presence of a high nobleman like Lescovar colluding directly with Defias assassins like Marzon the Silent Blade underscores how rotten Stormwind's political core has become in the absence of King Varian Wrynn. With court nobles manipulating affairs from within and outlaws pressing the borders from Westfall and the Redridge Mountains, striking at Lescovar represents an attempt to cut out a festering cancer before the kingdom crumbles completely.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Elling Trias want this handled outside the law?",a="Lord Lescovar holds immense influence and wealth within the House of Nobles. Pursuing ordinary legal accusations against a high-ranking lord without indisputable, politically disastrous proof would likely see the evidence suppressed and the whistleblowers executed. Trias recognizes that direct, clandestine action is the only reliable way to neutralize the threat.",al={"why outside law","trias illegal justice","why vigilante"},it="motive"},{q="Where is Tyrion hiding?",a="Tyrion conceals himself in the royal gardens of Stormwind Keep, just off the courtyard to the left after walking through the main gates. He lurks in the bushes to observe Lord Lescovar's quarters without alerting the guards.",al={"where is tyrion","find tyrion","tyrion location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Tyrion?",a="Tyrion is a covert operative and a trusted associate of Elling Trias. He has spent several weeks staking out Stormwind Keep to monitor Lord Gregor Lescovar and map out his clandestine Defias connections.",al={"who is tyrion","tyrion gnome","trias friend"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Lord Lescovar?",a="Lord Gregor Lescovar is a prominent Stormwind nobleman secretly collaborating with the Defias Brotherhood, acting as their highly placed insider to sabotage the kingdom from within its royal court.",al={"lord lescovar","who is lescovar","lescovar defias"},it="threat"},{q="Who is Marzon?",a="Marzon, known as the Silent Blade, is an elite Defias assassin who liaises directly with Lord Lescovar to coordinate attacks and assassinations on behalf of the Brotherhood.",al={"marzon","marzon the silent blade","silent blade"},sp=1,it="threat"},{q="Why is Tyrion worried about his reputation?",a="Beyond blowing his cover while conducting clandestine surveillance, Tyrion snarkily complains about how suspicious and unseemly it appears to have heavily armed adventurers loitering alongside him in the royal shrubbery under the noses of the castle guards.",al={"tyrion hiding bushes","reputation in bushes"}},{q="Who are you being sent after in Stormwind Castle?",a="Elling Trias sends you to deal with Lord Gregor Lescovar and his associate Marzon. Lescovar is a nobleman operating right inside Stormwind Keep, suspected of treasonous ties, while Marzon represents the dangerous conspirators outside the castle walls. Trias and his contact Tyrion want both men neutralized before their plotting can threaten the realm.",al={"who are we targeting","who is the target in infiltrating the castle","who are lescovar and marzon"},it="target",add="ae2213ef"},{q="Why does Elling Trias send you instead of using the Stormwind city guard?",a="Lord Lescovar is a high-ranking noble in Stormwind Keep, making an official accusation politically impossible without undeniable proof. The city guard answers to the court, where nobility holds sway, and alerting official channels would likely warn Lescovar or bury the matter in red tape. Trias relies on an independent adventurer to slip in, rendezvous with Tyrion, and enact decisive justice without tipping off the conspirators.",al={"why send me","why not tell the guards","why not stormwind guards"},it="why_me",add="7d59c2b3"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="Infiltrating the seat of human nobility to aid two seasoned underground operatives highlights the quiet, lethal tradecraft required to protect Stormwind from shadows inside its own court.",["race:Gnome"]="Seeing Tyrion run an intensive, long-term covert surveillance operation inside Stormwind Keep proves that gnomish ingenuity extends well beyond machinery into high-stakes espionage.",["faction:Alliance"]="With King Varian missing, the kingdom cannot afford betrayal in its highest legislative chamber; routing out conspirators in the Keep is critical to keeping the realm stable."},kw={"cheese shop","defias","elling trias","infiltrating the castle","lescovar","stormwind keep","tyrion"},rel={"npc:elling-trias","npc:tyrion","quest:350","quest:2746","subzone:stormwind-keep","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:gnome","subzone:dark-portal"},m={start="Elling Trias",["end"]="Tyrion",level="31",faction="Alliance",id=2745},src={"Infiltrating the Castle"}}
E["quest:2746"] = {t="quest",n="Items of Some Consequence",z="stormwind",s="Tyrion gathers silk and apples for a spy inside Stormwind Keep. The covert operative needs the materials to disguise Spybot and send it past the royal guards to listen in on Lord Lescovar.",h="Tyrion gathers silk and apples for a spy inside Stormwind Keep.",sec={{t="A Tightening Schedule",b="Elling Trias has moved the operation against Lord Gregor Lescovar forward. The cheese merchant suspects Lescovar's schemes inside Stormwind Keep threaten the realm. In the keep's gardens, Tyrion agrees to the tighter schedule, but says the disguise needs careful preparation.",sp=0},{t="The Art of the Disguise",b="Tyrion plans to send Spybot, a small mechanical contraption, past the castle guards to reach Lescovar inside the keep. A strange feminine disguise should turn suspicion aside. For it, you gather suitably sized apples from Clara's orchard just outside the city walls, along with bolts of silk for the puppet's clothes.",sp=0},{t="Uncovering Treason",b="Tyrion first began watching Lord Lescovar over suspicious leads tying the noble to the Twilight's Hammer cult. He now reveals that Lescovar is also colluding with Defias conspirators. With that treachery exposed, Lescovar can no longer remain in the royal court, and Tyrion's surveillance becomes a sting at the heart of the kingdom.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Tyrion need apples and silk cloth?",a="Tyrion needs apples and silk to disguise Spybot as a woman so it can pass the royal guards in Stormwind Keep. The silk becomes clothing, and the apples provide the shape needed to complete the disguise.",al={"why apples","what are the apples for","tyrion disguise materials","spybot disguise"},it="item"},{q="Who is Tyrion working for?",a="Tyrion works with Elling Trias, a Trade District cheese merchant who runs his own network of friends in Stormwind. Trias says the operation only indirectly does a favor for Mathias Shaw and SI:7.",al={"who does tyrion report to","tyrion allegiance","elling trias tyrion"},it="ties"},{q="Where do I find Clara's apples?",a="Clara's orchard is just outside Stormwind's city gates in northern Elwynn Forest. You can gather fresh apples around the farm.",al={"clara farm location","where are claras apples","fresh apples stormwind"},gp=true},{q="What did Tyrion originally suspect Lord Lescovar of doing?",a="Tyrion and Trias first suspected Lord Lescovar had ties to the Twilight's Hammer cult. They later uncovered his collaboration with the Defias Brotherhood, a deeper treason and an imminent threat to the crown.",al={"lescovar twilight hammer","why was lescovar investigated","tyrion lescovar history"},sp=1,it="threat"},{q="What is the next step after delivering these items?",a="After Spybot is outfitted and sent into the keep, you are tasked with confronting and eliminating the conspirators in 'The Attack!'.",al={"what happens next","after items of some consequence","next quest after items of some consequence"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why use a mechanical spybot instead of sneaking in personally?",a="Stormwind Keep's royal sentries scrutinize everyone entering the throne room and private courtyards. Disguised as a priestess, Spybot can pass them, speak with Lescovar, and draw him into the garden to meet Marzon, where no known agent could get close.",al={"why use spybot","why not sneak in yourself","stormwind keep security"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does Tyrion want to bring down Lord Lescovar?",a="Tyrion and his associate Elling Trias have been trailing Lord Lescovar for weeks under suspicion of subversive ties. While originally looking into potential cultist involvement with the Twilight's Hammer, discovering that Lescovar is actively conspiring with the Defias Brotherhood makes him an immediate and severe danger to Stormwind. Tyrion intends to expose and neutralize him before his treason can tear the city apart.",al={"why stop lescovar","tyrion motive","why investigate lescovar"},it="motive",add="7ec9a91a"},{q="Why does Tyrion need an outsider's help instead of the city guards?",a="Lord Lescovar is a nobleman inside Stormwind Keep, making an open accusation or direct guard intervention impossible without undeniable proof. The Stormwind authorities are not in a position to act on hunches against a high-ranking noble. Tyrion operates in the shadows on behalf of Master Trias, requiring an independent agent willing to collect clandestine supplies and eventually handle the dangerous, covert confrontation personally.",al={"why not city guards","why does tyrion need me","why rely on adventurer"},it="why_me",add="73f45f0b"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a Rogue, you can see how operatives like Tyrion and Elling Trias use unorthodox surveillance, with domestic intelligence working under the nobles' noses.",["profession:Tailoring"]="As a Tailor, you know fine silk can serve undercover schemes as well as formal gowns.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help protect the young King Anduin and Highlord Bolvar Fordragon by rooting out corrupt aristocrats who conspire with outlaws inside Stormwind Keep."},kw={"clara","elling trias","infiltrating the castle","lord lescovar","silk cloth","spybot","stormwind keep","the attack","tyrion"},rel={"quest:2745","quest:434","npc:tyrion","topic:defias-brotherhood","topic:twilight-s-hammer","topic:stormwind-kingdom","quest:65"},m={start="Tyrion",level="31",faction="Alliance",id=2746,ri={"Clara's Fresh Apple","Silk Cloth"}},src={"Items of Some Consequence"}}
E["quest:2998"] = {t="quest",n="Tome of Divinity",z="stormwind",s="A summons bearing the Tome of Divinity calls promising paladins from Elwynn to Stormwind. Answering Brother Wilhelm's call begins the sacred trials needed to master resurrection through the Holy Light.",h="A summons bearing the Tome of Divinity calls promising paladins from Elwynn to Stormwind.",sec={{t="A Summons to the Capital",b="Novice paladins in Elwynn Forest spend their early days helping locals and testing their strength against wolves, Defias bandits, and kobolds. When an initiate shows martial discipline and devotion to the Holy Light, mentors such as Brother Wilhelm send a personal summons. Leaders of the paladins take note of promising students and direct them to leave the local chapels behind and report straight to the kingdom's spiritual heart.",sp=0},{t="The Cathedral of Light",b="In Cathedral Square, Stormwind's Cathedral of Light is the supreme sanctuary of the kingdom's priesthood and the Knights of the Silver Hand. Duthorian Rall resides there and oversees those sworn to the Order. Beneath its soaring vaulted ceilings, high-ranking paladins set formal trials from the Tome of Divinity before each initiate. The challenges test compassion, fortitude, and a willingness to sacrifice.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends me to Stormwind for this quest?",a="Brother Wilhelm, the paladin trainer near the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire, sends you to Stormwind when you have shown promise and strength in the field.",al={"quest giver","who gives quest","brother wilhelm"},gp=true},{q="Where can I find Duthorian Rall?",a="Duthorian Rall resides inside the Cathedral of Light in Cathedral Square, in northwestern Stormwind City. He spends most of his days training paladins beneath its grand halls.",al={"duthorian rall location","where is duthorian rall","paladin master location"},gp=true},{q="Why is this summons so important for paladins?",a="Reporting to Duthorian Rall marks a passage from basic martial training into deep holy communion. The Tome of Divinity's trials begin there and ultimately grant the sacred power to call fallen allies back from death through the Light.",al={"why do this quest","quest importance","paladin trial"},it="purpose"},{q="Do non-human paladins receive this exact quest?",a="Brother Wilhelm's summons from Elwynn Forest is meant for human paladins. Dwarven paladins receive a parallel calling from their own trainers in Dun Morogh to visit Ironforge.",al={"dwarf paladin","can dwarves do this","is this quest human only"},gp=true},{q="What happens after reporting to Duthorian Rall?",a="When you greet Duthorian Rall, he welcomes you to Stormwind and immediately presents the Tome of Divinity's trials, which challenge your compassion and dedication to defending the weak.",al={"next quest","what happens next","tome of divinity next step"},it="next_step"},{q="Who is Duthorian Rall?",a="Duthorian Rall is among the most influential paladins in Stormwind and the Knights of the Silver Hand. He instructs new generations of holy warriors in the capital.",al={"who is duthorian","duthorian rall lore"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Brother Wilhelm send you to Duthorian Rall?",a="Brother Wilhelm holds great respect for Duthorian Rall, one of the Order's most influential paladins. Having overheard Duthorian speak highly of your service and mention that you are ready to be put to the test, Wilhelm simply wants to ensure you seize the opportunity. Guiding promising initiates toward advanced instruction is his duty and pride as a mentor in Goldshire.",al={"why does wilhelm send me","brother wilhelm motive","why talk to duthorian rall"},it="motive",rc="Human",add="69ec335a"}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="Your mentors formally recognize your deeds and send you before the high commanders of the Silver Hand, marking a rite of passage for paladins.",["race:Human"]="Your journey from rural Elwynn Forest to the grand Cathedral of Light anchors you to the kingdom's deepest spiritual and martial institutions.",["faction:Alliance"]="Stormwind's recruitment and testing of holy warriors helps the Alliance keep dedicated frontline healers and combatants through troubled times."},kw={"brother wilhelm","cathedral of light","duthorian rall","goldshire","paladin","redemption","stormwind","tome of divinity"},rel={"npc:duthorian-rall","npc:brother-wilhelm","subzone:cathedral-of-light","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:light"},m={start="Brother Wilhelm",["end"]="Duthorian Rall",level="12",faction="Alliance",id=2998},src={"Tome of Divinity (Brother Wilhelm)"}}
E["quest:322"] = {t="quest",n="Blessed Arm",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind, Blessed Arm carries lightforge iron toward a weapon against Morbent Fel. After salvaging the ingots from the wreck of the Flying Osprey in the Wetlands, you bring the precious metal to master dwarven smith Grimand Elmore, who can shape it to face the necromancer.",h="In Stormwind, Blessed Arm carries lightforge iron toward a weapon against Morbent Fel.",sec={{t="A Rare Metal Returns",b="Glorin Steelbrow packs the recovered lightforge iron for Stormwind. The metal is rare, and its power against foul and unholy beings demands a smith who knows how to work it. After the shipment came from the wreck of the Flying Osprey off the Wetlands coast, Glorin knew of only one artisan in the southern kingdoms suited to the task: master weaponsmith Grimand Elmore.",sp=0},{t="The Dwarven District's Forge",b="In Stormwind's Dwarven District, Grimand Elmore keeps one of the city's finest anvils. Years have passed since he last hammered lightforge iron, he says, when you bring him the recovered shipment. The veteran artisan is intrigued by the chance to strike at the necromancer Morbent Fel, and agrees to put his hammer to work.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this delivery?",a="The crate holds lightforge iron salvaged from the Flying Osprey wreck in the Wetlands. Glorin Steelbrow sends it to Grimand Elmore, who can shape the consecrated metal into a weapon against the necromancer Morbent Fel.",al={"why bring ingots to stormwind","blessed arm purpose","what is crate of lightforge ingots for"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Grimand Elmore?",a="Grimand Elmore is a respected dwarven weaponsmith who works in Stormwind's Dwarven District. Few craftsmen have the training to forge specialized metals like lightforge iron.",al={"grimand elmore lore","who is the smith in dwarven district"},it="identity"},{q="Why is lightforge iron so important against Morbent Fel?",a="Lightforge iron is renowned for its power against foul and unholy beings. Grimand Elmore can shape the consecrated metal into a weapon to confront the necromancer Morbent Fel.",al={"why lightforge iron","how does lightforge iron hurt morbent fel"},it="item"},{q="Where does Glorin Steelbrow send you?",a="Glorin Steelbrow sends you from Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands to Grimand Elmore's forge in Stormwind City's Dwarven District.",al={"where do i go for blessed arm","where is grimand elmore located"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Has Grimand Elmore worked with lightforge iron before?",a="Yes. Grimand says years have passed since he last worked with lightforge iron, and welcomes the chance to shape the storied metal again.",al={"did grimand forge lightforge before","elmore smithing experience"},it="history"},{q="What must happen before the weapon can be finished?",a="Grimand agrees to forge the recovered lightforge iron into Morbent's Bane. When he is finished, you take the weapon to Sven Yorgen in Duskwood.",al={"what comes after blessed arm","is weapon forged immediately"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Glorin Steelbrow want this delivery made?",a="Glorin knows that ordinary steel cannot break through the dark protections guarding Morbent Fel in Duskwood. Having recovered the lightforge iron you secured from the wreck of the Flying Osprey in the Wetlands, he recognizes your campaign against the necromancer and directs you to a skilled smith who can forge a weapon truly capable of harming him.",al={"glorin steelbrow motive","why does glorin help","why send ingots to grimand"},it="motive",add="983cc211"}},ang={["profession:Blacksmithing"]="Lightforge iron is rare and difficult to work. Watching the experienced dwarven smith Grimand Elmore take it on shows the skill needed to forge holy arms.",["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, carrying consecrated iron to shape a weapon against a Duskwood necromancer follows the Silver Hand's calling: meet dark sorcery with holy vigilance.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you carry aid between kingdoms, from a dwarven priest in Menethil Harbor to Stormwind's Dwarven District, for the beleaguered people of Duskwood."},kw={"blessed arm","dwarven district","glorin steelbrow","grimand elmore","lightforge iron","loch modan","morbent fel","stormwind"},rel={"quest:324","quest:1700","npc:glorin-steelbrow","subzone:dwarven-district","quest:55","quest:321","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Glorin Steelbrow",["end"]="Grimand Elmore",level="29",faction="Alliance",id=322},src={"Blessed Arm"}}
E["quest:325"] = {t="quest",n="Armed and Ready",z="stormwind",s="You carry Morbent's Bane back to Sven Yorgen, the weapon forged to strip away Morbent Fel's unholy defenses.",h="You carry Morbent's Bane back to Sven Yorgen, the weapon forged to strip away Morbent Fel's unholy defenses.",sec={{t="A Weapon Forged",b="Morbent Fel's hold over Raven Hill cemetery resists ordinary steel. Blades shatter or glance off the dark wards around the necromancer. A weapon made to break those wards is now ready. Grimand Elmore shaped the metal in Stormwind's Dwarven District, and sacred power consecrated it. Morbent's Bane can now sever Fel's tie to unlife.",sp=0},{t="Return to the Hermit",b="Sven Yorgen waits at his lonely camp near Duskwood's western border, after the encroaching darkness brought ruin to his family, farm, and companions. You bring him Morbent's Bane, forged to break Morbent Fel's wards. Sven recognizes the weapon's divine craftsmanship and the fire in your eyes. With the weapon in his hands, he can strike at the master of Raven Hill.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Morbent's Bane?",a="Morbent's Bane is a weapon forged and consecrated to break the magical wards surrounding Morbent Fel at Raven Hill.",al={"morbents bane","what is the weapon","morbent bane sword"},it="item"},{q="Who crafted the weapon?",a="Grimand Elmore, a blacksmith in Stormwind City's Dwarven District, fashioned the weapon from consecrated lightforge iron.",al={"who made morbents bane","grimand elmore role"},it="origin"},{q="Where do I deliver Morbent's Bane?",a="You deliver Morbent's Bane to Sven Yorgen at his camp in western Duskwood, near the Westfall border.",al={"where is sven","sven yorgen location","turn in location"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why can't Sven Yorgen fight Morbent Fel himself?",a="The dark forces in the woods drove Sven Yorgen from his home and cost him his family and companions. Isolated and hunted, he depends on Alliance champions to avenge them.",al={"why doesnt sven fight","sven yorgen backstory"}},{q="What happens after completing Armed and Ready?",a="After Sven receives the blessed weapon, he sends you to Raven Hill Cemetery to face Morbent Fel and strike him down.",al={"what comes next","next quest after armed and ready"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="What is the quickest route back to Sven's camp?",a="From Sentinel Hill in Westfall, travel east across the river to reach Sven's camp, a shorter and safer route than going west through Darkshire's dangers.",al={"fastest way to sven","how to get to sven quickly"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does Grimand Elmore want Morbent's Bane delivered to Sven?",a="Grimand Elmore is a master blacksmith of Stormwind who took up the task of forging a weapon capable of piercing dark magic. Having completed Morbent's Bane, he eagerly sends you back to Duskwood so that the weapon can be put to its intended purpose, wishing you victory against the necromancer and looking forward to hearing your tale of triumph.",al={"grimand elmore motive","why does grimand help","why help sven grimand"},it="motive",add="4a0f4d98"},{q="Why does Grimand Elmore need you to take the weapon instead of delivering it himself?",a="Grimand is a smith working out of the Dwarven District in Stormwind, not a wandering adventurer or courier. You brought him the materials and the grim news from Duskwood, and as the one preparing to face the fiend alongside Sven Yorgen, it falls on you to carry the consecrated arm back to the field.",al={"why me armed and ready","why doesnt grimand go to duskwood","why send player to sven"},it="why_me",add="2182c2f5"}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you know how holy power joined with dwarven steel can break wards protecting the undead.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="As a blacksmith, you can see how Grimand Elmore joined fine smithing with sacred rites to make a weapon against supernatural threats.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you see Stormwind artisans supply the expertise survivors in Duskwood need to confront the spreading blight."},kw={"armed and ready","duskwood","grimand elmore","morbent fel","morbent's bane","raven hill","stormwind","sven yorgen"},rel={"npc:sven-yorgen","quest:55","quest:322","quest:1700","zone:duskwood","subzone:sentinel-hill","zone:westfall","subzone:darkshire"},m={start="Grimand Elmore",["end"]="Sven Yorgen",level="29",faction="Alliance",id=325},src={"Armed and Ready (Classic)"}}
E["quest:332"] = {t="quest",n="Wine Shop Advert",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind, Renato Gallina draws passersby to his family's wine shop. He offers a voucher for a free bottle of vintage wine from their canal-side storefront, a small sign of trade in the reconstructed capital.",h="In Stormwind, Renato Gallina draws passersby to his family's wine shop.",sec={{t="A Taste of the Canals",b="Everyday life in Stormwind revolves around brisk commerce. Renato Gallina walks the Trade District's cobbled streets, promoting Gallina Winery, the small shop he runs with his sister, Suzetta. He hands flyers to thirsty travelers and locals, each offering a free tasting.",sp=0},{t="The Pinot Noir Vintage",b="The Gallina family offers a bottle of their famous pinot noir. Follow the ticket to the winery entrance near the canals, where Suzetta Gallina hands over the bottle. The family hopes a taste of their signature wine will bring newcomers back.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Gallina Winery located?",a="Gallina Winery is in Stormwind City's Trade District, along the canals near Renato Gallina's route.",al={"where is gallina winery","suzetta gallina location","where is wine shop advert turned in"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who are Renato and Suzetta Gallina?",a="Renato and Suzetta Gallina are siblings who run a wine shop in Stormwind. Renato promotes it with flyers, while Suzetta tends the shop and serves the wine.",al={"who are the gallinas","renato gallina","suzetta gallina lore"},it="people"},{q="What wine does the ticket earn?",a="The ticket earns a bottle of the Gallinas' famous pinot noir, their signature red wine.",al={"pinot noir wine","what wine do you get","pinot noir stormwind"},it="item"},{q="Why does Renato give out free wine tickets?",a="Renato gives out free wine tickets to draw customers into the canal-side shop and encourage them to return.",al={"why free wine","wine shop ticket purpose"},it="motive"},{q="Does this errand involve any danger or combat?",a="No. You take a promotional ticket from Renato and walk a short distance through the safe streets of the Trade District to Suzetta at the storefront.",al={"is wine shop advert dangerous","wine quest fights"},it="danger",gp=true},{q="Does the Gallina Winery sell other goods?",a="Suzetta stocks standard wines and other alcoholic drinks for travelers, guards on break, and local tavern suppliers.",al={"what else does suzetta sell","gallina winery drinks"},gp=true}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="The Gallinas' pinot noir pairs with hearty meals prepared in taverns across the Eastern Kingdoms.",["race:Human"]="As a human rebuilding a life in Stormwind, you may find family-run wineries along the canals a comforting sign of the city's revival.",["faction:Alliance"]="Even in turbulent times, with kings missing and war underway, Stormwind's Trade District keeps a lively market for domestic luxuries and imported goods."},kw={"canals","gallina winery","pinot noir","renato gallina","suzetta gallina","trade district","wine shop advert","wine ticket"},rel={"npc:renato-gallina","npc:suzetta-gallina","subzone:trade-district","subzone:canals-stormwind-city","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Renato Gallina",["end"]="Suzetta Gallina",faction="Alliance",id=332},src={"Wine Shop Advert"}}
E["quest:333"] = {t="quest",n="Harlan Needs a Resupply",z="stormwind",s="Harlan Bagley, a Stormwind merchant, cannot keep sturdy clothes and armor in stock. As demand surges, he sends an urgent cloth order to Rema Schneider at the Canal Tailor and Fit Shop, unaware of the conflicts brewing beyond the city walls.",h="Harlan Bagley, a Stormwind merchant, cannot keep sturdy clothes and armor in stock.",sec={{t="A Run on Sturdy Clothes",b="Across Stormwind City, Harlan Bagley's shelves are emptying fast. Citizens and wandering adventurers are buying reinforced tunics, traveling clothes, and battle-ready armor. Harlan wonders if people are preparing for a harsh season or winter, but the rush has left his shop short of finished cloth.",sp=0},{t="Questions on the Canals",b="Harlan sends a runner across the city's waterways to Rema Schneider, a seamstress at the Canal Tailor and Fit Shop. She is glad of his trade, yet the sudden demand for protective clothing troubles her. Rumors of tension spread through the kingdom, and Rema wonders whether the House of Nobles is hiding talk of open war from ordinary people.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Harlan Bagley?",a="Harlan Bagley is a clothier and shopkeeper in Stormwind City. Local tailors supply the knitted goods and travel-ready clothes he sells.",al={"harlan bagley","who is harlan","bagley stormwind"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Rema Schneider?",a="Rema Schneider is a professional tailor and seamstress at the Canal Tailor and Fit Shop in Stormwind. With her husband Corbett, she supplies merchants across the city with freshly sewn fabric and garments.",al={"rema schneider","tailor rema","canal tailor"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Harlan running out of clothing?",a="Citizens and travelers are buying armor and rugged clothes in unusually high numbers. Harlan jokes that they seem to expect a bitter winter, though rising unrest and danger across the kingdom's borders are the true cause.",al={"why out of cloth","why buying armor","harlan business booming"},it="motive"},{q="Why does Rema Schneider suspect the nobles?",a="Rema finds it strange that ordinary people are suddenly preparing for battle without an official declaration of conflict. The House of Nobles controls royal affairs while King Varian Wrynn is absent, and she fears the nobles are concealing an impending war from the public.",al={"rema nobles","stormwind nobles hiding war","why nobles suspect"},it="conflict"},{q="Where is the Canal Tailor and Fit Shop located?",a="The Canal Tailor and Fit Shop is along the waterways that run through Stormwind City, between the major city districts for convenient merchant deliveries.",al={"canal tailor location","where is rema schneider","where is canal tailor"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens after the cloth request is delivered?",a="After Rema receives the order, she asks her husband Corbett Schneider to carry another load of knitted goods across the city to Harlan at the Lionheart Armory. On his way back to the shop, Corbett stops at Trias' Cheese for a snack.",al={"corbett schneider walk","what does corbett do","rema husband"},it="next_step"}},ang={["profession:Tailoring"]="Stormwind's canal workshops supply larger shops, revealing the everyday workings of the city's textile trade.",["faction:Alliance"]="Stormwind's shoppers show growing unease in the Alliance heartland while King Varian Wrynn is absent.",["race:Human"]="Stormwind's working artisans distrust their rulers and suspect the nobility is keeping ordinary people in the dark about looming dangers."},kw={"bagley","canal","cloth","harlan","rema","resupply","schneider","stormwind","tailor"},rel={"npc:harlan-bagley","npc:rema-schneider"},m={start="Harlan Bagley",["end"]="Rema Schneider",faction="Alliance",id=333},src={"Harlan Needs a Resupply"}}
E["quest:334"] = {t="quest",n="Package for Thurman",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind City, Rema Schneider needs her son Thurman’s tailoring supplies at Larson Clothiers in the Mage Quarter. He left home without his shears and needles, and Rema asks you to carry them to his workshop.",h="In Stormwind City, Rema Schneider needs her son Thurman’s tailoring supplies at Larson Clothiers in the Mage...",sec={{t="A Mother's Errand",b="Rema Schneider worries that Thurman will fall behind in his tailoring work without his shears and needles. He left home in a rush, and his mother asks you to carry the tools across Stormwind’s canals to his workshop.",sp=0},{t="A Reluctant Apprentice",b="Larson Clothiers is in the Mage Quarter, near the Mage Tower. When Thurman receives his tools, he admits he left them behind on purpose so he could skip his daily chores and have fun. Rema’s intervention ends his free afternoon, and he returns to his stitching.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who starts the quest Package for Thurman?",a="Rema Schneider asks you to carry a sewing kit to her son, who works in the Mage Quarter.",al={"who gives quest","rema schneider quest","quest giver"},gp=true},{q="Where can Thurman Schneider be found?",a="Thurman Schneider works inside Larson Clothiers in Stormwind’s Mage Quarter, near the path to the Mage Tower.",al={"thurman location","where is thurman","find thurman"},gp=true},{q="Did Thurman actually forget his tools by accident?",a="Rema believes Thurman hurried out without his kit and asks you to bring it to him.",al={"did thurman forget","why did thurman leave tools","thurman slacking"},sp=1},{q="What shop does Thurman apprentice for?",a="Thurman apprentices as a tailor at Larson Clothiers, a garment shop in Stormwind’s Mage Quarter run by the Larson family.",al={"where does thurman work","larson clothiers","who does thurman work for"}},{q="Why does Rema Schneider ask an adventurer for help?",a="Rema believes Thurman’s apprenticeship is in jeopardy without his kit. Unable to leave her own obligations, she asks travelers heading toward the Mage Quarter to help.",al={"why ask player","rema help"},it="why_me"},{q="What happens after you deliver the sewing kit?",a="Thurman takes his kit and returns to helping the Larsons with their sewing.",al={"quest reward","after package for thurman","thurman reaction"},sp=1,it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does Rema Schneider want this done?",a="Rema is looking out for her son Thurman's future. He has secured a spot as an apprentice at Larson Clothiers in the Mage Quarter, but he rushed out without his shears and needles. Without his tools, Thurman cannot perform his duties or learn his trade, risking his standing with his employers. Believing it was an honest accident, she wants his kit delivered immediately so his training is not compromised.",al={"why does rema need the sewing kit delivered","rema schneider motive","why deliver the tools to thurman"},it="motive",add="3c7bea70"}},ang={["profession:Tailoring"]="Every grand tailor starts at the bottom, running seams and holding pins. At Larson Clothiers, even an apprentice may wish to slip away from chores.",["faction:Alliance"]="Stormwind’s ordinary citizens and artisans keep the capital clothed, fed, and running, one errand at a time."},kw={"apprentice","clothiers","larson","mage quarter","rema","schneider","sewing kit","stormwind","thurman"},rel={"npc:rema-schneider","subzone:mage-quarter","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Rema Schneider",["end"]="Thurman Schneider",faction="Alliance",id=334},src={"Package for Thurman"}}
E["quest:335"] = {t="quest",n="A Noble Brew",z="stormwind",s="Zardeth of the Black Claw schemes against Stormwind's nobles from beneath the Slaughtered Lamb. Lord Wishock's call for an investigation puts the hidden warlock coven at risk.",h="Zardeth of the Black Claw schemes against Stormwind's nobles from beneath the Slaughtered Lamb.",sec={{t="Threat from the Nobility",b="Beneath the Mage Quarter streets, warlocks gather in the Slaughtered Lamb and keep their coven hidden. Lord Wishock, a member of the House of Nobles, has heard of the dark magic below the city. He is urging his peers to launch a full investigation, which could bring the city guard and royal scrutiny down on the coven.",sp=0},{t="A Concoction in the Shadows",b="To avoid an open clash with Stormwind's ruling class, Zardeth of the Black Claw seeks a quiet remedy to keep Lord Wishock occupied. The brew calls for rare plants from distant parts of the Eastern Kingdoms: the pale Tear of Tilloa from Duskwood, and a Musquash Root gathered underwater beneath the Stonewrought Dam.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Lord Wishock?",a="Lord Wishock is a nobleman in Stormwind's House of Nobles. After hearing hints of warlock activity beneath the Mage Quarter, he began pressing the council to open a formal investigation.",al={"wishock","lord wishock","who is wishock"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Zardeth of the Black Claw?",a="Zardeth is a senior warlock in the crypts beneath Stormwind's Slaughtered Lamb. He works to shield the city's warlock cabal from discovery and a purge by the authorities.",al={"zardeth","zardeth black claw","who is zardeth"},it="identity"},{q="Where does the Tear of Tilloa come from?",a="The Tear of Tilloa is a delicate white flower found in the overgrown Garden of Stalvan, on the outskirts of Darkshire in Duskwood.",al={"tear of tilloa location","tear of tilloa","where is tear of tilloa"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Where is the Musquash Root found?",a="The Musquash Root grows only in the wetlands at the very base of the massive waterfalls beneath the Stonewrought Dam in the Wetlands.",al={"musquash root location","musquash root","where to get musquash root"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Why doesn't Stormwind's government already know about the warlocks?",a="Warlocks are deeply distrusted in Stormwind, so the coven beneath the Slaughtered Lamb hides its practice underground, away from the city guards and nobles. Lord Wishock has only just caught wind of it.",al={"stormwind warlocks secret","why are warlocks hiding","are warlocks illegal"},it="conflict"},{q="What does Zardeth intend to brew with these reagents?",a="Zardeth says the brew will keep Lord Wishock occupied and stall the investigation. What he intends for the nobleman becomes clear only when the brew is ready.",al={"what is the brew","noble brew purpose","why make the brew"},sp=1,it="purpose"},{q="Why does Zardeth of the Black Claw want this done?",a="Lord Wishock discovered the clandestine warlock coven operating beneath the Slaughtered Lamb in Stormwind's Mage Quarter. With Wishock actively rallying the House of Nobles to launch a formal investigation into their presence, Zardeth needs a concoction to keep the meddling noble preoccupied before the city authorities crack down on their dark practices.",al={"why help zardeth","zardeth motive","why does zardeth want a noble brew"},it="motive",add="e620a973"},{q="What is the Tear of Tilloa for?",a="The Tear of Tilloa is a delicate white flower harvested from the Garden of Stalvan near Darkshire. Zardeth requires it as a primary reagent for brewing a special mixture intended to neutralize Lord Wishock's political crusade against the coven.",al={"what does tear of tilloa do","tear of tilloa purpose","why need tear of tilloa"},it="item",add="9e466bd7"},{q="What is the Musquash Root for?",a="The Musquash Root grows at the mist-shrouded base of the falls beneath the Stonewrought Dam in the Wetlands. Zardeth uses its potent properties alongside the Tear of Tilloa to craft a brew potent enough to distract Lord Wishock.",al={"what does musquash root do","musquash root purpose","why need musquash root"},it="item",add="84ab02b5"},{q="Why does Zardeth need an adventurer rather than getting the ingredients himself?",a="Zardeth and his fellow warlocks must remain hidden beneath the Slaughtered Lamb. Leaving their sanctuary risks drawing the immediate attention of the city guard and the House of Nobles, especially while Lord Wishock is actively demanding an investigation.",al={"why me a noble brew","why does zardeth need me","why cant zardeth get reagents"},it="why_me",add="256dc9f2"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, the crypts beneath the Slaughtered Lamb are your safe haven in Stormwind. Helping Zardeth protects your brothers and sisters in the dark arts from discovery by the kingdom's righteous nobility.",["faction:Alliance"]="While King Varian Wrynn remains missing, political maneuvering in the House of Nobles is at an all-time high. That makes scandals within the city especially dangerous to its stability.",["profession:Herbalism"]="As a herbalist, you know the Tear of Tilloa and Musquash Root are rare plants that grow only in regions shaped by grim history or torrents of pristine water."},kw={"darkshire","house of nobles","musquash","slaughtered lamb","stonewrought dam","tilloa","wishock","zardeth"},rel={"npc:zardeth-of-the-black-claw","quest:397","topic:house-of-nobles","subzone:darkshire","zone:duskwood","subzone:stonewrought-dam","zone:wetlands"},m={start="Zardeth of the Black Claw",level="30",faction="Alliance",id=335,ri={"Musquash Root","Tear of Tilloa"}},src={"A Noble Brew"}}
E["quest:336"] = {t="quest",n="A Noble Brew",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind, a courier carries Black Claw Stout to Lord Baurles K. Wishock in the Royal Keep. Zardeth of the Black Claw has arranged the delivery from the cellar beneath the Slaughtered Lamb.",h="In Stormwind, a courier carries Black Claw Stout to Lord Baurles K.",sec={{t="A Noble Hypocrite",b="Lord Baurles K. Wishock spends time in the Hall of Petitioners in Stormwind Keep, speaking of his own importance and the kingdom’s future. Patrons of the Slaughtered Lamb know another side of him. At night, he drinks in the tavern’s upper rooms and leaves large bills unpaid. By day, he petitions to have the tavern shut down.",sp=0},{t="A Lethal Toast",b="Zardeth of the Black Claw brews Black Claw Stout beneath the Slaughtered Lamb to settle Wishock’s debt for good. He says the drink carries quite a kick. In the Hall of Petitioners, Wishock mistakes the courier for a servant and tosses over a copper coin. He drinks the stout greedily, then collapses dead in the halls of the keep.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Zardeth of the Black Claw?",a="Zardeth of the Black Claw is a warlock with a hidden cabal in catacombs beneath The Slaughtered Lamb in Stormwind’s Mage Quarter. He carries out dangerous, secret operations beyond the city guard’s sight.",al={"who is zardeth","zardeth of the black claw","who gives the quest"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Zardeth target Lord Wishock?",a="Wishock drinks in the upper floors of the Slaughtered Lamb at night without paying his bills, then spends his days in the Hall of Petitioners asking the authorities to close the tavern.",al={"why kill wishock","wishock motivation","why poisoned"},sp=1,it="motive"},{q="Where is Lord Wishock found?",a="Lord Baurles K. Wishock is found in the Hall of Petitioners, an antechamber in Stormwind Keep where nobles and citizens gather to lobby the realm’s regency.",al={"lord wishock location","where is wishock","hall of petitioners wishock"},it="target",gp=true},{q="How does Lord Wishock receive the brew?",a="Wishock mistakes the courier for a servant, takes the stout as a refreshing drink, and dismisses them with a copper coin.",al={"does wishock die","wishock death","what does the stout do"},sp=1},{q="Does delivering the stout attract the guards' attention?",a="The delivery appears to be an ordinary servant bringing a drink, and the courier can go on without a confrontation with the guards.",al={"do guards attack","am i wanted in stormwind","consequences of poisoning"},sp=1},{q="What quest follows this delivery?",a="The delivery is followed by 'You Have Served Us Well,' which sends you back to Zardeth beneath the Slaughtered Lamb.",al={"what comes next","after a noble brew","next quest"},sp=1,it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Who is Lord Wishock, and why is he targeted?",a="Lord Baurles K. Wishock is a self-important Stormwind noble lingering in the Hall of Petitioners to petition the royal court. Despite viewing himself as vital to the kingdom's future, he spends his nights drinking upstairs in the Slaughtered Lamb, running up massive drinking tabs he refuses to pay while actively campaigning to have the establishment shut down. Zardeth targets him to end his meddling and settle his unpaid debts.",al={"who is lord wishock","why kill wishock","who is wishock","lord wishock"},it="target",add="46bddf0f"},{q="Why does Zardeth need you to deliver the stout instead of doing it himself?",a="Zardeth and his fellow warlocks operate secretly out of the crypts beneath the Slaughtered Lamb in the heart of Stormwind. Appearing in person before the nobles and city guards in Stormwind Keep would invite immediate scrutiny and arrest, especially given Lord Wishock already knows Zardeth's establishment. By sending an unassuming adventurer, the delivery looks like an ordinary servant bringing refreshments, keeping Zardeth's scheme out of sight.",al={"why does zardeth need me","why deliver the brew","why cant zardeth give it to him"},it="why_me",add="c4eeba5d"}},kw={"baurles wishock","black claw stout","hall of petitioners","noble brew","slaughtered lamb","stormwind keep","zardeth"},rel={"quest:335","quest:397","npc:lord-baurles-k-wishock","npc:zardeth-of-the-black-claw"},m={start="Zardeth of the Black Claw",["end"]="Lord Baurles K. Wishock",level="30",faction="Alliance",id=336},src={"A Noble Brew (2)"}}
E["quest:337"] = {t="quest",n="An Old History Book",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind, a lost chronicle returns to the Royal Library. Titled The History of Stormwind, the battered book bears the library’s seal and vanished before the kingdom was rebuilt after the First War. Its return gives Head Librarian Milton Sheaf a chance to preserve the history of southern human lands.",h="In Stormwind, a lost chronicle returns to the Royal Library.",sec={{t="A Relic of the First War",b="Duskwood’s undead and ogres roam among the ruins where this mud-caked volume was found. The book is a rare relic from before Stormwind’s destruction. Its opening page bears the kingdom’s formal library seal. Someone checked it out decades ago, before the Horde razed the capital, and the book was presumed lost in the fall of the south.",sp=0},{t="Restoring Forgotten Annals",b="Milton Sheaf recognizes the book when it reaches him in the Royal Library of Stormwind Keep. The head librarian means to place it in the rare books archive, though years in the haunted wilderness have badly damaged its pages. The discovery spurs Sheaf to seek more lost knowledge. He looks north to Southshore, the town nearest the ruined kingdom of Alterac and its abandoned libraries.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is this book found?",a="You find the book among the hostile creatures roaming Duskwood, most often among undead in the cemeteries and fields or ogres in the southern hills.",al={"where to find old history book","book drop location","duskwood history book"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who do I bring the book to?",a="Bring the volume to Milton Sheaf, head librarian in the Royal Library inside Stormwind Keep.",al={"turn in location","where do i turn this in","milton sheaf location"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Why is the book in such poor condition?",a="The book was checked out before the First War and Stormwind’s sack. It spent decades in Duskwood’s wilderness, exposed to dirt and rot and handled by wandering scavengers and monsters.",al={"why is it muddy","why damaged"},it="origin"},{q="Does returning this book lead to other tasks?",a="Yes. Milton Sheaf sends you north to Southshore in the Hillsbrad Foothills to speak with Loremaster Dibbs, who can direct you to books in the Ruins of Alterac.",al={"what comes next","followup quest","book quest chain"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does Milton Sheaf care so much about this specific tome?",a="Few original records survived when the kingdom was leveled and Stormwind burned during the First War. Genuine pre-war texts help scholars piece together the kingdom’s past.",al={"why is the book important","importance of history of stormwind"},it="motive"},{q="Can Horde players complete this quest?",a="No. The book belongs to Stormwind’s Royal Library, and only Alliance librarians in Stormwind Keep can accept it.",al={"horde version","is this alliance only"},it="side",gp=true}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you help restore fragments of Stormwind’s heritage that survived the First War’s devastation.",["race:Human"]="As a human of the south, you help reclaim written records from the wilderness and rebuild a culture shattered by the Old Horde.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you know ancient libraries hold knowledge that can decay or be neglected when left in the wild."},kw={"an old history book","duskwood","milton sheaf","preserving knowledge","southshore","stormwind keep","stormwind library","the history of stormwind"},rel={"npc:milton-sheaf","subzone:southshore","zone:duskwood","topic:stormwind-kingdom","quest:579","quest:366","subzone:library-ironforge"},m={start="An Old History Book",["end"]="Milton Sheaf",level="25",faction="Alliance",id=337},src={"An Old History Book (quest)"}}
E["quest:343"] = {t="quest",n="Speaking of Fortitude",z="stormwind",s="Brother Kristoff prepares a sermon in Stormwind City's Cathedral of Light. For his message on the Fortitude of the Spirit, he seeks a book in Stormwind Keep's Royal Library.",h="Brother Kristoff prepares a sermon in Stormwind City's Cathedral of Light.",sec={{t="A Metaphor in Metal",b="Brother Kristoff, a priest in Stormwind's Cathedral of Light, is preparing a sermon on the Fortitude of the Spirit. He wants to draw on the craft of metalworking alongside scripture. To make his point, he needs a treatise called \"The Stresses of Iron.\" Its lessons on bearing pressure may help his congregation understand the strength of faith.",sp=0},{t="The Royal Stacks",b="The Royal Library holds Stormwind's histories, civic writings, and other works within Stormwind Keep. Its shelves contain centuries of writing, so Brother Kristoff sends messengers to Head Librarian Milton Sheaf. Sheaf knows the archive by heart and can guide them to obscure works on crafts.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Brother Kristoff?",a="Brother Kristoff is a priest serving the Church of the Holy Light in Cathedral Square, Stormwind City. He often asks visitors to find materials and references for his teachings and sermons.",al={"kristoff","who gives speaking of fortitude","brother kristoff"},it="identity"},{q="What book is Brother Kristoff looking for?",a="Brother Kristoff seeks \"The Stresses of Iron,\" a technical text on metalworking that he plans to cite as a metaphor for spiritual endurance.",al={"which book","the stresses of iron","kristoff book"},it="item"},{q="Who is Milton Sheaf?",a="Milton Sheaf is the head librarian of the Royal Library inside Stormwind Keep. He oversees the kingdom's books, scrolls, and civic records, and knows the collection well.",al={"milton sheaf","librarian stormwind","head librarian"},it="identity"},{q="Where is the Royal Library located?",a="The Royal Library is in the northeastern wing of Stormwind Keep, reached through the royal palace's main hall.",al={"library location stormwind","where is royal library","stormwind keep library"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does a priest need a metallurgy book?",a="Brother Kristoff is preparing a sermon titled \"Fortitude of the Spirit.\" He plans to compare iron's stress during forging with the way trials strengthen the human spirit.",al={"why metallurgy","why iron book","fortitude sermon"},it="motive"},{q="Does Milton Sheaf have the book ready right away?",a="Milton Sheaf says the library holds books on metalworking, but he needs to check for the exact title and arrange a search for Kristoff's book.",al={"does sheaf have book","hand in speaking of fortitude"},it="next_step",gp=true}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you can see how Stormwind's clergy draw on everyday crafts alongside devotion to the Light when teaching spiritual fortitude.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="As a blacksmith, you know the forge's hardships. Brother Kristoff plans to use \"The Stresses of Iron\" to explain endurance under pressure.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can see Cathedral Square's priesthood connected to Stormwind Keep's Royal Library, part of the capital's civic and scholarly life."},kw={"brother kristoff","cathedral of light","metallurgy","milton sheaf","royal library","speaking of fortitude","stormwind keep","the stresses of iron"},rel={"npc:brother-kristoff","npc:milton-sheaf","subzone:royal-library","subzone:stormwind-keep","topic:light","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Brother Kristoff",["end"]="Milton Sheaf",level="24",faction="Alliance",id=343},src={"Speaking of Fortitude"}}
E["quest:344"] = {t="quest",n="Brother Paxton",z="stormwind",s="At Stormwind's royal archives, Milton Sheaf sends you to Northshire Abbey for a missing dwarven treatise. The book was loaned months ago for copying, but has not returned to the city shelves.",h="At Stormwind's royal archives, Milton Sheaf sends you to Northshire Abbey for a missing dwarven treatise.",sec={{t="A Borrowed Volume",b="Stormwind's head librarian, Milton Sheaf, has a missing book on his hands. 'The Stresses of Iron,' a treatise on metallurgical techniques by dwarven prospector Margulf Blaggon, is gone from the capital's shelves. The book was loaned months ago to the clerics of Northshire Abbey so they could copy it. It was not misplaced in Stormwind.",sp=0},{t="Northshire's Scribe",b="At Northshire Abbey, Brother Paxton cares for the library and its books. The Holy Order of Northshire Clerics values knowledge, but copying a long technical manuscript by hand takes time. Paxton admits he has not finished duplicating Blaggon's work, so the original has yet to return to Stormwind.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Milton Sheaf send you to Northshire Abbey?",a="Milton Sheaf loaned Stormwind's copy of 'The Stresses of Iron' to Brother Paxton months ago so the abbey could make a duplicate. With no word and no book returned, Sheaf sends you to ask how the copying is going.",al={"why brother paxton","where is the book","milton sheaf errand"},it="motive"},{q="Who is Brother Paxton?",a="Brother Paxton is a cleric who cares for the library at Northshire Abbey. He catalogs and copies valuable books by hand for the abbey's collection.",al={"who is paxton","brother paxton lore","paxton northshire"},it="identity"},{q="What is 'The Stresses of Iron'?",a="'The Stresses of Iron' is a technical manual written decades ago by the dwarven miner Margulf Blaggon. It records his knowledge of mining ore and metallurgical stress deep in the mountains of Khaz Modan.",al={"what is stresses of iron","stresses of iron book","margulf blaggon book"},it="item"},{q="Why hasn't Paxton returned the book yet?",a="Brother Paxton is still copying the manuscript by hand for the abbey's shelves. The long work takes time and materials, and he is reluctant to give up the original before he finishes.",al={"why overdue","why is paxton taking so long","paxton delay"}},{q="Where can Brother Paxton be found?",a="Brother Paxton lives inside Northshire Abbey, home of the Holy Order of Northshire Clerics, in Northshire Valley in northern Elwynn Forest.",al={"paxton location","where is brother paxton"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens after you confront Brother Paxton?",a="Paxton admits he has the book and says he needs more writing supplies to finish copying it. He sends you to gather ink supplies.",al={"next quest after paxton","what does paxton need"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Milton Sheaf need an adventurer to find Brother Paxton?",a="Milton Sheaf is Stormwind's head librarian, bound by duty to oversee the Royal Library inside Stormwind Keep. He cannot simply abandon his post to walk out to Northshire Valley for a long-overdue book. When you arrive asking for 'The Stresses of Iron,' you provide him with a convenient messenger who is already traveling and willing to track down Brother Paxton.",al={"why me brother paxton","why does milton sheaf need me","why can't milton get the book himself"},it="why_me",add="4a96b020"}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="Margulf Blaggon's 'The Stresses of Iron' preserves decades of dwarven mining knowledge drawn from the mountains of Khaz Modan.",["race:Dwarf"]="The book sought after is dwarven craft by fellow miner Margulf Blaggon, and Stormwind's scribes value it enough to seek copies.",["class:Priest"]="At Northshire Abbey, you can see the clerics' scholarly work: copying books by hand to preserve knowledge for the order.",["faction:Alliance"]="You can see the ties between Stormwind and Ironforge in human libraries' study and preservation of foundational dwarven texts."},kw={"brother paxton","margulf blaggon","milton sheaf","northshire abbey","stormwind library","the stresses of iron","transcription"},rel={"npc:milton-sheaf","subzone:northshire-abbey","quest:343","quest:345","subzone:library-ironforge"},m={start="Milton Sheaf",["end"]="Brother Paxton",level="24",faction="Alliance",id=344},src={"Brother Paxton (quest)"}}
E["quest:345"] = {t="quest",n="Ink Supplies",z="stormwind",s="In Northshire Abbey, Brother Paxton needs fresh ink for his work as a monastic scribe. He sends you east to Lakeshire for Rethban ore, the mineral his fast-drying ink requires.",h="In Northshire Abbey, Brother Paxton needs fresh ink for his work as a monastic scribe.",sec={{t="A Scribe's Formula",b="Brother Paxton takes pride in his craft and uses a special ink for important writings such as The Stresses of Iron. His recipe dries quickly and resists smearing, but the ink can dry in its pot if left too long. To make more, he needs raw Rethban iron ore, mined in the rocky Redridge Mountains.",sp=0},{t="A Town Under Siege",b="Lakeshire has little room for a distant scribe’s request. Foreman Oslow oversees laborers busy strengthening barricades, rebuilding ruined structures, and defending the town from ongoing Blackrock orc raids. With no workers to spare for mining, travelers must seek the ore in the perilous Rethban Caverns themselves.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Brother Paxton need iron ore for ink?",a="Brother Paxton needs Rethban iron ore to make his special ink. Ground ore supplies the mineral pigment and setting qualities that give the ink its quick-drying, smear-proof script.",al={"why iron for ink","paxton ore ink","brother paxton ink recipe"},it="item"},{q="Who is Foreman Oslow?",a="Foreman Oslow oversees civic construction and repairs in Lakeshire. With Blackrock orcs pressing the town, he directs its rebuilding and fortification.",al={"foreman oslow","oslow lakeshire","who is oslow"},it="identity"},{q="Where does Brother Paxton send you?",a="Paxton sends you east from Elwynn Forest to Lakeshire, in the Redridge Mountains, to find Foreman Oslow.",al={"ink supplies destination","where is oslow","where do i go for ink supplies"},it="place"},{q="Why won't Foreman Oslow just give you the ore?",a="Blackrock orc attacks keep Lakeshire under pressure. Oslow’s workers are occupied repairing damaged buildings and fortifying the town, with no hands free to mine.",al={"why no ore","oslow refuses ore","why oslow mad"},it="conflict"},{q="What book is Brother Paxton attempting to copy?",a="Brother Paxton is copying The Stresses of Iron. His work stopped when his previous batch of quick-drying ink solidified in its container.",al={"paxton book","what is paxton copying","the stresses of iron"},it="purpose"},{q="What happens after speaking with Foreman Oslow?",a="Foreman Oslow tells you to gather Rethban iron ore yourself in the dangerous Rethban Caverns, north of Lake Everstill.",al={"next quest after ink supplies","what next after oslow","follow up ink supplies"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Brother Paxton want you to fetch Rethban ore?",a="Brother Paxton is dedicated to copying the scholarly treatise The Stresses of Iron for Northshire Abbey's library. He insists on brewing his own specialized ink, which relies on pulverized Rethban iron ore to ensure it dries rapidly and resists smudging. Unfortunately, his previous batch dried up completely before he could finish transcription, leaving his scholarly project stalled until fresh minerals arrive.",al={"why does brother paxton need ore","brother paxton motive","why ink supplies"},it="motive",add="3b01bf84"},{q="Why does Brother Paxton send you instead of getting the ore himself?",a="Brother Paxton is a devoted copyist confined to his duties within the cloistered walls of Northshire Abbey. Journeying all the way out to Lakeshire in the Redridge Mountains is far beyond his peaceful monastic routine, especially with travel routes growing increasingly perilous. As an able adventurer already traveling the realm, you can easily carry word to his usual contact.",al={"why cant paxton get the ore","why send an adventurer","why me ink supplies"},it="why_me",add="c7dba9bc"}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you can help the clergy with their scholarly work. Brother Paxton’s errand follows Brother Kristoff’s sermon on the Fortitude of the Spirit.",["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you can seek Rethban iron ore, found high in the crags of Redridge.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you see the contrast between Northshire Abbey’s quiet seclusion and the violence threatening Lakeshire."},kw={"brother paxton","foreman oslow","ink supplies","lakeshire","northshire abbey","redridge mountains","rethban ore","the stresses of iron"},rel={"npc:foreman-oslow","quest:344","quest:343","subzone:lakeshire","zone:redridge"},m={start="Brother Paxton",["end"]="Foreman Oslow",level="24",faction="Alliance",id=345},src={"Ink Supplies"}}
E["quest:346"] = {t="quest",n="Return to Kristoff",z="stormwind",s="Brother Kristoff is waiting in Stormwind for a borrowed book to return. After a long search and a delay in Northshire, you bring The Stresses of Iron back to the Cathedral of Light.",h="Brother Kristoff is waiting in Stormwind for a borrowed book to return.",sec={{t="A Long-Delayed Return",b="Brother Kristoff is waiting in Cathedral Square for The Stresses of Iron, a book on metallurgy. Its trail led from Stormwind Keep's Royal Library to Northshire Abbey, where Brother Paxton was copying the text by hand. Paxton ran short of Rethban ore for the scribe's ink, so the work stalled. With the ore retrieved and the copy complete, you bring the original book back to Stormwind.",sp=0},{t="The Labor of Scribes",b="Northshire's copyists preserve civic and spiritual lore through patient work. Brother Paxton asks you to apologize to Librarian Milton Sheaf, a sign of how thin the abbey's resources have worn. Scribes must copy valuable books stroke by stroke with mineral-rich ink before returning them to Stormwind's care, making a book request a long undertaking.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the book The Stresses of Iron about?",a="The Stresses of Iron is a treatise on metallurgy and metalworking. Brother Kristoff sought it for study in Cathedral Square, and the Northshire Abbey scribes needed a copy to preserve its knowledge.",al={"what is stresses of iron","stresses of iron book","what book is kristoff looking for"},it="item"},{q="Why was the book at Northshire Abbey?",a="The Royal Library lent The Stresses of Iron to Brother Paxton so he could make an illuminated copy for Northshire Abbey's archives. His work stalled when he ran short of Rethban ore for specialized ink.",al={"why was paxton holding the book","why was it in northshire"},it="history"},{q="Who is Brother Kristoff?",a="Brother Kristoff belongs to the Clergy of the Holy Light and is stationed in Cathedral Square outside the Cathedral of Light in Stormwind. He requested the book and offers spiritual blessings in gratitude.",al={"who is kristoff","kristoff stormwind"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Milton?",a="Milton Sheaf is the head librarian in Stormwind Keep's Royal Library. He permitted the loan of The Stresses of Iron and grew impatient over the long delay in its return.",al={"who is librarian milton","milton sheaf"},it="people"},{q="Where does this quest chain begin?",a="The chain begins in Stormwind's Cathedral Square, where Brother Kristoff offers Speaking of Fortitude. It leads to Librarian Milton Sheaf, then Northshire Abbey and Redridge Mountains, before bringing you back to Kristoff.",al={"how to start speaking of fortitude","quest chain start"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Does this quest have any follow-ups?",a="Return to Kristoff ends the Speaking of Fortitude chain. When you deliver The Stresses of Iron, Brother Kristoff thanks you and offers a blessing of the Light.",al={"what comes after return to kristoff","is there a next quest"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does Brother Paxton want the book returned to Brother Kristoff?",a="Brother Paxton only borrowed The Stresses of Iron so he could copy its contents at Northshire Abbey. Now that his transcription is complete, he has no further claim on the rare volume and owes its safe return to Stormwind's Cathedral of Light, hoping to mend any trouble caused by his lengthy delay.",al={"why return stresses of iron","brother paxton motive","why send book back to kristoff"},it="motive",add="46830297"}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you see how the Church of the Holy Light preserves and shares important scholarship across the kingdom.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you rely on safe roads linking Stormwind Keep, Northshire, and the embattled Redridge Mountains."},kw={"brother kristoff","brother paxton","cathedral square","milton sheaf","northshire abbey","return to kristoff","stormwind","the stresses of iron"},rel={"npc:brother-kristoff","quest:344","quest:343","subzone:cathedral-square","topic:light"},m={start="Brother Paxton",["end"]="Brother Kristoff",level="24",faction="Alliance",id=346},src={"Return to Kristoff"}}
E["quest:347"] = {t="quest",n="Rethban Ore",z="stormwind",s="Foreman Oslow sends you into Rethban Caverns in Redridge for a dark mineral the scribes of Northshire Abbey need for ink. It is too soft for strong weapons or armor, but its color makes it useful for their work.",h="Foreman Oslow sends you into Rethban Caverns in Redridge for a dark mineral the scribes of Northshire Abbey...",sec={{t="A Curious Mineral",b="Scribes at Northshire Abbey prize Rethban Ore for its dark, flat color. Bart Rethban discovered the mineral, but it has little use at an armorer’s anvil. Smelted metal from the ore lacks the strength needed for sturdy weapons or plate. Its raw color instead makes a valued base for manuscript dyes.",sp=0},{t="Contested Caverns",b="The main deposits lie in the northern mountains of Redridge, inside Rethban Caverns. Lakeshire’s stoneworkers have left the cavern, driven out by a fierce band of Redridge gnolls. The gnolls put drudgers to work chipping ore from the rocky veins for their own crude purposes.",sp=0},{t="Preserving the Word",b="Brother Paxton, a monk at Northshire Abbey, needs the pigment to copy historic texts. His work on The Stresses of Iron has stopped without the proper dye. Messengers and adventurers now travel into gnoll-held territory to bring him the raw stone.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Rethban Ore used for?",a="Smelted Rethban Ore is too weak for durable weapons or armor, but its dark, flat color makes a useful base for inks and dyes. Brother Paxton and other scribes at Northshire Abbey use it to copy historic manuscripts.",al={"why do we need rethban ore","rethban ore purpose","what is rethban ore for"},it="item"},{q="Who was Bart Rethban?",a="Bart Rethban was the explorer and prospector who discovered the dark ore veins in the northern mountains of Redridge. The mineral and the Rethban Caverns take their name from him.",al={"who discovered rethban ore","bart rethban lore"},it="origin"},{q="Why hasn't Lakeshire mined the ore recently?",a="Foreman Oslow and Lakeshire’s workers are occupied defending the town from Blackrock orc incursions. Redridge gnolls have also taken over Rethban Caverns and driven out the civilian miners.",al={"why isn't oslow mining it","why are the mines abandoned"},it="why_me"},{q="What book is Brother Paxton copying?",a="Brother Paxton is copying The Stresses of Iron. He needs the dark dye made from Rethban Ore to finish the text for the abbey’s library.",al={"what book is paxton writing","paxton manuscript"},it="purpose"},{q="Why do gnolls want the ore?",a="Redridge gnolls have their drudgers dig throughout the caverns. They may want the ore for crude implements, trade, or to fortify their mountain warrens against intruders.",al={"why are gnolls mining","gnoll drudgers rethban"}},{q="Where does this quest chain lead next?",a="After Brother Paxton receives the ore and prepares his inks, he sends you back to Stormwind to report your success to Kristoff, completing the errand for Northshire’s scribes.",al={"what quest comes after rethban ore","return to kristoff next"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Foreman Oslow want this done?",a="Foreman Oslow isn't seeking the ore for himself or Lakeshire's builders. Brother Paxton at Northshire Abbey sent you to Oslow to secure Rethban ore for bookbinding ink. Oslow is simply honoring the request by directing you to the source, since town stocks are empty and his workers cannot spare the time to dig it themselves.",al={"foreman oslow motive","why does oslow need ore","why does oslow help paxton"},it="motive",add="86e7e5db"},{q="Who is occupying the Rethban Caverns?",a="The Redridge gnolls have overrun the Rethban Caverns north of Lakeshire. Rather than letting the caverns sit idle, gnoll drudgers have begun digging up the dark ore veins for their own purposes, violently driving out any local miners who attempt to approach.",al={"rethban caverns enemies","who is in rethban caverns","redridge gnolls caverns"},it="target",add="fa5d21e9"}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you can take Rethban Ore from cavern veins with a pick instead of scavenging raw chunks from gnoll drudgers.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you can see how stretched the Kingdom of Stormwind’s supply lines are: monastery scribes rely on travelers to fetch writing supplies from war zones.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you share the duty of Stormwind’s scholars to preserve Northshire Abbey’s manuscripts and restore knowledge lost during the First and Second Wars."},kw={"bart rethban","brother paxton","foreman oslow","northshire abbey","redridge drudgers","rethban caverns","rethban ore","stresses of iron"},rel={"subzone:rethban-caverns","npc:foreman-oslow","quest:344","subzone:northshire-abbey","quest:345","quest:346","topic:gnoll"},m={start="Foreman Oslow",["end"]="Brother Paxton",level="24",faction="Alliance",id=347},src={"Rethban Ore (quest)"}}
E["quest:350"] = {t="quest",n="Look to an Old Friend",z="stormwind",s="Master Mathias Shaw sends you to seek an unusual contact in Stormwind's Trade District. Noble corruption shields traitors from ordinary justice, so Shaw turns to the city's finest cheesemonger and his intelligence network.",h="Master Mathias Shaw sends you to seek an unusual contact in Stormwind's Trade District.",sec={{t="Above the Law",b="Lord Gregor Lescovar and Marzon the Silent Blade have direct ties to the Defias Brotherhood, but Master Mathias Shaw has reached an intelligence dead end. Edwin VanCleef is dead in the Deadmines, and Bazil Thredd has been eliminated in the Stockade. No living bandit leaders remain to testify. Lescovar's noble rank and political ties also leave him beyond the reach of ordinary Royal Guard justice and formal SI:7 warrants.",sp=1},{t="The Cheesemonger's Ear",b="Master Mathias Shaw sends you to Elling Trias, who owns Trias' Cheese in the Trade District. Across Stormwind, Trias is known as a temperamental merchant selling imported wedges and wheels. He also runs an independent network of eyes and ears that rivals SI:7. Shaw hates turning to his former colleague, but exposing treason inside Stormwind Keep calls for methods beyond official royal channels.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Mathias Shaw send you to a cheese merchant?",a="Elling Trias is more than a cheesemonger. He runs Trias' Cheese near the Trade District entrance and maintains an independent, far-reaching intelligence network. Shaw hates asking him for help, but SI:7 needs unusual means to act against a nobleman beyond the reach of ordinary law enforcement.",al={"why elling trias","why talk to trias","why cheese shop"},it="identity"},{q="Why can't Mathias Shaw simply arrest Lord Lescovar?",a="Lord Lescovar is a high-ranking Stormwind noble with deep ties across the House of Nobles. Shaw lacks the testimony needed to make the evidence hold against an aristocrat.",al={"why not arrest lescovar","why cant shaw arrest lescovar","why lescovar untouchable"},it="motive"},{q="Who is Marzon the Silent Blade?",a="Marzon the Silent Blade is a lethal operative working closely with the Defias conspiracy. He secretly communicates with Lord Lescovar inside Stormwind's court.",al={"who is marzon","marzon silent blade role"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Trias mention Deathwing when you speak to him?",a="When Trias hears of the Defias Brotherhood conspiracy, he answers with bitter sarcasm. He scoffs that next you will tell him the long-lost Black Dragon Aspect Deathwing is alive and attacking the kingdom.",al={"why does trias say deathwing","trias deathwing line","deathwing attacking stormwind"},it="history"},{q="What happens after meeting with Elling Trias?",a="After hearing the full account of the conspiracy, Trias begins planning a quiet infiltration of Stormwind Keep to corner Lord Lescovar without alerting the rest of the noble court.",al={"next quest after trias","where to after look to an old friend"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Where is Elling Trias located?",a="Elling Trias is inside Trias' Cheese in Stormwind's Trade District, just off the main road from the city gates.",al={"trias location","where is trias cheese"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Mathias Shaw send you instead of handling this through SI:7?",a="Lord Gregor Lescovar is a powerful, well-connected nobleman, effectively placing him above conventional Stormwind law. Shaw lacks the witness testimony needed to officially prove the case against him in court. Official SI:7 or city guard action would trigger political outrage among the nobility without ironclad proof. You, however, operate off the record as an independent agent, allowing Shaw to pursue unconventional, discreet channels without drawing premature attention from Lescovar's allies in the House of Nobles.",al={"why send me","why not SI7","why does Shaw need me"},it="why_me",add="9cbff8f4"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you can see the uneasy rivalry between Mathias Shaw and Elling Trias. Street-level informants can hold more influence than the crown's official intelligence division.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you see how corruption in the House of Nobles hampers Stormwind's internal security while King Varian Wrynn remains missing."},kw={"defias","elling trias","lescovar","marzon","mathias shaw","stormwind","trade district","trias cheese"},rel={"npc:elling-trias","quest:2745","quest:65","topic:defias-brotherhood","subzone:trade-district","topic:stormwind-kingdom","npc:deathwing"},m={start="Master Mathias Shaw",["end"]="Elling Trias",level="31",faction="Alliance",id=350},src={"Look to an Old Friend"}}
E["quest:353"] = {t="quest",n="Stormpike's Delivery",z="stormwind",s="Grimand Elmore sends travelers north with an axe for Mountaineer Gringer Stormpike. The road leads from Stormwind's Dwarven District to an Ironforge outpost in Loch Modan.",h="Grimand Elmore sends travelers north with an axe for Mountaineer Gringer Stormpike.",sec={{t="A Weapon for the North",b="Grimand Elmore has been asked to make a weapon for Mountaineer Gringer Stormpike. The Stormpike clan is respected in Ironforge for its discerning taste and martial pride. Elmore turns to trustworthy travelers to carry the axe north, across the distance between Stormwind and the dwarven borderlands.",sp=0},{t="On Guard in Loch Modan",b="At Loch Modan's northern guard tower, Mountaineer Stormpike watches over lands troubled by wandering troggs and burrowing kobolds. The southern human kingdoms face rumors of unrest and banditry, while the dwarven frontier has dangers of its own. Stormpike needs a new blade to help keep the mountain passes secure.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Mountaineer Stormpike?",a="Gringer Stormpike is an Ironforge Mountaineer of the respected Stormpike clan. He is stationed at Loch Modan's northern guard tower, defending the valley road from troggs and local threats.",al={"gringer stormpike","who is stormpike","mountaineer gringer stormpike"}},{q="What is inside the package?",a="The package contains a custom dwarven axe forged by Grimand Elmore in Stormwind. Mountaineer Stormpike commissioned it for use against troggs and kobolds in Loch Modan.",al={"what am i delivering","stormpike parcel contents","grimand elmore weapon"}},{q="Where do I deliver the package?",a="Deliver the package to Mountaineer Stormpike at the northern guard tower in Loch Modan, along the road through the hills toward the northern mountain borders.",al={"where is stormpike","how to find mountaineer stormpike","loch modan guard tower location"}},{q="Why does a dwarf in Loch Modan buy weapons from Stormwind?",a="Grimand Elmore is a skilled dwarven weaponsmith in Stormwind's Dwarven District. The Stormpike clan values fine metalwork, and Gringer commissioned Elmore to make his axe despite the distance.",al={"why buy from stormwind","why elmore","dwarf ordering from human city"}},{q="How does this connect to Elmore's Task?",a="This delivery follows Elmore's Task. Grimand Elmore asks travelers to carry another favor between Stormwind and Khaz Modan.",al={"elmore questline","quest before stormpikes delivery","how to start this quest"}},{q="How do travelers reach Loch Modan from Stormwind?",a="Take the Deeprun Tram from Stormwind's Dwarven District to Ironforge. From the Great Gates, follow the eastern highway through Dun Morogh's snowy passes and North Gate Pass into Loch Modan.",al={"how to get to loch modan","travel to khaz modan","deeprun tram to loch modan"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you know the Stormpikes are honored among your kin. Helping a fellow mountaineer on Loch Modan's wild borders strengthens clan ties.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="As a blacksmith, you can recognize the skill in Grimand Elmore's work. Mountain guards value his dwarven metalwork enough to order it across kingdoms.",["faction:Alliance"]="As a member of the Alliance, you help carry military goods between Stormwind and the mountain outposts, where humans and dwarves rely on one another."},kw={"axe","elmore","grimand","gringer","guard tower","loch modan","mountaineer","stormpike"},rel={"npc:mountaineer-stormpike","quest:1097","zone:lochmodan","zone:ironforge","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:trogg","topic:kobold","topic:human"},m={level="15",id=353},src={"In-game quest text: Stormpike's Delivery","Stormpike's Delivery"},fv=true}
E["quest:373"] = {t="quest",n="The Unsent Letter",z="stormwind",s="In the Deadmines, The Unsent Letter waits to be carried to Stormwind. Its delivery reveals the grievances and shared history binding Edwin VanCleef to the city's master builders.",h="In the Deadmines, The Unsent Letter waits to be carried to Stormwind.",sec={{t="A Message From the Grave",b="Edwin VanCleef falls aboard his juggernaut beneath Moonbrook, leaving behind more than a broken rebellion. A newly penned, sealed letter is tucked into his clothing. He addressed it not to a criminal lieutenant or financier, but to Baros Alexston, Stormwind's City Architect.",sp=0},{t="Architects of Old",b="Carry the letter to City Hall in Cathedral Square, where Baros Alexston once worked alongside Edwin VanCleef during Stormwind's reconstruction after the Second War. Alexston reacts with disbelief at news of VanCleef's death. Horrified by the bandit leader's indiscriminate violence, he recognizes the grievance behind VanCleef's bitter crusade. VanCleef was an uncompromising idealist consumed by betrayal, whose rightful grievance turned to destructive madness.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where do I find the Unsent Letter?",a="An Unsent Letter is found on Edwin VanCleef aboard his ironclad ship in the Deadmines, deep in Westfall.",al={"unsent letter drop","how to get unsent letter","who drops unsent letter"}},{q="Who is Baros Alexston?",a="Baros Alexston is Stormwind's City Architect. He lives in City Hall, along the northeast edge of Cathedral Square.",al={"baros alexston location","where is baros alexston","city architect stormwind"}},{q="Why was Edwin VanCleef writing to the City Architect?",a="Edwin VanCleef and Baros Alexston were fellow stonemasons who rebuilt Stormwind after the Second War. Even after turning to banditry, VanCleef saw Alexston as a former peer connected to the masons' work and betrayal.",al={"why write baros","vancleef and baros relationship","letter to architect"}},{q="What does the letter reveal about VanCleef?",a="Alexston sees VanCleef as an idealist and a romantic to the end, poisoned by vengeance. VanCleef believed his war against the kingdom was justified because the ruling nobility refused to pay the masons.",al={"vancleef motive","what does the letter say","letter lore"}},{q="Do I need to finish the main Defias Brotherhood chain before turning this in?",a="No. Any Alliance adventurer who defeats VanCleef can loot and complete the letter, regardless of prior progress in the Defias Brotherhood storyline.",al={"quest prerequisite","can i do unsent letter early","do i need defias chain"}},{q="Where does this questline lead next?",a="After you deliver the letter, Alexston sends you to the Stockade to question Bazil Thredd, an imprisoned Defias leader who may know more about VanCleef's plans.",al={"next quest after unsent letter","lescovar chain","what follows baros alexston"},sp=1}},ang={["race:Human"]="For humans of Stormwind, the letter exposes the wounds left by the kingdom's reconstruction. The banditry in Westfall grew from political betrayals within the capital.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you can see how VanCleef's skill as a fighter and organizer gave way to suicidal obsession.",["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, the letter ties the Defias threat to Stormwind's civic administration and reveals a vendetta beyond a regional outlaw uprising."},kw={"baros alexston","cathedral square","city hall","deadmines","defias","edwin vancleef","stonemasons","unsent letter"},rel={"npc:baros-alexston","npc:edwin-vancleef","topic:defias-brotherhood","quest:65","subzone:cathedral-square","zone:deadmines","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start=":An Unsent Letter",["end"]="Baros Alexston",level="22",faction="Alliance",id=373},src={"The Unsent Letter"}}
E["quest:3765"] = {t="quest",n="The Corruption Abroad",z="stormwind",s="Argos Nightwhisper, a night elf envoy visiting Stormwind, seeks capable adventurers to cross the Great Sea and aid his brother in northern Kalimdor. His brother Gershala studies spreading ecological decay in Darkshore, where fresh hands are desperately needed.",h="Argos Nightwhisper, a night elf envoy visiting Stormwind, seeks capable adventurers to cross the Great Sea...",sec={{t="An Envoy in the Human Capital",b="While Stormwind contends with internal turmoil and regional unrest, representatives from the distant kaldorei lands can be found wandering its stone streets. Argos Nightwhisper came seeking seasoned champions willing to look beyond human borders. The kaldorei are relatively new allies to the Eastern Kingdoms, and formal military aid is scarce, leaving family members and researchers to recruit whatever independent champions answer the call.",sp=0},{t="The Call of Darkshore",b="The destination Argos points toward is Auberdine, a misty port town resting on the fog-shrouded coast of Darkshore. There, his brother Gershala conducts vital research into an ominous malaise afflicting the local wildlife and flora. Answering the summons means a long voyage from Stormwind Harbor across the Great Sea, marking a traveler's first real foray into the ancient wilderness of Kalimdor.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Argos Nightwhisper?",a="Argos Nightwhisper is a night elf visitor staying in Stormwind. He serves as an emissary of sorts for his family, specifically recruiting experienced Alliance adventurers to travel across the sea and assist his brother Gershala in Darkshore.",al={"argos","argos nightwhisper","who gives the corruption abroad"},it="identity"},{q="Where is Gershala Nightwhisper located?",a="Gershala Nightwhisper is stationed in Auberdine, a coastal night elf settlement situated along the western shores of Darkshore in northern Kalimdor.",al={"gershala location","where is gershala","turn in corruption abroad"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Gershala need help?",a="Gershala is investigating an unnatural corruption spreading across Darkshore's wilderness, infecting the local wildlife, water sources, and vegetation. He requires seasoned champions to help gather samples and investigate the root cause.",al={"why help gershala","what is wrong in darkshore"},it="motive"},{q="How do I get to Auberdine from Stormwind?",a="Board the ship at the southern-most dock of Stormwind Harbor, which sails straight across the Great Sea to Auberdine in Darkshore.",al={"how to reach auberdine","travel to darkshore from stormwind"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Can I do this quest if I already went to Darkshore?",a="If you already visited Auberdine and began Gershala's task, 'Researching the Corruption', directly from him, you can no longer pick up or complete this introductory summons from Argos.",al={"missed the corruption abroad","can i still do corruption abroad"},gp=true},{q="What is the relationship between Argos and Gershala?",a="Argos and Gershala Nightwhisper are brothers. While Gershala remains on the front lines studying the blight in Darkshore, Argos traveled across the sea to seek out capable allies in Stormwind.",al={"argos and gershala","are argos and gershala related"},it="ties"},{q="Why does Argos Nightwhisper need you to go instead of going himself?",a="Argos made the arduous journey across the seas specifically to recruit capable allies from the Eastern Kingdoms. His brother Gershala faces mounting trouble in Darkshore that demands seasoned hands, and Argos is remaining behind in the bustling capital to continue petitioning aid and finding capable travelers willing to make the long voyage back across the ocean.",al={"why send me","why can't Argos go","why does Argos need an adventurer"},it="why_me",add="c6dfa232"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="This mission demonstrates the fledgling bonds tying the night elves of Kalimdor to the human kingdom of Stormwind across the sea.",["race:NightElf"]="For night elves far from home, Argos provides a reminder of the troubles plaguing the ancestral forests of northern Kalimdor.",["race:Human"]="Venturing to Darkshore offers human adventurers their first glimpse of ancient kaldorei culture, far removed from the stone castles of Elwynn."},kw={"argos","auberdine","corruption","darkshore","gershala","nightwhisper","stormwind"},rel={"npc:argos-nightwhisper","npc:gershala-nightwhisper","quest:1275","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Argos Nightwhisper",["end"]="Gershala Nightwhisper",level="24",faction="Alliance",id=3765},src={"The Corruption Abroad"}}
E["quest:389"] = {t="quest",n="Bazil Thredd",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind, Bazil Thredd holds insight into the Defias Brotherhood's lingering plots. After an unsent letter is recovered from the Deadmines, City Architect Baros Alexston directs you to the Defias leader's right-hand man, now locked beneath the streets in the high-security Stockade.",h="In Stormwind, Bazil Thredd holds insight into the Defias Brotherhood's lingering plots.",sec={{t="A Bitter History",b="Baros Alexston shares a bitter history with Edwin VanCleef. Both led the Stonemasons Guild, charged with rebuilding Stormwind from the ashes of the First and Second Wars. When the kingdom's magnificent white walls and towers were finished, the nobility refused to pay the masons their promised wages. Some senior members received bureaucratic posts to quiet them, but VanCleef refused to abandon the rank-and-file laborers. He led a violent riot out of the city and founded the Defias Brotherhood.",sp=0},{t="A Turn to the Stockade",b="To learn VanCleef's full design and what the Brotherhood still plans against Stormwind, Alexston directs you to Bazil Thredd. Thredd was VanCleef's chief lieutenant during the mason uprising. He was captured and confined in the city's prison beneath the canals of the Mage Quarter. At the gates, Warden Thelwater warns that the inmates have rebelled, and the Stockade has become a warzone.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Bazil Thredd?",a="Bazil Thredd was Edwin VanCleef's primary lieutenant in the Stonemasons Guild and the early Defias uprising. Stormwind authorities captured him and imprisoned him deep within the Stockade.",al={"bazil thredd lore","who is thredd","thredd backstory"},it="target"},{q="Why does Baros Alexston send you to speak with Thredd?",a="After examining the unsent letter from the Deadmines, Alexston sees that Stormwind faces a threat beyond the Deadmines. As VanCleef's former right-hand man, Thredd understands the Brotherhood's inner workings and remaining schemes better than anyone else, Alexston believes.",al={"why talk to thredd","baros alexston motive","why go to stockade"},it="motive"},{q="Why was the Stonemasons Guild betrayed?",a="After the masons rebuilt Stormwind following the Second War, the House of Nobles refused to honor its financial agreements. The laborers were left unpaid and destitute. VanCleef rejected quiet bribes to silence him and led a riot out of the city gates.",al={"why werent stonemasons paid","defias motive","stonemason riot reason"},it="history"},{q="Where is the Stockade located?",a="The Stockade entrance lies along the canals in Stormwind's northeastern Mage Quarter. Warden Thelwater stands just inside, trying to hold back escaping prisoners.",al={"where is stockade","stockade entrance","how to find warden thelwater"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is happening inside the Stockade when you arrive?",a="When you arrive, Bazil Thredd and the other inmates have overpowered the guards, unlocked the holding cells, and seized the lower halls. Warden Thelwater struggles to keep the riot from spilling into Stormwind's streets.",al={"why is thelwater mad","stockade crisis","what happened in the stockade"},it="conflict"},{q="How did Baros Alexston avoid joining the Defias?",a="VanCleef refused compromise and chose armed rebellion, while Alexston was among the senior guild craftsmen who accepted government employment from the kingdom. He eventually became City Architect.",al={"is baros defias","baros alexston stonemason"},it="side"},{q="Why does Baros Alexston ask you instead of the city guards?",a="Baros Alexston holds an official post as Stormwind's City Architect, yet the mystery behind the Unsent Letter and Edwin VanCleef's schemes is delicate and personal. Involving regular city guards could spark panic among the nobles or alert Defias infiltrators within the city. Because you brought him the letter and operate outside the city's tangled bureaucracy, you are in the best position to interrogate VanCleef's imprisoned lieutenant quietly.",al={"why me bazil thredd","why send an adventurer to the stockade","why does baros need me"},it="why_me",add="6cadb033"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human, you see the Stonemasons Guild's rebellion laid bare the deep political fracture between Stormwind's ruling nobility and the commoners who built the city with their own hands.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance hero, you face a Defias threat reaching into the capital through the unsecured cells of the Stockade, even with Edwin VanCleef slain.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you know Thredd represents the hardened, organized underworld branch of the Defias, who traded construction hammers for shanks and street violence."},kw={"baros alexston","bazil thredd","defias","edwin vancleef","stonemasons guild","stormwind","the stockade","unsent letter","warden thelwater"},rel={"npc:baros-alexston","npc:warden-thelwater","zone:stockade","quest:373","quest:391","topic:stonemasons-guild","topic:stormwind-kingdom","subzone:mage-quarter"},m={start="Baros Alexston",["end"]="Warden Thelwater",level="22",faction="Alliance",id=389},src={"Bazil Thredd (quest)"}}
E["quest:392"] = {t="quest",n="The Curious Visitor",z="stormwind",s="After the Stockade uprising, Warden Thelwater has a troubling discovery about Bazil Thredd. For months before the riot, a man named Maelik visited Thredd with legitimate papers.",h="After the Stockade uprising, Warden Thelwater has a troubling discovery about Bazil Thredd.",sec={{t="A Breach in Protocol",b="Warden Thelwater learned that Bazil Thredd had not been abandoned by his former comrades, as the guards believed. Months before the riot, a quiet visitor began meeting with Thredd once or twice a week. He passed every inspection, carried authorized paperwork, and gave his name as Maelik. Thelwater suspects the visits helped coordinate the bloody uprising. He gathers a physical description and sends you to City Architect Baros Alexston to learn who the visitor was.",sp=0},{t="Ties to the Stonemasons",b="Baros Alexston worked closely with Edwin VanCleef and the Stonemasons Guild before their rebellion. The name Maelik means nothing to him, and the description could fit countless former craftsmen. Yet the visitor had valid clearance to enter the Stockade. That points beyond common criminals slipping past the guards: Defias sympathizers and agents remain deeply embedded in Stormwind's civic offices.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is the curious visitor mentioned in the quest?",a="The visitor gave his name as Maelik. For months before the Stockade riot, he visited Bazil Thredd once or twice a week and carried seemingly legitimate identification papers.",al={"who is maelik","thredd visitor","curious visitor identity"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Warden Thelwater send you to Baros Alexston?",a="Warden Thelwater sends you to Baros Alexston because he is Stormwind's City Architect and once worked alongside Edwin VanCleef and the Stonemasons Guild. Since the Defias began among the Stonemasons, Thelwater hopes Alexston may recognize the visitor through his former guild contacts.",al={"why baros alexston","who is baros","turn in to baros"},it="purpose"},{q="How did Maelik enter the Stockade without being caught?",a="Maelik entered the Stockade with legitimate paperwork that cleared prison security checks. The guards had no legal cause to deny him entry, which suggests a bureaucratic error or corrupt officials inside the kingdom's administration.",al={"how did visitor get in","maeliks papers","stockade security failure"}},{q="What role did Bazil Thredd play in the prison riots?",a="Bazil Thredd was an imprisoned leader of the Defias Brotherhood in the Stockade. He organized and led the inmates' violent uprising, likely coordinated through his visits with Maelik.",al={"who is bazil thredd","what did thredd do"}},{q="What happens after Baros Alexston reads the description?",a="Baros Alexston recognizes neither the name Maelik nor Thelwater's description. He agrees to investigate further because the visitor must have connections in the city.",al={"does baros recognize maelik","what happens next"},it="next_step"},{q="Why is the visitor important to the investigation of the Defias?",a="The regular visits show that the Stockade riot was a planned Defias plot, not a spontaneous outburst of lawless rage. Someone with high-level access to Stormwind's official papers helped make it possible.",al={"defias conspiracy","why does the visitor matter"}},{q="Why does Warden Thelwater want this done?",a="Bazil Thredd sat in the Stockade for years without a single visitor, apparently abandoned by the Defias Brotherhood. That changed months ago when a quiet stranger calling himself Maelik began visiting regularly with valid papers. Now that Thredd has orchestrated a violent prison riot, Thelwater realizes those visits were part of a broader conspiracy. He needs the mysterious visitor identified to uncover who helped orchestrate the uprising from outside.",al={"thelwater motive","why send visitor description","why does thelwater care about maelik"},it="motive",add="3d9e03e1"},{q="Why does Warden Thelwater send you instead of his own guards?",a="The Stockade has just been torn apart by a massive uprising, and the prison's garrison is completely stretched thin containing the aftermath and securing the remaining cells. Furthermore, because Maelik's visitation papers were approved legitimately, Thelwater cannot be certain how deep the corruption or negligence reaches within his own ranks. Having proven your loyalty and capability by putting down Thredd, you are an outsider he can safely trust.",al={"why send me","why not send guards","why can't thelwater send a guard"},it="why_me",add="156adb5f"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human, you can see how forged or sanctioned entry papers expose deep vulnerabilities and possible corruption within the Kingdom of Stormwind's government.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you know finding Bazil Thredd's mysterious contact matters to rooting out Defias sympathizers operating openly in the capital.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you recognize the craft behind passing every prison inspection with proper documentation."},kw={"baros alexston","bazil thredd","curious visitor","defias","maelik","stockade","stonemasons","warden thelwater"},rel={"quest:391","npc:warden-thelwater","npc:baros-alexston","topic:defias-brotherhood","topic:stormwind-kingdom","quest:65"},m={start="Warden Thelwater",["end"]="Baros Alexston",level="29",faction="Alliance",id=392},src={"The Curious Visitor"}}
E["quest:393"] = {t="quest",n="Shadow of the Past",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind, the trail from a Stockade prisoner leads into the city’s hidden dealings. Baros Alexston sends you to Mathias Shaw after a mysterious visitor spoke with Bazil Thredd.",h="In Stormwind, the trail from a Stockade prisoner leads into the city’s hidden dealings.",sec={{t="A Lead in the Shadows",b="Baros Alexston cannot identify the visitor who spoke with Bazil Thredd, the Stockade’s chief prisoner. Warden Thelwater’s account has brought investigators to the city architect, but he has no name to offer. Instead, Baros points you toward Master Mathias Shaw, who leads SI:7 and makes it his business to know Stormwind’s secrets.",sp=0},{t="Unmasking the Visitor",b="At SI:7 headquarters in Old Town, Mathias Shaw studies the sealed description and sees through the visitor’s alias, Maelik. The marks point to a professional killer, one who casts off names as easily as cloaks. Shaw knows him as an assassin often called Marzon.",sp=1},{t="Treachery in the Nobility",b="Mathias Shaw says Marzon works for Lord Gregor Lescovar, a Stormwind nobleman known for deceit. The connection reaches beyond the Defias Brotherhood’s rebellion in Westfall and into Stormwind’s aristocratic halls.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you to Mathias Shaw?",a="Baros Alexston, Stormwind’s city architect, sends you to Mathias Shaw because he cannot identify the visitor in the Stockade warden’s notes. Baros says Shaw owes him a personal favor.",al={"who gives this quest","quest giver shadow of the past"},gp=true},{q="Where is Master Mathias Shaw located?",a="Mathias Shaw is at SI:7 headquarters in Old Town, Stormwind. It is the covert intelligence center for the crown’s rogues, scouts, and intelligence officers.",al={"mathias shaw location","where is shaw","find mathias shaw"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who was the mysterious visitor to the Stockade?",a="The visitor called himself Maelik. Baros cannot identify him, so he sends the sealed description to Mathias Shaw.",al={"who is maelik","who is thredds visitor","who is the assassin"},sp=1,it="identity"},{q="Why is Lord Gregor Lescovar involved?",a="Baros does not mention Lord Gregor Lescovar. Mathias Shaw reveals Lescovar’s part after reading the visitor’s description.",al={"who does marzon work for","lescovar connection"},sp=1,it="ties"},{q="What does SI:7 stand for?",a="SI:7 means Stormwind Intelligence. It gathers intelligence and carries out covert operations for the Kingdom of Stormwind, at home and abroad.",al={"what is si7","si:7 meaning"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Baros Alexston have pull with SI:7?",a="Baros says Mathias Shaw owes him a favor, but does not explain what it was for.",al={"why does shaw owe baros","baros and shaw connection"},it="history"},{q="Why does Baros Alexston send you to Mathias Shaw?",a="Baros Alexston genuinely cannot identify the mysterious figure who visited Bazil Thredd in the Stockade. However, as the City Architect of Stormwind, he knows someone who tracks every illicit plot in the city. Master Mathias Shaw owes him a favor, making the leader of SI:7 the best person to pierce the visitor's disguises and uncover what dark schemes are brewing beneath the nobility's noses.",al={"why send to shaw","baros alexston motive","why mathias shaw"},it="motive",add="31db03ee"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you can see the heights of Alliance tradecraft and political surveillance when you report to Mathias Shaw in Old Town.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you see the investigation connect Defias banditry to Stormwind’s nobility.",["race:Human"]="As a human of Stormwind, you see the kingdom’s ruling class divided during King Varian Wrynn’s absence."},kw={"baros alexston","bazil thredd","gregor lescovar","maelik","marzon","mathias shaw","shadow of the past","si:7","stormwind"},rel={"npc:mathias-shaw","npc:baros-alexston","quest:392","quest:350","quest:2300","subzone:old-town","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Baros Alexston",["end"]="Master Mathias Shaw",level="29",faction="Alliance",id=393},src={"Shadow of the Past (quest)"}}
E["quest:394"] = {t="quest",n="The Head of the Beast",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind, The Head of the Beast carries you from Elling Trias to Master Mathias Shaw in Old Town. Reporting Lord Gregor Lescovar’s death confirms your place in Stormwind’s covert intelligence network.",h="In Stormwind, The Head of the Beast carries you from Elling Trias to Master Mathias Shaw in Old Town.",sec={{t="A Matter Resolved",b="Elling Trias sends you from the crime scene to Old Town after Lord Lescovar is struck down, ending the immediate danger to Stormwind’s leaders. A cheese merchant and veteran operative, Trias warns you not to be distracted by courtly praise.",sp=1},{t="Reporting to the Spymaster",b="Master Mathias Shaw directs Stormwind’s covert apparatus through SI:7 from hidden chambers in Old Town. When you report Lescovar’s death, Shaw recognizes your skill and ruthlessness, praises your efficiency, and thanks you for serving the people of Stormwind.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this quest?",a="You travel from Elling Trias to Master Mathias Shaw in Stormwind’s Old Town and confirm that Lord Gregor Lescovar has been slain.",al={"head of the beast quest","what do i do in head of the beast"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Mathias Shaw?",a="Mathias Shaw leads SI:7, Stormwind’s secretive intelligence agency and assassin guild, from Old Town.",al={"shaw","master shaw","si7 leader"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Elling Trias send you to Shaw instead of the palace guard?",a="Elling Trias works deep within Stormwind’s intelligence apparatus. Lescovar was a prominent nobleman engaged in high treason, so secrecy helps avoid a public scandal among the palace guard.",al={"why shaw not guards","why report to shaw"},it="why_me"},{q="What threat did Lescovar pose to Stormwind?",a="Lord Gregor Lescovar plotted with subversive agents against the crown and the capital’s safety, betraying the realm from within the nobility.",al={"lescovar threat","what did lescovar do"},it="threat"},{q="What happens after reporting Lescovar's death?",a="Mathias Shaw prepares to close the book on the conspiracy and sends you toward the final resolution of the threat looming over Stormwind.",al={"next quest after head of the beast","what comes next"},it="next_step"},{q="Where can Mathias Shaw be found?",a="Mathias Shaw can be found in SI:7’s command building in Old Town, in the eastern quarters of Stormwind City.",al={"shaw location","where is mathias shaw"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Elling Trias want this done?",a="Elling Trias may appear to be a simple cheese merchant, but he maintains deep ties with Mathias Shaw and Stormwind's intelligence network. Having helped uncover Lord Lescovar's treason, Trias wants the rogue noble's demise officially registered through SI:7's covert channels rather than royal bureaucracy, ensuring the kingdom's shadowy protectors know the threat is finished while keeping the nobility at arm's length.",al={"why does elling trias care","elling trias motive","why send to mathias shaw"},it="motive",add="c9b52599"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, reporting directly to Mathias Shaw confirms your reliability to the leader of Stormwind’s foremost shadow organization.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help stabilize the realm by removing corrupt aristocrats from Stormwind during King Varian Wrynn’s deeply destabilizing absence."},kw={"elling trias","head of the beast","lescovar","mathias shaw","old town","si:7","stormwind"},rel={"quest:434","quest:395","npc:mathias-shaw","npc:elling-trias","subzone:old-town","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Elling Trias",["end"]="Master Mathias Shaw",level="31",faction="Alliance",id=394},src={"The Head of the Beast"}}
E["quest:395"] = {t="quest",n="Brotherhood's End",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind Keep, Lord Gregor Lescovar's killing leaves dangerous questions behind. Master Mathias Shaw sends you to City Architect Baros Alexston and warns you to keep the killer's identity quiet.",h="In Stormwind Keep, Lord Gregor Lescovar's killing leaves dangerous questions behind.",sec={{t="Loose Ends in the Shadows",b="After Lord Gregor Lescovar and his Defias contact, Marzon the Silent Blade, are killed, Master Mathias Shaw urges caution. Killing a high-ranking noble inside the royal keep risks political trouble, even though Lescovar was deep in treason. Shaw tells you to share the broad strokes of the Defias conspiracy with Baros Alexston. Keep your own part in the killing, and the rogue cheese merchant Elling Trias's involvement, off the record.",sp=1},{t="A Breath of Relief",b="Baros Alexston, the City Architect who helped rebuild Stormwind as a stonemason, is relieved to hear that Lescovar is dead. Edwin VanCleef had marked Alexston and other prominent figures in the rebuilding effort for vengeance after the Stonemasons were cast out without pay. With Lescovar silenced and the conspiracy disrupted, Alexston believes the immediate threat to the kingdom's architects and nobility has passed.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What happens in Brotherhood's End?",a="After killing Lord Gregor Lescovar in Stormwind Keep, you report to Master Mathias Shaw at SI:7. Shaw sends you to City Architect Baros Alexston, who wants to know whether the Defias plot against the city's leaders has been foiled.",al={"what is brotherhoods end","brotherhoods end quest overview","brotherhoods end summary"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does Shaw tell you not to admit to killing Lescovar?",a="Lord Gregor Lescovar was a high nobleman in Stormwind's House of Nobles. Though he was proven to collude with the Defias, admitting to his assassination in the royal keep could bring political scandal and scrutiny. Shaw advises leaving the deed unattributed.",al={"why hide lescovar death","why lie about lescovar","shaw advice lescovar"}},{q="Why should nobody mention Elling Trias?",a="Elling Trias poses as a cheese merchant in the Trade District, but he is a veteran operative with many contacts in the city's shadows. Revealing his part in uncovering the conspiracy could expose his cover and compromise his underground network.",al={"why hide trias","trias secret","selling trias cheese vendor"},sp=1},{q="Why was Baros Alexston personally concerned about the Defias?",a="Baros Alexston belonged to the Stonemasons Guild and helped rebuild Stormwind alongside Edwin VanCleef. When the House of Nobles refused to pay the workers, the masons turned to banditry. Alexston stayed in the city's service and became a target of VanCleef's revenge.",al={"why does alexston care","baros alexston vancleef","alexston defias connection"}},{q="Does this quest mark the end of the Defias threat?",a="Killing Edwin VanCleef's key sympathizer in the House of Nobles does not erase the Defias presence. But removing Lescovar deals a critical blow to their efforts inside Stormwind's government and averts an immediate coup within the city walls.",al={"is the defias destroyed","are the defias dead now","does brotherhood end finish defias"},it="conflict"},{q="Where does this investigation lead next?",a="Relieved by your success against the conspirators, Baros Alexston prepares a report on the Defias Brotherhood for the King. He asks you to deliver it at an audience in Stormwind Keep, in An Audience with the King.",al={"what quest is next","next after brotherhoods end","who do i see next"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Master Mathias Shaw send you to Baros Alexston?",a="With Lord Gregor Lescovar dealt with and the immediate conspiracy broken, Baros Alexston came looking for you directly. As the City Architect responsible for rebuilding Stormwind after the First War, Alexston lives under constant threat from Edwin VanCleef's vendetta against the nobility. Shaw wants the noble council appraised of the Defias threat through official civic channels, while keeping SI:7's covert involvement and unsanctioned assassinations shielded from royal scrutiny.",al={"shaw motive","why talk to alexston","why shaw sends you"},it="motive",add="7fb09cca"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Uncovering the Defias conspiracy inside Stormwind Keep shows that the kingdom faces subversion from within its noble halls as well as from bandits across the countryside.",["class:Rogue"]="Mathias Shaw's warning reflects SI:7's unspoken rule: deliver the kingdom's justice in silence, without taking public credit for a noble's blood.",["race:Human"]="For humans of Stormwind, this assignment closes the loop on the Stonemasons' rebellion that began in the city's streets years ago, securing justice without tearing the kingdom apart."},kw={"baros alexston","brotherhood's end","defias","elling trias","gregor lescovar","mathias shaw","si:7","stormwind keep"},rel={"quest:394","quest:396","npc:baros-alexston","topic:defias-brotherhood","topic:stormwind-kingdom","quest:65"},m={start="Master Mathias Shaw",["end"]="Baros Alexston",level="31",faction="Alliance",id=395},src={"Brotherhood's End"}}
E["quest:396"] = {t="quest",n="An Audience with the King",z="stormwind",s="At Stormwind Keep, An Audience with the King brings the Defias report before the Crown. After the long investigation across Westfall and the Deadmines, the heroes carry City Architect Baros Alexston's findings to the capital.",h="At Stormwind Keep, An Audience with the King brings the Defias report before the Crown.",sec={{t="A Royal Summons",b="Edwin VanCleef has been defeated, and the conspiracy beneath Moonbrook has been dismantled. City Architect Baros Alexston prepares an official report for the Crown. He believes the adventurer who broke the guild's criminal enterprise should be honored before the monarch. You carry the detailed findings across Stormwind's grand canals to Stormwind Keep, expecting to meet the realm's sovereign.",sp=0},{t="An Empty Throne",b="Lady Katrana Prestor receives the report in the royal court, but King Varian Wrynn is not there. She says he is away on an extended diplomatic mission and cannot offer congratulations in person. Prestor accepts the findings, commends you for saving Stormwind from VanCleef's schemes, and offers a reward in the king's name. The uprising's grim truth remains hidden behind her account of the king's absence.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why am I delivering this report instead of Baros Alexston?",a="Baros Alexston believes you earned the honor through your fieldwork. You tracked the Defias conspiracy through Westfall and stormed the Deadmines, so he insists you present the findings and receive the Crown's recognition.",al={"why deliver report","baros alexston report","audience with king delivery"},it="why_me"},{q="Where is King Varian Wrynn?",a="King Varian Wrynn is not in Stormwind Keep. The court says he is away on a secret diplomatic mission, leaving his young son Anduin on the throne under Highlord Bolvar Fordragon's regency.",al={"where is the king","why isnt varian here","where is varian wrynn","missing king"}},{q="Who actually takes the Defias report?",a="Lady Katrana Prestor receives the report in the royal court. The chief adviser to the throne accepts Baros Alexston's findings, commends you for defeating Edwin VanCleef, and provides your reward on behalf of the Crown.",al={"who finishes the quest","who do i talk to in keep","who takes report"},it="identity"},{q="Does this quest end the Defias Brotherhood questline?",a="Yes. The report brings the Defias story, from early Westfall through the Deadmines, to its formal political conclusion.",al={"end of defias chain","is this the last defias quest","deadmines aftermath"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Lady Katrana Prestor seem so dismissive of the king's absence?",a="Lady Katrana Prestor keeps her composure in the royal court. She says King Varian is away on distant state business, easing concern about the Crown's whereabouts.",al={"why is prestor calm","prestor diplomatic mission","prestor excuse"}},{q="What happens to the Defias Brotherhood after this?",a="Edwin VanCleef is dead, and the brotherhood's great juggernaut project has been thwarted, leaving its leadership shattered. Scattered brigands and remnants still plague Westfall, Redridge, and Stormwind's alleys.",al={"are defias gone","what happens to defias now","is the brotherhood destroyed"}},{q="Why does Baros Alexston want the report delivered to the King?",a="Baros Alexston needs the crown formally informed that the Defias conspiracy has been broken and Edwin VanCleef slain. The Brotherhood's plots threatened Stormwind itself, and Alexston believes the highest authority in the realm must receive a full, direct accounting of the danger averted—and grant official royal commendation to the one who risked everything to stop them.",al={"why deliver the report","baros alexston report king","why report on defias"},it="motive",add="eac00c4f"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, delivering this report marks the end of one of the greatest internal crises threatening its chief human kingdom.",["race:Human"]="As a human of Stormwind, this audience avenges the terror across Westfall while revealing how fragile the kingless realm has become.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, reporting VanCleef's downfall in the seat of power shows how thin the line can be between a royal operative and an outlaw guildmaster."},kw={"audience with the king","baros alexston","brotherhood's end","defias report","edwin vancleef","katrana prestor","stormwind keep","varian wrynn"},rel={"quest:395","quest:65","npc:baros-alexston","subzone:stormwind-keep","topic:defias-brotherhood","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:varian-wrynn"},m={start="Baros Alexston",["end"]="Lady Katrana Prestor",level="31",faction="Alliance",id=396},src={"An Audience with the King"}}
E["quest:397"] = {t="quest",n="You Have Served Us Well",z="stormwind",s="The warlocks of Stormwind have secured their refuge beneath the Slaughtered Lamb. Practitioners report to Zardeth of the Black Claw, whose cabal has kept the city guard and curious nobles at bay.",h="The warlocks of Stormwind have secured their refuge beneath the Slaughtered Lamb.",sec={{t="A Silence Bought in Shadows",b="Stormwind's warlocks practice their dark arts beneath the Slaughtered Lamb, where the authorities have so far tolerated them. Lord Wishock threatens to expose or disrupt their hidden studies. The coven answers with a tainted draught that brings about his death, preserving its refuge beneath the inn.",sp=0},{t="The Master's Boon",b="Zardeth of the Black Claw hears that Lord Wishock has taken his final drink and judges the danger past. To thank the loyal practitioner for keeping the city guard and curious peers at bay, Zardeth sends his sniveling imp servant, Zggi, to bestow a dark token of gratitude.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Zardeth of the Black Claw?",a="Zardeth of the Black Claw is a prominent warlock who secretly operates in Stormwind City. He protects the city's hidden dark casters from discovery by local nobles, using ruthless measures against anyone who investigates their forbidden craft.",al={"who is zardeth","zardeth role","black claw leader"},it="identity"},{q="What happened to Lord Wishock?",a="Lord Wishock was given a specially prepared toxic brew by Stormwind's hidden warlocks. With him dead, his noble house will no longer investigate or disturb the practitioners beneath the city streets.",al={"did wishock die","what was the brew for","lord wishock fate"},sp=1},{q="Who is Zggi?",a="Zggi is an imp bound to serve Zardeth of the Black Claw. Grudging and covetous, Zggi wants to keep the master's treasures, but fears the punishment that would follow open defiance of Zardeth's orders.",al={"who is the imp zggi","zggi servant"},it="identity"},{q="Why was Lord Wishock targeted by the warlocks?",a="The warlocks targeted Wishock because he threatened to disturb and expose Stormwind's coven. They killed him to protect their work in demonology and shadow magic from interference by the nobility.",al={"why kill wishock","wishock threat"},it="motive"},{q="Where does this quest chain conclude?",a="The chain ends with Zggi, near Zardeth of the Black Claw in the warlock sanctum beneath the Slaughtered Lamb in Stormwind's Mage Quarter.",al={"where do i turn in you have served us well","zggi location"},it="place"},{q="Why is this task restricted strictly to warlocks?",a="The operation involves cabal politics and unlawful assassination. Only proven warlock disciples are trusted with this lethal subterfuge, keeping the broader Alliance authorities unaware.",al={"is this warlock only","why warlock quest"},it="why_me"},{q="Why does Zardeth send you to Zggi?",a="With Lord Wishock poisoned and the warlocks safe from his prying, Zardeth has prepared a special reward for your service to the coven. Rather than hand it to you himself, he directs you downstairs to his servant Zggi, who keeps watch over his treasures and carries out his master's commands.",al={"why talk to zggi","why does zardeth send you to zggi","zardeth gift zggi"},it="purpose",add="7c2d3142"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you learn the ruthless measures Stormwind's coven uses to survive, including killing nosy nobles before they turn the city guard against it.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you live beneath Stormwind's pristine spires and pious devotion, where hidden warlocks kill highborn meddlers to protect their presence."},kw={"a noble brew","black claw","imp","lord wishock","stormwind","the slaughtered lamb","zardeth","zggi"},rel={"quest:335","npc:zardeth-of-the-black-claw","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Zardeth of the Black Claw",["end"]="Zggi",level="30",faction="Alliance",id=397},src={"You Have Served Us Well"}}
E["quest:399"] = {t="quest",n="Humble Beginnings",z="stormwind",s="Baros Alexston seeks help from his home in Stormwind's Cathedral Square. His family's Westfall farm has burned, and thieves hold its ruins; he hopes to recover an heirloom from his youth.",h="Baros Alexston seeks help from his home in Stormwind's Cathedral Square.",sec={{t="A Builder's Roots",b="Baros Alexston grew up working the fields of Westfall. Now he is an accomplished architect in Stormwind City, advising on stonework and city buildings. His path from farm boy to city planner is rare in the kingdom, yet he remains attached to the modest beginnings that shaped him.",sp=0},{t="Tragedy in Westfall",b="Lawlessness swept across Westfall, and the Alexston Farmstead fell to it. Bandits and vagrants burned the house, forcing Baros's father from his livelihood. Family heirlooms were left behind amid the fire and occupation. Baros asks you to search the ruined, bandit-held farmstead west of Sentinel Hill for his first compass, hidden before the home fell.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Baros Alexston?",a="Baros Alexston is Stormwind's City Architect, residing near Cathedral Square. He grew up as a farmer's son in Westfall, then left the countryside to learn the craft of building.",al={"baros alexston","who is baros","city architect"},it="identity"},{q="Where is the Alexston Farmstead located?",a="The Alexston Farmstead lies west of Sentinel Hill in central Westfall. Thieves and rogues aligned with the Defias rabble burned it and took control of the property.",al={"alexston farmstead location","where is the farm","alexston farm"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is the compass important to Baros?",a="The compass matters to Baros only for its sentimental value. It was his first navigation tool as a boy on the farm, a reminder of his path from rural laborer to architectural planner. It has no use in his current craft, but remains an irreplaceable relic of his past.",al={"why compass","what is the compass","simple compass"},it="item"},{q="Who burned down the Alexston farm?",a="Thieves and outlaws terrorizing Westfall razed the farm. With the kingdom's military spread thin and unable to protect outlying homesteads, bandits seized the land and drove out the Alexston family.",al={"who burned the farm","why was farm destroyed","westfall farm burned"},it="conflict"},{q="Where can the compass be found on the farm?",a="Baros's compass was hidden before the family fled. You can find it in a small chest amid the charred ruins of the main farmhouse.",al={"compass location","where is compass","hidden compass"},gp=true},{q="What happened to Baros's father?",a="Baros's father survived the raid and fled the farm. He could not carry their possessions through the flames and bandits, but remembered where the family had hidden valuable keepsakes.",al={"baros father","alexston father","who is baros's dad"},it="people"},{q="Why does Baros Alexston need you to retrieve his compass?",a="Baros is the City Architect of Stormwind, deeply tied to his duties in Cathedral Square while Westfall has fallen entirely into anarchy. The Alexston Farmstead was torched and overrun by Defias thieves, far beyond the reach of his aging father or the neglected regional authorities. As a solitary civic official, Baros cannot simply march into bandit territory himself, leaving him reliant on an capable adventurer to brave the ruins and recover his keepsake.",al={"why can't baros get his compass","why send me for the compass","baros alexston why me"},it="why_me",add="64f512b7"}},ang={["race:Human"]="The Alexston Farmstead's fate reflects the decline of Westfall's yeomanry, where generations of human farmers have been driven from their land by lawlessness on Stormwind's doorstep.",["faction:Alliance"]="When you venture into Westfall on behalf of figures in the capital, you cross the divide between Stormwind's safe streets and the nearby frontier lands left unprotected."},kw={"alexston farmstead","baros alexston","cathedral square","humble beginnings","sentinel hill","simple compass","stormwind","westfall"},rel={"npc:baros-alexston","subzone:alexston-farmstead","zone:westfall","subzone:cathedral-square","subzone:sentinel-hill","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Baros Alexston",level="15",faction="Alliance",id=399,ri={"A Simple Compass"}},src={"Humble Beginnings"}}
E["quest:434"] = {t="quest",n="The Attack!",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind Keep, Tyrion and Elling Trias draw a traitor into a garden meeting. Their plan aims to catch conspirators working against the kingdom.",h="In Stormwind Keep, Tyrion and Elling Trias draw a traitor into a garden meeting.",sec={{t="A Garden Ambush",b="Tyrion, the spy, and Elling Trias, a cheese merchant, bring their investigation to a head inside Stormwind Keep. Tyrion has told Marzon that he and Lord Gregor Lescovar should meet again, and fed him false information. Then Tyrion sends an engineered automaton disguised as Priestess Tyriona into the library to tell Lescovar that his guest has arrived. Lescovar sends his guards away and enters the quiet garden to meet Marzon the Silent Blade, an assassin tied to the Defias Brotherhood.",sp=0},{t="Treason in the Keep",b="Hidden nearby, investigators hear Lescovar and Marzon confirm their suspicion: Stormwind nobles are aiding the Defias conspiracy against the kingdom. When their treasonous talk ends, the trap springs. Lescovar and the Silent Blade must be killed quickly in the courtyard, before the royal guards return and find a noble dead on the cobblestones. The strike cuts away one of the Defias's deepest footholds in Stormwind's seat of power.",sp=1},{t="Shadow Games",b="Elling Trias takes satisfaction in settling his personal score with Marzon, though he resents that his private plans also help Mathias Shaw and SI:7. Lescovar's death proves corruption has reached the court. The Defias Brotherhood had help, and someone among the nobility let it grow.",sp=2}},faq={{q="Who is Lord Gregor Lescovar?",a="Lord Gregor Lescovar is a prominent nobleman who lives in Stormwind Keep. He secretly worked with the Defias Brotherhood, using his rank and influence to undermine the realm from within the palace.",al={"lescovar","who is lescovar","gregor lescovar"},sp=1,it="target"},{q="Who is Marzon the Silent Blade?",a="Marzon the Silent Blade is an assassin for the Defias Brotherhood. He connects the outlaws with Lord Lescovar, carrying messages and plotting schemes until Tyrion draws him into the garden trap.",al={"marzon","silent blade","who is marzon"},sp=1,it="target"},{q="Why does Elling Trias care about this operation?",a="Elling Trias is a cheese merchant and an influential rogue with ties to Stormwind's underworld. Marzon targeted people close to him, so Trias plotted the assassin's downfall, even though it also helped Mathias Shaw and SI:7.",al={"trias role","why is cheese guy involved","elling trias why"},it="motive"},{q="How does Tyrion manage to lure Lescovar outside?",a="Tyrion sends an engineered automaton disguised as Priestess Tyriona into the library to tell Lescovar his guest has arrived. Lescovar dismisses his guards and goes to the garden. Tyrion had already told Marzon to meet again and fed him false information.",al={"spybot disguise","tyriona","how does lescovar get lured"},sp=1},{q="Why do the guards not immediately defend Lescovar?",a="Lescovar sends his guards away before the meeting to keep his dealings with the Defias secret. That leaves investigators a brief chance to ambush Lescovar and Marzon before the royal guards intervene.",al={"why don't guards help lescovar","guards lescovar"},sp=1},{q="What happens after Lescovar is slain?",a="After Lescovar and Marzon die, Elling Trias sends you to Old Town to tell Master Mathias Shaw of SI:7 that the threat has been dealt with, in The Head of the Beast.",al={"what next after the attack","head of the beast"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Tyrion want Lord Lescovar and Marzon killed?",a="Tyrion has spent considerable effort tracking corruption within Stormwind Keep, discovering that Lord Gregor Lescovar is deeply entangled with the Defias Brotherhood. Working in tandem with Elling Trias, Tyrion orchestrated an elaborate sting using false rumors and a mechanical disguise to draw Lescovar and his Defias contact, Marzon the Silent Blade, into the open. To dismantle the conspiracy threatening the city from within, both conspirators must be eliminated before their treasonous scheme can unfold further.",al={"why does tyrion want this","tyrion motive the attack","why kill lescovar tyrion"},it="motive",add="2fdb68e4"},{q="Why does Tyrion need you to carry out the attack instead of the guards?",a="Lord Lescovar is a high-ranking nobleman inside the royal court, and the Stormwind guards are bound by duty to obey and protect him. Until hard treason is spoken, the guards would arrest or strike down anyone making unproven accusations against a lord. Tyrion is also preoccupied managing his mechanical disguise to draw Lescovar out, leaving you as the discreet outside agent needed to witness their confession and strike swiftly before the guards return.",al={"why doesn't tyrion use guards","why me the attack","why not royal guards lescovar"},it="why_me",add="70ac8295"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you see how underworld dealings can reach into Stormwind's politics, even through a cheese shop and a quiet garden.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you see a Defias ally removed from Stormwind Keep, while the danger to the kingdom's leadership remains.",["race:Human"]="As a human of Stormwind, you learn that nobles within the royal palace secretly fuel the bandit crisis in Westfall and Redridge."},kw={"defias","elling trias","lescovar","marzon","priestess tyriona","silent blade","spybot","stormwind keep","the attack","tyrion"},rel={"npc:tyrion","npc:elling-trias","quest:394","quest:2746","quest:2300","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:alliance"},m={start="Tyrion",["end"]="Elling Trias",level="31",faction="Alliance",id=434},src={"The Attack!"}}
E["quest:543"] = {t="quest",n="The Perenolde Tiara",z="stormwind",s="Count Remington Ridgewell seeks a lost heirloom in the Ruins of Alterac. The Stormwind aristocrat sends mercenaries north to recover the Perenolde Tiara, once owned by Alterac's royal family and now said to be held by an ogre mage.",h="Count Remington Ridgewell seeks a lost heirloom in the Ruins of Alterac.",sec={{t="A Relic of a Ruined Kingdom",b="Alterac's royal family wore an emerald-set tiara crafted by master dwarven jewelers in Ironforge. During the Second War, King Aiden Perenolde betrayed the Grand Alliance and joined the Orcish Horde. His betrayal led to Alterac's conquest and collapse. In the fall of Alterac City, many treasures of the royal family vanished among the snowy rubble of the Alterac Mountains.",sp=0},{t="The Miser in the Ruins",b="Grel'borg the Miser, an ogre mage of the Crushridge ogres, came to hold the tiara among the ruins of Alterac. He searches the broken stones for baubles and abandoned wealth. Count Remington Ridgewell, a collector of historical oddities in Stormwind City, learns the tiara survived. He hires mercenaries to enter ogre-held territory, defeat Grel'borg, and bring the jewel back to his gallery.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was the Perenolde family?",a="The Perenoldes were the royal family of Alterac, the human realm in the north. During the Second War, King Aiden Perenolde collaborated with the invading Orcish Horde to spare his kingdom. The Alliance of Lordaeron uncovered his treachery, occupied Alterac, dismantled its throne, and left the kingdom to descend into lawlessness and ruin.",al={"house of perenolde","who were the perenoldes","perenolde lore"},it="people"},{q="Who made the Perenolde Tiara?",a="Master jewelers in Ironforge made the tiara. They set it with emeralds as a sign of nobility and wealth for Alterac's ruling family.",al={"tiara origin","who crafted perenolde tiara"},it="origin"},{q="Who holds the tiara now?",a="Grel'borg the Miser holds the tiara. The ogre mage scavenges the snowy Ruins of Alterac for treasures left behind by the ruined human city.",al={"grelborg","who has perenolde tiara","tiara location"},it="target"},{q="Why does Count Remington Ridgewell want the tiara?",a="Count Remington Ridgewell wants the tiara for his private collection. The wealthy noble and antiquarian lives in Stormwind City and hires mercenaries to retrieve lost treasures from perilous places across Azeroth.",al={"remington ridgewell motive","why get the tiara"},it="motive"},{q="Where are the Ruins of Alterac located?",a="The Ruins of Alterac lie in the northern Alterac Mountains, north of the Hillsbrad Foothills and the Durnholde region. Crushridge ogres and Syndicate outlaws now infest the abandoned city.",al={"alterac ruins location","where is alterac"},it="place"},{q="What happens to the tiara after you recover it?",a="After Count Ridgewell receives the muddy, tarnished heirloom, professional restorers clean and polish it. He then mounts it as a showpiece in his collection.",al={"tiara turn in","tiara fate"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="What is the Perenolde Tiara?",a="The Perenolde Tiara is a priceless royal heirloom crafted by master dwarven jewelers in Ironforge. Fitted with exquisite emeralds, it once adorned the heads of the ruling nobility of Alterac. When the treacherous kingdom collapsed and fell into ruin, the tiara disappeared into the ashes of history, coveted by collectors for both its extravagant beauty and historical pedigree.",al={"what is perenolde tiara","perenolde tiara lore","tiara of perenolde"},it="item",add="19149d4d"},{q="Why does Count Ridgewell hire an adventurer instead of sending his own men?",a="Count Remington Ridgewell is a fastidious Stormwind nobleman who worries about keeping his tailored pant cuffs spotless, hardly a man inclined to trek north into freezing wilderness. Furthermore, Alterac lies far beyond the jurisdiction and reach of the Stormwind city guard, overrun by hostile ogres and outlaws. Securing such an heirloom in remote ruins demands a hardy adventurer willing to do dangerous, dirty work for coin.",al={"why send me perenolde tiara","why not royal guard","why does ridgewell need me"},it="why_me",add="e2bd82b9"}},ang={["race:Human"]="For humans of the Alliance, the tiara recalls Alterac's betrayal during the Second War, when its human royalty sided with the Horde against their own kin.",["race:Dwarf"]="The tiara was crafted by Ironforge's master jewelers. Their fine work endured even as a human kingdom fell.",["faction:Alliance"]="By traveling north into the lawless Alterac Mountains, you can clear out dangerous Crushridge ogres and recover priceless historical artifacts for Stormwind's nobility."},kw={"alterac","crushridge","grel'borg","miser","perenolde","ridgewell","stormwind","tiara"},rel={"npc:count-remington-ridgewell","subzone:ruins-of-alterac","topic:alterac-kingdom","zone:ironforge","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Count Remington Ridgewell",faction="Alliance",id=543,ri={"Perenolde Tiara"}},src={"The Perenolde Tiara"}}
E["quest:5634"] = {t="quest",n="Desperate Prayer",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind, human priests seek a prayer for their own hour of need. At the Cathedral of Light, High Priestess Laurena teaches acolytes to call on the Holy Light when their lives are at risk.",h="In Stormwind, human priests seek a prayer for their own hour of need.",sec={{t="A Plea in the Dark",b="Priests in the Cathedral of Light learn to use their faith to shield companions, heal wounds, and strike at evil. Yet even the devout can be isolated, cornered, or brought close to death. In such moments, an acolyte may cry out to the Holy Light for help, with their own survival at stake.",sp=0},{t="The Cathedral's Blessing",b="High Priestess Laurena guides clergy in Stormwind's Cathedral Square and judges when an acolyte is ready for deeper teachings. Human initiates who show devotion to the Light across the kingdom receive this lesson as both protection and a charge to continue serving the realm.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of Desperate Prayer?",a="Desperate Prayer lets a wounded priest call on the Holy Light to heal their own critical injuries at once, without a long chant.",al={"what does desperate prayer do","why desperate prayer","desperate prayer purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Who grants this lesson in Stormwind?",a="High Priestess Laurena grants this lesson in the Cathedral of Light in Stormwind's Cathedral Square, once an acolyte has shown devotion and experience in the wider world.",al={"who teaches desperate prayer","where to get desperate prayer","high priestess laurena quest"},it="identity"},{q="Why do priests receive this specific teaching?",a="Priests of the Holy Light risk their lives to aid others. This prayer can help preserve a healer's life when they are alone or badly hurt.",al={"why do priests get desperate prayer","lore behind desperate prayer"},it="motive"},{q="Can any adventurer learn Desperate Prayer here?",a="No. Only priests devoted to the Holy Light and guided by the Church of the Light receive this lesson.",al={"can anyone learn desperate prayer","is this quest priest only"},it="for_you",gp=true},{q="Where does this rite take place?",a="The rite takes place in the Cathedral of Light, in the northern district of Stormwind City.",al={"desperate prayer location","where is laurena"},it="place"},{q="Is Desperate Prayer unique to human priests?",a="Both human and dwarven clergy in Alliance lands have access to Desperate Prayer, through their closely allied traditions of worshiping the Holy Light in Stormwind and Ironforge.",al={"do other races get desperate prayer","dwarf desperate prayer"}}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest, this rite marks your passage from apprentice acolyte to an active servant of the Holy Light, prepared to survive deadly trials in the field.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you receive this teaching from the Cathedral of Light's clergy, affirming Stormwind's place as the foremost seat of human faith.",["faction:Alliance"]="As a member of the Alliance, you know that blessings like Desperate Prayer help keep frontline healers alive to tend soldiers on dangerous frontiers."},kw={"cathedral of light","cathedral square","desperate prayer","high priestess laurena","holy light","laurena","priest","stormwind"},rel={"npc:high-priestess-laurena","topic:light"},m={start="High Priestess Laurena",level="10",faction="Alliance",id=5634},src={"Desperate Prayer (Cathedral Square)"}}
E["quest:5635"] = {t="quest",n="Desperate Prayer",z="stormwind",s="Promising priests from Elwynn Forest are summoned to Stormwind for further training in the Church of the Holy Light. After proving their devotion and discipline, they come before High Priestess Laurena at the Cathedral of Light.",h="Promising priests from Elwynn Forest are summoned to Stormwind for further training in the Church of the Holy...",sec={{t="A Summons to the Capital",b="Priestess Josetta guides novice priests in Goldshire, while other local mentors serve the outlying settlements of Elwynn Forest. When a disciple proves capable in spirit and deeds, word reaches the senior priesthood in Stormwind. A summons to the Cathedral of Light marks the move to deeper responsibilities in the faith and formal training at the spiritual heart of the Kingdom of Stormwind.",sp=0},{t="Guidance from the High Priestess",b="At the Cathedral, acolytes present themselves to High Priestess Laurena, one of the Church's senior leaders in Stormwind. She oversees their spiritual grounding and practical training as newly elevated priests. Her instruction prepares them for the harsh trials facing the Alliance and teaches the Light's miracles, including Desperate Prayer, the plea for salvation known among human practitioners.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the quest Desperate Prayer?",a="Desperate Prayer sends promising priests from Goldshire to Stormwind's Cathedral of Light for further training under High Priestess Laurena.",al={"desperate prayer quest","what is desperate prayer quest","why do desperate prayer"},it="purpose"},{q="Who gives the quest Desperate Prayer?",a="Priestess Josetta, the priest trainer at the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire, gives you the summons after you prove your devotion.",al={"who starts desperate prayer","desperate prayer quest giver"},it="identity"},{q="Who is High Priestess Laurena?",a="High Priestess Laurena is a senior leader of the Church of the Holy Light who trains acolytes inside Stormwind's Cathedral of Light.",al={"who is laurena","high priestess laurena lore"},it="identity"},{q="Where is the Cathedral of Light located?",a="The Cathedral of Light is in Cathedral Square, in the northern district of Stormwind City. It is the spiritual center for the kingdom's priests and paladins.",al={"where is cathedral of light","cathedral location stormwind"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is the quest named Desperate Prayer?",a="Human priests learn Desperate Prayer as a plea to the Light for immediate, self-preserving deliverance during their advanced training in Stormwind.",al={"why called desperate prayer","desperate prayer name meaning"},it="name"},{q="Do other races or classes get this quest?",a="This instruction is for priests advancing from Elwynn Forest to begin higher training in Stormwind.",al={"can dwarves do desperate prayer quest","is desperate prayer priest only"},gp=true},{q="Why does Priestess Josetta want you to visit the Cathedral of Light?",a="Priestess Josetta is acting on orders from the Church hierarchy. You have proven your devotion and capability in the field, drawing the attention of the church superiors in Stormwind. Josetta's role is to direct promising young acolytes toward higher mentorship, and she sends you to the Cathedral of Light so you can receive more advanced instruction in the ways of the Light.",al={"why does josetta send you","priestess josetta motive","why visit stormwind priest"},it="motive",add="24d97f9e"}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you move from novice service in Goldshire to training under the senior leadership of the Cathedral of Light.",["race:Human"]="As a human who follows the Holy Light, entering the Cathedral of Light affirms your duty to the kingdom's spiritual heart.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you belong to a people bound in part by the Church of the Holy Light, one of its strongest cultural and moral pillars amid looming threats."},kw={"cathedral of light","desperate prayer","goldshire","high priestess laurena","holy light","priest","priestess josetta","stormwind"},rel={"npc:high-priestess-laurena","npc:priestess-josetta","subzone:cathedral-of-light","topic:light","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Priestess Josetta",["end"]="High Priestess Laurena",level="10",faction="Alliance",id=5635},src={"Desperate Prayer (Goldshire)"}}
E["quest:5637"] = {t="quest",n="Desperate Prayer",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind, dwarven priests are called to deepen their service to the Light. High Priestess Laurena summons promising acolytes from Dun Morogh to the Cathedral of Light. There they take on wider duties among the Alliance.",h="In Stormwind, dwarven priests are called to deepen their service to the Light.",sec={{t="A Summons to the Cathedral",b="Dwarven priests trained in Dun Morogh can outgrow the lessons of local mentors like Maxan Anvol in Kharanos. When an acolyte shows promise, High Priestess Laurena sends a formal summons from the Cathedral of Light. Her attention means the young priest is ready for deeper study and greater duties in the faith.",sp=0},{t="Bonds Across Kingdoms",b="Ironforge keeps its own holy traditions in the Mystic Ward, while Stormwind's Church of the Holy Light welcomes humans and dwarves alike. The journey south by Deeprun Tram brings dwarven acolytes into the wider church community and strengthens the spiritual bond between the allied kingdoms.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is High Priestess Laurena calling dwarven priests to Stormwind?",a="High Priestess Laurena calls promising acolytes to continue their religious instruction at the Cathedral of Light. Local tutors such as Maxan Anvol send them when they have mastered the basic tenets, so they can learn advanced techniques like Desperate Prayer.",al={"why laurena call me","why go to stormwind priest","who is high priestess laurena"},it="purpose"},{q="What is Desperate Prayer in the lore?",a="Desperate Prayer is an urgent appeal to the Holy Light practiced by human and dwarven clerics. When a priest is near death, a sudden cry of faith knits wounds and restores vitality.",al={"desperate prayer lore","what is desperate prayer","how does desperate prayer work"},it="power"},{q="Where does this quest take place?",a="You begin in Kharanos in Dun Morogh, where Maxan Anvol teaches you. From there, you travel to Stormwind City and the Cathedral of Light in Cathedral Square, where High Priestess Laurena presides.",al={"quest location","where do i go","where is laurena"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why would a dwarf priest train under a human High Priestess?",a="Dwarves and humans share faith in the Holy Light, a bond strengthened during the Second War. Dwarven priests often serve in Ironforge's Mystic Ward, while Stormwind's Cathedral of Light welcomes practitioners from across the Alliance.",al={"why human trainer dwarf","dwarf church of light","ironforge vs stormwind light"},it="ties"},{q="How should a young traveler reach Stormwind from Dun Morogh?",a="Travel through Ironforge's Tinker Town and take the Deeprun Tram beneath the mountains to Stormwind's Dwarven District.",al={"how to get to stormwind","travel to stormwind dwarf","deeprun tram"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Who is Maxan Anvol?",a="Maxan Anvol is a dwarven priest trainer in Kharanos, Dun Morogh. He teaches young clerics the fundamentals until they are ready to study with senior church leaders in Stormwind.",al={"maxan anvol lore","who gave quest","kharanos priest trainer"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Maxan Anvol send you to Stormwind?",a="Maxan Anvol serves as your local tutor in Kharanos, but he knows when a young acolyte has outgrown the modest lessons of a snowy outpost. Word has reached him that High Priestess Laurena herself has summoned you to the Cathedral of Light. Maxan wants to ensure you don't squander your promise—whether the summons brings grave news or grand opportunity, advancing your mastery of the Light requires learning from the Church's foremost leaders in the human capital.",al={"why does maxan send you","maxan anvol motive","why go to stormwind priest quest"},it="motive",rc="Dwarf",add="9ecbae4a",nx={8}},{q="Why does Maxan Anvol send you instead of going himself?",a="The summons is not an errand or an official diplomatic dispatch; High Priestess Laurena specifically called for you by name. Maxan believes your demonstrated devotion and growth have caught the Cathedral's eye. Furthermore, Maxan must remain in Kharanos to minister to the local dwarven flock and guide raw beginners taking their first steps in the faith.",al={"why me desperate prayer","why doesn't maxan go to stormwind"},it="why_me",rc="Dwarf",add="12c7ba04"}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you move from basic duties in your parish to advanced holy techniques taught by the Church's leaders.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, your journey to Stormwind's Cathedral strengthens the spiritual bond between Ironforge and the human realm of Stormwind.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you share the Light with practitioners from Ironforge and Stormwind, united across racial borders."},kw={"cathedral of light","desperate prayer","dun morogh","kharanos","laurena","maxan anvol","priest","stormwind"},rel={"npc:high-priestess-laurena","npc:maxan-anvol","subzone:cathedral-of-light","topic:light","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Maxan Anvol",["end"]="High Priestess Laurena",level="10",faction="Alliance",id=5637},src={"Desperate Prayer (Kharanos)"}}
E["quest:5638"] = {t="quest",n="Desperate Prayer",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind, a summons carries a young priest from the Park to the Cathedral of Light. Nara Meideros sends you to High Priestess Laurena for further instruction.",h="In Stormwind, a summons carries a young priest from the Park to the Cathedral of Light.",sec={{t="A Word in the Park",b="In Stormwind’s Park, Nara Meideros keeps faith with Elune. The city’s spiritual guides share ties across their different traditions. When the Cathedral seeks a promising student, Nara sends you across the canals with quiet encouragement. The message brings good tidings, not cause for alarm.",sp=0},{t="The Call of the Cathedral",b="At the Cathedral of Light in Cathedral Square, you report to High Priestess Laurena. One of Stormwind’s senior clerical leaders, she guides young acolytes beyond their first prayers. Laurena teaches the sacred invocation called Desperate Prayer, a personal plea for divine aid. It can mend grievous wounds in an instant when a servant of the Light stands near death.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends me on this quest?",a="Priestess Nara Meideros, a night elf cleric in Stormwind’s Park, sends you word that the Cathedral leadership seeks you.",al={"quest giver","who gives desperate prayer","nara meideros"},it="people"},{q="Who do I need to report to in Stormwind?",a="Report to High Priestess Laurena inside the Cathedral of Light in Stormwind’s Cathedral Square.",al={"where to go","quest turn in","who is laurena"},it="target"},{q="What is the significance of Desperate Prayer?",a="Desperate Prayer is an invocation that calls on divine grace to restore its caster in an instant during extreme peril. It is taught to human and dwarven clerics of the Holy Light.",al={"what does desperate prayer do","priest ability lore","desperate prayer spell"},it="purpose"},{q="Why is a night elf directing priests to the human cathedral?",a="Night elf priestesses worship Elune, while humans and dwarves follow the Holy Light. Stormwind’s spiritual orders keep close contact and mutual respect, and share word when Alliance clerics need training.",al={"why nara meideros","park to cathedral","night elf elune stormwind"},it="why_here"},{q="At what point in training does this summons occur?",a="The summons comes around the tenth circle of experience, when a young priest has shown enough field skill to take on more demanding divine rites.",al={"what level is this","when do i get desperate prayer"},gp=true},{q="Where is the Cathedral of Light located?",a="The Cathedral of Light dominates Cathedral Square in northern Stormwind City, between the Dwarven District and the Park.",al={"cathedral location","where is cathedral square"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Nara Meideros want me to visit the Cathedral of Light?",a="Nara Meideros has no personal stake or grievance of her own; she is simply doing a favor for a fellow priest of your order. A priest visited the Park specifically seeking you out and requested that Nara deliver the message whenever you crossed paths. Noting the messenger's cheerful and upbeat demeanor, she passes along the summons with the reassuring thought that good news and important advancement await you under High Priestess Laurena's guidance.",al={"why does nara send me","nara meideros motive","why go to cathedral of light"},it="motive",add="8a572a98"},{q="Why does High Priestess Laurena summon me specifically?",a="As an aspiring priest of the Holy Light who has proven your mettle across your early adventures, your mentor recognizes that your spiritual attunement has matured. Laurena requires your personal presence because the deeper mysteries and responsibilities of the priesthood cannot be delegated or taught through intermediaries. She has prepared essential, direct lessons in your faith that will expand your sacred gifts and grant you the mastery required to safeguard your allies.",al={"why me desperate prayer","why does laurena want me","why summon me cathedral"},it="why_me",add="e569a4a2"}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest, this summons marks your entry into higher spiritual disciplines and opens the way to learn Desperate Prayer, an invocation that can save lives.",["race:Human"]="As a human, the Cathedral of Light is the chief sanctuary of human worship in the southern Eastern Kingdoms. Laurena’s guidance marks an important spiritual step.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can see the quiet solidarity between Darnassus and Stormwind’s holy orders in the cooperation between Nara Meideros and the Cathedral clergy."},kw={"cathedral of light","desperate prayer","high priestess laurena","holy light","nara meideros","priest quest","stormwind","the park"},rel={"npc:high-priestess-laurena","npc:nara-meideros","subzone:cathedral-of-light","topic:light","topic:elune","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Nara Meideros",["end"]="High Priestess Laurena",level="10",faction="Alliance",id=5638},src={"Desperate Prayer (Park)"}}
E["quest:5676"] = {t="quest",n="Arcane Feedback",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind, Arcane Feedback prepares priests to face hostile spellcasters. High Priestess Laurena teaches the rite in the Cathedral of Light, where faith is shaped into a defense against arcane power.",h="In Stormwind, Arcane Feedback prepares priests to face hostile spellcasters.",sec={{t="A Shield Against the Arcane",b="At the Cathedral of Light, High Priestess Laurena warns acolytes that arcane magic remains a danger. The Holy Light brings healing, warmth, and divine order, while raw magic can turn volatile and lead to corruption or catastrophe. Warlocks, renegade sorcerers, and magical beasts threaten the faithful. Priests learn that faith can become an active ward against spells around them.",sp=0},{t="Turn the Torrent Inward",b="Arcane Feedback turns a hostile spellcaster's power back against them. The ward does more than deflect spells: it burns through the caster's mana and causes agony. Laurena teaches the rite to human priests preparing to travel beyond Stormwind, so the Cathedral's emissaries can face sorcery with a defense of their own.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the quest Arcane Feedback?",a="The rite teaches a human priest a protective discipline under the Church of the Light. High Priestess Laurena shows how to resist and retaliate against hostile spellcasters.",al={"arcane feedback quest","what is arcane feedback","why do this quest"},it="purpose"},{q="Who offers this quest and where can she be found?",a="High Priestess Laurena offers the training in the Cathedral of Light, in Cathedral Square in Stormwind City.",al={"who gives arcane feedback","arcane feedback quest giver","where is laurena"},it="identity"},{q="Why does the Church of the Holy Light view arcane magic as an enemy?",a="The Church teaches devotion, moral clarity, and reliance on divine grace. Its priests regard uncontrolled arcane magic as a hazard because its volatile, addictive forces have drawn demonic incursions and brought havoc to Azeroth.",al={"why do priests hate arcane","church vs arcane","is arcane bad"},it="conflict"},{q="How does the Arcane Feedback ward work conceptually?",a="The spell surrounds the priest with a retaliatory aura. When a hostile spell strikes it, the backlash drains the attacker's mana and causes physical shock.",al={"how does arcane feedback work","arcane feedback lore"},it="power"},{q="Can any priest learn this from Laurena?",a="In Stormwind, Laurena teaches this discipline to human priests as part of the Cathedral of Light's traditions.",al={"can dwarves learn arcane feedback","who can get arcane feedback","priest racial spell"},gp=true},{q="What level is expected of an acolyte undertaking this training?",a="Priests learn this technique around their twentieth circle of experience, as they leave basic church duties for dangerous frontier lands.",al={"what level for arcane feedback","arcane feedback level requirement"},gp=true},{q="Why does High Priestess Laurena offer to teach you Arcane Feedback?",a="High Priestess Laurena considers arcane magic to be among the greatest threats facing the faithful. Rather than leaving priests defenseless against enemy spellcasters, the priesthood found it necessary to master counter-measures. Laurena imparts this spell to ensure you possess the spiritual and mystical wards needed to protect both yourself and your companions from those who wield destructive arcane power against you.",al={"why does laurena teach arcane feedback","high priestess laurena motive","why learn arcane feedback"},it="motive",add="1a3af0d5"}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you gain a way to hinder those who wield mana when divine diplomacy fails.",["race:Human"]="As a human priest in Stormwind, you follow the Cathedral of Light's training, joining devotion with discipline against magic.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance priest, you help meet the threat of renegade cabals and dark practitioners across the Eastern Kingdoms."},kw={"anti-magic","arcane feedback","cathedral of light","high priestess laurena","holy light","human priest","laurena","priest","stormwind"},rel={"npc:high-priestess-laurena"},m={start="High Priestess Laurena",level="20",faction="Alliance",id=5676},src={"Arcane Feedback (Stormwind)"}}
E["quest:579"] = {t="quest",n="Stormwind Library",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind Keep, Donyal Tovald copies the kingdom’s histories for those with library scrips. Young King Anduin Wrynn has set aside royal funds for the work, opening these accounts of Azeroth to citizens and scholars.",h="In Stormwind Keep, Donyal Tovald copies the kingdom’s histories for those with library scrips.",sec={{t="A Royal Mandate for Knowledge",b="While Highlord Bolvar Fordragon and Lady Katrana Prestor guide Stormwind’s defenses and court in King Varian’s absence, young King Anduin turns royal support toward learning. He funds copies of ancient manuscripts and historical journals, so the kingdom’s past can be preserved and studied. Within Stormwind Keep, the Royal Library keeps these written accounts and copies them for those in royal service.",sp=0},{t="The Scrip Exchange",b="Hand copying delicate parchment takes time, ink, and royal sanction. Librarian Donyal Tovald accepts official library scrips issued to adventurers and scholars across Alliance territories. In return, he provides copies of historical works, from the ancient histories of the Eastern Kingdoms to accounts of distant lands, offering knowledge of conflicts beyond the capital.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Stormwind Library quest?",a="You can exchange a Library Scrip with librarian Donyal Tovald for a readable book. These books share histories of Alliance people, places, and events across Azeroth.",al={"what does this quest do","stormwind library quest purpose","why do this quest"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Donyal Tovald?",a="Donyal Tovald oversees the Royal Library in Stormwind Keep. He manages the kingdom’s written histories and distributes copies under King Anduin’s order.",al={"who is donyal tovald","librarian stormwind","who gives the books"},it="identity"},{q="Where do you obtain a Library Scrip?",a="Library Scrips are given across Alliance territories by scholars, magistrates, and officials who value learning about the wider world.",al={"where do i get library scrip","how to get library scrip","library scrip source"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Why is young King Anduin funding the library?",a="King Anduin Wrynn funds copies of historical works because he values learning and education. While still a child, he set aside royal funds to make the kingdom’s histories available to the public under Regent Bolvar Fordragon’s guidance.",al={"why does anduin care about books","anduin library funding","king anduin books"},it="motive"},{q="Where is the library located in Stormwind?",a="The Royal Library is inside Stormwind Keep, the great fortress in the eastern part of the city. Donyal Tovald can be found among its shelves and reading tables.",al={"where is stormwind library","royal library location","where is donyal tovald located"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Can I read the books I receive?",a="Yes. Each book from the library can be read and offers background on legends and historical events across Azeroth.",al={"are the books readable","can you open the books","do books do anything"},it="item",gp=true},{q="What is the Library Scrip used for?",a="A Library Scrip serves as official royal authorization to redeem a copied tome from the Royal Library of Stormwind. Thanks to funding provided by young King Anduin Wrynn, the library reproduces historical writings and accounts for citizens, but Donyal Tovald requires a valid voucher before he can part with one of these carefully transcribed volumes.",al={"what is library scrip","library scrip purpose","why library scrip"},it="item",add="c9ea8ca7"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you can turn to the Royal Library for the kingdom’s histories, alongside your arcane studies in the Mage Quarter.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance citizen, you can find records of the triumphs and tragedies of the Alliance of Lordaeron, and the bonds between humans, dwarves, gnomes, and high elves.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you know the value of preserving history. Old Stormwind lost countless archives when it was sacked during the First War, and scholars now protect and copy the histories that survived the kingdom’s rebuilding."},kw={"anduin wrynn","books","donyal tovald","library scrip","lore tomes","stormwind keep","stormwind library","transcription"},rel={"npc:donyal-tovald","subzone:royal-library","topic:alliance"},m={start="Donyal Tovald",["end"]="Donyal Tovald",level="1",faction="Alliance",id=579,ri={"Library Scrip"}},src={"Stormwind Library"}}
E["quest:6261"] = {t="quest",n="Dungar Longdrink",z="stormwind",s="At Stormwind's Trade District roost, Dungar Longdrink arranges swift gryphon transport for supplies bound to Westfall's embattled defenders.",h="At Stormwind's Trade District roost, Dungar Longdrink arranges swift gryphon transport for supplies bound to...",sec={{t="A Vital Supply Chain",b="Defias outlaws and feral harvest golems have pushed Westfall close to breaking point. Quartermaster Lewis and the People's Militia are desperate for provisions. Lewis sent word to the capital, and armorer Osric Strang packed the requested equipment. Carrying military cargo on foot through bandit-ridden Elwynn and Westfall takes precious time. Stormwind's new aerial routes offer a vital link to the frontier.",sp=0},{t="The Master of the Roost",b="The gryphon roost sits in Stormwind's Trade District, where Dungar Longdrink coordinates courier and passenger flights. Wildhammer dwarves traditionally raise and handle these majestic beasts. They carry people and cargo across human lands when roosts at both ends know the route. Bringing Osric's heavy crate straight to Dungar teaches couriers how aerial logistics work. It connects the capital's stockpiles directly to frontier outposts such as Sentinel Hill.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Dungar Longdrink?",a="Dungar Longdrink manages Stormwind City's gryphons from the flight roost in the Trade District. He oversees courier beasts and passenger travel across Alliance territories in southern Lordaeron and Azeroth.",al={"dungar","who is dungar","stormwind gryphon master"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Osric sending this crate via gryphon?",a="Quartermaster Lewis and the People's Militia in Westfall are desperately short of gear against the bandits. Moving heavy supplies by foot or wagon takes days and risks ambush, while a trained gryphon can carry Osric's crate across borders in minutes.",al={"why use gryphon","why not walk","osric crate delivery"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Thor, and why must I speak to him first?",a="Thor is the gryphon master at Sentinel Hill in Westfall. Gryphons follow specific routes between known points, so Dungar's mounts can fly you back only after you have checked in with Thor and mapped the path from the other end.",al={"who is thor","why visit thor","thor gryphon"},it="ties"},{q="What happens after Dungar accepts the crate?",a="After inspecting the crate, Dungar readies a gryphon and directs you to carry it straight to Quartermaster Lewis at Sentinel Hill.",al={"what next","return to lewis","next quest"},it="next_step"},{q="Where does this quest fit into the flight chain?",a="This is the third step in an introduction to the flight network. It begins in Westfall with 'A Swift Message', takes you to Stormwind in 'Continue to Stormwind', brings you to Dungar, and ends with 'Return to Lewis'.",al={"quest chain","flight questline","how many quests"},gp=true},{q="Why does Stormwind rely on dwarven gryphons?",a="Since the Second War joined the Alliance of Lordaeron with the Wildhammer clan of the Hinterlands, gryphons have been the Alliance realms' chief scouts and transports. They offer fast travel around ruined roads and hostile blockades.",al={"why gryphons in stormwind","alliance gryphons lore"},it="history"},{q="Why does Osric Strang want this done?",a="Osric assembled the gear requested by Quartermaster Lewis and urgently needs it delivered to Westfall. The soldiers stationed there are hard-pressed and cannot afford to go without fresh supplies and proper equipment. By sending you to Dungar Longdrink and taking advantage of gryphon flight, Osric ensures these vital provisions arrive as swiftly as possible.",al={"osric strang motive","why send the crate","why does osric want this"},it="motive",add="915b1473"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Connecting Stormwind to regional settlements by gryphon helps keep order while the kingdom's central army is away.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you carry an ancestral bond with gryphons into the human kingdom, where handlers such as Dungar Longdrink and Thor guide them.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you rely on individual merchants and local handlers to keep frontier outposts armed while the House of Nobles neglects Westfall."},kw={"dungar longdrink","gryphon master","osric strang","osric's crate","sentinel hill","stormwind","thor","trade district","westfall"},rel={"npc:osric-strang","quest:6285","quest:6281","quest:6181","subzone:trade-district","npc:thor","zone:westfall","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Osric Strang",["end"]="Dungar Longdrink",level="10",faction="Alliance",id=6261},src={"Dungar Longdrink (Classic)"}}
E["quest:690"] = {t="quest",n="Malin's Request",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind, Malin asks for help recovering relics from fallen Stromgarde. Archmage Malin sends seasoned Alliance adventurers north to Refuge Pointe in the Arathi Highlands, where an expedition seeks the magical relics left behind when Stromgarde fell.",h="In Stormwind, Malin asks for help recovering relics from fallen Stromgarde.",sec={{t="A Master's Lost Belongings",b="Archmage Malin serves in Stormwind's Wizard's Sanctum and acts for his former mentor, Archmage Trelane. When Stromgarde fell into chaos, Trelane made a desperate stand at the Tower of Arathor. As hostile forces took the city, he had to abandon his post and leave powerful enchanted possessions behind. Malin fears those relics may fall into hostile hands. He sends capable mercenaries north to strengthen his agents in the field and reclaim Trelane's lost belongings.",sp=0},{t="The Strained Outpost at Refuge Pointe",b="Refuge Pointe lies on the road to Trelane's relics, in the central Arathi Highlands. The outpost is a hard-pressed refuge for Stromgarde loyalists, and Malin's chief contact there is the dwarf Skuerto. Syndicate outlaws, Witherbark trolls, and Boulderfist ogres press the outpost from every side. When you arrive, Skuerto and the garrison are stretched too thin to welcome you warmly without immediate help.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Archmage Malin?",a="Archmage Malin is a human wizard in Stormwind's Wizard's Sanctum. Once an apprentice to Archmage Trelane of Stromgarde, he now directs efforts from Stormwind to recover his mentor's magical research.",al={"archmage malin","who is malin","malin stormwind"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Malin need help in Arathi?",a="Stromgarde fell under siege, forcing Archmage Trelane to flee the Tower of Arathor. Malin's agents are trying to recover Trelane's abandoned relics, but they are overwhelmed and need reinforcements.",al={"why go to arathi","malin mission purpose","why arathi highlands"},it="motive"},{q="Where is Skuerto located?",a="Skuerto is a dwarf scout stationed at Refuge Pointe, an Alliance encampment on the main trade road through the central Arathi Highlands.",al={"find skuerto","skuerto location","where is refuge pointe"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happened to the Tower of Arathor?",a="The Tower of Arathor was an arcane stronghold in Stromgarde. As the kingdom fell, Archmage Trelane tried to hold it against Syndicate rogues and Boulderfist ogres, but its defenses failed and he had to flee.",al={"tower of arathor fall","what happened to stromgarde","trelane tower"},it="history"},{q="What happens after reporting to Skuerto?",a="Skuerto is overwhelmed and dismissive when you arrive. He sends you to his companions at Refuge Pointe to begin recovering Trelane's scattered belongings.",al={"malin request follow up","next quest after malin","skuerto next quest"},it="next_step"},{q="Who is Archmage Trelane?",a="Archmage Trelane is a prominent Stromgarde mage and Archmage Malin's mentor. He was among the key defenders of the Arathi capital before the kingdom fell.",al={"archmage trelane","who is trelane","trelane stromgarde"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Archmage Malin need an adventurer for this task?",a="Archmage Malin is tied to his station in the Wizard's Sanctum of Stormwind, far to the south. While he already has agents stationed at Refuge Pointe in the Arathi Highlands, they have reported that the situation around the fallen city of Stromgarde is dire and requires reinforcements. An itinerant adventurer possesses the freedom to travel north quickly and the combat grit to venture into hostile, contested ruins that formal emissaries cannot easily reach.",al={"why send an adventurer","why me malin","why malin doesn't go himself"},it="why_me",add="5671e9ba"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage visiting the Wizard's Sanctum, you can help Malin preserve precious arcane research and relics tied to Arathor's mages.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can help strengthen Refuge Pointe, the Alliance's fragile remaining foothold in Arathi.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you can help recover the treasures of Stromgarde, the cradle of human civilization, and preserve the heritage of Arathor."},kw={"arathi highlands","malin","refuge pointe","skuerto","stormwind","stromgarde","tower of arathor","trelane","wizard's sanctum"},rel={"npc:archmage-malin","npc:skuerto","subzone:refuge-pointe","zone:arathi","subzone:tower-of-arathor"},m={start="Archmage Malin",["end"]="Skuerto",level="32",faction="Alliance",id=690},src={"Malin's Request"}}
E["quest:7497"] = {t="quest",n="The Journey Has Just Begun",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind, Major Mattingly recognizes the artisan who brought down Onyxia. He teaches the craft needed to make a cloak from her scales.",h="In Stormwind, Major Mattingly recognizes the artisan who brought down Onyxia.",sec={{t="A Rare Mastery",b="Few who helped bring down Onyxia can also work her hide. When an artisan with master leatherworking reports to Major Mattingly in Stormwind, the officer recognizes how much those skills matter in the battles ahead.",sp=0},{t="Protection Against the Black Dragonflight",b="Onyxia's death leaves the black dragonflight a threat. Major Mattingly teaches the artisan to treat and stitch her scales into an Onyxia Scale Cloak. The garment wards against the fiery breath of her brother, Nefarian, the Lord of Blackrock.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who offers the quest The Journey Has Just Begun?",a="Major Mattingly in Stormwind City offers this to Alliance heroes who fought in the campaign against Onyxia and have master leatherworking.",al={"who gives the journey has just begun","where to get journey has just begun","journey has just begun quest giver"},it="identity"},{q="What does this quest teach?",a="Major Mattingly teaches master leatherworkers how to make an Onyxia Scale Cloak from Onyxia's scales.",al={"what recipe do i get","onyxia cloak recipe","reward for journey has just begun"},it="for_you",gp=true},{q="Why is the Onyxia Scale Cloak necessary?",a="The cloak is treated to shield its wearer from the fiery breath of Nefarian, the Lord of Blackrock.",al={"why do i need onyxia cloak","what is onyxia scale cloak for","shadow flame protection"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is the Lord of Blackrock mentioned by Major Mattingly?",a="The Lord of Blackrock is Nefarian, a powerful black dragon and Onyxia's brother. He rules Blackrock Spire and continues the black dragonflight's schemes.",al={"who is lord of blackrock","who is nefarian","mattingly dragon warning"},it="target"},{q="Why must the hero be a leatherworker to receive this knowledge?",a="Working dragon scales without destroying their magical warding calls for the advanced skill of a master leatherworker.",al={"why leatherworking only","can anyone get this quest","leatherworker requirement"},it="why_me"},{q="Does Onyxia's death resolve the black dragon threat in Stormwind?",a="No. Onyxia is dead, but her brother Nefarian still commands Blackrock Mountain and plots against the Alliance and the mortal races.",al={"is stormwind safe now","onyxia dead what next","black dragonflight after onyxia"},sp=1,it="threat"},{q="Why does Major Mattingly offer you this knowledge?",a="Major Mattingly knows that slaying Onyxia was only the opening strike. The brood mother is dead, but her kin still menace Azeroth from the heights of Blackrock Mountain. To eliminate the remaining black dragonflight, champions must survive the searing flames of Nefarian himself. Mattingly shares this specialized technique so that Alliance heroes can fashion protective cloaks from Onyxia's scales and finish the war.",al={"why does mattingly teach you","major mattingly motive","mattingly reason"},it="motive",add="b42a6800"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance hero, you carry Stormwind's victory over Onyxia into the coming offensive against her brother Nefarian at Blackrock Mountain."},kw={"black dragonflight","blackrock","leatherworking","major mattingly","nefarian","onyxia","onyxia scale cloak","stormwind"},rel={"npc:major-mattingly","npc:onyxia","topic:black-dragonflight","quest:7781","topic:alliance"},m={start="Major Mattingly",faction="Alliance",id=7497},src={"The Journey Has Just Begun (Alliance)"}}
E["quest:7781"] = {t="quest",n="The Lord of Blackrock",z="stormwind",s="Nefarian's severed head is bound for Stormwind Keep after his defeat in Blackwing Lair. Highlord Bolvar Fordragon receives the trophy, a sign that the master of Blackrock Mountain has fallen. The victory is among the Alliance's greatest military triumphs in recent history.",h="Nefarian's severed head is bound for Stormwind Keep after his defeat in Blackwing Lair.",sec={{t="A Monument to Victory",b="Nefarian, brood-master of the Black Dragonflight and ruler of Upper Blackrock Spire, has long threatened the surrounding human kingdoms. His defeat ends his twisted experiments and schemes. Carrying his battle-scarred head back to Stormwind gives proof that the Lord of Blackrock has fallen to the Alliance's greatest heroes.",sp=0},{t="Audience at Stormwind Keep",b="Highlord Bolvar Fordragon governs the kingdom from the throne room of Stormwind Keep. The dragon's severed head shocks the royal court and commands reverence. With the kingdom strained by internal political strife and threats from beyond, the victory lifts morale and earns a place in Alliance history.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Lord of Blackrock quest about?",a="You claim Nefarian's severed head in Blackwing Lair and carry the trophy to Stormwind City. There you present it to Highlord Bolvar Fordragon on behalf of the kingdom.",al={"lord of blackrock quest","nefarian head quest alliance","head of nefarian stormwind"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Nefarian?",a="Nefarian is a great black dragon and the son of Deathwing. He rules from Blackwing Lair in Blackrock Mountain, commands the Blackrock orcs, and conducts sinister experiments to create the chromatic dragonflight.",al={"who is nefarian","lord of blackrock","nefarian lore"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Highlord Bolvar Fordragon?",a="Highlord Bolvar Fordragon is the paladin ruling Stormwind as regent while King Varian Wrynn is absent. He holds court in Stormwind Keep's throne room and watches over the young Prince Anduin Wrynn.",al={"bolvar fordragon","who is bolvar","highlord bolvar"},it="people"},{q="Why is this trophy brought to Stormwind Keep?",a="Nefarian's rule in Blackrock Mountain threatens the kingdom of Stormwind and the entire southern continent. Bringing his head to the kingdom's military leadership confirms the dragon's defeat and gives the realm a victory to rally around.",al={"why stormwind","why bring head to keep","why bolvar"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What happens after giving the head to Bolvar?",a="Highlord Bolvar Fordragon is astounded and declares the triumph will be recorded in history. The next stage of the event has the head mounted publicly for all Stormwind to see.",al={"what happens next","lord of blackrock part 2","nefarian head turn in"},it="next_step"},{q="Does turning in this head affect the whole city?",a="Yes. Nefarian's head is delivered to the capital and raised above the city gates, announcing the dragon's death to citizens and soldiers and strengthening Stormwind's defenders with resolve.",al={"city buff","rallying cry","head of nefarian buff"},gp=true},{q="Why does bringing the Head of Nefarian to Stormwind matter?",a="Nefarian was the black dragon masterminding the threats from Blackrock Spire, manipulating mortal kingdoms and forging monstrous armies right at Stormwind's doorstep. Delivering his severed head to Highlord Bolvar Fordragon is irrefutable proof that the brood's terror has been shattered, giving the Alliance a monumental victory to celebrate and display before the realm.",al={"why bring head of nefarian to stormwind","head of nefarian motive","why deliver nefarian head"},it="motive",add="150c64a2"},{q="Why must you carry the head to Stormwind instead of royal guards?",a="You and your companions fought your way through Blackwing Lair and struck down the dragon lord yourselves. Bearing the grisly prize back to Stormwind Keep is your right as the champions who vanquished him, ensuring Highlord Bolvar Fordragon receives the news firsthand from the heroes who actually slew the beast.",al={"why do i have to deliver nefarian's head","why not royal guards nefarian head","why me nefarian trophy"},it="why_me",add="7e2ee731"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, presenting Nefarian's head is a crowning military achievement. It crushes the dragonflight's schemes against human lands.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you know Blackrock Mountain has sent countless incursions and plots against Stormwind. Its master's defeat brings the realm long-sought retribution and relief."},kw={"blackrock mountain","blackwing lair","highlord bolvar fordragon","head of nefarian","lord of blackrock","nefarian","stormwind keep"},rel={"npc:bolvar-fordragon","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:alliance"},m={start="Head of Nefarian",["end"]="Highlord Bolvar Fordragon",faction="Alliance",id=7781},src={"The Lord of Blackrock (Alliance)"}}
E["quest:7782"] = {t="quest",n="The Lord of Blackrock",z="stormwind",s="At Stormwind's gates, the Alliance gathers to mark a victory over Blackrock. After you report to Grand Admiral Jes-Tereth in Stormwind Keep, the heroes go to the Valley of Heroes, where Field Marshal Stonebridge prepares a public commemoration for the city.",h="At Stormwind's gates, the Alliance gathers to mark a victory over Blackrock.",sec={{t="A City's Triumph",b="The Alliance's campaign against the Blackrock clan and the Black Dragonflight's brood reaches its public end. After Nefarian's severed head is presented inside Stormwind Keep, Highlord Bolvar Fordragon sends the champions across the city to the Valley of Heroes. Field Marshal Stonebridge waits there to receive the trophy and begin the celebrations.",sp=1},{t="Rallying the Alliance",b="Field Marshal Stonebridge raises Nefarian's severed head above the great arches at Stormwind's main entrance. The sight reaches the whole city, and the Rallying Cry of the Dragonslayer inspires the defenders, visiting dignitaries, and citizens. They know Deathwing's brood has suffered a crushing blow.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What happens when you complete this quest?",a="Field Marshal Stonebridge hangs Nefarian's severed head high on the stone gateway arch in the Valley of Heroes. The Rallying Cry of the Dragonslayer then strengthens friendly fighters and guards throughout Stormwind City.",al={"nefarian head quest turn in","what does stonebridge do","rallying cry trigger"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Who is Field Marshal Stonebridge?",a="Field Marshal Stonebridge is a senior officer in Stormwind's army, stationed in the Valley of Heroes near the city's entrance. She arranges public commemorations of military victories, including the display of defeated draconic foes' heads.",al={"stonebridge","field marshal stonebridge"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Highlord Bolvar Fordragon send you here?",a="After receiving word of Nefarian's defeat in the throne room, Highlord Bolvar Fordragon sends you to the city gates. There, the Alliance military can display the victory openly and raise morale across the capital.",al={"bolvar","why go to valley of heroes"},sp=1,it="motive"},{q="Does this turn-in affect the whole city?",a="Yes. When Stonebridge takes the trophy, a proclamation rings through Stormwind and the Rallying Cry of the Dragonslayer reaches everyone within the city borders.",al={"world buff nefarian","does stormwind get buff"},sp=1},{q="Where is the Valley of Heroes located?",a="The Valley of Heroes is the grand causeway leading into Stormwind City. Towering statues line it, honoring the heroes of the Second War who entered the Dark Portal.",al={"valley of heroes location","where is stonebridge"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who was the 'Lord of Blackrock'?",a="The black dragon Nefarian was the Lord of Blackrock. He is Deathwing's son and rules the upper spires of Blackrock Mountain.",al={"who is lord of blackrock","nefarian identity"},sp=2,it="target"},{q="Why does Bolvar send you instead of going himself?",a="You and your companions were the champions who braved the heights of Blackwing Lair and brought down Nefarian. As the victor, the honor of presenting the dragon's severed head to Stormwind's military leadership and triggering the citywide triumph belongs rightfully to you.",al={"why send me","why not bolvar","why must i deliver the head"},it="why_me",add="3a42f3f3"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Nefarian's head at the Valley of Heroes brings the Alliance races together. Citizens from Ironforge, Darnassus, and Gnomeregan see that the dark forces plaguing the Eastern Kingdoms can be broken.",["race:Human"]="For the kingdom of Stormwind, defeating Blackrock's master removes a grave draconic threat from its northern border.",["class:Warrior"]="The Rallying Cry of the Dragonslayer gives strength to fighters heading out to defend the realm."},kw={"blackrock","dragonslayer","nefarian","rallying cry","stonebridge","stormwind","valley of heroes"},rel={"subzone:valley-of-heroes","npc:field-marshal-stonebridge","zone:stormwind","quest:7781","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:alliance"},m={start="Highlord Bolvar Fordragon",["end"]="Field Marshal Stonebridge",faction="Alliance",id=7782},src={"The Lord of Blackrock (Alliance 2)"}}
E["quest:8311"] = {t="quest",n="Hallow's End Treats for Jesper!",z="stormwind",s="Jesper lies sick in Stormwind during Hallow's End, longing for the treats and fun beyond the orphanage. Too ill to go out, he asks Alliance adventurers to gather sweets for him.",h="Jesper lies sick in Stormwind during Hallow's End, longing for the treats and fun beyond the orphanage.",sec={{t="A Sheltered Child",b="Jesper stays in the orphanage in Stormwind's Cathedral Square, sick during Hallow's End. He cannot enjoy the childhood pleasure of gathering sweets across Azeroth, so he hopes passing adventurers will share the holiday spirit and collect treats for him.",sp=0},{t="Tricks for Treats Across the Alliance",b="To bring Jesper the sweets he hopes for, you travel beyond Elwynn Forest. You visit the innkeepers of Stormwind, Ironforge, and Darnassus, along with the gnome exile Talvash del Kissel. Each asks you to perform before giving you a treat. You cluck like a chicken, dance, flex, or chug like a train, earning regional sweets such as Stormwind Nougat and Gnomeregan Gumdrops.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Jesper?",a="Jesper is a young orphan in the Stormwind orphanage. During Hallow's End, he longs for holiday candy but is too sick to gather it himself.",al={"jesper stormwind","orphan jesper","who is jesper"},it="identity"},{q="Why can't Jesper go trick-or-treating himself?",a="Jesper is sick, so he must stay inside the orphanage while the rest of the city celebrates Hallow's End.",al={"why can't jesper leave","is jesper sick","jesper trick or treat"},it="why_me"},{q="Which treats does Jesper want?",a="Jesper asks for four regional sweets: Stormwind Nougat, Ironforge Mints, Darnassus Marzipan, and Gnomeregan Gumdrops.",al={"jesper treats","hallows end treats list","jesper candy needed"},it="purpose"},{q="Where do you obtain the Gnomeregan Gumdrop?",a="Talvash del Kissel gives out Gnomeregan Gumdrops while staying in Ironforge's Mystic Ward.",al={"gnomeregan gumdrop location","who gives gumdrop","talvash candy"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What tricks do the innkeepers make you perform?",a="The innkeepers ask you to flex in Stormwind, dance in Darnassus, cluck like a chicken in Ironforge, and make a train noise for Talvash.",al={"hallow's end tricks","innkeeper tricks","trick for treats alliance"},gp=true},{q="What does Jesper give you in return for the candy?",a="After receiving all four holiday candies, Jesper gives the traveler some pumpkin treats he has saved.",al={"jesper reward","treats for jesper completion"},it="for_you"},{q="Why does Jesper want the Hallow's End treats collected?",a="Jesper is a sick orphan confined to the Stormwind orphanage under the watchful eye of Matron Nightingale, leaving him unable to join the Hallow's End celebrations across the Alliance capitals. To experience the holiday like any other child, he hopes to taste the festive sweets unique to each allied capital, offering a trade of his own pumpkin treats so he does not miss out entirely.",al={"why does jesper want treats","jesper motivation candy","why hallows end treats jesper"},it="motive",add="103fae29"},{q="What is the Stormwind Nougat for?",a="Stormwind Nougat is a traditional local confection handed out by the Trade District's innkeeper during Hallow's End. It represents the human kingdom's contribution to the festival treats Jesper wants you to gather for him, earned by showing off your strength to the innkeeper.",al={"stormwind nougat use","what is stormwind nougat","who wants stormwind nougat"},it="item",add="423b280b"},{q="What is the Gnomeregan Gumdrop for?",a="The Gnomeregan Gumdrop is a signature sweet distributed on behalf of the exiled gnomes by Talvash del Kissel in Ironforge. It is one of the four unique sweets Jesper asks you to gather so he can taste the festive treats of all the Alliance peoples.",al={"gnomeregan gumdrop use","what is gnomeregan gumdrop","who wants gnomeregan gumdrop"},it="item",add="37e1df8a"},{q="What is the Ironforge Mint for?",a="The Ironforge Mint is a dwarven confectionery treat given away by the innkeeper of Ironforge during the autumn holiday. Jesper needs it as part of his complete four-city collection of Hallow's End candies, awarded after humoring the innkeeper with a spirited chicken impression.",al={"ironforge mint use","what is ironforge mint","who wants ironforge mint"},it="item",add="e8e502ad"},{q="What is the Darnassus Marzipan for?",a="Darnassus Marzipan is an exquisite night elf confection handed out by the innkeeper of Craftsmen's Terrace in Darnassus. It completes the assortment of regional Hallow's End delicacies that Jesper longs to enjoy while stuck in the Stormwind orphanage.",al={"darnassus marzipan use","what is darnassus marzipan","who wants darnassus marzipan"},it="item",add="61787ad3"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, this holiday brings distant capitals together. You travel from Stormwind's grand streets to Ironforge's mountain halls and Darnassus's boughs to bring joy to an orphaned child.",["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, your home is lost to troggs and radiation. In Ironforge, Talvash del Kissel keeps Gnomeregan Gumdrops part of the holiday."},kw={"darnassus","gumdrop","hallow's end","ironforge","jesper","marzipan","nightingale","nougat","stormwind","talvash","trick-or-treat"},rel={"npc:talvash-del-kissel","quest:8356","quest:8353","quest:8357","quest:8355","zone:ironforge","zone:darnassus"},m={start="Jesper",faction="Alliance",id=8311,ri={"Darnassus Marzipan","Gnomeregan Gumdrop"}},src={"Hallow's End Treats for Jesper!"}}
E["quest:8356"] = {t="quest",n="Flexing for Nougat",z="stormwind",s="During autumn's Hallow's End, you gather festive sweets for an orphan in Stormwind. Innkeeper Allison at the Gilded Rose asks you to flex before she gives you Stormwind Nougat.",h="During autumn's Hallow's End, you gather festive sweets for an orphan in Stormwind.",sec={{t="A Hallow's End Tradition",b="Hallow's End brings a lighter mood to Stormwind's streets. The holiday marks the turning of the seasons and wards off dark spirits. Common folk celebrate with disguises, revelry, and trick-or-treating. Alliance innkeepers join in, offering traditional sweets to those who perform a harmless trick.",sp=0},{t="Entertaining the Innkeeper",b="At the Gilded Rose in the Trade District, Innkeeper Allison asks for a show before handing out holiday candy, even when you're gathering sweets for Jesper, an orphaned boy. She comments playfully on your physique and asks you to flex your muscles. When you do, she gives you a piece of chewy Stormwind Nougat.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Innkeeper Allison make people flex?",a="Hallow's End trades tricks for treats, so Innkeeper Allison asks you to show off your muscles before giving you the sweet.",al={"why flex for nougat","what does allison want","flex emote why"},it="motive"},{q="Where does this quest take place?",a="You meet Innkeeper Allison at the Gilded Rose, in the heart of Stormwind's Trade District, where she tends the tavern counter.",al={"where is flexing for nougat","allison location","gilded rose innkeeper"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is the Stormwind Nougat meant for?",a="The nougat is for Jesper, an orphan boy staying in Stormwind. He hopes to taste traditional festival treats from each major Alliance city during Hallow's End.",al={"who gets the nougat","who wants stormwind nougat","jesper candy"},it="purpose"},{q="What is Stormwind Nougat?",a="Stormwind Nougat is a regional sweet Stormwind's innkeepers hand out during Hallow's End. Festival-goers know it as one of the human kingdom's signature treats.",al={"stormwind nougat lore","hallow's end nougat","stormwind candy"},it="item"},{q="Can Horde players obtain this treat from Allison?",a="No. Innkeeper Allison lives deep within Alliance-controlled Stormwind City and serves Alliance members. Horde adventurers perform their own festive tricks for innkeepers in their capital cities.",al={"can horde flex for nougat","horde version of nougat"},it="side",gp=true},{q="Does this quest happen year-round?",a="No. Innkeeper Allison offers this request only during Hallow's End, the seasonal festival when trick-or-treating customs fill the cities.",al={"when is flexing for nougat available","is this quest seasonal","hallows end timing"},gp=true}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, this playful exchange reflects Stormwind's lighter community spirit during Hallow's End and other seasonal festivals, bringing citizens and wandering heroes together for a laugh.",["race:Human"]="As a human in Stormwind, you know indulging children and trading tricks for treats is a cherished seasonal custom. It offers brief relief from the darker perils facing the kingdom.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you know bloody battlefields well. Flexing for an innkeeper is a harmless, if slightly undignified, show of strength."},kw={"flexing for nougat","gilded rose","hallow's end","innkeeper allison","jesper","stormwind city","stormwind nougat","trick or treat"},rel={"npc:innkeeper-allison","quest:8311","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Innkeeper Allison",faction="Alliance",id=8356},src={"Flexing for Nougat (Alliance)"}}
E["quest:8569"] = {t="quest",n="Past Efforts in Warsong Gulch",z="stormwind",s="In Warsong Gulch, soldiers fight for Ashenvale while commanders honor their sacrifices. Capital officers accept the Ribbon of Sacrifice as a sign of steadfast service, even when battles bring no clear victory.",h="In Warsong Gulch, soldiers fight for Ashenvale while commanders honor their sacrifices.",sec={{t="Honoring the Fallen and the Valiant",b="The Silverwing Sentinels and Warsong Outriders fight brutal skirmishes along Ashenvale’s southern border. Many battles end without a clear victory. Stormwind, Orgrimmar, and other capitals honor those who hold their ground despite the odds. The Ribbon of Sacrifice marks fighters who gave themselves to the struggle.",sp=0},{t="The War Effort at Home",b="Far from the front, Alliance Brigadier Generals and Horde Warbringers oversee their forces. Recruiters send new fighters to Warsong Gulch, while quartermasters and tacticians account for veterans returning from hard campaigns. By honoring courage in stalemate or defeat, their leaders help keep soldiers committed to holding Ashenvale.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this commendation?",a="The commendation honors fighters who gave everything in Warsong Gulch. Capital commanders accept the Ribbon of Sacrifice to recognize their perseverance and sustain morale.",al={"why do past efforts","past efforts purpose","what does past efforts mean"},it="purpose"},{q="Who accepts these tokens of sacrifice?",a="Alliance Brigadier Generals and Horde Warbringers accept the tokens in major cities, including Stormwind and Orgrimmar.",al={"who takes past efforts","where to turn in past efforts","who is the brigadier general"}},{q="Why does the military reward efforts that did not lead to victory?",a="Commanders know the fighting in Ashenvale’s forests takes a heavy toll. Honoring soldiers’ dedication shows that their sacrifice matters even when they do not win.",al={"why reward ribbon of sacrifice","why reward loss","heroic effort meaning"},it="motive"},{q="Where does the conflict of Warsong Gulch take place?",a="Warsong Gulch lies along Ashenvale’s southern border. The Warsong Outriders gather lumber there while the Silverwing Sentinels resist them.",al={"where is warsong gulch","warsong gulch location","what is warsong gulch"},it="place"},{q="Can members of both the Alliance and Horde undertake this?",a="Yes. Both factions honor returning soldiers through their military leaders in their respective capitals.",al={"is this both factions","horde or alliance past efforts","can horde turn this in"}},{q="What does the Ribbon of Sacrifice represent?",a="The Ribbon of Sacrifice honors fighters who endured fierce clashes in Warsong Gulch and remained willing to fight for their people.",al={"ribbon of sacrifice lore","what is ribbon of sacrifice","sacrifice ribbon"},it="item"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance soldier, presenting a ribbon to a Brigadier General affirms your pledge to defend the ancient forests and support your night elven allies against Warsong aggression.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, presenting a token to a Warbringer affirms that the blood spent securing wood and survival in Ashenvale was not wasted.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you know the brutal melee in the gulch. Discipline means fighting fiercely even when victory hangs in the balance."},kw={"ashenvale","brigadier general","orgrimmar","past efforts","ribbon of sacrifice","stormwind","warbringer","warsong gulch"},rel={"topic:alliance","topic:horde"},m={start="Alliance Brigadier General,  Horde Warbringer",level="1",faction="Both",id=8569,ri={"Warsong Gulch Ribbon of Sacrifice"}},src={"Past Efforts in Warsong Gulch"}}
E["quest:8646"] = {t="quest",n="Hammershout the Elder",z="stormwind",s="During the Lunar Festival, Hammershout the Elder appears in Stormwind's Park. Travelers honor the old races and receive a ceremonial token from him.",h="During the Lunar Festival, Hammershout the Elder appears in Stormwind's Park.",sec={{t="Honoring Ancient Blood",b="During the Lunar Festival, revered ancestor spirits appear across Azeroth with wisdom and blessings for travelers who pay their respects. Hammershout the Elder appears in Stormwind's Park district. His presence near the heart of human civilization recalls the ancient races who walked the land before today's kingdoms rose.",sp=0},{t="Tokens of Ancestral Reverence",b="Hammershout the Elder asks for no trial or oath, only acknowledgment of the past. He is relieved and grateful when people still honor the old races. In return, he gives travelers a ceremonial token, a sign of the bond between the living and the spirits who came before.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Elder Hammershout?",a="Hammershout the Elder is an ancestral spirit who appears during the Lunar Festival. He represents Azeroth's ancient lineages and offers blessings and tokens in Stormwind to those who honor him.",al={"hammershout","who is hammershout","elder hammershout identity"}},{q="Where can Elder Hammershout be found?",a="Hammershout the Elder appears in Stormwind's Park district during the Lunar Festival.",al={"hammershout location","where is hammershout","hammershout elwynn"}},{q="Why does Elder Hammershout mention the 'olden races'?",a="His words reflect the Lunar Festival's celebration of antiquity and ancestor worship. The festival honors the ancient peoples and traditions that shaped Azeroth before modern settlements rose.",al={"olden races meaning","what does hammershout mean"}},{q="What token does Elder Hammershout offer?",a="Hammershout the Elder offers a Coin of Ancestry, a ceremonial token given by the Lunar Festival spirits to travelers who seek out elders and pay their respects.",al={"hammershout reward","hammershout token","what does he give"}},{q="Can Horde adventurers speak with Elder Hammershout?",a="Yes. Horde travelers can speak with Hammershout the Elder, though they must tread carefully in Stormwind, the Alliance capital.",al={"can horde talk to hammershout","hammershout horde"}},{q="Is this encounter tied to an active holiday?",a="Hammershout the Elder appears during the annual Lunar Festival, granting blessings before fading back to the spirit realm.",al={"is hammershout always there","lunar festival elder"}}},ang={["race:Human"]="In Stormwind's Park, Hammershout the Elder reminds you to respect Azeroth's history, which reaches back before the modern human kingdom.",["faction:Alliance"]="When you visit Stormwind's Park, Hammershout the Elder recalls reverence, peace, and the world's shared ancestral past.",["faction:Horde"]="To reach Hammershout the Elder, you must enter Stormwind and make your way to the Park, a daring journey for a Horde pilgrim."},kw={"ancestor","elder hammershout","the park","hammershout","lunar festival","olden races","stormwind"},rel={"zone:stormwind","subzone:park"},m={id=8646},src={"Hammershout the Elder"}}
E["quest:9260"] = {t="quest",n="Investigate the Scourge of Stormwind",z="stormwind",s="Scourge forces press against Stormwind, with necropolises looming beyond its walls. Lieutenant Orrin calls defenders to strike their camps, gather Necrotic Stones, and study the runes there.",h="Scourge forces press against Stormwind, with necropolises looming beyond its walls.",sec={{t="Undead at the Capital's Threshold",b="Scourge forces have reached the outskirts of Stormwind City. Necropolises float overhead as undead and cultists take hold near the kingdom’s greatest bastion. Lieutenant Orrin gathers defenders outside the city to drive them back before they threaten the capital.",sp=0},{t="The Whispering Runes",b="Glowing runes mark the dirt around Scourge camps, and their purpose remains unclear. The circles crackle with magic like that of the necropolises and carry eerie whispers. Lieutenant Orrin can only guess who, if anyone, hears those unnatural voices.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Lieutenant Orrin?",a="Lieutenant Orrin is an officer coordinating Stormwind’s defenses. He works with the Argent Dawn and organizes local fighters to gather intelligence and break up Scourge footholds near the city.",al={"orrin","lieutenant orrin","who gives this quest"},it="identity"},{q="Why is the Scourge attacking Stormwind?",a="The Lich King has sent necropolises and invasion forces across Azeroth to spread terror and swell the ranks of the undead. Stormwind is a major stronghold of the living, making it a target for the Scourge.",al={"why scourge here","scourge invasion stormwind","why attack stormwind"},it="threat"},{q="What are the glowing runic circles?",a="The Scourge has placed glowing runic circles near its camps. They pulse with dark magic and carry unnatural whispers, though their purpose is not known.",al={"runic circles","glowing runes","what do circles do"},it="place"},{q="What are Dim Necrotic Stones?",a="Dim Necrotic Stones are magical objects carried by lesser Scourge forces. They hold lingering necrotic energy and interest the Argent Dawn.",al={"dim necrotic stone","necrotic stones","what are necrotic stones"},it="item"},{q="What role does the Argent Dawn play in this mission?",a="The Argent Dawn is an independent order that fights the Scourge wherever it appears. Lieutenant Orrin works with the order to secure intelligence and stones for its war against the Lich King’s armies.",al={"argent dawn","argent dawn connection"},it="allies"},{q="Are the runic circles dangerous to approach?",a="The circles give off unsettling energy and discordant whispers. Careful scouts can approach them and learn about Scourge communications without losing their sanity.",al={"are runes safe","whispers in runes"},it="danger"},{q="Why does Lieutenant Orrin want this investigated?",a="The Lich King has unleashed his undead forces directly outside Stormwind's gates beneath an ominous hovering necropolis. Lieutenant Orrin knows the city cannot afford to sit idly by while invaders mass at the doorstep. He urgently needs to understand the strange magic behind their glowing runic circles and thin out their ranks before the undead establish a permanent foothold right outside the kingdom's walls.",al={"why does orrin want this done","lieutenant orrin motive","why investigate the scourge"},it="motive",add="c2a78be7"},{q="Who are you being sent against outside Stormwind?",a="You are fighting the invading forces of the Scourge gathered beneath the necropolis just outside the city. These undead shock troops and aberrations have set up an encampment at Stormwind's gates to sow chaos and threaten the kingdom on behalf of the Lich King.",al={"who am i fighting","who are the enemies outside stormwind","what scourge are outside"},it="target",add="9cb0511c"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, defending Stormwind’s gates is a matter of survival. The Scourge has reached even this southern stronghold.",["class:Paladin"]="As a Paladin, you face the Scourge outside Stormwind and can bring holy wrath against its runes while protecting the kingdom’s people.",["class:Priest"]="As a Priest, you can study the twisted whispers in the runes and learn about the shadow magic binding the Scourge’s frontline forces."},kw={"argent dawn","invasion","lich king","lieutenant orrin","necropolis","necrotic stones","runic circles","scourge","stormwind"},rel={"npc:lieutenant-orrin","topic:scourge","topic:argent-dawn","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:lich-king"},m={start="Lieutenant Orrin",level="6",faction="Alliance",id=9260},src={"Investigate the Scourge of Stormwind"}}
E["quest:93963"] = {t="quest",n="Exploring the Alliance",z="stormwind",s="You begin Exploring the Alliance in Stormwind Keep, then travel to meet the rulers of Ironforge and Darnassus. Their lands show the breadth of the Alliance before you turn toward Westfall.",h="You begin Exploring the Alliance in Stormwind Keep, then travel to meet the rulers of Ironforge and Darnassus.",sec={{t="A Tour of Allied Lands",b="Randal Emerson, an attendant in Stormwind Keep’s southern antechamber, sends you beyond the human capital. You are newly arrived on Azeroth, and the Alliance invites you to see its allied peoples firsthand. The journey takes you beyond the keep to learn the distinct cultures, traditions, and strength of those who stand with Stormwind.",sp=0},{t="Audiences with the High Seats",b="Your travels cross land and sea to the leaders of the Alliance. In Ironforge, you meet King Magni Bronzebeard in the mountain halls, and High Tinker Gelbin Mekkatorque, leader of the displaced gnomes. In Darnassus, atop Teldrassil, you meet High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind. Their cities and peoples reveal the ties among humans, dwarves, gnomes, and night elves.",sp=0},{t="A World in Need of Aid",b="After the long journey, you return to Stormwind. Understanding Azeroth helps you aid your own people, while your order prepares to establish itself in Dalaran. For now, the troubled territories near the capital need help, beginning with Westfall’s struggling farmlands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the quest Exploring the Alliance?",a="You travel across Azeroth to meet the leaders of the Alliance’s major seats of power. The journey brings you before the rulers of Ironforge and Darnassus, and High Tinker Gelbin Mekkatorque, leader of the gnomes in exile.",al={"exploring the alliance quest","what is this quest"}},{q="Who is Randal Emerson?",a="Randal Emerson is an attendant in Stormwind Keep’s southern antechamber. He gives travelers directions for reaching the other capital cities.",al={"randal emerson","who gives directions"}},{q="Which leaders must be visited during this journey?",a="You visit King Magni Bronzebeard in Ironforge, High Tinker Gelbin Mekkatorque, and High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind in Darnassus. Each leads a core race and seat of authority within the Alliance.",al={"leaders visited","who do i talk to"}},{q="Why is Dalaran mentioned upon completing the quest?",a="Your order is preparing to establish its presence in Dalaran. While those arrangements are underway, you are encouraged to learn about Azeroth and aid nearby territories.",al={"why dalaran mentioned","order in dalaran"}},{q="Where does the path lead after completing this journey?",a="After returning to Stormwind Keep, you head toward the countryside near the capital, specifically Westfall. Its troubled communities urgently need capable defenders.",al={"where to go next","after exploring the alliance"}},{q="Why is the adventurer treated as a guest of the Alliance?",a="You are treated as an outsider newly arrived on Azeroth, and you are expected to understand the wider world so you can protect and aid your own people. The journey introduces you to the Alliance’s varied cultures.",al={"guest of the alliance","why guest"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance newcomer, you visit its principal strongholds and meet the leaders who hold the pact together.",["race:Skyborne"]="As a Skyborne guest on Azeroth, you are urged to learn about the allied nations that shelter you while your order prepares to establish itself in Dalaran."},kw={"dalaran","darnassus","exploring the alliance","high tinker mekkatorque","ironforge","magni bronzebeard","randal emerson","stormwind keep","tyrande whisperwind","westfall"},rel={"subzone:stormwind-keep","topic:alliance","zone:ironforge","zone:darnassus","npc:magni-bronzebeard","npc:tyrande-whisperwind","zone:westfall","subzone:dalaran"},m={id=93963},src={"In-game quest text: Exploring the Alliance"},fv=true}
E["quest:95065"] = {t="quest",n="Fishin' Time",z="stormwind",s="At Stormwind harbor, Gilbert Gray's bait runs low as the fish begin to bite. He asks passersby to fetch supplies from a shop along the city's canals.",h="At Stormwind harbor, Gilbert Gray's bait runs low as the fish begin to bite.",sec={{t="A Day by the Water",b="Gilbert Gray spends quiet days fishing at the edge of Stormwind harbor. He watches his bobber on the water, but a good run of biting fish can empty his bait tin. With his supplies gone and the fish still biting, the elderly angler asks passersby to bring him more.",sp=0},{t="Supplies Along the Canals",b="Catherine Leland runs a tackle shop along the stone canals, just west of the Trade District. She supplies fishermen across Stormwind with lures and bait, including regulars like Gilbert Gray.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Gilbert Gray?",a="Gilbert Gray is an elderly fisherman at Stormwind harbor. He spends his days casting into the sea and asks passersby to fetch bait and lures when his supplies run low.",al={"gilbert gray","old gray","who gives this quest"}},{q="Who is Catherine Leland?",a="Catherine Leland runs a fishing supply shop along the city canals, just west of the Trade District. She sells fishing equipment and bait to Stormwind's anglers.",al={"catherine leland","fishing vendor stormwind","leland stormwind"}},{q="Where does Gilbert Gray fish?",a="Gilbert Gray fishes at Stormwind harbor, where he enjoys the open view of the sea.",al={"gilbert gray location","where is gilbert gray","harbor fisherman"}},{q="What supplies does Gilbert Gray need?",a="Gilbert Gray needs nightcrawlers for bait and a shiny bauble for a lure. Catherine Leland sells both along the canals.",al={"quest items fishin time","what bait does gray want"}},{q="Why doesn't Gilbert Gray fetch the supplies himself?",a="The fish are biting, and Gilbert Gray does not want to leave his spot or miss a good catch by going back into the city for supplies.",al={"why cant gray buy bait","why does gray need help"}},{q="Where along the canals is Catherine Leland's shop located?",a="Catherine Leland's shop is along the canals just west of the Trade District, beside the stone walkways over the city's waterways.",al={"catherine leland location","where is lelands shop","trade district canals"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance citizen, helping Gilbert Gray with an everyday need supports life and morale across Stormwind.",["race:Human"]="As a human who calls Stormwind home, helping an elder enjoy a quiet afternoon of fishing offers a break from kingdom politics."},kw={"canals","catherine leland","fishin time","gilbert gray","nightcrawlers","shiny bauble","stormwind harbor","trade district"},rel={"subzone:canals-stormwind-city","subzone:trade-district","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={level="12",id=95065},src={"In-game quest text: Fishin' Time"},fv=true}
E["quest:95161"] = {t="quest",n="Remember That I Love You",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind, a blood-stained letter is bound for Jeremy Heartweaver. He has left the orphanage for a new home with Avette Fellwood in Duskwood.",h="In Stormwind, a blood-stained letter is bound for Jeremy Heartweaver.",sec={{t="A Message for an Orphan",b="Children at the Stormwind Orphanage have lost their families to war, hardship, and the chaos gripping the kingdom. Jeremy Heartweaver was one of them until Avette Fellwood adopted him. She took him to live in Duskwood, where the woods are gloomy and life brings peril and hard labor. The orphanage caretakers believed a home with a family offered him more than remaining in the city.",sp=0},{t="A Grim Token",b="A Blood-Stained Letter is meant for Jeremy, in Avette Fellwood's care. The trail leads south past Elwynn Forest's safety and into Duskwood's shadow. What tragedy followed Jeremy beyond Stormwind's gates, and why does the letter bear such a grim mark?",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Jeremy Heartweaver?",a="Jeremy Heartweaver is a young boy who was raised at the Stormwind Orphanage. Avette Fellwood recently adopted him, and he now lives and works in Duskwood.",al={"jeremy","who is jeremy","orphan jeremy"}},{q="Who is Avette Fellwood?",a="Avette Fellwood is Jeremy's adoptive mother and lives in Duskwood. The matrons of Stormwind regard her as a sweet woman who likely took Jeremy in to gain another pair of hands for her daily labor.",al={"avette","who is avette","adoptive mother"}},{q="What is the Blood-Stained Letter?",a="The Blood-Stained Letter is meant for Jeremy Heartweaver and goes into the hands of his adoptive guardian, Avette Fellwood. It carries echoes of violence or tragedy.",al={"blood-stained letter","the letter","what is the letter"}},{q="Where do I find Avette Fellwood?",a="Avette Fellwood lives in Duskwood, the dark forest directly south of Elwynn Forest, across the river.",al={"avette fellwood location","where is avette","find avette"}},{q="Why was Jeremy sent to Duskwood?",a="Jeremy was adopted from the Stormwind Orphanage. His caretakers believed a family and honest labor in dangerous Duskwood were better than life as an orphan in the orphanage.",al={"why duskwood","why did jeremy leave stormwind","orphanage duskwood"}},{q="Which faction can take this quest?",a="Only the Alliance can take this assignment. It begins in Stormwind, the human capital, and leads into Alliance-held Duskwood.",al={"is this alliance","alliance only","horde quest"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, tokens of fallen or vanished kin carried to adopted orphans speak to the personal costs of the kingdom's turbulent state.",["race:Human"]="As a human of Stormwind, you cross from the realm's relatively safe heart to Duskwood's haunted, forgotten settlements."},kw={"avette fellwood","blood-stained letter","duskwood","jeremy heartweaver","remember that i love you","stormwind","stormwind orphanage"},rel={"zone:duskwood"},m={level="22",id=95161},src={"In-game quest text: Remember That I Love You"},fv=true}
E["quest:97894"] = {t="quest",n="Business in Auberdine",z="stormwind",s="Borgus Steelhand seeks news of his brother Gorbold in Auberdine. The dwarven merchant asks travelers sailing west to check on Gorbold, who recently began trading in the night elven port. Their route links Stormwind Harbor with the shores of northern Kalimdor.",h="Borgus Steelhand seeks news of his brother Gorbold in Auberdine.",sec={{t="A Dwarf Far from Home",b="Borgus Steelhand trusts his family's name among traders. His brother, Gorbold Steelhand, crossed the Great Sea recently to work a merchant stall in Auberdine. Gorbold hoped to profit by supplying ships that call at Darkshore. Weeks have passed without a word, and Borgus worries about how his brother fares so far from Ironforge and Stormwind.",sp=0},{t="The Harbor Passage",b="Travel from the Eastern Kingdoms to Kalimdor once meant a winding passage through Menethil Harbor or neutral goblin ports such as Booty Bay. Borgus directs travelers to a vessel at the southern-most dock of Stormwind Harbor. It sails directly to Auberdine's long wooden piers.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Borgus Steelhand?",a="Borgus Steelhand is a dwarven merchant in Stormwind. He trusts his family's reputation for fair trading and seeks travelers to carry word to his brother Gorbold across the sea.",al={"borgus steelhand","who gives business in auberdine","borgus"}},{q="Where is Gorbold Steelhand located?",a="Gorbold Steelhand is in Auberdine, the main port settlement in Darkshore on Kalimdor's northwest coast. He works at a merchant stall serving arriving ships.",al={"where is gorbold","find gorbold steelhand","gorbold location"}},{q="How do you reach Auberdine from Stormwind?",a="A ship sails from the southern-most pier in Stormwind Harbor across the Great Sea to Auberdine's docks in Darkshore.",al={"boat to auberdine","how to get to darkshore from stormwind","stormwind to auberdine boat"}},{q="Why is Borgus worried about his brother?",a="Gorbold left weeks ago to join a merchant stall in Auberdine, hoping to profit by supplying ships. He has sent no word home, so Borgus asks travelers to find out how he fares.",al={"why check on gorbold","what happened to gorbold"}},{q="What kind of settlement is Auberdine?",a="Auberdine is a coastal settlement in Darkshore, built and inhabited mainly by night elves. It is the Alliance's main shipping hub and ferry crossing between northern Kalimdor and Teldrassil.",al={"what is auberdine","auberdine town"}},{q="What is the Steelhand family known for?",a="The Steelhand family is known for trade and for claiming to offer fair deals to travelers and dockworkers.",al={"steelhand family","steelhands"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you can find dwarven merchants such as the Steelhands trading far beyond the Khaz Modan mountains, even in the night elves' quiet, shadowed settlements.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you can sail directly between Stormwind Harbor and Auberdine, linking the human kingdom with the Kaldorei lands of northern Kalimdor."},kw={"auberdine","borgus steelhand","business in auberdine","darkshore","gorbold steelhand","merchant","steelhand","stormwind harbor"},rel={"subzone:auberdine","npc:gorbold-steelhand","zone:darkshore","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={level="17",id=97894},src={"In-game quest text: Business in Auberdine"},fv=true}
E["quest:97914"] = {t="quest",n="Expanding Horizons",z="stormwind",s="Thundris Windweaver sends word from Auberdine across the Great Sea to Stormwind. The letter asks City Architect Baros Alexston to recognize Auberdine's work and its home.",h="Thundris Windweaver sends word from Auberdine across the Great Sea to Stormwind.",sec={{t="Bridging Two Hemispheres",b="Auberdine now links Darkshore to Stormwind by sea. Night elves once kept to Kalimdor's forests, apart from the Eastern Kingdoms, but after the Third War they joined the Grand Alliance. The new passage gives the northern port a direct tie to the human kingdom. Local leaders want the shipping route secured and Auberdine connected to the wider Alliance. Ameth'Aran and Bashal'Aran, ruined cities nearby, have long drawn more notice than the living coastal settlement.",sp=0},{t="A Missive to the City Architect",b="The letter crossing the Great Sea is addressed to Baros Alexston, Stormwind's City Architect. He oversees construction and infrastructure in the human capital, including public works and logistics. Thundris Windweaver wants Auberdine's work recognized and its home made known.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends you on this quest?",a="Thundris Windweaver, an influential night elf in Auberdine, asks you to carry the letter. He feels the settlement is overlooked by Darnassus and by allies across the ocean, and seeks a formal link with the human kingdom.",al={"quest giver expanding horizons","who gives expanding horizons","thundris quest"}},{q="Who is Baros Alexston?",a="Baros Alexston is Stormwind's City Architect. He is a respected civic planner who knew Edwin VanCleef when they were younger, and oversees construction and structural administration throughout the capital.",al={"baros alexston lore","who is baros","city architect stormwind"}},{q="Why is Auberdine reaching out to Stormwind?",a="Auberdine wants its harbor recognized as a gateway for supplies, commerce, and Alliance travel. Local leaders hope the new sea routes between Darkshore and the Eastern Kingdoms will strengthen economic and logistical ties with the human kingdom.",al={"why send letter to stormwind","auberdine stormwind connection","why contact humans"}},{q="How does travel work between Auberdine and Stormwind?",a="A vessel now sails from Auberdine across the Great Sea to Stormwind Harbor, bringing supplies and life to Auberdine's shores.",al={"boat to stormwind","how to get to stormwind from auberdine"}},{q="What are Ameth'Aran and Bashal'Aran?",a="Ameth'Aran and Bashal'Aran were prosperous highborne cities in ancient Darkshore. The Great Sundering shattered the continent ten thousand years ago, and the cities now lie in haunted ruins, more prominent in kaldorei history than living villages like Auberdine.",al={"ameth aran lore","bashal aran","ancient darkshore cities"}},{q="Why deliver this to an architect instead of King Anduin or Bolvar?",a="Thundris Windweaver gives no reason for his choice. He asks you to take the letter to Baros Alexston, Stormwind's City Architect, so Auberdine's work can be recognized.",al={"why baros alexston","why not bolvar","why not highlord bolvar"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the kaldorei, opening sea routes to the Eastern Kingdoms breaks with ten thousand years of seclusion and binds your people to human civilization.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you see the reach of the rebuilt kingdom grow when you return to Stormwind carrying a kaldorei settlement's seal.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you see the work needed to unite peoples across two continents into one faction."},kw={"ameth'aran","auberdine","baros alexston","bashal'aran","darkshore","darnassus","expanding horizons","harbor","stormwind","thundris windweaver"},rel={"npc:baros-alexston","subzone:auberdine","topic:stormwind-kingdom","zone:darnassus","subzone:ameth-aran","quest:954","topic:human"},m={level="17",id=97914},src={"In-game quest text: Expanding Horizons"},fv=true}
E["quest:98191"] = {t="quest",n="A Friend of the Family",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind, A Friend of the Family carries a rare likeness of King Terenas to the Cathedral of Light. Highlord Bolvar Fordragon entrusts the Menethil Statuette to an adventurer for Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker, who will keep it safe.",h="In Stormwind, A Friend of the Family carries a rare likeness of King Terenas to the Cathedral of Light.",sec={{t="A Rare Remembrance",b="King Terenas Menethil II helped shape the Grand Alliance during the Second War and lived with deep personal devotion. Though he held great standing among humanity's kingdoms, he was humble and disliked monuments made in his honor. Few likenesses were commissioned, and fewer survived Lordaeron's ruin and the Scourge's devastation.",sp=0},{t="Touched by Grace",b="Highlord Bolvar Fordragon sees more than fine carving in the surviving Menethil Statuette. The Holy Light has begun to gather within it, giving the figure a quiet spiritual presence. Bolvar decides Stormwind Keep is no place for such a sacred piece. He sends it across the city to the Cathedral of Light, into the care of Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker, who trains paladins.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was King Terenas Menethil II?",a="King Terenas Menethil II ruled the Kingdom of Lordaeron and was beloved by its people. During the Second War, he brought the human kingdoms together with the dwarves, gnomes, and high elves to form the Grand Alliance, which defeated the Orcish Horde. He was slain when his realm fell.",al={"terenas menethil","who is terenas","king of lordaeron"},it="people"},{q="Why are statues of King Terenas so rare?",a="King Terenas was humble and disliked grand monuments made in his honor. Few likenesses were carved, and almost none survived the Scourge's destruction of Lordaeron.",al={"why are there few statues","terenas statuette rarity","why so few memorials"},it="item"},{q="Why is the Menethil Statuette glowing with the Light?",a="Bolvar notices that the Light has gathered in the statuette. He calls Terenas a good and devout man, but gives no reason why this likeness holds holy power.",al={"why does statuette have light","holy statuette","coalescing light"},it="power"},{q="Who is Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker?",a="Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker is a veteran human paladin of the Knights of the Silver Hand and a master at the Cathedral of Light. He is stationed in Cathedral Square, where he trains aspiring paladins and oversees holy matters for Stormwind's faithful.",al={"who is shadowbreaker","lord grayson role"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Highlord Bolvar send the statuette to the Cathedral?",a="Bolvar honors Terenas as the father of the Alliance and believes the statuette belongs in the Cathedral of Light. It has gathered holy power, and he entrusts it to the holy orders rather than keeping it among the court officials in Stormwind Keep.",al={"why send to cathedral","why not keep in stormwind keep"},it="motive"},{q="Where is the Cathedral of Light located?",a="The Cathedral of Light dominates Cathedral Square in the heart of Stormwind City, between the Dwarven District, Trade District, and Mage Quarter. It is the main sanctuary and center of worship for the Church of the Holy Light in the southern kingdoms.",al={"where is cathedral of light","cathedral square location"},it="place",gp=true}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you safeguard a relic of King Terenas that bears the Light's touch. It honors the ruler who first sanctioned the founding of the Knights of the Silver Hand.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you can see how holy power gathered in a simple carved likeness. It speaks to Lordaeron's faithful legacy, even after the kingdom's lands were destroyed.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you remember King Terenas Menethil II as a founding pillar of the Alliance of Lordaeron. Any artifact tied to him is a treasured sign of unity and remembrance."},kw={"bolvar","cathedral","lordaeron","menethil","shadowbreaker","statuette","stormwind","terenas"},rel={"item:menethil-statuette","quest:98190","npc:lord-grayson-shadowbreaker","subzone:cathedral-of-light","topic:lordaeron","topic:light","topic:alliance"},m={start="Highlord Bolvar Fordragon",["end"]="Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker",level="25",faction="Alliance",id=98191},src={"A Friend of the Family (2)"},fv=true}
E["subzone:canals-stormwind-city"] = {t="subzone",n="Canals (Stormwind City)",z="stormwind",s="Stormwind's Canals wind between the city's districts, where walkers and anglers share the waterside paths.",h="Stormwind's Canals wind between the city's districts, where walkers and anglers share the waterside paths.",sec={{t="Arteries of the Capital",b="You can follow the Canals between Stormwind's districts, from the Trade District's markets to Old Town's aged alleys, the cathedral gardens, and the Dwarven District. Stone bridges, archways, and waterside walks pass the Gallina Winery, tailor shops, and quiet homes. Merchants and fishermen use the waterways, while the fortified Stockade entrance lies beneath the streets, holding Stormwind's most dangerous criminals and rebels.",sp=0},{t="A Gruesome History and Lurking Shadows",b="Stormwind's Canals were left in ruins when the Horde sacked the city during the First War. The waterways were restored as the capital rose again after the Second War. They are clean and repaired now, though rumors speak of a massive albino crocolisk beneath the docks.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What happened to the canals during the First War?",a="The Horde sacked Stormwind during the First War, leaving the city and its waterways in ruins. The Canals were restored when the capital was rebuilt after the Second War.",al={"canal history","canals first war","stormwind sack canals"},it="history"},{q="Is there really a monster in the Stormwind canals?",a="No one can say for certain. Rumors tell of a massive white crocolisk lurking in the waterways, though guards and residents often dismiss the tales as tavern gossip. Reports continue, and adventurers are warned not to fall in.",al={"stormwind crocodile","canal alligator","sewer beast","white crocolisk"},it="threat"},{q="Where is the entrance to the Stockade located?",a="The Stockade entrance lies along the northernmost stretch of the canal around the Mage Quarter, guarded by the Stormwind City Guard.",al={"where is stockade","stockade entrance","how to get to stockade"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Can players swim through the canals to travel around Stormwind?",a="You can swim through the Canals, then find stone stairs or docks along the waterside paths to climb back to the street.",al={"swimming in canals","travel by water stormwind","water route stormwind"},gp=true},{q="What are the Canals?",a="The Canals are a sprawling network of waterways and paved stone embankments that weave throughout Stormwind City, dividing its major districts. While primarily serving as waterways and thoroughfares, their walkways and docks are lined with small shops, tailoring establishments, and fishing spots. The canals also provide access to the secure entrance of the Stormwind Stockade.",al={"what are the canals","stormwind canals lore","canal district"},it="place",add="8ec6c1e0"},{q="Are the Canals dangerous?",a="For the most part, the Canals are safe and well-traveled by city residents, shopkeepers, and local anglers. However, you should still watch your step near the water. Rumors persist among the locals of a monstrous albino crocolisk lurking beneath the surface, posing a real threat to anyone unwary enough to fall in.",al={"is it safe in the canals","canal danger","canals dangerous"},it="danger",add="74e84108"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="As an aspiring cook, you can fish along the quiet canal banks without leaving the safety of the capital's walls.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can see how the Canals were restored after the First War's ruins, as Stormwind became a working, picturesque city."},kw={"canal district","canals","crocolisk","gallina","sewers","stockade","stormwind","waterways"},rel={"zone:stormwind","zone:stockade","subzone:trade-district","subzone:old-town","subzone:dwarven-district","topic:first-war","topic:alliance-of-lordaeron","quest:66"},src={"Canals (Stormwind City)"}}
E["subzone:cathedral-of-light"] = {t="subzone",n="Cathedral of Light",z="stormwind",s="The Cathedral of Light rises over Cathedral Square as Stormwind's chief sanctuary of the Church of the Holy Light. It is the spiritual heart of the city and the center of human priesthood and the Knights of the Silver Hand.",h="The Cathedral of Light rises over Cathedral Square as Stormwind's chief sanctuary of the Church of the Holy...",sec={{t="Sanctuary of the Faithful",b="Archbishop Benedictus leads the faithful from the Cathedral of Light, rebuilt after the First War's devastation. Archbishop Alonsus Faol and Bishop Benedictus guided its restoration, and its towering form remains a beacon of resilience. After the Scourge took Lordaeron during the Third War, the Church moved its seat south to Stormwind. From this great hall, Benedictus gives spiritual guidance to the Alliance.",sp=0},{t="Halls of Devotion and Arms",b="The Cathedral of Light is both a place of prayer and healing and the main headquarters of the Knights of the Silver Hand in the southern kingdoms. Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker and Duthorian Rall train promising squires through the sacred trials of the Tome of Valor and the Tome of Divinity. High Priestess Laurena guides devout acolytes in the deepest tenets of the Light, preparing holy champions to defend the realm from the growing threats of the Defias Brotherhood and the Scourge.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who leads the Church inside the cathedral?",a="Archbishop Benedictus leads the Church of the Holy Light from Stormwind. After Lordaeron fell and Archbishop Alonsus Faol died, Benedictus took spiritual leadership of the reformed Church.",al={"cathedral leader","who is the archbishop","who leads the church"},it="residents"},{q="What is the cathedral's connection to the paladins?",a="The Cathedral of Light is the Knights of the Silver Hand's headquarters in Stormwind. Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker and Duthorian Rall instruct new squires, give them sacred tomes, and direct crusaders against the realm's enemies.",al={"silver hand stormwind","paladin order stormwind","why are paladins here"}},{q="What lies beneath the cathedral floor?",a="The cathedral's catacombs lie beneath the main sanctuary. They hold the remains of honored heroes, priests, and paladins.",al={"cathedral basement","cathedral catacombs","what is under the cathedral"}},{q="What is the Cathedral of Light?",a="The Cathedral of Light is the grand spiritual heart of the Church of the Holy Light and the Alliance. Located in Stormwind's Cathedral Square, it serves as a holy sanctuary for prayer, meditation, and healing. Promising priests and paladins of the Knights of the Silver Hand travel from across the realm to study under its vaulted roofs, while beneath its cobalt-inlaid stone halls rest the honored dead.",al={"what is cathedral of light","cathedral of light purpose","stormwind cathedral"},it="place",add="2c1d9b08"},{q="What happened to the Cathedral of Light in the past?",a="During the First War, the original cathedral was heavily damaged by the Old Horde. Following the Second War, Archbishop Alonsus Faol and his then-apprentice Benedictus oversaw its complete reconstruction. With the fall of Lordaeron in the Third War, it rose to become the primary seat of the faith.",al={"cathedral of light history","stormwind cathedral history","what happened at cathedral of light"},it="history",add="e612604f"},{q="Is the Cathedral of Light dangerous?",a="No. The Cathedral of Light is a peaceful sanctuary within the guarded heart of Stormwind City. It is a place dedicated to contemplation, worship, and the healing arts. Unless you are an enemy of the Alliance or an intruder fleeing the city guard, you will find only safety, mentors, and fellow practitioners of the Light within its halls.",al={"is cathedral of light dangerous","is stormwind cathedral safe","cathedral of light danger"},it="danger",add="b98edca3"}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you find your order's chief hall in Stormwind's Cathedral of Light, where Duthorian Rall and Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker guide you through the sacred trials of the Tomes of Valor and Divinity.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you find the Church of the Holy Light's chief seat in the southern kingdoms at the Cathedral of Light, where High Priestess Laurena and Archbishop Benedictus guide your devotion and sacred healing."},kw={"benedictus","cathedral of light","cathedral square","duthorian rall","holy light","laurena","shadowbreaker","silver hand","stormwind"},rel={"subzone:cathedral-square","topic:church-of-the-holy-light","topic:knights-of-the-silver-hand","npc:archbishop-benedictus","npc:lord-grayson-shadowbreaker","npc:high-priestess-laurena","npc:duthorian-rall","zone:stormwind"},src={"Cathedral of Light"}}
E["subzone:cathedral-square"] = {t="subzone",n="Cathedral Square",z="stormwind",s="In Cathedral Square, faith and civic life meet beneath the Cathedral of Light. City Hall, the orphanage, and the Argent Dawn's Stormwind headquarters all stand here.",h="In Cathedral Square, faith and civic life meet beneath the Cathedral of Light.",sec={{t="The Holy District",b="Northwest of the Trade District and southeast of the Dwarven District, Cathedral Square draws the faithful from across the Kingdom of Stormwind. The Cathedral of Light rises above it, the foremost sanctuary of the Holy Light across Azeroth. Priests, paladins, and healers come to study, pray, and train. Citizens and pilgrims mingle with local schoolchildren, led by School Mistress Danna, in the square.",sp=0},{t="Civic Heart and Holy Order",b="Prayer shares the district with the work of the kingdom. City Hall and the Stormwind Orphanage anchor its civic life. Along the avenues, armorers and weaponsmiths serve holy crusaders, including Righteous Plates and Just Maces. The Argent Dawn keeps its Stormwind base here, where recruiters and representatives coordinate relief efforts and rally champions against the Scourge in the northern kingdoms.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Cathedral Square?",a="Cathedral Square gathers worship and civic life around the Cathedral of Light in Stormwind City. City Hall, the local orphanage, and shops also fill the district.",al={"cathedral district","holy district","what is this place"},it="place"},{q="Who trains in Cathedral Square?",a="Priests, paladins, and healers study and train in Cathedral Square and the Cathedral of Light. Medics and caregivers study here with First Aid trainers.",al={"class trainers here","who trains here","paladin priest trainers"},it="people"},{q="Why is the Argent Dawn located here?",a="The Argent Dawn keeps a base in Cathedral Square to recruit champions and coordinate support from Stormwind for its fight against the Scourge in the Plaguelands.",al={"argent dawn stormwind","argent dawn presence"},it="ties"},{q="Where does Cathedral Square lead?",a="Bridges and canal paths connect Cathedral Square to the Trade District to the southeast, the Dwarven District to the northwest, and the Park to the southwest.",al={"connected districts","where does this go"},gp=true},{q="Why is it called Cathedral Square?",a="The district takes its name from the magnificent Cathedral of Light that towers over it. Dominating Stormwind's skyline, this grand edifice stands as the foremost monument to the Holy Light in all of Azeroth, naturally lending its name and holy purpose to the surrounding streets and civic plazas.",al={"cathedral square name meaning","why cathedral square","how did cathedral square get its name"},it="name",add="2ce95091"},{q="Who lives in or runs Cathedral Square?",a="Cathedral Square serves as Stormwind's spiritual and civic core. The priesthood and paladins of the Cathedral of Light guide its religious life, while civic leaders oversee affairs from City Hall. It is also home to the city's orphanage, dedicated weapon and armor merchants, and prominent organizations like the Argent Dawn, who maintain an active presence here.",al={"who runs cathedral square","who lives in cathedral square","cathedral square residents"},it="residents",add="aa9b3d24"},{q="Is Cathedral Square dangerous?",a="No, Cathedral Square is one of the safest and most well-protected places in the kingdom. Shielded within Stormwind's walls and patrolled by city guards, it is guarded day and night by stalwart paladins and holy priests dedicated to preserving the peace.",al={"is cathedral square safe","cathedral square danger","threats in cathedral square"},it="danger",add="e4d635a7"}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you can find mentors, sacred vows, and armorers for holy warriors in Cathedral Square.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you can study the Holy Light, pray, and minister to Stormwind's citizens in the square's halls and spires."},kw={"argent dawn","cathedral of light","cathedral square","city hall","holy district","orphanage","paladin","priest","stormwind"},rel={"subzone:cathedral-of-light","zone:stormwind","topic:argent-dawn","topic:light","subzone:trade-district","subzone:dwarven-district"},src={"Cathedral Square"}}
E["subzone:champions-hall"] = {t="subzone",n="Champions' Hall",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind's Old Town, Champions' Hall is guarded and reserved for Alliance officers. Its quartermasters supply weapons, armor, and regalia to veterans who have proven themselves in battle.",h="In Stormwind's Old Town, Champions' Hall is guarded and reserved for Alliance officers.",sec={{t="The Alliance Officer's Barracks",b="Champions' Hall stands behind a guarded entrance in Old Town, reserved for the Alliance's distinguished combatants. Military commanders gather around maps of Azeroth to discuss ongoing campaigns, among arms and the insignias of rank. Only Alliance soldiers who have earned the rank of Knight or higher may enter. Inside, quartermasters supply battle-hardened soldiers with elite weapons, armor, and mounts made to aid them against the Horde in contested lands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Champions' Hall located?",a="Champions' Hall lies in southern Old Town in Stormwind City, behind a guarded entrance.",al={"where is champions hall","pvp vendor stormwind location","how to find champions hall"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is allowed inside the Champions' Hall?",a="Alliance soldiers who have earned the rank of Knight or higher in battle may enter Champions' Hall. Recruits without that standing and civilians are turned away.",al={"can anyone enter","champions hall requirements","why cant i enter champions hall"},it="for_you",gp=true},{q="What is inside the Champions' Hall?",a="Quartermasters inside offer officer-tier weapons, armor, insignia, and specialized war mounts. Alliance tacticians and generals gather around tables covered with maps of Azeroth.",al={"what does champions hall have","what vendors are in champions hall","champions hall rewards"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="What is the Horde equivalent of this building?",a="The Horde counterpart is the Hall of Legends in Orgrimmar, where decorated Horde warriors receive the same military supplies.",al={"horde version of champions hall","orgrimmar pvp room","horde pvp barracks"}},{q="What is Champions' Hall?",a="The Champions' Hall serves as the officer's barracks for the Alliance within Stormwind City. Tucked into Old Town, it is an exclusive sanctuary where decorated military officers and proven combatants of the Alliance gather, review war strategies, and equip themselves with specialized arms and armor.",al={"what is the champions hall","champions hall stormwind","what is this place"},it="place",add="5bb2303a"},{q="Why is it called Champions' Hall?",a="It takes its name from the proven champions of the Alliance who have earned the right to step through its threshold. Only those who have achieved distinction on the battlefield—reaching the officer rank of Knight or higher—are considered true champions worthy of entering its halls.",al={"why is it called champions hall","champions hall name meaning","who are the champions"},it="name",add="68396c8b"},{q="Is Champions' Hall dangerous?",a="Not to Alliance soldiers. Located deep within Stormwind's Old Town and guarded behind an enchanted portal, the barracks is heavily secured by Alliance officers and quartermasters. However, any Horde infiltrator reckless enough to breach Stormwind would find the hall occupied by some of the Alliance's most formidable veterans.",al={"is champions hall dangerous","is it safe in champions hall","threats in champions hall"},it="danger",add="b22714b1"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, Champions' Hall honors those in Stormwind who devote their lives to repelling Horde incursions.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior on the front lines, you can look to Champions' Hall for heavy battle gear and arms reserved for proven battlefield leaders."},kw={"champions hall","grand marshal","knight","officer barracks","old town","pvp vendors","quartermaster","stormwind"},rel={"subzone:old-town","zone:stormwind","subzone:hall-of-legends","topic:alliance","topic:horde","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Champions' Hall"}}
E["subzone:command-center"] = {t="subzone",n="Command Center",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind's Old Town, the Command Center trains recruits while most of the army serves abroad. Also called the Stormwind Barracks, it houses the city's military officers and a seasoned skeleton crew focused on drilling recruits and local militia.",h="In Stormwind's Old Town, the Command Center trains recruits while most of the army serves abroad.",sec={{t="A Thin Line of Defense",b="In Old Town, Stormwind's Command Center is a garrison and training ground for the kingdom's soldiers. Its halls are quieter than usual, with much of the royal army committed to campaigns abroad. Veteran instructors, including Ander Germaine and martial artist Wu Shen, train fresh warriors to strengthen the city's defenses.",sp=0},{t="Old Town's Martial Hub",b="When you ask for instruction in heavy arms or tactical combat, Stormwind's guards may point you to the Barracks. The building sits near the Pig and Whistle Tavern and the shadowy operations elsewhere in Old Town. It helps keep order in a district known for tavern brawls and roguish activity.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the Command Center so empty?",a="Most of Stormwind's standing army has been sent to distant outposts and foreign battlefields across the world. A seasoned skeleton crew remains to instruct recruits and organize local defense.",al={"why few guards here","where is stormwind army","barracks empty"},it="purpose"},{q="Is the Command Center the same as the Stormwind Barracks?",a="Yes. The building is officially called the Command Center, though city guards and local residents often call it the Stormwind Barracks when giving directions.",al={"stormwind barracks","are command center and barracks the same","barracks location"},it="name"},{q="Who leads the training here?",a="Ander Germaine coordinates and trains Stormwind's warriors, alongside instructors such as Wu Shen and Ilsa Corbin.",al={"who trains warriors here","warrior trainer command center","who runs the barracks"},it="in_charge"},{q="Where is the Command Center located?",a="You find the Command Center in Old Town, near the Pig and Whistle Tavern and the district's training facilities.",al={"where is command center","command center location","how to find command center"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the Command Center?",a="The Command Center serves as the operational headquarters and training barracks for Stormwind's military. Situated in Old Town, it is the primary hub where army officers and warrior trainers drill recruits and coordinate the defense of the kingdom.",al={"what is command center","command center stormwind","what is this building"},it="place",add="3e3491ec"},{q="Is the Command Center dangerous?",a="Not at all. The Command Center is a fortified stronghold situated safely in the heart of Stormwind City. It is manned by seasoned veterans and elite combat instructors loyal to the Alliance, making it one of the most secure facilities in the capital.",al={"is command center dangerous","danger command center","is it safe"},it="danger",add="1a0e6604"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you can train at Stormwind's Command Center, where veterans such as Ander Germaine and Wu Shen teach recruits to fight as disciplined frontline soldiers."},kw={"ander germaine","barracks","command center","old town","stormwind barracks","warrior trainer","wu shen"},rel={"subzone:old-town","zone:stormwind","subzone:pig-and-whistle-tavern","quest:2300","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:alliance"},src={"Command Center"}}
E["subzone:cut-throat-alley"] = {t="subzone",n="Cut-Throat Alley",z="stormwind",s="Behind the canal shops, Cut-Throat Alley lies quiet and empty in Stormwind City. Reach it through the Shady Lady near the Dwarven District, where a paved courtyard ends at an unoccupied residence.",h="Behind the canal shops, Cut-Throat Alley lies quiet and empty in Stormwind City.",sec={{t="A Secluded Nook",b="Cut-Throat Alley lies in a quiet corner of Stormwind, charted with the Dwarven District but apart from its forge fires and soot. No main avenue leads here; the only footpath passes through the Shady Lady, a small canal-side shop just south of the bridge from Cathedral Square. Beyond its door, a paved dead end holds stacked crates, forgotten barrels, and one empty two-story residence. Passing guards and ordinary citizens cannot see the alley, which stays silent amid the capital.",sp=0}},faq={{q="How do you get to Cut-Throat Alley?",a="Follow the canal front along the edge of the Dwarven District, just south of the footbridge to Cathedral Square. Find the Shady Lady and walk through the shop to reach the alley.",al={"find cut throat alley","cut throat alley location","where is cut-throat alley","how to enter cut-throat alley"},it="arrival",gp=true},{q="Why does the map call this the Dwarven District?",a="Cut-Throat Alley falls within the Dwarven District's bounds and is usually counted as part of it. It shares none of the district's smoke and has no street connection; enter through the Shady Lady on the canal front.",al={"minimap dwarven district","why does it say dwarven district","cut-throat alley name bug"},gp=true},{q="Is anyone living in Cut-Throat Alley?",a="No one lives in Cut-Throat Alley. Its lone two-story house is abandoned, and the alley has only stacked cargo crates and empty barrels, with no residents, shopkeepers, or city watchmen.",al={"cut throat alley npcs","who lives in cut throat alley","empty house cut throat alley"},it="residents"},{q="Are there any quests in Cut-Throat Alley?",a="No formal duties or civic assignments lead into Cut-Throat Alley. It is an overlooked, secluded corner of the capital.",al={"cut throat alley quests","cut throat alley storyline"},gp=true},{q="What is Cut-Throat Alley?",a="Cut-Throat Alley is a secluded, unpopulated back alley tucked away behind the Shady Lady along the Stormwind canals. Though officially considered part of the Dwarven District, it remains isolated from the rest of the quarter, lacking the heavy smoke and bustle found nearby. It contains scattered crates, barrels, and an unoccupied two-story residence.",al={"what is cut throat alley","cut throat alley lore","about cut-throat alley"},it="place",add="636e4761"},{q="Is Cut-Throat Alley dangerous?",a="Despite its sinister name, the alley is completely peaceful and devoid of hostile threats. You will find neither wandering cutthroats nor lurking cutpurses here—only an empty yard, quiet crates, and a deserted townhouse away from the city guard's usual patrol routes.",al={"cut throat alley dangerous","are there enemies in cut throat alley","danger cut throat alley"},it="danger",add="e98a554d"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a Rogue, you can reach this unpatrolled dead end only through the rear door of a shady canal shop. It offers a hideout away from the Stormwind City Guard's eyes."},kw={"cathedral square","cut-throat alley","dwarven district","secret alley","shady lady","stormwind canals"},rel={"subzone:dwarven-district","subzone:canals-stormwind-city","subzone:cathedral-square","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:alliance"},src={"Cut-Throat Alley"}}
E["subzone:dwarven-district"] = {t="subzone",n="Dwarven District",z="stormwind",s="Dwarven craftsmen keep their furnaces and workshops working in Stormwind's northern quarter. The district brings a piece of Khaz Modan to the human capital, with the Deeprun Tram linking it to Ironforge.",h="Dwarven craftsmen keep their furnaces and workshops working in Stormwind's northern quarter.",sec={{t="A Home Away from Khaz Modan",b="Dwarven artisans, smiths, and engineers make their home in Stormwind's northern quarter. Heavy stonework, smelting works, and craft shops recall Ironforge. At Potts' Plates, craftspeople from Khaz Modan find familiar company. On the district's eastern side, an open, arched tunnel leads to the Stormwind station of the Deeprun Tram, linking the human capital directly to Ironforge.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is there a dwarven enclave in Stormwind?",a="The chronicles of this era do not record how the enclave began. Today, dwarven smiths, miners, and engineers fill its forges and workshops, while the Deeprun Tram links the quarter directly to Ironforge.",al={"why dwarves in stormwind","dwarf area origin","why is it called dwarven district"},it="origin"},{q="How do you get to Ironforge from here?",a="On the district's eastern side, an open, arched tunnel leads directly to the Deeprun Tram station. The underground route carries travelers between Stormwind and Ironforge within minutes.",al={"how to get to ironforge","where is the tram","deeprun tram entrance"},gp=true},{q="What professions are trained in the Dwarven District?",a="The Dwarven District is Stormwind's premier hub for mining, blacksmithing, and engineering. Heavy forges, anvils, and dedicated trainers support all three crafts.",al={"professions dwarven district","trainers in dwarven district","blacksmith trainer stormwind"},gp=true},{q="Where can hunters train in Stormwind?",a="Stormwind's hunters make their headquarters at the Hunter's Guild in the Dwarven District, alongside dwarven marksmen and trade supplies.",al={"hunter trainer stormwind","hunter lodge","stormwind hunter guild"},gp=true},{q="What is the Dwarven District?",a="The Dwarven District is the bustling industrial heart of Stormwind City, nestled in its northern corner. Filled with billowing forge smoke and the ringing of smiths' hammers, this enclave serves as the primary home and workshop for the city's dwarf population, as well as many gnomes. Beyond its foundries and workshops, it houses the Stormwind terminus of the Deeprun Tram, directly connecting the human capital to Ironforge.",al={"what is dwarven district","dwarven district stormwind","tell me about dwarven district"},it="place",add="e5d74eee"},{q="What happened to establish the Dwarven District?",a="How the district came to be is not recorded in the chronicles of this era. Today it is the home and workplace of Stormwind's dwarven smiths, miners, and engineers, a permanent fixture of the city's community and industry, linked to Ironforge by the Deeprun Tram.",al={"dwarven district history","how did dwarven district form","history of dwarven district"},it="history",add="60b8a274"},{q="Who lives in the Dwarven District?",a="The district is populated predominantly by dwarves and gnomes who make their living as blacksmiths, miners, engineers, and gunsmiths. You will also find visiting travelers fresh off the Deeprun Tram, local merchants catering to craftspeople, and members of the city's Hunter's Guild who gather here alongside their companion animals.",al={"who lives in dwarven district","dwarven district residents","dwarven district inhabitants"},it="residents",add="c66f318a"},{q="Is the Dwarven District dangerous?",a="Within Stormwind's guarded walls, the district is generally safe from external invasion. However, the heavy industry carries its own hazards, from scalding forges and unstable engineering contraptions to the thick haze choking the air. Quiet corners like Cut-Throat Alley also invite lowlifes and illicit dealings away from the watchful eyes of the city watch.",al={"is dwarven district safe","danger in dwarven district","threats dwarven district"},it="danger",add="ab83050b"},{q="Why is it called the Dwarven District?",a="It takes its name from the dwarves who live and work here. Its smithies, forges, and stonework mirror the sights, sounds, and craftsmanship of their mountain homeland, creating a distinct corner of Stormwind dedicated to dwarven culture and heavy industry.",al={"why is it called dwarven district","dwarven district name","name dwarven district"},it="name",add="04c5fe8f"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf far from Khaz Modan, you can find familiar comfort in the roar of working blast furnaces and quick passage back to Ironforge.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="As a blacksmith, you can use Stormwind's most capable smithing facilities, with expansive smelting forges, sturdy anvils, and veteran instructors."},kw={"deeprun tram","dwarven district","hunters guild","ironforge","potts plates","stormwind"},rel={"subzone:deeprun-tram","zone:stormwind","zone:ironforge","subzone:cathedral-square","subzone:old-town","subzone:cut-throat-alley"},src={"Dwarven District"}}
E["subzone:gryphon-roost"] = {t="subzone",n="Gryphon Roost",z="stormwind",s="Gryphons take travelers from Stormwind’s eastern ramparts across the Eastern Kingdoms. Dungar Longdrink, a human gryphon master, manages the roost beside the Trade District.",h="Gryphons take travelers from Stormwind’s eastern ramparts across the Eastern Kingdoms.",sec={{t="Gateway to the Skies",b="From the eastern ramparts, gryphons carry travelers from Stormwind to Alliance garrisons and settlements across the Eastern Kingdoms. Dungar Longdrink, the seasoned gryphon master, coordinates flights to Ironforge, Lakeshire, Sentinel Hill, and other destinations.",sp=0},{t="A Touch of the Aerie",b="Gryphons and their handlers bring a trace of Hinterlands tradition within Stormwind’s walls. The Wildhammer clan has long revered gryphons as partners and introduced aerial warfare and transport to the broader Alliance during the Second War. Leather, feed, and fresh winds mark the roost amid the city’s stonework.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Gryphon Roost located in Stormwind?",a="The Gryphon Roost sits on Stormwind’s eastern ramparts, reached by a stairway from the Trade District. It overlooks the canals between the Trade District and Old Town.",al={"where is the roost","stormwind flight master location","find gryphon roost"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who manages the roost's flights?",a="Dungar Longdrink, a human flight master, manages the roost’s flights. He organizes routes and rents trained gryphons to travelers bound for allied settlements across the continent.",al={"who is the flight master","stormwind flight master","dungar longdrink"},it="residents"},{q="Why are dwarves running the roost in a human city?",a="Stormwind’s flight master, Dungar Longdrink, is human. The Wildhammer dwarves have a long tradition of gryphon riding, while Dungar manages the roost’s flights.",al={"why dwarves in stormwind roost","wildhammer in stormwind","dwarven gryphons"},it="ties"},{q="Where can the gryphons fly from here?",a="The roost connects Stormwind with Alliance destinations including Sentinel Hill, Lakeshire, Darkshire, and Ironforge. Other routes reach settlements across the Eastern Kingdoms.",al={"flight paths from stormwind","where do gryphons go","roost flight connections"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="What is the Gryphon Roost?",a="The Gryphon Roost is Stormwind City's aerial transit hub, perched just off the bustling Trade District. It serves as both stables and aerie for the kingdom's flying mounts, allowing messengers, soldiers, and travelers to quickly journey across Alliance lands aboard trained gryphons.",al={"what is gryphon roost","gryphon roost purpose","stormwind gryphon roost"},it="place",add="c47c3c58"},{q="Is the Gryphon Roost dangerous?",a="Not at all. The roost is nestled deep within the fortified heart of Stormwind, well protected by city guards. The gryphons housed here are thoroughly tamed and accustomed to crowds of travelers.",al={"is gryphon roost safe","gryphon roost dangers","threats at gryphon roost"},it="danger",add="4cbfa62c"},{q="Why is it called the Gryphon Roost?",a="The facility takes its straightforward name from its purpose: a dedicated aerie and nesting perch for the city's winged gryphons, where the beasts can rest, feed, and roost between long cross-country flights.",al={"why is it called gryphon roost","gryphon roost name origin","meaning of gryphon roost"},it="name",add="5a6ce60b"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you can see your people’s long tradition of gryphon riding carried into Stormwind. Trained gryphons connect the human capital with Khaz Modan.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you can carry messages by air from Stormwind to territories such as Westfall and Redridge, helping coordinate responses there."},kw={"dungar longdrink","flight master","gryphon roost","stormwind flight","trade district","wildhammer"},rel={"zone:stormwind","quest:6261","subzone:trade-district","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Gryphon Roost"}}
E["subzone:mage-quarter"] = {t="subzone",n="Mage Quarter",z="stormwind",s="The Mage Quarter forms the arcane heart of Stormwind City, resting across the canals in the capital's southwestern corner. Towering over its cobblestone streets and esoteric specialty shops stands the Wizard's Sanctum, where the kingdom's conjurers hone their craft. Beneath the district's scholarly surface also lie shadowy recesses, harboring practitioners of far darker arts.",h="The Mage Quarter forms the arcane heart of Stormwind City, resting across the canals in the capital's...",sec={{t="Sanctum of the Arcane",b="Reachable by bridges crossing the canals from Cathedral Square or the Trade District, the Mage Quarter caters entirely to the mystical needs of the Alliance. Centered around the spire of the Wizard's Sanctum, human and allied spellcasters gather to study the weave of arcane magic and train apprentices. The surrounding streets are crowded with purveyors of tailoring cloth, reagents, alchemical supplies, and enchanted staves, creating an insular district dedicated to research and the defense of the kingdom.",sp=0},{t="Secrets Beneath the Surface",b="Not all sorcery practiced in the quarter is approved by the kingdom's high conjurers. While establishments like The Blue Recluse offer quiet refuge for scholars, the infamous Slaughtered Lamb tavern conceals a covert coven of warlocks in its subterranean crypts. There, out of sight of the city guard and the holy eyes of Cathedral Square, demonologists study forbidden fel rites and bind otherworldly entities while masquerading beneath the district's general tolerance of mystic anomalies.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Wizard's Sanctum?",a="The Wizard's Sanctum is the prominent tower dominating the Mage Quarter. It serves as the primary academy, library, and training grounds for Stormwind's mages, housing scholars, mystic trainers, and defensive spellcasters tasked with protecting the capital.",al={"mage tower","wizards sanctum","mage sanctum stormwind"}},{q="Where can warlocks train in the Mage Quarter?",a="Warlocks gather secretly beneath The Slaughtered Lamb, an unassuming tavern in the quarter. Down in its crypts and hidden cellars, practitioners of fel magic can study dark rituals, summon demons, and train outside the scrutiny of the city guard.",al={"warlock trainer location","slaughtered lamb basement","stormwind warlock trainers"},gp=true},{q="What kind of shops are in the Mage Quarter?",a="The district is filled with specialty trades catering to casters and crafters. Visitors can find tailoring shops like Duncan's Textiles and Larson Clothiers, alchemy and herbalism merchants, enchanting vendors, pyrotechnic suppliers, and staff merchants.",al={"mage quarter vendors","what shops are here","stores in mage quarter"},gp=true},{q="How do you reach the Mage Quarter?",a="The Mage Quarter occupies the southwestern corner of Stormwind City. It can be accessed directly by crossing the bridges that span the Canals from either the Trade District or Cathedral Square.",al={"where is mage quarter","how to get to mage quarter","directions to mage quarter"},it="arrival",gp=true},{q="What is the Mage Quarter?",a="The Mage Quarter is the arcane center of Stormwind City, nestled in its southwestern corner across the canals from Cathedral Square and the Trade District. Dominated by the towering spire of the Wizard's Sanctum, it serves as the primary haven for scholars, alchemists, tailors, and practitioners of the mystic arts throughout the kingdom.",al={"what is mage quarter","mage quarter stormwind","mage district"},it="place",add="cffe9f84"},{q="Who lives in or runs the Mage Quarter?",a="The quarter is populated primarily by the kingdom's mages, arcane researchers, scholars, and related tradesfolk such as alchemists and clothiers. The wizard community operating out of the Wizard's Sanctum oversees magical matters and works to ensure the safety of the capital and its surrounding lands, though darker practitioners secretly harbor beneath the local taverns as well.",al={"who lives in mage quarter","who runs mage quarter","mage quarter inhabitants"},it="residents",add="4d297df6"},{q="Is the Mage Quarter dangerous?",a="On the surface, the Mage Quarter is a peaceful center of learning and commerce heavily watched by the city guard. However, beneath the jovial facade of The Slaughtered Lamb tavern lies a clandestine warlock coven practicing dark, demonic summonings in the shadows, unmolested by the city's authorities above.",al={"is mage quarter safe","mage quarter danger","dangers in mage quarter"},it="danger",add="1c00796e"},{q="Why is it called the Mage Quarter?",a="It earned its name as the designated hub for Stormwind's spellcasters, established around the Wizard's Sanctum where the city's mages live, study, and hone their arcane crafts.",al={"why mage quarter","how did mage quarter get its name"},it="name",add="ddf0f180"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="The district serves as your central home in Stormwind, offering master trainers and spell reagents inside the Wizard's Sanctum.",["class:Warlock"]="Beneath the public guise of The Slaughtered Lamb tavern lies the hidden coven where practitioners of the dark arts convene to train and summon minions in secret."},kw={"arcane","blue recluse","canals","mage quarter","slaughtered lamb","stormwind","wizard's sanctum"},rel={"zone:stormwind","subzone:slaughtered-lamb","subzone:canals-stormwind-city","subzone:trade-district","subzone:cathedral-square","topic:alliance"},src={"Mage Quarter"}}
E["subzone:old-town"] = {t="subzone",n="Old Town",z="stormwind",s="In Old Town, soldiers train beside weathered tenements and crowded alleys. The quarter largely survived the First War and remains home to Stormwind’s military Command Center and the covert headquarters of SI:7.",h="In Old Town, soldiers train beside weathered tenements and crowded alleys.",sec={{t="A Relic of the Old Kingdom",b="Old Town keeps much of the shape of Stormwind before the First War. While the Stonemasons rebuilt the rest of the city from the ground up, this quarter escaped total ruin. It never gained the pristine marble facades and grand canals found in the Trade District and Cathedral Square. Working folk, laborers, and the city’s poorest residents live among its crowded tenements. Its cobbled streets are narrower, dirtier, and more chaotic than those elsewhere in the capital, preserving the feel of the old kingdom.",sp=0},{t="Soldiers, Spies, and Taverns",b="Old Town holds Stormwind’s military officers, barracks, and combat trainers in the Command Center. Nearby, the Champions’ Hall gathers the Alliance’s finest warriors. At the district’s edge, SI:7 keeps its covert compound under the leadership of Master Mathias Shaw. Off-duty footmen and shadowy operatives meet at the Pig and Whistle Tavern, one of the city’s liveliest watering holes.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Old Town look so much dirtier than the rest of Stormwind?",a="Old Town largely survived the Horde’s razing of Stormwind during the First War. The Stonemasons did not rebuild it from scratch, so it missed the pristine new masonry and grand architecture found elsewhere in the city.",al={"why is old town run down","old town poverty","why is old town gross"},it="ruin"},{q="What is SI:7 and where is it located?",a="SI:7 is Stormwind and the Alliance’s secretive intelligence agency, overseen by Master Mathias Shaw. Its covert headquarters lies in the back of Old Town, past the training yards and military stables.",al={"si7 location","what is si:7","stormwind spies"}},{q="What is the Command Center in Old Town used for?",a="Stormwind’s Command Center is the primary garrison and headquarters for its military. Officers coordinate the city’s defenses there, while warriors and hunters train alongside stable masters and riding instructors.",al={"command center purpose","old town barracks","stormwind military headquarters"},it="purpose"},{q="Where is the tavern in Old Town?",a="The Pig and Whistle Tavern sits near the center of Old Town. Hungry soldiers, adventurers, and travelers gather there, and it is known for hearty cooking recipes.",al={"old town inn","pig and whistle location","where is pig and whistle"},gp=true},{q="What is Old Town?",a="Old Town is the oldest surviving district in Stormwind City. Unlike the rest of the capital, much of Old Town survived the First War when the Orcish Horde sacked the city. Today, it stands as a rustic, impoverished quarter that houses Stormwind's lower classes, common laborers, and rogue elements, alongside vital military facilities such as the Command Center and the headquarters of SI:7.",al={"what is old town","old town stormwind","about old town"},it="place",add="ddeb3ebc"},{q="What happened to Old Town during the First War?",a="When the orcish Horde razed Stormwind City at the end of the First War, most of the capital was devastated. However, Old Town escaped total destruction and was spared the worst of the fires. Because its buildings remained mostly intact, it was left largely as-is during the grand postwar reconstruction that rebuilt the gleaming stone districts you see elsewhere in the city.",al={"old town history","what happened to old town","how did old town survive"},it="history",add="70a73a68"},{q="Who lives in Old Town?",a="Old Town is home to Stormwind's poorer populace, including laborers, beggars, pickpockets, and thieves. However, it also serves as a crucial base for the city's military and security forces. Stormwind's army operates out of the central Command Center, while Master Mathias Shaw directs the secretive operatives of SI:7 from their headquarters tucked away in the district.",al={"who lives in old town","old town residents","who controls old town"},it="residents",add="73f1f985"},{q="Is Old Town dangerous?",a="While it is guarded by the city watch and houses the kingdom's military Command Center, Old Town harbors a rough underbelly. Cutpurses, thieves, and assassins lurk in its narrow alleyways and dark corners, and shady shops deal in poisons and hidden blades. Honest travelers should keep a tight grip on their coin purses when navigating its crowded streets.",al={"is old town dangerous","danger in old town","is old town safe"},it="danger",add="3b861739"},{q="Why is it called Old Town?",a="It earns its name literally: it is the original, historic quarter of Stormwind. Because its structures were not completely razed during the First War, its buildings predate the modern reconstruction overseen by the Stonemasons, making it the oldest standing part of the entire city.",al={"why is it called old town","how did old town get its name","old town name"},it="name",add="840898dc"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you can find SI:7’s headquarters behind Old Town’s ordinary alleys, where master spies and covert handlers offer guidance.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you can seek combat training and gear at the Command Center and Champions’ Hall, where battle-tested veterans gather."},kw={"champions hall","command center","first war","mathias shaw","old town","pig and whistle","si:7","stormwind"},rel={"zone:stormwind","subzone:command-center","npc:mathias-shaw","subzone:pig-and-whistle-tavern","subzone:champions-hall","subzone:trade-district","subzone:dwarven-district","topic:first-war"},src={"Old Town"}}
E["subzone:park"] = {t="subzone",n="Park",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind's western edge, Park offers visiting night elves a haven amid the stone city. It lies between Cathedral Square and the Mage Quarter, with greenery and quiet for rest. Druid trainers here are the only ones in the Eastern Kingdoms.",h="In Stormwind's western edge, Park offers visiting night elves a haven amid the stone city.",sec={{t="A Grove in the Stone Capital",b="Stormwind's Park brings a quiet stretch of wilderness into the stone capital. Once a place for the city's people to seek recreation, it became an enclave for night elf emissaries and travelers from across the Great Sea. Shaded canopies shelter the district, and a central Moonwell stands amid its grounds. The grove offers a glimpse of Kalimdor's sacred glades in the heart of the human kingdom.",sp=0},{t="Sanctuary and Fellowship",b="Night elves have a foothold in foreign lands within the Park. Kaldorei priests such as Nara Meideros tend visiting pilgrims, while druidic mentors guide those devoted to the wild. Weary travelers can also rest from the clatter of the Trade District and the solemn duties of the Cathedral.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Park located in Stormwind?",a="Park lies along Stormwind City's far western edge. You can reach it by heading southwest from Cathedral Square or northwest from the Mage Quarter.",al={"where is the park","how to get to the park","park location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why are there so many night elves in the Park?",a="Visiting night elves found refuge in Park to escape Stormwind's towering stone streets. Its groves and serene air reminded them of home, and they established a Moonwell in the square.",al={"why night elves here","stormwind night elf district","kaldorei district"},it="residents"},{q="Can I train druid abilities here?",a="Yes. Park is the only place in the Eastern Kingdoms with Alliance druid trainers, who offer Kaldorei practitioners guidance and training away from Kalimdor.",al={"druid trainers stormwind","where to train druid eastern kingdoms","park druid training"},gp=true},{q="What is the glowing pool in the center of the Park?",a="The pool at the center of Park is a consecrated night elven Moonwell. Kaldorei visitors created it as a sacred font of spiritual peace and lunar power amid the human city.",al={"park moonwell","glowing fountain park","pool in the park"}},{q="What is the Park?",a="The Park is a lush, verdant district nestled in the western corner of Stormwind City. Once built primarily for leisure, it now serves as a green haven and sanctuary for visiting night elves seeking respite from the city's vast stone thoroughfares. Among its tranquil groves stands a sacred moonwell and the only gathering of druid trainers in the Eastern Kingdoms.",al={"what is the park","park stormwind overview","what district is the park"},it="place",add="a403a5e6"},{q="What happened to the Park?",a="Originally dedicated to simple leisure for Stormwind's citizens, the district transformed following the Third War when night elves allied with the Alliance and arrived in the capital. Finding comfort in its trees and greenery away from the stone streets, the night elves established a permanent enclave here, consecrated a glowing moonwell, and brought the practice of druidism to human lands.",al={"park history","history of the park","what happened at the park"},it="history",add="7a811135"},{q="Is the Park dangerous?",a="No, the Park is one of the most peaceful and serene districts in Stormwind. Protected by city guards and guarded by visiting night elf sentinels and druids, it offers quiet respite away from the bustling trade and military districts of the capital.",al={"is the park safe","is the park dangerous","threats in the park"},it="danger",add="83a38db8"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Park gives night elves a welcome taste of home, with a glowing Moonwell and familiar teachers of Elune and the wild.",["class:Druid"]="In Park, you find your sole sanctuary for druid training and counsel across the Eastern Kingdoms."},kw={"druid","kaldorei","moonwell","nara meideros","night elf","park","stormwind"},rel={"zone:stormwind","subzone:cathedral-square","subzone:mage-quarter","topic:night-elf","topic:druid","npc:nara-meideros","npc:argos-nightwhisper","quest:3765"},src={"Park"}}
E["subzone:petitioner-s-chamber"] = {t="subzone",n="Petitioner's Chamber",z="stormwind",s="Petitioners wait for the crown in a chamber just inside Stormwind Keep. Nobles, church dignitaries, and visiting subjects spend the time mingling, drinking, or awaiting an audience.",h="Petitioners wait for the crown in a chamber just inside Stormwind Keep.",sec={{t="A Room of Waiting and Influence",b="The Petitioner's Chamber lies just to the right as you enter Stormwind Keep. Count Remington Ridgewell and Bishop DeLavey wait there for audiences with boy-king Anduin Wrynn and Highlord Bolvar Fordragon. Between formal visits, the chamber gives nobles and clergy room to mingle, trade gossip, and quietly press their concerns. Who holds influence in the realm can often be seen in who speaks with whom.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Petitioner's Chamber located?",a="The Petitioner's Chamber is inside Stormwind Keep, immediately to your right as you ascend the main entrance ramp.",al={"where is petitioners chamber","how to find petitioner chamber","petitioner room location"},gp=true},{q="Who gathers in this room?",a="Petitioners, court attendees, and nobles gather there, including Count Remington Ridgewell, Caledra Dawnbreeze, and Bishop DeLavey of the Church of the Holy Light.",al={"who is in petitioners chamber","npcs in petitioner chamber","who waits here"},it="people"},{q="Why is it also called the Hall of Petitioners?",a="The chamber takes its name from its role as a waiting room for subjects who have petitioned the crown. They wait until Highlord Bolvar Fordragon, the royal council, or the regent grants them entry to the throne room.",al={"hall of petitioners","why called hall of petitioners","petitioners hall"},it="name"},{q="What happens here during city quests?",a="Visitors come to the chamber to deliver goods or speak with nobles and clergy in the keep. Some bring refined drinks such as port to aristocrats waiting on court business.",al={"petitioner chamber quests","what quests lead here"},gp=true},{q="What is the Petitioner's Chamber?",a="The Petitioner's Chamber is the public reception hall of Stormwind Keep, located just to the right as you ascend the grand ramp into the palace. It serves as an official waiting room for subjects, foreign emissaries, and visiting nobility seeking an audience with the crown or the royal court.",al={"what is petitioners chamber","hall of petitioners stormwind","what is this room"},it="place",add="7fbb3fec"},{q="Is the Petitioner's Chamber dangerous?",a="Not in the slightest. The chamber sits safely inside the heavily guarded halls of Stormwind Keep, protected by the Royal Guard. Unless you bring trouble directly into the palace, it is one of the most secure and peaceful antechambers in the kingdom.",al={"is petitioners chamber safe","danger petitioners chamber","threats in petitioners chamber"},it="danger",add="7106fd20"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, the chamber is where domestic appeals, church affairs, and noble requests wait for the royal council's attention.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you may find Bishop DeLavey in this antechamber, where the Holy Light's hierarchy meets the royal court."},kw={"bishop delavey","caledra dawnbreeze","count remington ridgewell","hall of petitioners","petitioners chamber","stormwind keep"},rel={"subzone:stormwind-keep","npc:count-remington-ridgewell","npc:bishop-delavey","quest:335","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:alliance"},src={"Petitioner's Chamber"}}
E["subzone:pig-and-whistle-tavern"] = {t="subzone",n="Pig and Whistle Tavern",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind City's Old Town, the Pig and Whistle Tavern welcomes travelers and local laborers. Veterans gather there to remember the kingdom's past conflicts.",h="In Stormwind City's Old Town, the Pig and Whistle Tavern welcomes travelers and local laborers.",sec={{t="A Refuge in Old Town",b="In Old Town's winding alleys, the Pig and Whistle Tavern offers warmth, ale, and lodging. Common citizens, working folk, and travelers fresh from the road gather there. Merchants such as recipe vendor Kendor Kabonka share the room with grizzled veterans, who trade memories of the First and Second Wars over their tankards.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Pig and Whistle Tavern located?",a="The Pig and Whistle Tavern stands in Old Town, Stormwind City's eastern district, among military barracks, rogue dens, and working-class quarters.",al={"where is pig and whistle","pig and whistle location","old town tavern"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who frequents the tavern?",a="Travelers, guards off duty, and veteran soldiers who swap stories of the First and Second Wars frequent the tavern. Merchant Kendor Kabonka, who sells cooking recipes, is there as well.",al={"who is in pig and whistle","pig and whistle patrons"},it="people"},{q="What services does the tavern provide?",a="The Pig and Whistle Tavern offers weary travelers a place to rest and buy food, drink, and specialized cooking recipes.",al={"is pig and whistle an inn","pig and whistle services"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="What is the Pig and Whistle Tavern?",a="The Pig and Whistle Tavern is a welcoming tavern tucked within the Old Town district of Stormwind City. Serving as a home away from home for weary Alliance travelers, it provides a warm hearth, strong drink, and safe shelter. Inside, veteran soldiers often gather to drink and share memories of the First and Second Wars, while travelers and locals mingle away from the busier trade districts.",al={"pig and whistle tavern","pig and whistle","what is the pig and whistle"},it="place",add="97956e92"},{q="Is the Pig and Whistle Tavern dangerous?",a="Not at all. The tavern is a peaceful refuge situated firmly under the protection of the Stormwind City guard. While Old Town can harbor shady dealings in its shadowed alleys, inside the tavern you will find only resting travelers, war veterans trading tales of past campaigns, and local tradesfolk unwinding over an ale.",al={"is pig and whistle dangerous","danger pig and whistle"},it="danger",add="7bd4ea21"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Cooks come to the tavern to find Kendor Kabonka, who sells a collection of rare cooking recipes from across Azeroth.",["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance soldiers and travelers passing through the capital, the tavern offers a welcoming hearth and company with veterans of the realm's earlier wars."},kw={"cooking","kendor kabonka","old town","pig and whistle","stormwind","tavern"},rel={"subzone:old-town","zone:stormwind","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:second-war","topic:alliance"},src={"Pig and Whistle Tavern"}}
E["subzone:royal-gallery"] = {t="subzone",n="Royal Gallery",z="stormwind",s="Stormwind Keep's Royal Gallery honors figures from the kingdom's history and the Grand Alliance. Past the courtyard garden, its statues and works of art fill a quiet hall of remembrance.",h="Stormwind Keep's Royal Gallery honors figures from the kingdom's history and the Grand Alliance.",sec={{t="A Hall of Heroes",b="The Royal Gallery lies beyond Stormwind Keep's interior garden, beside the Royal Library. Its statues honor King Llane Wrynn, the fallen ruler of Stormwind; Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore of Kul Tiras; and Lady Mara Fordragon, patron of the refugees who fled to Lordaeron after the First War. Courtly visitors such as Lady Dena Kennedy come to this quiet hall, where the kingdom's noble heritage is remembered.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Royal Gallery located?",a="The Royal Gallery lies inside Stormwind Keep, beyond the small interior courtyard park and beside the Royal Library.",al={"royal gallery location","how to get to royal gallery","where is it"},gp=true},{q="Which historical figures are commemorated here?",a="The gallery commemorates King Llane Wrynn, Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore, and Mara Fordragon with grand statues honoring the kingdom and its closest allies.",al={"statues in royal gallery","who are the statues of","who is honored here"},it="purpose"},{q="Who can be found visiting the gallery?",a="Lady Dena Kennedy visits the gallery to admire its art and quiet atmosphere.",al={"who is here","npcs in royal gallery","lady dena kennedy"},it="residents"},{q="What is the difference between the Royal Gallery and the Royal Library?",a="The Royal Gallery and the Royal Library are separate chambers beside each other in Stormwind Keep's royal wing. The library holds royal archives and scholars, while the gallery displays fine art and memorial sculpture.",al={"royal gallery vs library","is it part of the library"}},{q="What is the Royal Gallery?",a="The Royal Gallery is an intimate exhibition hall nestled within Stormwind Keep, situated just beyond the small courtyard park and adjacent to the Royal Library. It serves as a commemorative wing displaying exquisite fine art and grandiose marble statues honoring illustrious figures of the Alliance and the Kingdom of Stormwind.",al={"what is the royal gallery","royal gallery stormwind","what is this place"},it="place",add="57ab90b0"},{q="Is the Royal Gallery dangerous?",a="Not in the slightest. The gallery sits deep within the heart of Stormwind Keep, heavily guarded by the city's elite royal sentries. It remains a tranquil, safe hall of remembrance where nobles and courtiers can reflect upon the kingdom's greatest heroes without fear of harm.",al={"is royal gallery dangerous","threats in royal gallery","royal gallery safe"},it="danger",add="0132543d"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, the gallery honors the sacrifices of its people and leaders such as Daelin Proudmoore and King Llane.",["race:Human"]="As a human of Stormwind, you can see House Wrynn and House Fordragon's heritage honored within the keep."},kw={"daelin proudmoore","dena kennedy","llane wrynn","mara fordragon","royal gallery","statues","stormwind keep"},rel={"subzone:stormwind-keep","subzone:royal-library","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Royal Gallery"}}
E["subzone:royal-library"] = {t="subzone",n="Royal Library",z="stormwind",s="Scholars come to the Royal Library in Stormwind Keep for the kingdom’s records and histories. Head Librarian Milton Sheaf watches over its scrolls and treatises, from ancient wars to accounts of realms beyond the sea.",h="Scholars come to the Royal Library in Stormwind Keep for the kingdom’s records and histories.",sec={{t="A Repository of the Realm",b="The Royal Library offers quiet among Stormwind Keep’s guarded halls and courtly intrigues. Milton Sheaf oversees its shelves of southern human history, from surviving texts written before the First War to recent military chronicles and recovered tomes. Alliance scholars, priests, and travelers may browse its treatises. They cover the founding of the Alliance of Lordaeron and the recent arrival of Thrall’s Horde in Kalimdor.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Royal Library located?",a="The Royal Library lies inside Stormwind Keep, in the eastern part of Stormwind City. From the keep’s grand foyer, follow the corridors to its scholar and archive wings.",al={"where is the library","stormwind library location","how to find library"},gp=true},{q="Who runs the library?",a="Milton Sheaf is the head librarian. He manages the records and helps scholars and adventurers find missing volumes or treatises on the kingdom.",al={"who is the librarian","head librarian","milton sheaf"},it="residents"},{q="What kinds of books can be read here?",a="Visitors can read histories of the Alliance of Lordaeron, the Guardians of Tirisfal, and the aftermath of the Second War. The shelves also hold reports on the New Horde and regional histories of Stormwind and Alterac.",al={"books in library","readable lore books","what to read"}},{q="Who may use the library?",a="Adventurers of every Alliance race may browse the Royal Library’s collection of scrolls, tomes, and texts on many subjects.",al={"can i use the library","who can read in the library"}},{q="What is the Royal Library?",a="The Royal Library is the grand archive housed within the walls of Stormwind Keep. It preserves an extensive collection of historical tomes, ancient scrolls, and academic treatises on the subjects that shape the world. Scholars and adventurers across the Alliance are welcome to browse its shelves, seeking knowledge of kingdoms past, arcane lore, and the wider lands of Azeroth.",al={"what is royal library","about royal library","stormwind library lore"},it="place",add="0be1be66"},{q="Is the Royal Library dangerous?",a="Not in the slightest. The library sits deep inside the fortified heart of Stormwind Keep, watched over by the royal guards of the realm. It is entirely peaceful—a quiet haven where scholars, chroniclers, and wandering adventurers can study in safety.",al={"is royal library safe","danger in royal library","royal library enemies"},it="danger",add="c9a9445a"},{q="Why is it called the Royal Library?",a="It bears the royal name because it serves as the official court library of House Wrynn and the Kingdom of Stormwind. Situated directly inside the royal palace of Stormwind Keep, the archives were founded and maintained under royal patronage to preserve the heritage, laws, and arcane knowledge of the kingdom.",al={"why called royal library","royal library name origin","why royal library"},it="name",add="45bbfcdd"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you can find rare firsthand accounts of Tirisfal’s past, ancient dragon hunts, and the legacy of the Last Guardian.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can read the treaties and war chronicles that bind human, dwarven, and elven peoples through generations of conflict."},kw={"mathias shaw","milton sheaf","royal library","stormwind keep","stormwind library"},rel={"subzone:stormwind-keep","zone:stormwind","npc:milton-sheaf","quest:579","quest:337","npc:mathias-shaw","topic:second-war"},src={"Royal Library"}}
E["subzone:si-7-stormwind-city"] = {t="subzone",n="SI:7 (Stormwind City)",z="stormwind",s="Tucked away in the eastern corner of Old Town, this unassuming stone manor houses the headquarters of SI:7, the kingdom of Stormwind's elite intelligence and espionage service. Behind its heavy doors, spymaster Master Mathias Shaw and his senior operatives quietly monitor threats to the realm, coordinating undercover agents across the kingdom.",h="Tucked away in the eastern corner of Old Town, this unassuming stone manor houses the headquarters of SI:7...",sec={{t="Heart of the Kingdom's Espionage",b="To the casual passerby in Old Town, this fortified stone structure looks little different from a standard manor or military barracks. In truth, it serves as the nerve center for Stormwind Intelligence, Section 7. Directed by Master Mathias Shaw, SI:7 gathers intelligence, conducts surveillance, and executes covert operations to protect the kingdom from subversion. While the city guard patrols the open cobblestones and the Royal Guard defends Stormwind Keep, SI:7 works in the margins, training handlers and dispatching stealthy operatives against foreign enemies, saboteurs, and domestic unrest alike.",sp=0},{t="A Watchful Eye on the Shadows",b="With King Varian Wrynn mysteriously missing and the Defias Brotherhood spreading chaos through Westfall and Duskwood, the headquarters hums with constant covert activity. Intelligence reports funnel into the building from deep-cover scouts across human lands. Down in the cellars and weapon-lined training rooms, lethal techniques are refined and missions assigned to counter threats long before they can reach the boy-king's throne room.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is SI:7?",a="SI:7 stands for Stormwind Intelligence, Section 7. It is the premier covert espionage, reconnaissance, and assassination agency serving the Crown of Stormwind.",al={"what is si7","who are si:7","si 7 meaning"},it="place"},{q="Who leads SI:7 in Stormwind?",a="Master Mathias Shaw leads the organization from within the building. Mathias oversees all field assignments, intelligence networks, and strategic reconnaissance for the crown.",al={"who is the leader of si7","si7 boss","who runs si:7"},it="residents"},{q="Where in the city is this building located?",a="The headquarters is situated in Old Town, tucked along the southeastern edge of the district near the canal and training yards.",al={"where is si7","si7 location","how to get to si7"},gp=true},{q="Why is SI:7 so interested in Westfall?",a="SI:7 tracks subversive activities throughout Stormwind's territories, and the Defias Brotherhood represents the most dangerous insurrection within the realm.",al={"defias brotherhood si7","why is si7 watching defias"}},{q="Is SI:7 dangerous?",a="SI:7 poses no threat to loyal citizens and allies of Stormwind. Inside its walls, the kingdom's covert intelligence network trains and coordinates its operatives. However, cross them or threaten the crown, and you will find their master rogues, scouts, and assassins among the deadliest adversaries in the Eastern Kingdoms.",al={"is SI:7 dangerous","danger in SI:7","is SI:7 safe"},it="danger",add="3c33de19"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="For Alliance rogues, the SI:7 building is a vital professional hub offering advanced class training, poison supplies, and clandestine assignments direct from Spymaster Mathias Shaw.",["faction:Alliance"]="As the unseen foundation of Stormwind's defense, SI:7's intelligence network provides the Alliance military with crucial reconnaissance against threats to the throne."},kw={"barracks","defias","espionage","mathias shaw","old town","rogues","si7","si:7","spymaster","stormwind"},rel={"npc:mathias-shaw","subzone:old-town","zone:stormwind","quest:2300","quest:65","topic:defias-brotherhood","topic:stormwind-kingdom","subzone:ravenholdt-manor"},src={"SI:7 (Stormwind City)"}}
E["subzone:slaughtered-lamb"] = {t="subzone",n="Slaughtered Lamb",z="stormwind",s="Tucked away in Stormwind's Mage Quarter, the Slaughtered Lamb appears to be nothing more than a quiet, seedy tavern. Beneath its floorboards, however, sprawling catacombs hide the sanctum and training grounds of the Alliance's illicit warlocks.",h="Tucked away in Stormwind's Mage Quarter, the Slaughtered Lamb appears to be nothing more than a quiet, seedy...",sec={{t="A Thin Disguise",b="On the surface, the Slaughtered Lamb offers little more than dark corners and sparse patronage, attended by barkeep Jarel Moor, who warns casual visitors to stay away from the shadows. That warning is literal. Descending through the back passages reveals a subterranean complex of crypts and summoning circles, where human warlocks and transfer practitioners from Khaz Modan openly study fel arcana sheltered from the disapproving eyes of the Church of the Holy Light and the Kirin Tor.",sp=0},{t="The Noble's Tab",b="Operating a fel coventry in the heart of the capital invites constant peril. When Lord Baurles K. Wishock discovered the warlocks lurking in the basement, he threatened to rally the House of Nobles and petition the throne for a full investigation. In truth, the aristocrat was merely trying to dodge a ruinous bar tab. Before his agitation could draw real scrutiny, Zardeth of the Black Claw arranged for Wishock to drink a fatal concoction, permanently silencing the meddler and preserving the haven's secrets.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What actually goes on under the Slaughtered Lamb?",a="The catacombs beneath the tavern serve as the hidden sanctum for Stormwind's warlocks. Practitioners of demonology and shadow magic gather there to teach apprentices, conduct summonings, and practice fel arts forbidden in the streets above.",al={"what is under slaughtered lamb","slaughtered lamb basement","who is in slaughtered lamb"},it="purpose"},{q="Does the Stormwind City Guard know about the warlocks?",a="The tavern operates under a precarious veil of plausible deniability. Fel magic is viewed with deep distrust by the Church of the Holy Light and the Mage Academy, forcing the coven to operate in secrecy and aggressively quiet anyone who threatens to expose them to the royal authorities.",al={"do guards know about warlocks","why aren't warlocks arrested","is slaughtered lamb illegal"},it="ties"},{q="Who was Lord Wishock, and what happened to him?",a="Lord Baurles K. Wishock is a nobleman and tavern regular who discovered the warlocks hiding below. He caused a stir in the House of Nobles and lobbied for a full investigation, hoping to petition the king to shut the establishment down.",al={"baurles wishock","lord wishock fate","who is wishock"},sp=1,it="conflict"},{q="Why do gnome warlocks come here?",a="After the fall of Gnomeregan, its warlock masters relocated to Ironforge, where Magni keeps a careful watch on them. Lago Blackwrench sends novices to Gakin the Darkbinder in the Slaughtered Lamb for training.",al={"gnome warlocks stormwind","khaz modan warlocks"},it="why_here"},{q="What is the Slaughtered Lamb?",a="On the surface, the Slaughtered Lamb is a quiet, seedy tavern nestled in Stormwind's Mage Quarter. Above ground, it seems almost neglected, with an empty taproom tended only by its bartender, Jarel Moor. Beneath its floorboards, however, stretches a sprawling network of subterranean crypts and catacombs. These dark depths serve as the hidden sanctum for Stormwind's practicing warlocks, shielding their forbidden fel rites and summonings from the disapproving gaze of the city guard and the House of Nobles.",al={"what is slaughtered lamb","slaughtered lamb tavern","the slaughtered lamb"},it="place",add="28eb4e6b"},{q="What happened at the Slaughtered Lamb?",a="The tavern's secretive basement was nearly exposed when Lord Baurles K. Wishock discovered the warlocks hiding beneath it. He caused a stir in the House of Nobles and lobbied for a full investigation, hoping to petition the king to shut the establishment down.",al={"slaughtered lamb history","what happened at the slaughtered lamb","slaughtered lamb background"},sp=1,it="history",add="f1944543"},{q="Who runs the Slaughtered Lamb?",a="The upper taproom is kept by Jarel Moor, a bartender who quietly warns curious patrons to steer clear of the dark corners. Below ground, the shadowy enclave is populated by secretive warlock mentors and conjurers, including figures like Zardeth of the Black Claw. They instruct human apprentices as well as gnome transfers, keeping a low profile so business and dark sorcery can proceed undisturbed.",al={"who runs slaughtered lamb","slaughtered lamb bartender","who is in slaughtered lamb"},it="residents",add="531ea530"},{q="Is the Slaughtered Lamb dangerous?",a="The warlocks harboring here guard their secrets jealously from anyone who threatens to expose their subterranean covens.",al={"is slaughtered lamb dangerous","slaughtered lamb danger","is it safe in the slaughtered lamb"},sp=1,it="danger",add="ecc63b24"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="The catacombs below are your primary sanctuary in Stormwind, offering class trainers, demon-binding rituals, and tasks essential to mastering the dark arts.",["faction:Alliance"]="While the Alliance champions the Light and order, the Slaughtered Lamb reveals the kingdom's unspoken willingness to tolerate dark magic in its shadow."},kw={"catacombs","jarel moor","mage quarter","slaughtered lamb","stormwind","warlock","wishock","zardeth"},rel={"subzone:mage-quarter","zone:stormwind","quest:1715","quest:335","quest:397","npc:zardeth-of-the-black-claw","npc:lord-baurles-k-wishock","topic:house-of-nobles"},src={"Slaughtered Lamb"}}
E["subzone:stormwind-keep"] = {t="subzone",n="Stormwind Keep",z="stormwind",s="Stormwind Keep stands high above the capital as the stone fortress and seat of power for the Kingdom of Stormwind. Rebuilt after its ruin in the First War, it currently houses the royal court of the young boy-king Anduin Wrynn and his regent, Highlord Bolvar Fordragon.",h="Stormwind Keep stands high above the capital as the stone fortress and seat of power for the Kingdom of...",sec={{t="The Rebuilt Citadel",b="Perched upon a plateau overlooking the entire city, Stormwind Keep serves as both a palace and a military bastion. The original stronghold was burned to the ground by the Old Horde when King Llane was assassinated near the end of the First War. Raised anew upon the old foundations after the Alliance reclaimed the kingdom, the reconstructed keep houses not only the grand throne room and the War Room, but peaceful garden courtyards and the expansive Royal Library.",sp=0},{t="A Divided Court",b="Behind the keep's banners and polished stone lies an uneasy peace. With King Varian Wrynn mysteriously missing en route to a diplomatic summit at Theramore, governance rests on ten-year-old King Anduin Wrynn. Effective rule falls to Highlord Bolvar Fordragon and the noble Lady Katrana Prestor. While Bolvar handles defense and military affairs, court politics remain paralyzed by aristocratic infighting, leaving the outlying territories vulnerable and the crown deeply distracted.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who rules in Stormwind Keep right now?",a="King Anduin Wrynn technically holds the throne, but because he is only ten years old, Highlord Bolvar Fordragon governs as regent alongside Lady Katrana Prestor as royal advisor.",al={"who is in charge","who leads stormwind","who is the king"},it="residents"},{q="What happened to King Varian Wrynn?",a="King Varian vanished under mysterious circumstances while traveling across the sea to a peace conference in Theramore. His sudden disappearance left the throne vacant, forcing Bolvar and the court to crown young Anduin to ensure political stability.",al={"where is varian","varian missing","what happened to the king"}},{q="Was the keep destroyed in the First War?",a="Yes. Following the murder of King Llane Wrynn by Garona, the Old Horde overwhelmed the city and completely razed the keep. The current fortress was rebuilt upon the ancient foundations after the Alliance prevailed in the Second War.",al={"did the orcs destroy the keep","first war castle destruction"},it="history"},{q="What major wings can be visited inside the keep?",a="The complex contains the main throne room, the War Room directly behind it, the Petitioner's Chamber for visiting supplicants, an open garden courtyard, the Royal Gallery, and the Royal Library.",al={"keep rooms","what is inside the keep","wings of stormwind keep"}},{q="What is Stormwind Keep?",a="Stormwind Keep is the majestic fortress and seat of power for the human kingdom of Stormwind. Overlooking the entirety of the city, the stronghold serves as both the royal palace and the heart of the realm's government. Inside its fortified stone walls, you will find the royal court, the throne room, audience chambers for petitioners, the Royal Library, and peaceful interior gardens, alongside barracks for the castle's elite personal guard.",al={"what is stormwind keep","stormwind keep purpose","about stormwind keep"},it="place",add="3e1bbfc4"},{q="Is Stormwind Keep dangerous?",a="For loyal subjects and allies of the Alliance, Stormwind Keep is one of the safest sanctuaries in the world. Heavily garrisoned by elite royal guards and protectors of the crown, it stands vigilant against outside threats. However, beneath the surface of peaceful courtly life lies subtle political intrigue, with noble factions and royal advisors vying for influence over the young king while the kingdom contends with rising turmoil across the realm.",al={"is stormwind keep dangerous","stormwind keep safe","is the keep hostile"},it="danger",add="a781e02c"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The keep is the heart of the Alliance's eastern military command, where Bolvar Fordragon and the marshals direct defenses against rising threats across Elwynn, Westfall, and beyond.",["race:Human"]="Rebuilt from ashes after the devastation of the First War, the fortress stands as a testament to the resilience and pride of Stormwind's people."},kw={"anduin wrynn","bolvar fordragon","castle stormwind","katrana prestor","royal library","stormwind keep","throne room","war room"},rel={"topic:varian-wrynn","subzone:war-room","subzone:royal-library","subzone:petitioner-s-chamber","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:first-war"},src={"Stormwind Keep"}}
E["subzone:stormwind-stockade"] = {t="subzone",n="Stormwind Stockade",z="stormwind",s="Stormwind Stockade holds the city’s most dangerous prisoners beneath the canals near the Mage Quarter. A coordinated revolt has driven the guards from the lower cells, leaving the prison in chaos.",h="Stormwind Stockade holds the city’s most dangerous prisoners beneath the canals near the Mage Quarter.",sec={{t="A Prison Under Siege",b="Warden Thelwater oversees the Stockade, where Stormwind keeps cutthroats, Defias operatives, captured Blackrock orcs, and Dark Iron dwarves. Now a violent uprising led by the Defias conspirator Bazil Thredd has forced the guards from the lower cells. The prisoners roam freely through the corridors. Thelwater has managed to secure the entrance, but the revolt still threatens to reach the canals. He depends on adventurers to enter the prison and put down the uprising.",sp=0},{t="Bureaucracy and Backroom Schemes",b="The House of Nobles has used the Stockade to hold prisoners whose fates serve its political aims. Murderers and other high-value prisoners sentenced to death elsewhere have had their executions delayed by aristocratic interference. Among them are Dextren Ward, a graverobber from Duskwood, and Targorr the Dread, a Blackrock executioner from Redridge. Ironforge has also taken notice. When human bureaucracy delays justice, it secretly hires mercenaries to execute dangerous prisoners such as Kam Deepfury.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is the entrance to the Stockade located?",a="The entrance is in Stormwind City's canal district, on the northern bend beside the bridge into the Mage Quarter. A guarded doorway leads down a stone stairwell to the underground cells.",al={"stockade entrance","how to get to stockades","stockade location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who started the riot inside the prison?",a="Bazil Thredd planned and began the revolt. The imprisoned Defias Brotherhood ringleader led the prisoners in overpowering the guards, taking their weapons, and seizing the underground cellblocks.",al={"who is bazil thredd","who leads the stockade riot","who runs the stockade"},it="conflict"},{q="Why are there orcs and Dark Iron dwarves in a Stormwind jail?",a="Stormwind holds hostile prisoners captured across its contested territories. Targorr the Dread was taken from the Redridge Mountains, while Kam Deepfury represents the Dark Iron threat. Some are kept as military prisoners; others remain alive by noble decree, held for political leverage instead of being executed swiftly.",al={"why are there orcs in stockades","dark iron prisoners stockade"},it="residents"},{q="Why are Duskwood and Redridge asking people to kill prisoners here?",a="Darkshire and Lakeshire sentenced Dextren Ward and Targorr the Dread to death, but the House of Nobles stayed their executions. Frustrated by Stormwind's interference, local leaders quietly hire sellswords to carry out the sentences.",al={"duskwood stockade quest","crime and punishment","what comes around"},it="motive"},{q="What is the Stormwind Stockade?",a="The Stockade is a high-security subterranean prison complex carved out beneath the canals of Stormwind City. Presided over by Warden Thelwater, it was built to house the kingdom's most dangerous criminals, including murderers, political insurgents, Defias brigands, and foreign hostiles awaiting judgment.",al={"what is the stockade","stormwind stockade info","what is stockade"},it="place",add="e9dc0ba3"},{q="What happened at the Stormwind Stockade?",a="A violent, prisoner-led revolt broke out inside the complex, orchestrated by the captured Defias mastermind Bazil Thredd. The rioting inmates overpowered their jailers, drove the guards completely out of the cell blocks, and took control of the facility. The city guard is now keeping the crisis secret while recruiting mercenaries to retake it.",al={"what happened in the stockade","stockade history","why is there a riot in the stockades"},it="history",add="d734f0f2"},{q="Is the Stormwind Stockade dangerous?",a="It is extremely dangerous right now. The inmates roam free within the halls without supervision, armed and organized under Defias leadership alongside cutthroats, Blackrock orcs, and Dark Iron infiltrators. Anyone entering must fight their way through lawless, hostile corridors where the guards hold no ground.",al={"how dangerous is the stockade","is stockade dangerous","danger in stockades"},it="danger",add="10925a1c"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance hero, you can see why keeping the Stockade secure matters to Stormwind's defense. Its halls reveal how far the Defias Brotherhood has reached into the capital.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you can read the riot as a glimpse of the Defias Brotherhood's operations under Bazil Thredd. The criminal underworld is deeply organized beneath the crown's nose."},kw={"bazil thredd","canals","defias","dextren ward","kam deepfury","prison","riot","stockade","stormwind","targorr","warden thelwater"},rel={"zone:stockade","zone:stormwind","npc:warden-thelwater","quest:389","quest:391","topic:defias-brotherhood","npc:targorr-the-dread","npc:dextren-ward"},src={"Stormwind Stockade"}}
E["subzone:stormwind-stockade-classic"] = {t="subzone",n="Stormwind Stockade (Classic)",z="stormwind",s="Prisoners now control the Stormwind Stockade beneath Stormwind City's canal district. A revolt has driven the guards from its halls.",h="Prisoners now control the Stormwind Stockade beneath Stormwind City's canal district.",sec={{t="A Prison in Revolt",b="The Stockade lies off the canals between Old Town and the Mage Quarter, holding Stormwind's most dangerous prisoners. Warden Thelwater oversees the underground prison. Its inmates include Defias Brotherhood cutthroats, a Blackrock orc, an ogre, and a Dark Iron dwarf. Bazil Thredd recently led a coordinated riot that overwhelmed the garrison. The surviving guards fled, leaving the prisoners in control of the halls.",sp=0},{t="Bureaucracy and Retribution",b="The Stockade's disorder lays bare deep cracks in Stormwind's rule. Targorr the Dread, a feared Blackrock orc, and Dextren Ward, a grave robber who sold bodies, had both been sentenced to death. Influential nobles kept them alive through endless stays of execution. Fed up with aristocratic delays, Lakeshire, Darkshire, and the dwarven garrison at Dun Modr bypassed royal channels. They hired outsiders to enter the chaos and execute key ringleaders.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is the Stockade located?",a="The Stockade entrance lies inside Stormwind City, along the northern canal bank between Old Town and the Cathedral and Mage districts.",al={"stockade entrance","how to get to stockade","stockade location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is currently running the prison?",a="Warden Thelwater is the prison's official warden, but the rebellion drove him out. Bazil Thredd, who started the uprising, now controls the prison with allied Defias rioters.",al={"who is in charge of stockade","stockade boss","bazil thredd"},it="in_charge"},{q="Why are there orcs and Dark Iron dwarves locked up in Stormwind?",a="Stormwind holds prisoners of war and saboteurs there. Targorr the Dread is a captured Blackrock orc raider from the nearby mountains, and Kam Deepfury is a Dark Iron dwarf imprisoned for subversion against the Alliance.",al={"why are there orcs in stockade","kam deepfury","targorr the dread"},it="ties"},{q="Why were condemned murderers kept alive instead of executed?",a="Stormwind nobles repeatedly delayed executions for convicts such as Dextren Ward and Targorr. Their political interference and bureaucratic delays angered outer territories such as Redridge and Duskwood.",al={"why werent they executed","stormwind nobles","dextren ward execution"},it="motive"},{q="What is the Stormwind Stockade?",a="The Stockade is a heavily guarded, high-security prison complex built beneath the canal district of Stormwind City. Under the authority of Warden Thelwater, it was intended to lock away the realm's worst offenders—ranging from petty street thieves and grave-robbers to political insurgents, Defias conspirators, and ruthless murderers.",al={"what is the stockade","stockade stormwind","explain the stockade"},it="place",add="d4f3da71"},{q="What happened at the Stormwind Stockade?",a="A violent prisoner revolt recently erupted inside the cells, spearheaded by the cunning mastermind Bazil Thredd. The rioting inmates overpowered the guards, murdering watchmen and driving Warden Thelwater out into the canals. With the city guard locked outside, the convicts seized complete control of the complex, turning the subterranean halls into a fortified haven for cutthroats and conspirators.",al={"what happened here","stockade riot story","stockade history"},it="history",add="5c482541"},{q="Is the Stormwind Stockade dangerous?",a="It is exceptionally dangerous. The narrow stone corridors are swarming with liberated killers, Defias mercenaries, ferocious Blackrock orcs, and Dark Iron infiltrators. Trapped together in cramped quarters, the inmates will violently swarm anyone who enters, and the risk of hostile reinforcements spilling out into the city canals remains an active threat to Stormwind's safety.",al={"how dangerous is the stockade","is the stockade safe","stockade danger"},it="danger",add="b72eefeb"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The riot beneath the capital's streets humiliates Highlord Bolvar Fordragon's administration. It shows Stormwind's vulnerability from within while the king remains absent.",["race:Human"]="For humans in the outlying towns, the Stockade's failure shows that the House of Nobles puts legal delays in the capital ahead of protecting border settlements from murderers."},kw={"bazil thredd","defias","dextren ward","kam deepfury","prison","stockade","stormwind stockade","targorr the dread","uprising","warden thelwater"},rel={"zone:stockade","npc:warden-thelwater","topic:defias-brotherhood","npc:targorr-the-dread","npc:kam-deepfury","npc:dextren-ward","zone:stormwind"},src={"Stormwind Stockade (Classic)"}}
E["subzone:trade-district"] = {t="subzone",n="Trade District",z="stormwind",s="Past the Valley of Heroes, Trade District draws Stormwind’s merchants and travelers. Its bank, Auction House, guild registry, and shops serve citizens and adventurers alike.",h="Past the Valley of Heroes, Trade District draws Stormwind’s merchants and travelers.",sec={{t="The Crossroads of Commerce",b="You pass beneath the stone arches from the Valley of Heroes into Trade District. The open plaza is Stormwind’s main marketplace and a hub for goods and travel. The Auction House stands at its center, with the Stormwind Counting House, the city’s main bank, and The Gilded Rose nearby. From here, routes lead to Old Town, the Cathedral Square, and the Mage Quarter. Coin, raw goods, and supplies for adventurers pass through the district on their way across the realm.",sp=0},{t="Bazaars and Guild Halls",b="Shops line the paved avenues and canals, offering goods for daily needs and travel. Weller’s Arsenal and Lionheart Armory sell blades and mail, while The Empty Quiver offers bows. Stalls sell fresh flowers and aged vintages from the Gallina Winery. Just inside the gates, the Stormwind Visitor’s Center handles newly registered guild charters and tabard designs. On the eastern side, an elevated ramp leads to the Gryphon Roost, connecting Stormwind’s markets with Alliance territories.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Trade District located?",a="Trade District lies just past Stormwind’s main gates and the Valley of Heroes. Cathedral Square is to the northwest, Old Town to the east, and the Mage Quarter lies across the canals to the southwest.",al={"trade district location","where is trade district","how to get to trade district"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Where can I find the bank and the inn?",a="The Stormwind Counting House and The Gilded Rose are along Trade District’s southwest perimeter, near the main thoroughfare.",al={"trade district bank","gilded rose location","stormwind bank trade district"},gp=true},{q="Where do I register a guild or design a tabard in Stormwind?",a="The Stormwind Visitor’s Center is on your left just inside Trade District’s city gates. The Guild Master and tabard design services are there.",al={"guild master stormwind","guild registrar","make a guild"},gp=true},{q="Where can I take a gryphon flight from the Trade District?",a="Take the stone ramp on Trade District’s eastern side to reach the Gryphon Roost, where the flight master sends gryphons across the kingdom and beyond.",al={"flight master stormwind","gryphon roost stormwind","where is flight master"},gp=true},{q="What is the Trade District?",a="The Trade District is the bustling commercial heart of Stormwind City, situated immediately inside the main gates past the Valley of Heroes. It serves as the primary hub for commerce, banking, and travel in the kingdom. Travelers arrive here to trade goods, purchase provisions from bustling shops, send mail, and visit the Stormwind Counting House. It also houses the city's primary gryphon roost, offering flight paths across the Eastern Kingdoms.",al={"trade district overview","what is this place","stormwind trade district"},it="place",add="747b4250"},{q="Why is it called the Trade District?",a="The district takes its name from its role as Stormwind's main commercial marketplace, sometimes referred to as the Bazaar District. Merchants, shopkeepers, and traveling traders gather here to sell almost every variety of goods—from armor, weapons, and arcane reagents to fresh cheese, flowers, and fine wine. Centered around commerce, it houses both the city's banking vaults and its bustling mercantile houses.",al={"why trade district","trade district name origin","bazaar district"},it="name",add="d6628855"},{q="Is the Trade District dangerous?",a="Under normal circumstances, the Trade District is exceptionally safe. Patrolled constantly by Stormwind City guards and situated right inside the grand gates, it is protected from outside threats. While thieves or political tension might lurk quietly in the shadows of the capital, honest folk and visiting adventurers can trade, bank, and conduct their business in peace without fear of wilderness perils.",al={"trade district safe","is trade district dangerous","any threats in trade district"},it="danger",add="7971c440"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance champion, you can bank, trade at the Auction House, organize your guild, and take flight from Trade District."},kw={"auction house","bazaar","counting house","gilded rose","gryphon roost","stormwind","trade district","visitor center"},rel={"zone:stormwind","subzone:valley-of-heroes","subzone:gryphon-roost","subzone:cathedral-square","subzone:old-town","subzone:mage-quarter","subzone:canals-stormwind-city"},src={"Trade District"}}
E["subzone:valley-of-heroes"] = {t="subzone",n="Valley of Heroes",z="stormwind",s="Stone statues watch over the Valley of Heroes, where Stormwind's southern road crosses the moat into the city. They honor the leaders of the Alliance Expedition to Draenor, and guards hold this fortified entrance.",h="Stone statues watch over the Valley of Heroes, where Stormwind's southern road crosses the moat into the city.",sec={{t="A Monument to the Lost",b="You cross the moat beneath statues honoring the commanders of the Alliance Expedition. Stormwind's rebuilding after the Second War raised these monuments along the causeway. The champions marched through the Dark Portal into Draenor to seal the rift forever, giving their lives so Azeroth might survive. As you head north toward the Trade District, you pass Archmage Khadgar, Kurdran Wildhammer, Ranger-Captain Alleria Windrunner, Force Commander Danath Trollbane, and High General Turalyon.",sp=0},{t="The City Bastion",b="General Marcus Jonathan watches Stormwind's gates from horseback, overseeing the guards and the traffic in and out. The valley is the city's main defense against an overland invasion. Major Mattingly, Field Marshal Stonebridge, and rows of seasoned guards keep watch beside him, guarding the capital from threats beyond its walls.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who are the statues lining the path?",a="The five statues honor the commanders of the Sons of Lothar who led the Alliance Expedition to Draenor: High General Turalyon, Ranger-Captain Alleria Windrunner, Archmage Khadgar, Kurdran Wildhammer, and Force Commander Danath Trollbane.",al={"statues in stormwind","who are the heroes","valley statues","names on statues"},it="people"},{q="Why were these monuments placed at the city gate?",a="Stormwind raised the statues during its restoration after the Second War to honor heroes believed lost in Draenor's destruction. They remind those entering the city of the price paid to keep the kingdom safe.",al={"why build statues here","valley of heroes purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Who commands the guards stationed at the entrance?",a="General Marcus Jonathan commands the Stormwind City Guard and oversees security at the entrance. Major Mattingly and Field Marshal Stonebridge support him.",al={"guard captain","who is the guy on the horse","who leads stormwind defense"},it="in_charge"},{q="Where does the Valley of Heroes lead?",a="The bridge leads north into Stormwind City's Trade District. South through the gates, the road enters Elwynn's forests.",al={"where does bridge go","directions stormwind gate"},it="place"},{q="What is the Valley of Heroes?",a="The Valley of Heroes is the grand, lush entryway that lies before the main gates of Stormwind City. A broad stone bridge spans the moat between Elwynn Forest and the city's gates, flanked by towering monuments commemorating legendary champions. For anyone arriving by foot from the south, it serves as the grand threshold to the human kingdom's capital.",al={"what is valley of heroes","valley of heroes stormwind","about valley of heroes"},it="place",add="f5acfed9"},{q="What happened at the Valley of Heroes?",a="Following the Second War and during the rebuilding of Stormwind, this valley was reshaped into an enduring memorial. Five monumental statues were erected to honor the Alliance Expedition that marched through the Dark Portal into the shattered world of Draenor to seal the dimensional rift. Believed lost forever on the other side, these five commanders were immortalized in stone as an eternal tribute to their sacrifice.",al={"valley of heroes history","valley of heroes lore","what happened here"},it="history",add="5176beb8"},{q="Is the Valley of Heroes dangerous?",a="No. The Valley of Heroes is heavily fortified and serves as the primary entrance to the Alliance capital. Watched over by senior officers like General Marcus Jonathan and constantly patrolled by the city guard, it is one of the most secure places in all of Azeroth for Alliance travelers.",al={"is valley of heroes safe","is valley of heroes dangerous","danger in valley of heroes"},it="danger",add="7507c845"},{q="Why is it called the Valley of Heroes?",a="The valley takes its name from the colossal stone statues standing along its approach. Each depicts a prominent leader of the Alliance Expedition to Draenor—Turalyon, Alleria Windrunner, Khadgar, Danath Trollbane, and Kurdran Wildhammer—who sacrificed everything to protect Azeroth from the demonic threat beyond the Dark Portal.",al={"why is it called valley of heroes","valley of heroes name origin","why valley of heroes"},it="name",add="6b62f2c8"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As a citizen of the Grand Alliance, you can honor the human, high elven, and dwarven martyrs remembered together in the valley.",["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you can look to the statue of General Turalyon, one of the original champions of the Knights of the Silver Hand."},kw={"alleria","danath","khadgar","kurdran","marcus jonathan","stormwind gate","turalyon","valley of heroes"},rel={"subzone:stormwind-gate","zone:stormwind","zone:elwynn","subzone:trade-district","npc:general-marcus-jonathan","topic:alliance","topic:second-war","subzone:dark-portal"},src={"Valley of Heroes"}}
E["subzone:war-room"] = {t="subzone",n="War Room",z="stormwind",s="Deep inside Stormwind Keep, the War Room gathers the arms, records, and charts used to plan the Alliance’s defense.",h="Deep inside Stormwind Keep, the War Room gathers the arms, records, and charts used to plan the Alliance’s...",sec={{t="Nerve Center of the Keep",b="Beyond Stormwind Keep’s grand chambers, commanders turn to military logistics and high-level campaign planning. Swords, blunderbusses, and heavy artillery cannons line the stone walls. Military treatises and chronicles of past wars fill nearby tables. At the center, a large map lets commanders assess Alliance deployments across Azeroth, while the royal court handles affairs of state just steps away.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the War Room located?",a="Deep inside Stormwind Keep, beyond its central corridors, the War Room has heavy fortifications, weapon racks, and a large tactical map table.",al={"war room location","how to find war room","where is the map room"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the purpose of this room?",a="The War Room is the Alliance military’s strategic planning headquarters within Stormwind. High commanders review intelligence, coordinate troop movements, and study conflicts past and present.",al={"what is war room for","war room purpose","why does the keep have a war room"},it="purpose"},{q="What historical lore can be found here?",a="The tables hold books on military strategy and chronicles of the kingdom’s past wars, close at hand for commanders planning Alliance campaigns.",al={"war room books","books in stormwind keep","historical tomes war room"},it="history"},{q="What is the War Room?",a="The War Room is a strategic military chamber within Stormwind Keep, located just off the main throne room hall. It serves as the high command center where commanders, tacticians, and Alliance leaders assemble to oversee ongoing military campaigns. Filled with maps, weaponry, strategy tomes, and cannons, the room is dedicated entirely to the defense and strategic mobilization of Stormwind and its allies.",al={"what is war room","about war room","stormwind war room"},it="place",add="bec1bb93"},{q="Who oversees the War Room?",a="The room is staffed by the Alliance's high-ranking military strategists, generals, and spellcasters who coordinate theater operations. Mages and battle officers maintain constant watch over regional conflicts, drafting tactics and directing reinforcements across the kingdom's borders.",al={"who is in war room","who runs war room","war room commanders"},it="residents",add="2eaea60b"},{q="Is the War Room dangerous?",a="Not to members of the Alliance. It sits deep inside Stormwind Keep, surrounded by the elite royal guard and military brass. For intruders or agents of the Horde, however, infiltrating this fortified strategic sanctuary would mean certain death.",al={"war room safe","is war room safe","war room threats"},it="danger",add="3751c6cd"},{q="Why is it called the War Room?",a="The room earns its name from its dedicated purpose: it is the nerve center where the kingdom's military actions are orchestrated. Lined with blunderbusses, swords, cannons, and tactical maps, every feature in the chamber exists to plan and wage the Alliance's campaigns.",al={"war room name meaning","why called war room"},it="name",add="6b32db00"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance soldier or champion, you can look to the War Room for plans to defend the realm from lingering threats across the Eastern Kingdoms and beyond.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you may value the military order kept inside Stormwind Keep, among its heavy munitions and strategic maps."},kw={"dark portal","grim batol","map room","stormwind keep","strategy table","war room"},rel={"subzone:stormwind-keep","zone:stormwind","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:alliance","subzone:grim-batol","subzone:dark-portal"},src={"War Room"}}
E["topic:terenas-menethil-ii"] = {t="topic",n="Terenas Menethil II",z="stormwind",s="Across Lordaeron, Terenas Menethil II carries the weight of a kingdom through war and its aftermath. For more than five decades, he ruled as a wise and diplomatic king, forged the Alliance of Lordaeron during the Second War, and gave shelter to the young Prince Varian Wrynn. His murder by his corrupted son, Prince Arthas, began Lordaeron’s collapse to the Scourge.",h="Across Lordaeron, Terenas Menethil II carries the weight of a kingdom through war and its aftermath.",sec={{t="Architect of the Alliance",b="When refugees from Stormwind reached the north with Sir Anduin Lothar, King Terenas Menethil II answered their call. He gathered the monarchs of the divided human kingdoms, along with envoys from Ironforge and Quel'Thalas, and brought them together in the Alliance of Lordaeron. Terenas did not claim command of its armies. He chose Lothar as supreme commander, uniting humanity’s kingdoms for the first time in millennia. Together, they defeated the Old Horde.",sp=0},{t="The Strains of Victory",b="After the Second War, Terenas insisted that surviving orcs be held in internment camps rather than executed. He believed peace might hold once their demonic fury faded. The camps placed a heavy tax burden on Lordaeron’s allies. Gilneas shut itself behind the Greymane Wall, Stromgarde left the Alliance over political disputes, and the high elves withdrew entirely. Terenas was left to bear the cost as the coalition fractured.",sp=0},{t="The Fall of the Throne",b="Terenas faced orc revolts led by Thrall, whispers of death cults in the north, and a mysterious plague. A wandering prophet urged the king to abandon Lordaeron and flee across the sea to Kalimdor, but Terenas dismissed him as mad. Soon after, Prince Arthas returned from his northern campaign, hailed as a victor. During the royal celebrations, Arthas knelt before his father, drew the runeblade Frostmourne, and drove it through Terenas’s heart. The kingdom was shattered.",sp=2}},faq={{q="Who was King Terenas Menethil II?",a="King Terenas Menethil II ruled Lordaeron for more than fifty years and stood at the heart of northern politics. He founded the Alliance of Lordaeron to fight the Horde in the Second War and governed from Capital City until his murder.",al={"who is terenas","terenas menethil","king of lordaeron"},it="identity"},{q="How did Terenas die?",a="Terenas died by his son Prince Arthas Menethil’s hand in the throne room. Corrupted by the runeblade Frostmourne during his expedition to Northrend, Arthas returned to Capital City hailed as a victor and drove the blade through his father’s heart.",al={"how did terenas die","arthas kills dad","terenas death"}},{q="What was Terenas's relationship with Stormwind?",a="Terenas helped Stormwind survive. After the southern kingdom fell in the First War, he gave its survivors haven and raised Prince Varian Wrynn alongside his own son Arthas. He treated Varian like a second son until Stormwind could be reclaimed and rebuilt.",al={"terenas and stormwind","terenas and varian","did terenas help stormwind"},it="ties"},{q="Why did the Alliance of Lordaeron break apart under his rule?",a="Terenas chose to hold captured orcs in internment camps after the Second War rather than execute them. Their great cost stirred anger among the member realms. Gilneas built the Greymane Wall and isolated itself, Stromgarde left over policy disputes, and the elves of Quel'Thalas withdrew entirely.",al={"why did alliance break","why did kingdoms leave lordaeron","internment camp taxes"},it="conflict"},{q="Did Terenas know about the Plague of Undeath?",a="Terenas knew of strange cults and a spreading sickness in the north, but underestimated the danger. Dalaran urged him to quarantine northern towns, yet he hesitated, fearing more suffering for his people. He sent Prince Arthas and Uther the Lightbringer to investigate, unaware of the trap awaiting them.",al={"did terenas know about plague","terenas plague response"}},{q="Why didn't Terenas listen to the mysterious Prophet?",a="A cloaked prophet came to Terenas’s council chamber and urged him to evacuate Lordaeron’s people west to Kalimdor. Terenas dismissed him as an unhinged zealot, believing his armies, paladins, and sturdy kingdom could endure the coming trials.",al={"terenas and prophet","medivh and terenas","why didnt terenas flee"},it="motive"},{q="Who were King Terenas's closest allies?",a="During his reign, Terenas counted King Thoras Trollbane of Stromgarde and Uther the Lightbringer among his closest personal friends, regarding Uther almost like a brother. He also took in Prince Varian Wrynn and Sir Anduin Lothar as refugees, fostering Varian like a second son alongside Prince Arthas. Though nations like Gilneas and Quel'Thalas eventually abandoned the Alliance over taxes and borders, Terenas maintained the steadfast loyalty of Stormwind, Ironforge, Kul Tiras, and the Kirin Tor of Dalaran until his death.",al={"terenas allies","who supported terenas","allies of king terenas"},it="allies",add="be9b83e5"},{q="What is the history of King Terenas Menethil II?",a="Born to the royal Menethil dynasty that ruled Lordaeron for generations, Terenas oversaw over five decades of peace and prosperity. When Stormwind fell in the First War, he rallied the human realms, high elves, and dwarves to form the original Alliance of Lordaeron, successfully repelling the Horde in the Second War. Terenas advocated interning rather than executing defeated orcs, which strained Alliance coffers and pushed several kingdoms away. His long, noble reign ended abruptly when his own son, Prince Arthas, returned corrupted from Northrend and murdered him in the royal throne room.",al={"history of terenas","terenas menethil reign","story of king terenas"},it="history",add="aa06bf27"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human, you remember King Terenas as a legendary patriarch who united the seven kingdoms against impossible odds. His sudden betrayal and death at his own son’s hands remain a national tragedy.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you inherit the legacy of the coalition Terenas forged with Anduin Lothar to defeat the Old Horde in the Second War.",["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you follow a path Terenas helped shape with Archbishop Alonsus Faol and Uther the Lightbringer when they fostered the Knights of the Silver Hand. Terenas guided his own son into the order.",["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you once called Capital City home under Terenas, your last living sovereign. His fall doomed the realm to the Scourge."},kw={"alliance of lordaeron","arthas","capital city","frostmourne","lordaeron","menethil","second war","terenas","third war","uther"},rel={"topic:lordaeron","topic:alliance-of-lordaeron","topic:second-war","topic:third-war","topic:varian-wrynn","topic:anduin-lothar","topic:scourge","subzone:greymane-wall"},src={"Terenas Menethil II"}}
E["zone:stormwind"] = {t="city",n="Stormwind City",z="stormwind",s="In Stormwind City, the crown rests on a young prince while King Varian is missing. Rebuilt after the First War, the city is now the heart of the Grand Alliance, though debt and political turmoil trouble its white stone districts.",h="In Stormwind City, the crown rests on a young prince while King Varian is missing.",sec={{t="Rise from the Ashes",b="Stormwind was founded over a thousand years ago by descendants of the Arathi. For generations, it was a flourishing, self-sufficient realm. The Orcish Horde crossed the Dark Portal and laid waste to the southern continent, razing the capital during the First War. Survivors followed Sir Anduin Lothar north across the Great Sea to Lordaeron. After the Horde fell in the Second War, King Terenas Menethil II and the Alliance paid to rebuild the city. The Stonemasons Guild raised New Stormwind from polished white stone, with canals running through its boroughs.",sp=0},{t="A Divided Court",b="Stormwind’s grand appearance hides a kingdom in debt and a court divided. The House of Nobles and the Stonemasons Guild fought over wages, and the dispute left the kingdom paralyzed by debt. The guild’s workers rioted and were driven from the city they had built. King Varian Wrynn has vanished on his way to a diplomatic summit. To keep panic at bay, the crown went to his ten-year-old son, Prince Anduin Wrynn. Highlord Bolvar Fordragon now rules as Regent and military commander, with royal advisor Lady Katrana Prestor at his side.",sp=0},{t="Heart of the Grand Alliance",b="With Lordaeron overrun by the Scourge, Stormwind has become humanity’s greatest haven and the Alliance’s center. High Tinker Mekkatorque’s underground Deeprun Tram links the city directly to Ironforge, the dwarven kingdom. Across the Valley of Heroes, towering statues honor the Sons of Lothar, who vanished beyond the Dark Portal. The Cathedral of Light draws the faithful, while the Wizard’s Sanctum houses arcane study. Trade, culture, and defense across the southern seas all meet in Stormwind.",sp=0},{t="Where the Masons Went",b="The stonemasons gathered again in Westfall under their guildmaster, Edwin VanCleef. There they became the Defias Brotherhood, red-masked bandits now strangling the kingdom’s farmland. The builders of Stormwind’s white walls have sworn to make the House of Nobles pay for every stone.",sp=1,bt={"defias.masons"}},{t="A Friend at Court",b="The Defias Brotherhood found help within Stormwind Keep. Lord Gregor Lescovar of the House of Nobles secretly dealt with the Brotherhood, passing along the kingdom’s plans while sitting among the lords who had cheated the stonemasons.",sp=1,bt={"unsent.lescovar"}},{t="Shadows in the Keep",b="Lady Katrana Prestor has secretly guided the House of Nobles’ decisions. She inflamed its conflict with the stonemasons and ignored pleas for military aid from settlements such as Westfall and Redridge. She also whispered poison to Highlord Bolvar, keeping Stormwind’s legions idle and divided as unrest beyond the city walls threatens the throne.",sp=2,bt={"prestor.onyxia"}}},faq={{q="Who rules Stormwind right now?",a="Ten-year-old Prince Anduin Wrynn holds Stormwind’s crown, while Highlord Bolvar Fordragon governs as Regent and commands its military. Bolvar relies on royal advisor Lady Katrana Prestor’s counsel as King Varian Wrynn remains missing.",al={"current king","who is the king","who leads stormwind","king of stormwind"},it="in_charge"},{q="What happened to King Varian Wrynn?",a="King Varian vanished under suspicious circumstances while sailing to a diplomatic summit in Theramore. His disappearance was kept quiet to preserve stability, though rumors spread through the streets and countryside.",al={"where is varian","missing king","varian gone","varian wrynn missing"},it="leader"},{q="Why was the city rebuilt, and by whom?",a="The Orcish Horde burned the original city to the ground during the First War. After the Second War, the Alliance of Lordaeron funded the rebuilding, and master craftsman Edwin VanCleef led the Stonemasons Guild in raising the capital from white stone.",al={"who rebuilt stormwind","stonemasons guild","new stormwind","city rebuilding"},sp=1,it="ruin"},{q="Why did the stonemasons rebel against the crown?",a="The House of Nobles took on heavy debts while expanding Stormwind’s military, then refused to pay the Stonemasons Guild its promised wages. When Edwin VanCleef demanded payment, the nobles disbanded the guild. The workers rioted and were driven from the city.",al={"defias origin","why defias mad","stonemasons riot"},sp=1,it="conflict"},{q="Who are the giant statues in the Valley of Heroes?",a="The Valley of Heroes honors the Sons of Lothar: General Turalyon, Ranger Captain Alleria Windrunner, Archmage Khadgar, Kurdran Wildhammer, and Danath Trollbane. The statues commemorate the heroes who entered the Dark Portal to draenor to seal the rift and protect Azeroth.",al={"statues at the entrance","valley of heroes statues","sons of lothar statues"},it="fame"},{q="How does Stormwind connect to Ironforge?",a="The Deeprun Tram, an underground railway, connects Stormwind to Ironforge. High Tinker Gelbin Mekkatorque built it at King Magni Bronzebeard’s request, so the capitals could trade swiftly and reinforce one another in war.",al={"deeprun tram","train to ironforge","how to get to ironforge"},it="place"},{q="Why isn't Stormwind sending troops to help Westfall and Redridge?",a="The royal court, guided by Lady Katrana Prestor, says Stormwind cannot spare troops from its walls and nearby borders. Kingdom finances are strained, and political infighting has paralyzed the House of Nobles, leaving regional towns to depend on their local militias.",al={"stormwind army missing","why no help for westfall","reinforcements refused"},it="ties"},{q="What is Stormwind City?",a="Stormwind City is the capital of the human kingdom of Stormwind and the greatest bastion of humanity left standing in Azeroth. Built north of Elwynn Forest along the coastline, it serves as the beating heart, primary port, and cultural center of the Grand Alliance. Reconstructed from the ashes of the First War, its fortified stone walls shelter craftsmen, scholars, soldiers, and refugees who look to the city as a symbol of human perseverance.",al={"about stormwind city","stormwind capital","what is stormwind"},it="place",add="9beefbfb"},{q="What happened to Stormwind City in the past?",a="Originally founded over a thousand years ago by descendants of the Arathor bloodline, the kingdom prospered for centuries through conflicts with gnolls and jungle trolls. However, during the First War, the Orcish Horde besieged the capital. Following the tragic murder of King Llane Wrynn, the city was breached, sacked, and burned to the ground. Sir Anduin Lothar led the surviving refugees north across the sea to Lordaeron, returning only after the Second War to reclaim their homeland and rebuild.",al={"stormwind history","destruction of stormwind","stormwind first war"},it="history",add="edb1c1aa"},{q="Is Stormwind City dangerous?",a="Behind its colossal gates and vigilant City Guard, Stormwind is one of the most heavily fortified sanctuaries in the world. However, unseen dangers linger within. The nearby Stockade has seen violent riots, cultists and thieves prowl the shadowed canals, and political unrest stirred by the Defias Brotherhood keeps the House of Nobles on edge. While open warfare rarely breaches the walls, corruption, treason, and hidden conspiracies whisper through the Keep and back alleys alike.",al={"is stormwind safe","danger in stormwind","threats to stormwind"},it="danger",add="d0a4b7c8"},{q="Who are the Defias Brotherhood?",a="The Defias Brotherhood is a ruthless guild of outlaws, brigands, thieves, and pirates who openly threaten the stability of the kingdom. They are recognizable by their signature red bandanas, worn to symbolize the blood spilled by their cause. Though they operate heavily out of Westfall, Redridge, and the Deadmines, their reach extends directly into Stormwind, where their spies and sympathizers undermine the crown's authority and sow discord among the working classes.",al={"defias brotherhood","who are the defias","defias gang"},it="threat",add="163d181d"},{q="What is the Cathedral of Light?",a="Soaring above Cathedral Square, the Cathedral of Light is the preeminent spiritual center for humanity and the Grand Alliance. Rebuilt after the Second War under Archbishop Alonsus Faol and then-bishop Benedictus, it serves as the seat of the Church of the Holy Light and a headquarters for the Order of the Silver Hand. Paladins and priests travel from across the realms to train, seek wisdom, and meditate within its grand, peaceful halls.",al={"cathedral of light","stormwind cathedral","church of light stormwind"},it="place",add="b1d432aa"},{q="How did I end up in Stormwind City?",a="If you began your journey in Northshire and worked your way through Elwynn Forest, the main road carried you straight through the Valley of Heroes and into the capital's fortified gates. If you hail from Dun Morogh or Ironforge, you likely boarded the Deeprun Tram, the marvel of gnomish engineering that links the dwarven stronghold directly to the Dwarven District beneath the mountains. Travelers from further across Azeroth arrive at Stormwind's gates after long treks through the southern kingdoms, seeking the last great bastion of humanity.",al={"how did i get here","how did i arrive in stormwind","how did i get to stormwind"},it="arrival",add="3414b788"},{q="What am I supposed to be doing in Stormwind City?",a="Stormwind is the beating heart of the Alliance and a haven to rest, train, and supply yourself. Beneath its gleaming white ramparts, however, the kingdom is deeply fractured. King Varian Wrynn has vanished under mysterious circumstances, leaving the boy-king Anduin and Highlord Bolvar Fordragon struggling against political paralysis in the Keep. Meanwhile, the surrounding frontiers in Westfall and Redridge cry out for aid against rampant banditry, and the Defias Brotherhood plots in the shadows. You are here to hone your craft, report to your faction leaders, and lend your sword to a beleaguered realm.",al={"why am i here","what do i do here","what is my purpose in stormwind"},it="purpose",add="68c43aeb"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human, Stormwind is your people’s last great seat of sovereign power after Lordaeron, Alterac, and Dalaran fell in the north.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can look to Stormwind for naval might, spiritual grounding, and vital diplomatic leadership. It is the Grand Alliance’s most populous metropolis.",["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you can find the Cathedral of Light, the south’s chief sanctuary of your faith. It trains knights of the Silver Hand and upholds justice.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you can find SI:7’s headquarters beneath Old Town’s stone streets. It runs the Alliance’s chief intelligence and espionage network.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you can travel the Deeprun Tram to your kin in the Dwarven District. They maintain close trade and military ties with the human kingdom."},kw={"anduin","bolvar","cathedral","deeprun","prestor","stonemasons","stormwind","vancleef","wrynn"},rel={"topic:stormwind-kingdom","subzone:stormwind-keep","subzone:valley-of-heroes","subzone:cathedral-of-light","subzone:deeprun-tram","topic:defias-brotherhood"},src={"Stormwind City"}}
